404,\n      \"CONFLICT\": 409,\n      \"INTERNAL\": 500,\n      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429,\n      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,\n      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410\n    },\n    \"newErrorCodesForThisPrd\": {\n      \"RATE_LIMITED\": \"Sign-in and forgot-password rate limiters (FR-6, FR-17) short-circuit to this before any DB work.\",\n      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": \"Defense-in-depth on change-password's requireUser() guard (FR-20, FR-23) — middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests, this is the handler-level backstop.\",\n      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": \"Invite/reset token is missing, wrong type, expired, or already used (FR-12, FR-18, FR-19) — distinct from NOT_FOUND because the token row may exist but be unusable; mapped to 410 Gone.\"\n    },\n    \"notModeledAsEndpoints\": \"Component 9's service functions (createUser, createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser — FR-22) are an internal module surface called by prisma/seed.ts (FR-28) and by later PRDs' admin UI, not by any form in this PRD. No endpoint is defined for them here; inventing an admin API now would be scope creep past NFR-8. Likewise /invite/[token] and /reset-password/[token]'s GET render (token validity check for FR-12) happens inside the Server Component itself via a direct Prisma lookup, not a client-side API call — no GET endpoint is defined for that for the same reason.\",\n    \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]\n  },\n\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider callback, invoked internally by signIn('credentials') from the /login page. Runs the authorize() chokepoint: rate-limit check (10/IP/5min) before any DB work, email normalize, status/lockout branch (dummy bcrypt-compare for timing safety on a non-existent user), bcrypt compare (cost 12), failedLoginCount/lockedUntil mutation, audit() writes, and on success stamps id/role/firstName/lastName/email into the JWT. Wire format (form-encoded body, redirect-based response) is owned by Auth.js, not src/server/http.ts.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"email\": \"string\",\n        \"password\": \"string\",\n        \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\",\n        \"callbackUrl\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"redirectSuccess\": \"same-origin callbackUrl if relative, else /dashboard (FR-7)\",\n        \"redirectFailure\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — same generic message for unknown-user and wrong-password (FR-4)\",\n        \"redirectLocked\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — locked-account message includes remaining minutes (FR-4)\",\n        \"redirectDisabled\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — distinct disabled-account message (FR-4)\",\n        \"redirectRateLimited\": \"/login?error=RateLimited — 'Too many attempts' message (FR-6)\"\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-8\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js session read. The jwt callback applies the passwordChangedAt invalidation check (throttled to once per 5 minutes per token) before returning session.user; a token issued before the latest passwordChangedAt comes back null, forcing re-login on that device.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"data\": {\n          \"user\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"orNull\": \"null when unauthenticated or invalidated by passwordChangedAt\"\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-9\", \"FR-10\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out, clears the session cookie. Invoked by the top-bar user menu's 'Sign out' action, which then redirects to /login.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"redirect\": \"/login\" },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-25\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js CSRF token issuance, consumed by every auth form (sign-in, sign-out, and this PRD's own POST endpoints reuse the same Auth.js session's CSRF protection) per NFR-1.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string\" },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-1\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/invite/accept\",\n      \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit from /invite/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash of the submitted token (must be type INVITE, unused, within 7-day expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, then as one service-layer step: hashes it, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, marks the token used, signs the user in, and audits auth.invite.accepted — kept atomic so a failure partway doesn't leave a used token with no activated account.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/dashboard\" } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-15\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Always responds 200 with the same generic message regardless of whether the account exists (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2's intent). Rate-limited 3/email/hr and 10/IP/hr via component 3's limiter — the limiter key is the submitted email/IP itself, not account existence, so a 429 here doesn't leak whether an account exists. For an existing ACTIVE user only: issues a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, 60-min expiry), revokes that user's older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"email\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" } },\n        \"429\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\", \"message\": \"Too many attempts. Try again later.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-18\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Submit from /reset-password/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash (must be type PASSWORD_RESET, unused, within 60-min expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, sets the new hash and passwordChangedAt, clears failedLoginCount/lockedUntil, marks the token used, and audits auth.password.reset.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/login\" } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This reset link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-19\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/change-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Submit from /account/security, behind requireUser() (FR-23) — the route handler re-checks the session as a backstop even though middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests. Checks the current password against the stored hash (wrong value is a field-level VALIDATION_ERROR, not a generic failure), validates the new password against the shared policy module, bumps passwordChangedAt (invalidating every other session via the jwt callback's check), and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out by their own action.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"currentPassword\": \"string\", \"newPassword\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"Password updated.\" } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n        \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"message\": \"string\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-23\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":46,"newStart":1,"newLines":126,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T15:09:02Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T21:45:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"architect\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\","," ","   \"sharedEnvelope\": {","-    \"description\": \"Every endpoint (present and future) routes through src/server/http.ts. Documented once here so arch-api-contracts doesn't repeat it per-endpoint and so dev-planning knows new endpoints must reuse it, not reinvent it.\",","+    \"description\": \"Two families of endpoint exist in this PRD. (1) Auth.js (NextAuth v5)'s own catch-all route (/api/auth/callback/credentials, /api/auth/session, /api/auth/signout, /api/auth/csrf) — its request/response wire format is owned by the library, not src/server/http.ts, and is documented per-endpoint below only at the level dev-planning needs (inputs, outcomes, which FRs they satisfy). (2) Four new form-submission endpoints (invite/accept, forgot-password, reset-password, change-password) that are genuinely ours and MUST route through the existing src/server/http.ts chokepoint (ok/apiError/withHandler/parseBody) per NFR-7 — no parallel envelope. That chokepoint's ApiErrorCode union currently only has VALIDATION_ERROR/NOT_FOUND/CONFLICT/INTERNAL (see src/server/http.ts); this PRD needs three more values, which dev-planning/dev must EXTEND that union and errorCodeToStatus map with, not fork a second error-mapping file.\",","     \"success\": { \"data\": \"<payload>\" },","-    \"successPaginated\": { \"data\": \"<array>\", \"meta\": { \"page\": \"number\", \"pageSize\": \"number\", \"total\": \"number\" } },","     \"error\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"string\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"object (optional)\" } },","     \"errorCodeToStatus\": {","       \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,","       \"NOT_FOUND\": 404,","       \"CONFLICT\": 409,","-      \"INTERNAL\": 500","+      \"INTERNAL\": 500,","+      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429,","+      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,","+      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410","     },","-    \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-10\", \"FR-11\", \"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-15\"]","+    \"newErrorCodesForThisPrd\": {","+      \"RATE_LIMITED\": \"Sign-in and forgot-password rate limiters (FR-6, FR-17) short-circuit to this before any DB work.\",","+      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": \"Defense-in-depth on change-password's requireUser() guard (FR-20, FR-23) — middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests, this is the handler-level backstop.\",","+      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": \"Invite/reset token is missing, wrong type, expired, or already used (FR-12, FR-18, FR-19) — distinct from NOT_FOUND because the token row may exist but be unusable; mapped to 410 Gone.\"","+    },","+    \"notModeledAsEndpoints\": \"Component 9's service functions (createUser, createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser — FR-22) are an internal module surface called by prisma/seed.ts (FR-28) and by later PRDs' admin UI, not by any form in this PRD. No endpoint is defined for them here; inventing an admin API now would be scope creep past NFR-8. Likewise /invite/[token] and /reset-password/[token]'s GET render (token validity check for FR-12) happens inside the Server Component itself via a direct Prisma lookup, not a client-side API call — no GET endpoint is defined for that for the same reason.\",","+    \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]","   },"," ","   \"endpoints\": [","     {","+      \"method\": \"POST\",","+      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",","+      \"description\": \"Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider callback, invoked internally by signIn('credentials') from the /login page. Runs the authorize() chokepoint: rate-limit check (10/IP/5min) before any DB work, email normalize, status/lockout branch (dummy bcrypt-compare for timing safety on a non-existent user), bcrypt compare (cost 12), failedLoginCount/lockedUntil mutation, audit() writes, and on success stamps id/role/firstName/lastName/email into the JWT. Wire format (form-encoded body, redirect-based response) is owned by Auth.js, not src/server/http.ts.\",","+      \"requestSchema\": {","+        \"email\": \"string\",","+        \"password\": \"string\",","+        \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\",","+        \"callbackUrl\": \"string\"","+      },","+      \"responseSchema\": {","+        \"redirectSuccess\": \"same-origin callbackUrl if relative, else /dashboard (FR-7)\",","+        \"redirectFailure\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — same generic message for unknown-user and wrong-password (FR-4)\",","+        \"redirectLocked\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — locked-account message includes remaining minutes (FR-4)\",","+        \"redirectDisabled\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — distinct disabled-account message (FR-4)\",","+        \"redirectRateLimited\": \"/login?error=RateLimited — 'Too many attempts' message (FR-6)\"","+      },","+      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-8\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\"]","+    },","+    {","       \"method\": \"GET\",","-      \"path\": \"/api/health\",","-      \"description\": \"Liveness/readiness check. Runs SELECT 1 against Prisma with a 2000ms budget; wrapped in withHandler per ADR-4. The only concrete endpoint this PRD requires.\",","+      \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\",","+      \"description\": \"Auth.js session read. The jwt callback applies the passwordChangedAt invalidation check (throttled to once per 5 minutes per token) before returning session.user; a token issued before the latest passwordChangedAt comes back null, forcing re-login on that device.\",","       \"requestSchema\": {},","       \"responseSchema\": {","-        \"200\": {","-          \"data\": {","-            \"status\": \"ok\",","-            \"db\": \"ok\",","-            \"time\": \"string (ISO 8601)\"","-          }","+        \"data\": {","+          \"user\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\" }","         },","-        \"503\": {","-          \"data\": {","-            \"status\": \"error\",","-            \"db\": \"error\",","-            \"time\": \"string (ISO 8601)\"","-          }","-        }","+        \"orNull\": \"null when unauthenticated or invalidated by passwordChangedAt\"","       },","-      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-16\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-12\", \"FR-13\"]","+      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-9\", \"FR-10\"]","+    },","+    {","+      \"method\": \"POST\",","+      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",","+      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out, clears the session cookie. Invoked by the top-bar user menu's 'Sign out' action, which then redirects to /login.\",","+      \"requestSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\" },","+      \"responseSchema\": { \"redirect\": \"/login\" },","+      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-25\"]","+    },","+    {","+      \"method\": \"GET\",","+      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",","+      \"description\": \"Auth.js CSRF token issuance, consumed by every auth form (sign-in, sign-out, and this PRD's own POST endpoints reuse the same Auth.js session's CSRF protection) per NFR-1.\",","+      \"requestSchema\": {},","+      \"responseSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string\" },","+      \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-1\"]","+    },","+    {","+      \"method\": \"POST\",","+      \"path\": \"/api/auth/invite/accept\",","+      \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit from /invite/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash of the submitted token (must be type INVITE, unused, within 7-day expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, then as one service-layer step: hashes it, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, marks the token used, signs the user in, and audits auth.invite.accepted — kept atomic so a failure partway doesn't leave a used token with no activated account.\",","+      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },","+      \"responseSchema\": {","+        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/dashboard\" } },","+        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },","+        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\" } }","+      },","+      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-15\"]","+    },","+    {","+      \"method\": \"POST\",","+      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",","+      \"description\": \"Always responds 200 with the same generic message regardless of whether the account exists (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2's intent). Rate-limited 3/email/hr and 10/IP/hr via component 3's limiter — the limiter key is the submitted email/IP itself, not account existence, so a 429 here doesn't leak whether an account exists. For an existing ACTIVE user only: issues a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, 60-min expiry), revokes that user's older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\",","+      \"requestSchema\": { \"email\": \"string\" },","+      \"responseSchema\": {","+        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" } },","+        \"429\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\", \"message\": \"Too many attempts. Try again later.\" } }","+      },","+      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-18\"]","+    },","+    {","+      \"method\": \"POST\",","+      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",","+      \"description\": \"Submit from /reset-password/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash (must be type PASSWORD_RESET, unused, within 60-min expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, sets the new hash and passwordChangedAt, clears failedLoginCount/lockedUntil, marks the token used, and audits auth.password.reset.\",","+      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },","+      \"responseSchema\": {","+        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/login\" } },","+        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },","+        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This reset link is invalid or has expired.\" } }","+      },","+      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-19\"]","+    },","+    {","+      \"method\": \"POST\",","+      \"path\": \"/api/auth/change-password\",","+      \"description\": \"Submit from /account/security, behind requireUser() (FR-23) — the route handler re-checks the session as a backstop even though middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests. Checks the current password against the stored hash (wrong value is a field-level VALIDATION_ERROR, not a generic failure), validates the new password against the shared policy module, bumps passwordChangedAt (invalidating every other session via the jwt callback's check), and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out by their own action.\",","+      \"requestSchema\": { \"currentPassword\": \"string\", \"newPassword\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },","+      \"responseSchema\": {","+        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"Password updated.\" } },","+        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },","+        \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"message\": \"string\" } }","+      },","+      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-23\"]","     }","   ],","   \"status\": \"complete\""]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T15:09:02Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"sharedEnvelope\": {\n    \"description\": \"Every endpoint (present and future) routes through src/server/http.ts. Documented once here so arch-api-contracts doesn't repeat it per-endpoint and so dev-planning knows new endpoints must reuse it, not reinvent it.\",\n    \"success\": { \"data\": \"<payload>\" },\n    \"successPaginated\": { \"data\": \"<array>\", \"meta\": { \"page\": \"number\", \"pageSize\": \"number\", \"total\": \"number\" } },\n    \"error\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"string\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"object (optional)\" } },\n    \"errorCodeToStatus\": {\n      \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,\n      \"NOT_FOUND\": 404,\n      \"CONFLICT\": 409,\n      \"INTERNAL\": 500\n    },\n    \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-10\", \"FR-11\", \"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-15\"]\n  },\n\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/health\",\n      \"description\": \"Liveness/readiness check. Runs SELECT 1 against Prisma with a 2000ms budget; wrapped in withHandler per ADR-4. The only concrete endpoint this PRD requires.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": {\n          \"data\": {\n            \"status\": \"ok\",\n            \"db\": \"ok\",\n            \"time\": \"string (ISO 8601)\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"503\": {\n          \"data\": {\n            \"status\": \"error\",\n            \"db\": \"error\",\n            \"time\": \"string (ISO 8601)\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-16\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-12\", \"FR-13\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false}}
