{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QN8taJKAbMkCWmY52TJFDN","type":"tool_result","content":"---\n# Tech Stack Decisions — Ticket abcd-5\n\nADR-style decisions evaluating intake's detected stack (`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`) against the FR/NFR list. This is a frontend-only, single-page React app with no backend — every decision below stays inside that boundary.\n\n## ADR-1: Keep React 19 + Vite, no framework change\n\n**Context:** Intake detected React ^19.2.8 + Vite ^8.2.0, already scaffolded, PRD explicitly pins this stack and states \"no backend.\"\n\n**Decision:** Accept the detected stack as-is. All ten FRs (FR-1..FR-10) are UI/state features layered onto the existing `HomePage`/`Card`/`Grid`/`EmptyState`/`SearchInput`/`ProfileModal` components — nothing requires SSR, routing, or a different framework.\n\n**Consequences:** No migration cost. Design phase works entirely within `src/components`, `src/pages`, `src/lib`, `src/data`.\n\n## ADR-2: No new npm dependencies — extend existing modules only\n\n**Context:** NFR-3 explicitly forbids new dependencies and requires extending `Grid`, `Card`, `EmptyState`, `SearchInput`, `filterItems` rather than duplicating them.\n\n**Decision:** All new capability (department filter, sort, view toggle, favorites, pagination, stats bar) is built with plain React state/props and edits to the existing components/`filterItems.js`. No state-management library, no UI kit, no date/format library.\n\n**Consequences:** Slightly more manual wiring (e.g. sort comparator, favorites reducer) than a library would give, but zero dependency risk and matches the PRD constraint directly.\n\n## ADR-3: Local component state (useState/useReducer) — no global state library\n\n**Context:** NFR-1 requires synchronous client-side filtering/sorting/pagination over \"at most a few hundred items\" with no debouncing/memoization required. NFR-3 bars new dependencies (rules out Redux/Zustand/etc.), and intake's stack notes confirm \"no router/global state lib.\"\n\n**Decision:** Hold search text, department filter, sort mode, view mode, favorites set, favorites-only toggle, and visible-count (pagination) as React state colocated in `HomePage` (or a single custom hook it owns), derived filtering/sorting done with plain array methods on each render — no memoization layer required at this data scale.\n\n**Consequences:** Re-render cost stays trivial at \"a few hundred items\"; if the dataset ever grows an order of magnitude, revisit with `useMemo`. Must still avoid accidental O(n²) patterns (e.g. re-filtering inside a loop) per NFR-1.\n\n## ADR-4: localStorage for favorites persistence, with in-memory fallback\n\n=== check for CLAUDE.md near /Users/ikramaansari/artifacts (project root) ===\n=== list home dir top level relevant ===\ntotal 432\ndrwxr-xr-x+  78 ikramaansari  staff   2496 Oct 19 13:16 .\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 root          admin    160 Aug 29  2025 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 ikramaansari  staff     96 Jan  8  2026 .anaconda\ndrwxr-xr-x   12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Dec 24  2025 .android\ndrwx------    3 ikramaansari  staff     96 Jul  4  2022 .aws\n-rw-r--r--    1 ikramaansari  staff    447 Jan  8  2026 .bash_profile\ndrwxr-xr-x@   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Aug  4 16:09 .cache\n-r--------    1 ikramaansari  staff      7 Sep 16  2021 .CFUserTextEncoding\ndrwxr-xr-x    2 ikramaansari  staff     64 Mar  9  2024 .cgminer\ndrwx------   21 ikramaansari  staff    672 Oct 19 05:09 .claude\n-rw-------    1 ikramaansari  staff  62007 Oct 19 13:16 .claude.json\n-rw-------@   1 ikramaansari  staff  35082 Aug  3 13:56 .claude.json.backup\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 ikramaansari  staff     96 Dec 23  2025 .cocoapods\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 ikramaansari  staff    160 Jan  8  2026 .conda\ndrwx------    6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Aug  3 15:38 .config\ndrwx------    3 ikramaansari  staff     96 Oct 27  2021 .cups\ndrwxr-xr-x@  16 ikramaansari  staff    512 Sep  7 12:49 .cursor\ndrwx------    2 ikramaansar