{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CgrjohQBuGkZoioT1UU4Bd","type":"tool_result","content":"93\t## Functional Requirements\n94\t\n95\t### FR-1 Data model\n96\t\n97\t```prisma\n98\tenum Gender { FEMALE MALE OTHER UNDISCLOSED }\n99\tenum GuardianRelationship { MOTHER FATHER GUARDIAN GRANDPARENT OTHER }\n100\t\n101\tmodel StudentProfile {\n102\t  userId            String     @id\n103\t  user              User       @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n104\t  admissionNumber   String     @unique        // \"S2026-0001\"\n105\t  dateOfBirth       DateTime   @db.Date\n106\t  gender            Gender     @default(UNDISCLOSED)\n107\t  gradeLevelId      String\n108\t  gradeLevel        GradeLevel @relation(fields: [gradeLevelId], references: [id])\n109\t  enrollmentDate    DateTime   @db.Date\n110\t  addressLine1      String?\n111\t  city              String?\n112\t  medicalNotes      String?                   // visible to ADMIN and the student's teachers only\n113\t  emergencyContact  String?\n114\t  emergencyPhone    String?\n115\t}\n116\t\n117\tmodel TeacherProfile {\n118\t  userId          String    @id\n119\t  user            User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n120\t  employeeNumber  String    @unique           // \"T-0001\"\n121\t  title           String?                     // \"Ms.\", \"Mr.\", \"Dr.\"\n122\t  qualifications  String?\n123\t  hireDate        DateTime? @db.Date\n124\t}\n125\t\n126\tmodel ParentProfile {\n127\t  userId      String  @id\n128\t  user        User    @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n129\t  occupation  String?\n130\t  address     String?\n131\t}\n132\t\n133\tmodel ParentStudentLink {\n134\t  id            String               @id @default(cuid())\n135\t  parentId      String\n136\t  studentId     String\n137\t  relationship  GuardianRelationship\n138\t  isPrimary     Boolean              @default(false)   // primary contact for emails\n139\t  createdAt     DateTime             @default(now())\n140\t  @@unique([parentId, studentId])\n141\t  @@index([studentId])\n142\t}\n143\t```\n144\t\n145\tRelations from `User` to each profile and to `ParentStudentLink` (as parent and as student) must be added.\n146\t\n147\t### FR-2 User list (`/admin/users`)\n148\t1. `DataTable` columns: avatar + full name, email, role `Chip`, status `Chip` (Invited = warning, Active = success, Disabled = default, Archived = outlined), grade level (students), last sign-in, actions menu.\n149\t2. Filters: role (multi-select), status, grade level (shown when role filter includes Student), search by name, email, admission number or employee number. Archived users are hidden unless \"Show archived\" is checked.\n150\t3. Row actions: View, Edit, Resend invitation (status Invited), Unlock (when `lockedUntil > now`), Disable / Enable, Archive / Restore.\n151\t4. Bulk actions on selected rows: Resend invitations, Disable, Export CSV.\n152\t\n153\t### FR-3 Create / edit user (`/admin/users/new`, `/admin/users/[id]/edit`)\n154\t1. The form is an MUI `Stepper`. Step 1 selects role. Step 2 shows common fields (first name, last name, email, phone) plus role-specific fields:\n155\t   - Student: admission number (auto-suggested as `S<year>-<4-digit sequence>`), date of birth, gender, grade level, enrollment date (defaults to today), address, emergency contact and phone, medical notes, and a \"Parents/guardians\" section to link existing parents or create new parent users inline.\n156\t   - Teacher: employee number (auto-suggested `T-<4-digit sequence>`), title, qualifications, hire date.\n157\t   - Parent: occupation, address, and a \"Children\" section to link existing students.\n158\t2. Checkbox \"Send invitation email now\" (default checked) calls `sendInvite`.\n159\t3. Email changes on an existing user require a confirmation dialog and invalidate pending invite tokens.\n160\t4. Role cannot be changed after creation (show read-only).\n161\t5. Validation: date of birth must make the student between 3 and 21 years old; phone must match E.164-ish pattern `^\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$`.\n162\t\n163\t### FR-4 User detail (`/admin/users/[id]`)\n164\t1. Shows profile data, status, last sign-in, linked family members (with links), and the 20 most recent audit entries where the user is actor or entity.\n165\t\n166\t### FR-5 Status changes\n167\t1. Disable sets `status = DISABLED`; the user's sessions stop working within 5 minutes (extend the PRD-01 session check to also reject disabled/archived users).\n168\t2. Archive sets `archivedAt = now` and `status = DISABLED`; archived users are excluded from all pickers app-wide but their historical records remain visible.\n169\t3. An admin cannot disable or archive their own account, and the last active admin cannot be disabled (error \"At least one active admin is required.\").\n170\t\n171\t### FR-6 Parent–student links\n172\t1. Managed from either the student or the parent form, and from a \"Family\" card on the student detail page.\n173\t2. A student can have at most 4 linked parents; exactly one link per student may be `isPrimary` (setting one clears the others).\n174\t3. `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` exports:\n175\t   - `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` → ADMIN: `\"ALL\"`; STUDENT: `[user.id]`; PARENT: linked student ids; TEACHER: student ids in sections they homeroom or courses they teach (returns `[]` until PRD-05 adds those relations; PRD-05 must extend this function).\n176\t   - `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` → throws `FORBIDDEN` (or `NOT_FOUND` for parents/students, to avoid revealing existence).\n177\t\n178\t### FR-7 CSV import (`/admin/users/import`)\n179\t1. Download template button provides `students-template.csv` with columns: `first_name,last_name,email,admission_number,date_of_birth,gender,grade_level,enrollment_date,parent1_first_name,parent1_last_name,parent1_email,parent1_phone,parent1_relationship,parent2_first_name,parent2_last_name,parent2_email,parent2_phone,parent2_relationship`. A second template `teachers-template.csv` has `first_name,last_name,email,employee_number,title,phone`.\n180\t2. Upload (maximum 2 MB, maximum 2,000 rows) → parsed in the browser with `papaparse` → preview `DataGrid` showing each row as Valid, Warning (for example parent email already exists — will link to the existing parent) or Error (with reason per cell).\n181\t3. \"Import N valid rows\" sends the rows to `POST /api/users/import` in batches of 200. The server re-validates every row (never trusts the client), creates users and links in one transaction per batch, and returns per-row results.\n182\t4. Option \"Send invitations after import\" (default off). Grade levels are matched by `name` or `shortName`, case-insensitive. Dates accept `YYYY-MM-DD` only.\n183\t5. After import, show a summary (created students, created parents, linked existing parents, failed rows) and a \"Download error report\" CSV listing failed rows with reasons.\n184\t6. Re-importing the same file creates no duplicates: rows whose email already exists are reported as \"Skipped — already exists\".\n185\t\n186\t### FR-8 Student detail page (`/students/[studentId]`)\n187\t1. Header: avatar, name, admission number, grade level, status. Tabs from `src/config/student-tabs.ts` filtered by role; this PRD registers the \"Overview\" tab (profile, family, emergency contact; medical notes only for ADMIN and TEACHER).\n188\t2. Access via `assertCanViewStudent`.\n189\t\n190\t### FR-9 Parent \"My children\" (`/my-children`)\n191\t1. Visible to PARENT only. Lists linked children as cards (name, grade level, admission number) linking to `/students/[id]`. If none are linked: empty state \"No children are linked to your account yet. Contact the school office.\"\n192\t\n193\t### FR-10 Profile (`/account/profile`)\n194\t1. Any user sees their own profile (read-only name, email, role) and can edit phone and, for parents, occupation and address. Add \"Profile\" to the user menu.\n195\t\n196\t### FR-11 Directory pickers\n197\t1. `GET /api/users/search?role=TEACHER&q=to` returns at most 20 `{ id, name, email, role }` matches for combobox pickers (ADMIN and TEACHER only), excluding archived users. Build a reusable `UserPicker` component on MUI `Autocomplete` (async options, `multiple` support, avatar + name + role in `renderOption`).\n198\t\n199\t### FR-12 Audit log viewer (`/admin/audit-log`)\n200\t1. Table: time, actor (name), action, entity type, entity id (linked when it is a user), IP. Filters: actor, action prefix (for example `auth.`), date range. Clicking a row opens a right-anchored MUI `Drawer` with pretty-printed metadata JSON. Read-only; no edits or deletes.\n201\t\n202\t### FR-13 Navigation\n203\t1. Administration group gains: Users, Import users, Audit log. Parents get \"My children\". All users get \"Profile\" in the user menu.\n204\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"744674dc-d209-4d85-a196-0650535a8eff","uuid":"f732650e-d9df-43ec-a8ca-030497c61f52","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:15:04.465Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/03-user-management.md","content":"## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1 Data model\n\n```prisma\nenum Gender { FEMALE MALE OTHER UNDISCLOSED }\nenum GuardianRelationship { MOTHER FATHER GUARDIAN GRANDPARENT OTHER }\n\nmodel StudentProfile {\n  userId            String     @id\n  user              User       @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  admissionNumber   String     @unique        // \"S2026-0001\"\n  dateOfBirth       DateTime   @db.Date\n  gender            Gender     @default(UNDISCLOSED)\n  gradeLevelId      String\n  gradeLevel        GradeLevel @relation(fields: [gradeLevelId], references: [id])\n  enrollmentDate    DateTime   @db.Date\n  addressLine1      String?\n  city              String?\n  medicalNotes      String?                   // visible to ADMIN and the student's teachers only\n  emergencyContact  String?\n  emergencyPhone    String?\n}\n\nmodel TeacherProfile {\n  userId          String    @id\n  user            User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  employeeNumber  String    @unique           // \"T-0001\"\n  title           String?                     // \"Ms.\", \"Mr.\", \"Dr.\"\n  qualifications  String?\n  hireDate        DateTime? @db.Date\n}\n\nmodel ParentProfile {\n  userId      String  @id\n  user        User    @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  occupation  String?\n  address     String?\n}\n\nmodel ParentStudentLink {\n  id            String               @id @default(cuid())\n  parentId      String\n  studentId     String\n  relationship  GuardianRelationship\n  isPrimary     Boolean              @default(false)   // primary contact for emails\n  createdAt     DateTime             @default(now())\n  @@unique([parentId, studentId])\n  @@index([studentId])\n}\n```\n\nRelations from `User` to each profile and to `ParentStudentLink` (as parent and as student) must be added.\n\n### FR-2 User list (`/admin/users`)\n1. `DataTable` columns: avatar + full name, email, role `Chip`, status `Chip` (Invited = warning, Active = success, Disabled = default, Archived = outlined), grade level (students), last sign-in, actions menu.\n2. Filters: role (multi-select), status, grade level (shown when role filter includes Student), search by name, email, admission number or employee number. Archived users are hidden unless \"Show archived\" is checked.\n3. Row actions: View, Edit, Resend invitation (status Invited), Unlock (when `lockedUntil > now`), Disable / Enable, Archive / Restore.\n4. Bulk actions on selected rows: Resend invitations, Disable, Export CSV.\n\n### FR-3 Create / edit user (`/admin/users/new`, `/admin/users/[id]/edit`)\n1. The form is an MUI `Stepper`. Step 1 selects role. Step 2 shows common fields (first name, last name, email, phone) plus role-specific fields:\n   - Student: admission number (auto-suggested as `S<year>-<4-digit sequence>`), date of birth, gender, grade level, enrollment date (defaults to today), address, emergency contact and phone, medical notes, and a \"Parents/guardians\" section to link existing parents or create new parent users inline.\n   - Teacher: employee number (auto-suggested `T-<4-digit sequence>`), title, qualifications, hire date.\n   - Parent: occupation, address, and a \"Children\" section to link existing students.\n2. Checkbox \"Send invitation email now\" (default checked) calls `sendInvite`.\n3. Email changes on an existing user require a confirmation dialog and invalidate pending invite tokens.\n4. Role cannot be changed after creation (show read-only).\n5. Validation: date of birth must make the student between 3 and 21 years old; phone must match E.164-ish pattern `^\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$`.\n\n### FR-4 User detail (`/admin/users/[id]`)\n1. Shows profile data, status, last sign-in, linked family members (with links), and the 20 most recent audit entries where the user is actor or entity.\n\n### FR-5 Status changes\n1. Disable sets `status = DISABLED`; the user's sessions stop working within 5 minutes (extend the PRD-01 session check to also reject disabled/archived users).\n2. Archive sets `archivedAt = now` and `status = DISABLED`; archived users are excluded from all pickers app-wide but their historical records remain visible.\n3. An admin cannot disable or archive their own account, and the last active admin cannot be disabled (error \"At least one active admin is required.\").\n\n### FR-6 Parent–student links\n1. Managed from either the student or the parent form, and from a \"Family\" card on the student detail page.\n2. A student can have at most 4 linked parents; exactly one link per student may be `isPrimary` (setting one clears the others).\n3. `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` exports:\n   - `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` → ADMIN: `\"ALL\"`; STUDENT: `[user.id]`; PARENT: linked student ids; TEACHER: student ids in sections they homeroom or courses they teach (returns `[]` until PRD-05 adds those relations; PRD-05 must extend this function).\n   - `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` → throws `FORBIDDEN` (or `NOT_FOUND` for parents/students, to avoid revealing existence).\n\n### FR-7 CSV import (`/admin/users/import`)\n1. Download template button provides `students-template.csv` with columns: `first_name,last_name,email,admission_number,date_of_birth,gender,grade_level,enrollment_date,parent1_first_name,parent1_last_name,parent1_email,parent1_phone,parent1_relationship,parent2_first_name,parent2_last_name,parent2_email,parent2_phone,parent2_relationship`. A second template `teachers-template.csv` has `first_name,last_name,email,employee_number,title,phone`.\n2. Upload (maximum 2 MB, maximum 2,000 rows) → parsed in the browser with `papaparse` → preview `DataGrid` showing each row as Valid, Warning (for example parent email already exists — will link to the existing parent) or Error (with reason per cell).\n3. \"Import N valid rows\" sends the rows to `POST /api/users/import` in batches of 200. The server re-validates every row (never trusts the client), creates users and links in one transaction per batch, and returns per-row results.\n4. Option \"Send invitations after import\" (default off). Grade levels are matched by `name` or `shortName`, case-insensitive. Dates accept `YYYY-MM-DD` only.\n5. After import, show a summary (created students, created parents, linked existing parents, failed rows) and a \"Download error report\" CSV listing failed rows with reasons.\n6. Re-importing the same file creates no duplicates: rows whose email already exists are reported as \"Skipped — already exists\".\n\n### FR-8 Student detail page (`/students/[studentId]`)\n1. Header: avatar, name, admission number, grade level, status. Tabs from `src/config/student-tabs.ts` filtered by role; this PRD registers the \"Overview\" tab (profile, family, emergency contact; medical notes only for ADMIN and TEACHER).\n2. Access via `assertCanViewStudent`.\n\n### FR-9 Parent \"My children\" (`/my-children`)\n1. Visible to PARENT only. Lists linked children as cards (name, grade level, admission number) linking to `/students/[id]`. If none are linked: empty state \"No children are linked to your account yet. Contact the school office.\"\n\n### FR-10 Profile (`/account/profile`)\n1. Any user sees their own profile (read-only name, email, role) and can edit phone and, for parents, occupation and address. Add \"Profile\" to the user menu.\n\n### FR-11 Directory pickers\n1. `GET /api/users/search?role=TEACHER&q=to` returns at most 20 `{ id, name, email, role }` matches for combobox pickers (ADMIN and TEACHER only), excluding archived users. Build a reusable `UserPicker` component on MUI `Autocomplete` (async options, `multiple` support, avatar + name + role in `renderOption`).\n\n### FR-12 Audit log viewer (`/admin/audit-log`)\n1. Table: time, actor (name), action, entity type, entity id (linked when it is a user), IP. Filters: actor, action prefix (for example `auth.`), date range. Clicking a row opens a right-anchored MUI `Drawer` with pretty-printed metadata JSON. Read-only; no edits or deletes.\n\n### FR-13 Navigation\n1. Administration group gains: Users, Import users, Audit log. Parents get \"My children\". All users get \"Profile\" in the user menu.\n","numLines":112,"startLine":93,"totalLines":256}}}
