{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q51aSGYP1Wq1x9SEoaxetU","type":"tool_result","content":"90\t## Functional Requirements\n91\t\n92\t### FR-1 Data model\n93\t\n94\t```prisma\n95\tenum EmailStatus { PENDING SENDING SENT FAILED }\n96\t\n97\tmodel Notification {\n98\t  id         String    @id @default(cuid())\n99\t  userId     String\n100\t  user       User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n101\t  type       String                       // key from notification type registry\n102\t  title      String                       // max 140 chars\n103\t  body       String?                      // max 500 chars, plain text\n104\t  link       String?                      // relative app path, e.g. \"/courses/abc/assignments/xyz\"\n105\t  readAt     DateTime?\n106\t  createdAt  DateTime  @default(now())\n107\t  @@index([userId, readAt, createdAt])\n108\t}\n109\t\n110\tmodel NotificationPreference {\n111\t  userId     String\n112\t  type       String\n113\t  inApp      Boolean  @default(true)\n114\t  email      Boolean  @default(true)\n115\t  updatedAt  DateTime @updatedAt\n116\t  @@id([userId, type])\n117\t}\n118\t\n119\tmodel EmailOutbox {\n120\t  id            String      @id @default(cuid())\n121\t  toEmail       String\n122\t  toName        String?\n123\t  subject       String\n124\t  html          String\n125\t  text          String\n126\t  status        EmailStatus @default(PENDING)\n127\t  attempts      Int         @default(0)\n128\t  lastError     String?\n129\t  nextAttemptAt DateTime    @default(now())\n130\t  sentAt        DateTime?\n131\t  createdAt     DateTime    @default(now())\n132\t  @@index([status, nextAttemptAt])\n133\t}\n134\t```\n135\t\n136\t### FR-2 Notification type registry (`src/server/notifications/types.ts`)\n137\t1. Export `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` as a typed record: key → `{ label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }`. Categories: `ACCOUNT`, `ACADEMIC`, `ATTENDANCE`, `COMMUNICATION`, `FINANCE`, `SYSTEM`.\n138\t2. Register in this PRD: `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` (email only, not shown in preferences), `system.test` (admin test message).\n139\t3. Later PRDs add their own keys (for example `assignment.published`, `attendance.absent`). TypeScript must reject unknown keys in `notify()`.\n140\t\n141\t### FR-3 `notify()` service (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`)\n142\t1. Signature: `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })`.\n143\t2. For each recipient: skip archived or disabled users; read preference rows (falling back to registry defaults); create a `Notification` row when in-app is enabled or `mandatoryInApp` is true; enqueue an `EmailOutbox` row when email is enabled and the user has an email.\n144\t3. Uses `createMany` so notifying 1,000 users performs at most 3 database round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\n145\t4. Must never throw to the caller: failures are logged and the calling feature's transaction is unaffected. Callers invoke `notify()` after their own transaction commits.\n146\t5. Helper `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (deduplicated) — used by attendance, grades and assignments later.\n147\t\n148\t### FR-4 Email templates (`src/server/email/templates/`)\n149\t1. Built with `@react-email/components`, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\n150\t2. A base layout: school logo and name header, content area, footer with school address, \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` and the sentence \"You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.\"\n151\t3. Templates in this PRD: `invite` (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), `password-reset` (link, 60-minute expiry notice), `generic-notification` (title, body, call-to-action button to `APP_URL + link`).\n152\t4. `sendAuthEmail()` from PRD-01 now enqueues `invite` / `password-reset` templates via the outbox.\n153\t\n154\t### FR-5 Dispatcher\n155\t1. `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` selects `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now` using `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, marks them `SENDING`, sends via Nodemailer, and marks `SENT` or schedules a retry.\n156\t2. Retry schedule: attempts 1–5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; after the 5th failure set `FAILED`.\n157\t3. Trigger options: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` protected by header `Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}` (for an external scheduler, every minute), and `npm run worker:email` — a Node script that loops `dispatchEmails` every 15 seconds for local development and simple deployments.\n158\t4. New env vars: `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS`, `SMTP_SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM` (for example `\"SchoolHub <no-reply@schoolhub.test>\"`), `CRON_SECRET`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (`smtp` | `console`, default `console` in development). The console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\n159\t\n160\t### FR-6 Notification bell (top bar)\n161\t1. Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell. Shows unread count badge (displays \"9+\" above 9). Polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 seconds while the tab is visible (pause on `visibilitychange` hidden).\n162\t2. The bell is an MUI `IconButton` + `Badge`. Clicking opens an MUI `Popover` containing a `List` with the 10 most recent notifications (unread ones bold with a dot), each showing title, body (2-line clamp) and relative time (\"5 min ago\"). Clicking an item marks it read and navigates to `link`. Footer: \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\".\n163\t\n164\t### FR-7 Notifications page (`/notifications`)\n165\t1. Paginated list (20 per page), filter tabs All / Unread, category filter. Bulk \"Mark all as read\". Each row has a mark read / unread toggle.\n166\t2. Notifications older than 180 days are deleted by `purgeOldNotifications()`, called by the dispatcher endpoint once per day (track last run in memory; acceptable to run more than once per day after restarts).\n167\t\n168\t### FR-8 Preferences (`/account/notifications`)\n169\t1. MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader`-style group rows): each type visible to the user's role shows label, description, an \"In app\" switch and an \"Email\" switch. Mandatory in-app types show a disabled MUI `Switch` with tooltip \"Required by the school\".\n170\t2. Changes save immediately (optimistic UI with rollback on error) via `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`.\n171\t\n172\t### FR-9 Admin email log (`/admin/email-log`)\n173\t1. Table: created, recipient, subject, status, attempts, last error. Filter by status. Row action \"Retry now\" for `FAILED` rows resets `attempts = 0`, `status = PENDING`, `nextAttemptAt = now`.\n174\t2. Button \"Send test notification to me\" calls `notify({ type: 'system.test', … })` for the current admin.\n175\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54b3bb1c-c2bb-4763-9a84-dd2308368397","uuid":"e3a34ef4-781a-4fb8-90f9-dd7012990665","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:11:34.692Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/04-notifications.md","content":"## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1 Data model\n\n```prisma\nenum EmailStatus { PENDING SENDING SENT FAILED }\n\nmodel Notification {\n  id         String    @id @default(cuid())\n  userId     String\n  user       User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  type       String                       // key from notification type registry\n  title      String                       // max 140 chars\n  body       String?                      // max 500 chars, plain text\n  link       String?                      // relative app path, e.g. \"/courses/abc/assignments/xyz\"\n  readAt     DateTime?\n  createdAt  DateTime  @default(now())\n  @@index([userId, readAt, createdAt])\n}\n\nmodel NotificationPreference {\n  userId     String\n  type       String\n  inApp      Boolean  @default(true)\n  email      Boolean  @default(true)\n  updatedAt  DateTime @updatedAt\n  @@id([userId, type])\n}\n\nmodel EmailOutbox {\n  id            String      @id @default(cuid())\n  toEmail       String\n  toName        String?\n  subject       String\n  html          String\n  text          String\n  status        EmailStatus @default(PENDING)\n  attempts      Int         @default(0)\n  lastError     String?\n  nextAttemptAt DateTime    @default(now())\n  sentAt        DateTime?\n  createdAt     DateTime    @default(now())\n  @@index([status, nextAttemptAt])\n}\n```\n\n### FR-2 Notification type registry (`src/server/notifications/types.ts`)\n1. Export `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` as a typed record: key → `{ label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }`. Categories: `ACCOUNT`, `ACADEMIC`, `ATTENDANCE`, `COMMUNICATION`, `FINANCE`, `SYSTEM`.\n2. Register in this PRD: `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` (email only, not shown in preferences), `system.test` (admin test message).\n3. Later PRDs add their own keys (for example `assignment.published`, `attendance.absent`). TypeScript must reject unknown keys in `notify()`.\n\n### FR-3 `notify()` service (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`)\n1. Signature: `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })`.\n2. For each recipient: skip archived or disabled users; read preference rows (falling back to registry defaults); create a `Notification` row when in-app is enabled or `mandatoryInApp` is true; enqueue an `EmailOutbox` row when email is enabled and the user has an email.\n3. Uses `createMany` so notifying 1,000 users performs at most 3 database round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\n4. Must never throw to the caller: failures are logged and the calling feature's transaction is unaffected. Callers invoke `notify()` after their own transaction commits.\n5. Helper `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (deduplicated) — used by attendance, grades and assignments later.\n\n### FR-4 Email templates (`src/server/email/templates/`)\n1. Built with `@react-email/components`, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\n2. A base layout: school logo and name header, content area, footer with school address, \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` and the sentence \"You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.\"\n3. Templates in this PRD: `invite` (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), `password-reset` (link, 60-minute expiry notice), `generic-notification` (title, body, call-to-action button to `APP_URL + link`).\n4. `sendAuthEmail()` from PRD-01 now enqueues `invite` / `password-reset` templates via the outbox.\n\n### FR-5 Dispatcher\n1. `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` selects `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now` using `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, marks them `SENDING`, sends via Nodemailer, and marks `SENT` or schedules a retry.\n2. Retry schedule: attempts 1–5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; after the 5th failure set `FAILED`.\n3. Trigger options: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` protected by header `Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}` (for an external scheduler, every minute), and `npm run worker:email` — a Node script that loops `dispatchEmails` every 15 seconds for local development and simple deployments.\n4. New env vars: `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS`, `SMTP_SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM` (for example `\"SchoolHub <no-reply@schoolhub.test>\"`), `CRON_SECRET`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (`smtp` | `console`, default `console` in development). The console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\n\n### FR-6 Notification bell (top bar)\n1. Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell. Shows unread count badge (displays \"9+\" above 9). Polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 seconds while the tab is visible (pause on `visibilitychange` hidden).\n2. The bell is an MUI `IconButton` + `Badge`. Clicking opens an MUI `Popover` containing a `List` with the 10 most recent notifications (unread ones bold with a dot), each showing title, body (2-line clamp) and relative time (\"5 min ago\"). Clicking an item marks it read and navigates to `link`. Footer: \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\".\n\n### FR-7 Notifications page (`/notifications`)\n1. Paginated list (20 per page), filter tabs All / Unread, category filter. Bulk \"Mark all as read\". Each row has a mark read / unread toggle.\n2. Notifications older than 180 days are deleted by `purgeOldNotifications()`, called by the dispatcher endpoint once per day (track last run in memory; acceptable to run more than once per day after restarts).\n\n### FR-8 Preferences (`/account/notifications`)\n1. MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader`-style group rows): each type visible to the user's role shows label, description, an \"In app\" switch and an \"Email\" switch. Mandatory in-app types show a disabled MUI `Switch` with tooltip \"Required by the school\".\n2. Changes save immediately (optimistic UI with rollback on error) via `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`.\n\n### FR-9 Admin email log (`/admin/email-log`)\n1. Table: created, recipient, subject, status, attempts, last error. Filter by status. Row action \"Retry now\" for `FAILED` rows resets `attempts = 0`, `status = PENDING`, `nextAttemptAt = now`.\n2. Button \"Send test notification to me\" calls `notify({ type: 'system.test', … })` for the current admin.\n","numLines":86,"startLine":90,"totalLines":217}}}
