oles/auth and response-envelope conventions from PRD-00 (success/list/error shapes, pagination, error codes).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/me/notification-preferences must refuse inApp=false for mandatory (mandatoryInApp) types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table row for PUT /api/me/notification-preferences\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar navigation entry for the notifications page (and any admin email-log entry) in src/config/navigation.ts, following the existing NavItem convention (currently only a Dashboard entry exists).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions, cross-referenced with current src/config/navigation.ts (only Dashboard registered); PRD does not explicitly list the nav entries to add\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 sample Notification rows (one read, two unread) of type system.test linking to /dashboard, for student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element built from @mui/material / @mui/icons-material / MUI X packages; no hand-styled raw HTML where an MUI component exists; every MUI component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, notistack, etc.) must not appear in notification/email UI code; email templates are exempt and use @react-email/components instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"notify() for 1,000 recipients must complete in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"GET /api/notifications/unread-count must respond in under 50ms, backed by the (userId, readAt, createdAt) index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"An email must never be sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row-level locking via FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED); rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes must be recovered back to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Notification link values must be relative paths starting with \\\"/\\\" (validated) to prevent open redirects; email HTML must escape all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Every outbound email must include both HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at the preferences page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization: every notification/email-log route enforces access via requireUser()/requireRole() from src/server/auth (own-notifications-only for user-facing routes, ADMIN-only for /api/admin/email-log and related actions, CRON_SECRET bearer check for the internal dispatch route) — hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement rule), applied to this PRD's API surface\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Dispatching without the correct CRON_SECRET bearer token returns 401 using the standard error envelope.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Acceptance Criteria #6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Scope must not expand beyond this PRD's sections: no SMS/push, no real-time websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
