{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TefxYjpBtt92wo1fHDAuRM","type":"tool_result","content":"176:## API\n177-\n178-| Method & path | Role | Notes |\n179-|---|---|---|\n180-| `GET /api/notifications` | any | `?unread=true&category=&page=` — own notifications only |\n181-| `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` | any | `{ data: { count } }` |\n182-| `POST /api/notifications/:id/read` · `/unread` | owner | |\n183-| `POST /api/notifications/read-all` | any | |\n184-| `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` | any | Merged with registry defaults |\n185-| `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` | any | `{ type, inApp, email }`; `inApp=false` refused for mandatory types |\n186-| `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` | `CRON_SECRET` | Returns `{ sent, failed, retried }` |\n187-| `GET /api/admin/email-log` | ADMIN | |\n188-| `POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry` | ADMIN | |\n189-| `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` | ADMIN | |\n190-\n191-## Non-Functional Requirements\n192-\n193-1. **Performance:** `notify()` for 1,000 recipients must finish in under 2 seconds. Unread-count endpoint must respond in under 50 ms (indexed).\n194-2. **Reliability:** an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row locking). A crash mid-send leaves rows in `SENDING`; rows stuck in `SENDING` for more than 10 minutes return to `PENDING`.\n195-3. **Security:** notification `link` values must be relative paths starting with `/` (validated) to prevent open redirects. Email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\n196-4. **Deliverability:** every email has both HTML and plain-text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing at the preferences page.\n197-\n198-## Acceptance Criteria\n199-\n200-1. Given a user with default preferences, when `notify()` is called for type `system.test`, then one `Notification` row and one `EmailOutbox` row are created and the bell count increases by 1 within 30 seconds.\n201-2. Given a parent turned off email for a type, when that type is notified, then only the in-app row is created.\n202-3. Given an SMTP failure, when the dispatcher runs, then the row has `attempts = 1`, `status = PENDING` and `nextAttemptAt` about 1 minute later; after 5 failures the status is `FAILED` and it appears in the admin email log.\n203-4. Given two dispatcher invocations run at the same moment over 10 pending emails, then each email is sent exactly once.\n204-5. Given a user clicks a notification in the bell, then it is marked read and the browser navigates to its link.\n205-6. Given a request to dispatch without the correct bearer token, then the response is `401`.\n206-7. Given the invite flow from PRD-01, when an admin resends an invite, then an `EmailOutbox` row with the invite template is created instead of only a log line.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b09f90f4-bdfe-409b-ac12-21f6b1ffd7b1","uuid":"a462af41-4fd2-4c80-925d-cd7c3e0bc798","timestamp":"2026-10-20T06:00:27.845Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"176:## API\n177-\n178-| Method & path | Role | Notes |\n179-|---|---|---|\n180-| `GET /api/notifications` | any | `?unread=true&category=&page=` — own notifications only |\n181-| `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` | any | `{ data: { count } }` |\n182-| `POST /api/notifications/:id/read` · `/unread` | owner | |\n183-| `POST /api/notifications/read-all` | any | |\n184-| `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` | any | Merged with registry defaults |\n185-| `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` | any | `{ type, inApp, email }`; `inApp=false` refused for mandatory types |\n186-| `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` | `CRON_SECRET` | Returns `{ sent, failed, retried }` |\n187-| `GET /api/admin/email-log` | ADMIN | |\n188-| `POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry` | ADMIN | |\n189-| `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` | ADMIN | |\n190-\n191-## Non-Functional Requirements\n192-\n193-1. **Performance:** `notify()` for 1,000 recipients must finish in under 2 seconds. Unread-count endpoint must respond in under 50 ms (indexed).\n194-2. **Reliability:** an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row locking). A crash mid-send leaves rows in `SENDING`; rows stuck in `SENDING` for more than 10 minutes return to `PENDING`.\n195-3. **Security:** notification `link` values must be relative paths starting with `/` (validated) to prevent open redirects. Email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\n196-4. **Deliverability:** every email has both HTML and plain-text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing at the preferences page.\n197-\n198-## Acceptance Criteria\n199-\n200-1. Given a user with default preferences, when `notify()` is called for type `system.test`, then one `Notification` row and one `EmailOutbox` row are created and the bell count increases by 1 within 30 seconds.\n201-2. Given a parent turned off email for a type, when that type is notified, then only the in-app row is created.\n202-3. Given an SMTP failure, when the dispatcher runs, then the row has `attempts = 1`, `status = PENDING` and `nextAttemptAt` about 1 minute later; after 5 failures the status is `FAILED` and it appears in the admin email log.\n203-4. Given two dispatcher invocations run at the same moment over 10 pending emails, then each email is sent exactly once.\n204-5. Given a user clicks a notification in the bell, then it is marked read and the browser navigates to its link.\n205-6. Given a request to dispatch without the correct bearer token, then the response is `401`.\n206-7. Given the invite flow from PRD-01, when an admin resends an invite, then an `EmailOutbox` row with the invite template is created instead of only a log line.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
