{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EXkiMUaA81zKAggwoNksYR","type":"tool_result","content":"```prisma\nenum CourseKind { CORE ELECTIVE }\nenum EnrollmentStatus { ACTIVE DROPPED }\n\nmodel Section {\n  id                String       @id @default(cuid())\n  academicYearId    String\n  academicYear      AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])\n  gradeLevelId      String\n  gradeLevel        GradeLevel   @relation(fields: [gradeLevelId], references: [id])\n  name              String                         // \"7A\"\n  homeroomTeacherId String?\n  homeroomTeacher   User?        @relation(\"HomeroomTeacher\", fields: [homeroomTeacherId], references: [id])\n  roomId            String?\n  room              Room?        @relation(fields: [roomId], references: [id])\n  capacity          Int          @default(30)      // 1–60\n  createdAt         DateTime     @default(now())\n  updatedAt         DateTime     @updatedAt\n  members           SectionMember[]\n  courses           Course[]\n  @@unique([academicYearId, name])\n}\n\nmodel SectionMember {\n  id         String   @id @default(cuid())\n  sectionId  String\n  section    Section  @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId  String\n  student    User     @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n  joinedAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  academicYearId String                             // denormalised for the uniqueness rule\n  @@unique([studentId, academicYearId])            // one section per student per year\n}\n\nmodel Course {\n  id              String       @id @default(cuid())\n  academicYearId  String\n  academicYear    AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])\n  subjectId       String\n  subject         Subject      @relation(fields: [subjectId], references: [id])\n  sectionId       String?                          // null for cross-section electives\n  section         Section?     @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id])\n  teacherId       String\n  teacher         User         @relation(\"CourseTeacher\", fields: [teacherId], references: [id])\n  coTeacherIds    String[]     @default([])        // additional teachers with full course access\n  name            String                           // default \"<Subject> – <Section>\"\n  code            String                           // default \"<SUBJECTCODE>-<SECTION>\", e.g. \"MATH-7A\"\n  kind            CourseKind   @default(CORE)\n  description     String?\n  capacity        Int?\n  archivedAt      DateTime?\n  createdAt       DateTime     @default(now())\n  updatedAt       DateTime     @updatedAt\n  enrollments     Enrollment[]\n  @@unique([academicYearId, code])\n}\n\nmodel Enrollment {\n  id          String           @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId    String\n  course      Course           @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId   String\n  student     User             @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n  status      EnrollmentStatus @default(ACTIVE)\n  enrolledAt  DateTime         @default(now())\n  droppedAt   DateTime?\n  @@unique([courseId, studentId])\n  @@index([studentId, status])\n}\n```\n7:Introduce the two grouping concepts the rest of SchoolHub depends on: **sections** (homeroom groups such as \"7A\", one per student per academic year) and **courses** (a subject taught to a section by a teacher, such as \"Mathematics – 7A\"). Add enrollment management, class rosters, \"My courses\" pages for teachers and students, and the course home page with its tab framework.\n141:  code            String                           // default \"<SUBJECTCODE>-<SECTION>\", e.g. \"MATH-7A\"\n170:4. \"Create core courses\" dialog lists all active subjects with a checkbox and teacher picker per subject; submitting creates one CORE course per checked subject with default name and code, and enrolls all current members.\n234:5. Given Tom teaches Mathematics – 7A, when Tom opens `/my-courses`, then that course appears; when Tom opens a course he does not teach, then he gets the 403 page.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36f35059-30cc-4350-81e2-330ee67c124d","uuid":"260776a7-e71f-4b38-8704-b557584e5563","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:32:46.370Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"```prisma\nenum CourseKind { CORE ELECTIVE }\nenum EnrollmentStatus { ACTIVE DROPPED }\n\nmodel Section {\n  id                String       @id @default(cuid())\n  academicYearId    String\n  academicYear      AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])\n  gradeLevelId      String\n  gradeLevel        GradeLevel   @relation(fields: [gradeLevelId], references: [id])\n  name              String                         // \"7A\"\n  homeroomTeacherId String?\n  homeroomTeacher   User?        @relation(\"HomeroomTeacher\", fields: [homeroomTeacherId], references: [id])\n  roomId            String?\n  room              Room?        @relation(fields: [roomId], references: [id])\n  capacity          Int          @default(30)      // 1–60\n  createdAt         DateTime     @default(now())\n  updatedAt         DateTime     @updatedAt\n  members           SectionMember[]\n  courses           Course[]\n  @@unique([academicYearId, name])\n}\n\nmodel SectionMember {\n  id         String   @id @default(cuid())\n  sectionId  String\n  section    Section  @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId  String\n  student    User     @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n  joinedAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  academicYearId String                             // denormalised for the uniqueness rule\n  @@unique([studentId, academicYearId])            // one section per student per year\n}\n\nmodel Course {\n  id              String       @id @default(cuid())\n  academicYearId  String\n  academicYear    AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])\n  subjectId       String\n  subject         Subject      @relation(fields: [subjectId], references: [id])\n  sectionId       String?                          // null for cross-section electives\n  section         Section?     @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id])\n  teacherId       String\n  teacher         User         @relation(\"CourseTeacher\", fields: [teacherId], references: [id])\n  coTeacherIds    String[]     @default([])        // additional teachers with full course access\n  name            String                           // default \"<Subject> – <Section>\"\n  code            String                           // default \"<SUBJECTCODE>-<SECTION>\", e.g. \"MATH-7A\"\n  kind            CourseKind   @default(CORE)\n  description     String?\n  capacity        Int?\n  archivedAt      DateTime?\n  createdAt       DateTime     @default(now())\n  updatedAt       DateTime     @updatedAt\n  enrollments     Enrollment[]\n  @@unique([academicYearId, code])\n}\n\nmodel Enrollment {\n  id          String           @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId    String\n  course      Course           @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId   String\n  student     User             @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n  status      EnrollmentStatus @default(ACTIVE)\n  enrolledAt  DateTime         @default(now())\n  droppedAt   DateTime?\n  @@unique([courseId, studentId])\n  @@index([studentId, status])\n}\n```\n7:Introduce the two grouping concepts the rest of SchoolHub depends on: **sections** (homeroom groups such as \"7A\", one per student per academic year) and **courses** (a subject taught to a section by a teacher, such as \"Mathematics – 7A\"). Add enrollment management, class rosters, \"My courses\" pages for teachers and students, and the course home page with its tab framework.\n141:  code            String                           // default \"<SUBJECTCODE>-<SECTION>\", e.g. \"MATH-7A\"\n170:4. \"Create core courses\" dialog lists all active subjects with a checkbox and teacher picker per subject; submitting creates one CORE course per checked subject with default name and code, and enrolls all current members.\n234:5. Given Tom teaches Mathematics – 7A, when Tom opens `/my-courses`, then that course appears; when Tom opens a course he does not teach, then he gets the 403 page.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EXkiMUaA81zKAggwoNksYR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
