{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgT4iCoLm5nkGXdjj8QwZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The arch-api-contracts step for abcd-05 is finished, so the architect phase is complete. It produced 17 endpoints, one for each route in the PRD-05 API table once its combined rows are split out. A check script confirmed the JSON is valid, every cited requirement ID exists in `requirements.json`, and both files carry `ticketId` `abcd-05`.\n\n- **`artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json`:** each endpoint lists its method, path, request and response shapes, error cases and requirement IDs. Shared data shapes (Section, Course, Enrollment, the inputs, enroll results and the \"full section\" error) are defined once in a `schemas` block and referenced from the endpoints.\n- **`artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json`:** `status: complete`, `endpointCount: 17`, and four advisory notes, none of them blocking.\n\nThings dev-planning should know:\n- **Old files replaced:** both files I wrote previously held leftovers from ticket abcd-04. The files under `artifacts/dev-planning/` probably are abcd-04's too, so treat them as stale.\n- **List response shape:** the PRD shows lists as `{ data, page, pageSize, total }`, but the existing `paginated()` helper in `src/server/http.ts` returns `{ data, meta: { page, pageSize, total } }`. I followed the helper.\n- **Decisions the PRD doesn't spell out:**\n  - Adding students directly to a core course is refused, since core membership is managed through the section.\n  - Section, kind and academic year can't be changed after a course is created, so editing a course never silently rewrites its roster.\n  - Move-section and re-activating an enrollment accept an optional \"override capacity\" flag.\n  - `/api/me/courses` returns an empty list for admins.\n  - Copy-to-year skips sections already in the top grade and lists them in a `skipped` field.\n- **Student roster privacy:** students get classmates' names only, with no IDs either. Admins and teachers get the full roster.\n- **Auth:** routes use the existing temporary `requireRole` check, per the system design's decision, because the real per-user login check comes with PRD-01. Until then, endpoints that depend on who's asking (like \"my courses\") behave as if everyone is the same placeholder user."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":54025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36f35059-30cc-4350-81e2-330ee67c124d","uuid":"3ea9f24b-5718-4081-997a-824c307b52f8","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:34:07.851Z","request_id":"req_011CgT4iCTWsDYW1CAmFEAip"}
