{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DzNtjHFPoibUKze9i4DUnB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC, SCH-001)\n2\t\n3\tPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:02:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (37 FR + 12 NFR),\n6\t`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (94% confidence, 4 blockers),\n7\t`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n8\t`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n9\t\n10\t## Overview\n11\t\n12\tPRD-01 replaces the `PLACEHOLDER_USER` stand-ins with real authentication:\n13\tAuth.js v5 Credentials sign-in, 8-hour JWT sessions, invite activation,\n14\tpassword reset and change, lockout and rate limiting, an edge middleware\n15\tgate, and real session-backed `requireUser()` / `requireRole()`. This is a\n16\tbrownfield change on Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma + MUI v9. **No new\n17\truntime dependency**: `next-auth` 5 beta and `bcrypt` 6 are already installed.\n18\t\n19\tBrownfield facts re-checked on disk for this design:\n20\t- All User auth columns already exist (`passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`,\n21\t  `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`).\n22\t  `AuthToken.tokenHash` is already `@unique`. The only schema gap is the\n23\t  two AuditLog indexes.\n24\t- `requireRole(` has **50 call sites in 43 files: 33 `route.ts`, 8 pages/layouts,\n25\t  1 in `navigation.ts` (a comment), 1 in `course-access.ts` (a comment)**.\n26\t  None use `await` today, and every caller is already in an async function.\n27\t  `course-access.ts` and `student-access.ts` take an `AccessUser {id, role}`\n28\t  argument and don't call `requireRole`, so they stay untouched (NFR-9).\n29\t- `navigationForRole(role)` already exists in `src/config/navigation.ts`.\n30\t  FR-33 is just about feeding it the real role.\n31\t- `src/server/http.ts` already has `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parseBody`\n32\t  and the codes UNAUTHENTICATED/FORBIDDEN/RATE_LIMITED/CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR.\n33\t- The project uses a `src/` dir, so Next only picks up middleware at\n34\t  **`src/middleware.ts`**, not at the repo root. FR-12's \"middleware.ts\" means that file.\n35\t\n36\t### Intake blockers and how they're resolved\n37\t\n38\t| Blocker | Resolution |\n39\t|---|---|\n40\t| FR-1 schema divergences (`ip` vs `ipAddress`, extra `ARCHIVED`, different indexes) | **Resolved, additive only** (ADR-9). Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED`, keep the existing indexes. Add `@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to AuditLog in one migration, `auth_reconcile`. FR-4's `status !== 'ACTIVE'` check already rejects ARCHIVED. |\n41\t| FR-25 `createUser` / `setUserStatus` signatures differ from PRD | **Resolved: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures.** No second `createUser`. A duplicate email already maps P2002 → CONFLICT through `withHandler`. `createUser` must lower-case the email (FR-2). Dev only verifies this and adds a one-line fix if it's missing. |\n42\t| FR-28/29 `requireRole()` is sync, Auth.js `auth()` is async | **Resolved: go async** (ADR-2). Each of the 50 call sites gets a mechanical `await`. The return shape stays a superset of `{id, role}`. The 8 server pages/layouts switch to the redirecting page variants (Component 7). |\n43\t| NFR-6 mui-mcp must be reachable | **Not blocking at architect time.** The `useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools are registered in this environment. The Dev phase must still confirm it can reach them before writing UI, and must stop and report a blocker if it can't. |\n44\t\n45\t---\n46\t\n47\t## Component Breakdown\n48\t\n49\t### 1. Data model (`prisma/schema.prisma`, migration `auth_reconcile`)\n50\t- Add the two AuditLog indexes only. No renames, no drops, no column changes.\n51\t- `User.email` stays `String @unique`. Lower-casing is enforced in app code\n52\t  at every write and lookup through one zod transform (Component 6). Skip\n53\t  `citext`, because switching the column type isn't additive.\n54\t- _FR-1, FR-2, NFR-9, NFR-12 (columns are already UTC `DateTime`)._\n55\t\n56\t### 2. Auth.js core, split config (ADR-1)\n57\t- **`src/server/auth/auth.config.ts`** (edge-safe, no Prisma or bcrypt imports):\n58\t  - `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8 * 3600, updateAge: 15 * 60 }`\n59\t  - `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, `providers: []`\n60\t  - `callbacks.session`: copies `id, role, firstName, lastName, email` from the token to `session.user`\n61\t  - `callbacks.redirect`: `safeCallbackUrl()` (Component 6)\n62\t  - Cookies use the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and `__Secure-` + Secure in production. Don't override them.\n63\t- **`src/server/auth/auth.ts`** (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })], callbacks: { ...authConfig.callbacks, jwt } })`,\n64\t  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update }`.\n65\t- **`jwt` callback** (Node only; does session revocation, ADR-4):\n66\t  - On `trigger === 'signIn'`: copy the user fields, then set `authTime = now`\n67\t    and `checkedAt = now`.\n68\t  - On `trigger === 'update'` with `{ reauth: true }` (FR-23): set `authTime = now`.\n69\t  - Otherwise, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`: run\n70\t    `select { passwordChangedAt, status, role, firstName, lastName }`.\n71\t    Return `null` if `status !== 'ACTIVE'` or `passwordChangedAt > authTime`.\n72\t    Otherwise refresh `role` and the names, and set `checkedAt = now`.\n73\t  - **Use the custom `authTime` claim, not JWT `iat`.** Auth.js re-signs the\n74\t    token on every `updateAge` refresh, so `iat` moves forward and would\n75\t    hide an older password change.\n76\t- **`src/types/next-auth.d.ts`**: module augmentation for the typed `session.user` and JWT fields.\n77\t- **`src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`**: `export const { GET, POST } = handlers`.\n78\t  Static siblings like `accept-invite/` win over the catch-all in Next's\n79\t  route matching, so they can live side by side.\n80\t- _FR-3, FR-10, FR-11, FR-34, NFR-2._\n81\t\n82\t### 3. Credential verification (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts`)\n83\tA plain exported `authorizeCredentials(input, request)` that `Credentials.authorize`\n84\tdelegates to, so integration tests can call it without going over HTTP (FR-36).\n85\tOrder of checks:\n86\t1. `rateLimit('login:ip:' + getClientIp(request), 10, 5 min)`. Over the limit → throw `AuthError('rate_limited')`.\n87\t2. Parse `{email, password}` with `signInSchema` (trim + lower-case the email).\n88\t3. Look up the user by email.\n89\t4. **Reject missing or ineligible users only after the bcrypt compare.**\n90\t   Compare against the user's hash, or against a module-level `DUMMY_HASH`\n91\t   (cost 12) if the user is missing or has no hash. Every path runs exactly\n92\t   one bcrypt compare (NFR-3, NFR-4).\n93\t5. Branches:\n94\t   - missing user → `invalid`\n95\t   - `status === 'DISABLED'` → `disabled`\n96\t   - `status !== 'ACTIVE'` (INVITED, ARCHIVED) or `archivedAt` set → `invalid`\n97\t   - `lockedUntil > now` → `locked:<minutes>`, where minutes = `ceil((lockedUntil - now) / 60000)`\n98\t   - wrong password → run `registerFailure`, then `invalid` (or `locked:15` if this attempt triggered the lock)\n99\t   - success → set `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lastLoginAt = now`, return the user\n100\t6. Lockout logic is the pure function `computeLockout(currentCount, now)`, which returns\n101\t   `{ failedLoginCount, lockedUntil | null }` (5 failures → lock for 15 min and reset the count to 0).\n102\t   The DB write is one `update` with `failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }`, followed by a\n103\t   conditional lock update when the returned count reaches 5. **Ceiling:** concurrent\n104\t   failures can overshoot the count by one before the lock lands, which doesn't\n105\t   matter here.\n106\t7. Audit entries, passing the request so the IP is recorded:\n107\t   - `auth.login.success`\n108\t   - `auth.login.failure` with `{ email, reason }` only\n109\t   - `auth.lockout`\n110\t   - `actorId` is the user id when the user is known, otherwise null.\n111\t8. `class AuthError extends CredentialsSignin { code }`. The login form reads the\n112\t   error `code` from `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` and maps it to\n113\t   the FR-5 / FR-7 messages. For `locked:N`, it renders \"Try again in N minutes.\"\n114\t   N is a duration, so no timezone conversion is needed (NFR-12).\n115\t- _FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-9, NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-12._\n116\t\n117\t### 4. Token module (`src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, ADR-5)\n118\tThis is the only code that touches the `AuthToken` model.\n119\t- `createToken(userId, type, ttl: { minutes?, days? }, tx?)`:\n120\t  - In one transaction, `updateMany { userId, type, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`,\n121\t    which invalidates older unused tokens (FR-20, FR-26). Then insert the new row.\n122\t  - The raw token is `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`. Only\n123\t    `sha256(raw)` (hex) is stored.\n124\t  - Returns the raw token.\n125\t- `verifyToken(raw, type)`:\n126\t  - Find by `tokenHash`, then confirm with `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers.\n127\t  - Returns `{ token, user }`, or `null` if the token is missing, has the wrong\n128\t    type, is used or is expired.\n129\t- `consumeToken(tokenId, tx?)`: `updateMany { id, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`.\n130\t  Throws `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` if the update count is 0, which makes a\n131\t  double-submit fail cleanly.\n132\t- Pure `hashToken(raw)` is exported so the unit tests can use it.\n133\t- _FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1._\n134\t\n135\t### 5. Rate limiter (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`, ADR-6)\n136\t- `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs, now = Date.now()) → { ok, retryAfterMs }`\n137\t  over a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`. It prunes old timestamps on each call.\n138\t- Exports `__resetRateLimits()` for tests.\n139\t- Add a `ponytail: per-process limiter` comment: it resets on restart and isn't\n140\t  shared across instances. Swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if the app scales\n141\t  horizontally.\n142\t- `getClientIp(request)` goes in the existing **`src/server/http.ts`**. It returns\n143\t  the first `x-forwarded-for` entry, trimmed, or `null`. The limiter and `audit()` share it.\n144\t- _FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-11._\n145\t\n146\t### 6. Validators and pure helpers (`src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, client-safe)\n147\t- `emailField`: `z.string().trim().toLowerCase().email()`.\n148\t- `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `acceptInviteSchema {token, password, confirm}`,\n149\t  `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordSchema {currentPassword, newPassword, confirm}`.\n150\t- `passwordChecks(pw, email)` returns `{ length, letter, digit, notEmail }`. Both the\n151\t  checklist UI and the schema's `superRefine` use it.\n152\t- `safeCallbackUrl(url)`: returns `url` only if it starts with `/` and not with `//`\n153\t  or `/\\`. Otherwise it returns `/dashboard`.\n154\t- **Server-only `src/server/auth/password-policy.ts`**:\n155\t  - Reads `common-passwords.txt` once into a `Set`.\n156\t  - Exports `assertPasswordAllowed(pw, email)`, which runs `passwordChecks` plus\n157\t    the common-list check and throws `VALIDATION_ERROR` with\n158\t    `details.fieldErrors.password` if any rule fails.\n159\t  - Every password-setting service calls it.\n160\t- The 1,000-word list never ships to the client. The checklist shows four rules\n161\t  live, and the \"not a common password\" rule appears only from the server's\n162\t  error response.\n163\t- _FR-2, FR-8, FR-17, FR-18, NFR-8._\n164\t\n165\t### 7. Authorization helpers (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, ADR-2)\n166\tDelete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Every helper goes through one internal resolver:\n167\t```ts\n168\ttype SessionUser = { id; role; firstName; lastName; email }   // superset of AccessUser\n169\tgetCurrentUser = cache(async (): Promise<SessionUser | null> => (await auth())?.user ?? null)\n170\trequireUser(): Promise<SessionUser>                // throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED\n171\trequireRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>        // throws UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN\n172\trequirePageUser(): Promise<SessionUser>            // redirect('/login?callbackUrl=…')\n173\trequirePageRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>    // redirect('/login…') / redirect('/forbidden')\n174\t```\n175\t- **Route handlers** (33 files) change from `requireRole(` to `await requireRole(`.\n176\t  `withHandler` already maps a thrown `AppError` to the 401/403 envelope.\n177\t- **Server pages/layouts** (8 files) change to `await requirePageRole(` because a\n178\t  thrown AppError in a page would render `error.tsx`, not a redirect.\n179\t  `redirect()` throws `NEXT_REDIRECT` and must never run inside `withHandler`,\n180\t  since it would be caught there and turned into an INTERNAL error. That's why\n181\t  the page variants are separate exports instead of a flag.\n182\t- The page variants read the current path from the `x-pathname` request header,\n183\t  which `src/middleware.ts` sets, to build `callbackUrl`. If the header is\n184\t  missing, they fall back to `/dashboard`.\n185\t- **Guardrail for missed awaits:** turn on `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises`\n186\t  for `src/**`. Typecheck alone misses a bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statement.\n187\t- No `permissions.ts`, no `can()`.\n188\t- _FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9, NFR-10._\n189\t\n190\t### 8. Edge middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) and `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n191\t- `public-routes.ts` exports `PUBLIC_PAGE_PATHS = ['/', '/login', '/forgot-password', '/invite/', '/reset-password/']`\n192\t  (a trailing `/` means prefix match) and\n193\t  `PUBLIC_API_PATHS = ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`.\n194\t  `/api/auth/` covers the Auth.js catch-all and the three unauthenticated POSTs.\n195\t  The list has **no sign-up path** (FR-37).\n196\t- `export default NextAuth(authConfig).auth(req => …)` runs these steps in order:\n197\t  1. **CSRF origin check (NFR-2):** for any non-GET/HEAD `/api/*` request that\n198\t     isn't under `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`'s own endpoints, if `Origin` is present\n199\t     and doesn't equal the app origin, return 403 FORBIDDEN in the JSON envelope.\n200\t     Auth.js CSRF tokens only protect Auth.js's own endpoints. Custom POSTs rely\n201\t     on this check plus SameSite=Lax.\n202\t  2. If the path is public → `next()`.\n203\t  3. If there's no session: `/api/*` → 401 `{error:{code:'UNAUTHENTICATED',…}}`.\n204\t     Pages → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=<path+search>`.\n205\t  4. Otherwise → `next()` and set the `x-pathname` request header.\n206\t- `matcher` excludes `_next/static`, `_next/image`, `favicon.ico` and files\n207\t  with extensions.\n208\t- Middleware only decodes the JWT. It doesn't check revocation, because the\n209\t  Node `jwt` callback does that. NFR-7's real guard is the server-side helper\n210\t  on every page and handler.\n211\t- _FR-12, FR-37, NFR-2, NFR-7, NFR-8._\n212\t\n213\t### 9. Auth services (`src/server/services/auth.ts`, Node)\n214\tRoute handlers stay thin: zod parse → service → `ok()`. Every service below\n215\trecords an audit entry with the request so the IP is captured.\n216\t- `acceptInvite({token, password}, request)`:\n217\t  1. `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')`, or throw `INVALID_TOKEN`.\n218\t  2. `assertPasswordAllowed(password, user.email)`.\n219\t  3. `bcrypt.hash(password, 12)`.\n220\t  4. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `status = ACTIVE` and\n221\t     `passwordChangedAt = now`, then `consumeToken`.\n222\t  5. Audit `auth.invite.accepted`.\n223\t  6. Return `{ email }`. **The client then calls `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo: '/dashboard'})`.**\n224\t     Minting an Auth.js session by hand in a custom route is fragile, so the\n225\t     design reuses the one sign-in path.\n226\t- `requestPasswordReset({email}, request)`:\n227\t  - `rateLimit('forgot:ip:'+ip, 10, 1h)`. Over the limit → `RATE_LIMITED` 429.\n228\t    An IP-level response doesn't reveal whether an account exists.\n229\t  - `rateLimit('forgot:email:'+email, 3, 1h)`. Over the limit → **return the\n230\t    generic success message silently**. A 429 here would reveal that the email\n231\t    was tried before.\n232\t  - If the user exists and is ACTIVE: `createToken(id, 'PASSWORD_RESET', {minutes: 60})`,\n233\t    then `sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link)`.\n234\t  - Unknown or inactive email: no DB write.\n235\t  - Always return `{ message: \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" }`.\n236\t- `resetPassword({token, password}, request)`:\n237\t  1. `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`.\n238\t  2. Policy check, then hash.\n239\t  3. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `passwordChangedAt = now`,\n240\t     `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lockedUntil = null`, then `consumeToken`.\n241\t  4. Audit `auth.password.reset`.\n242\t- `changePassword(user, {currentPassword, newPassword}, request)`:\n243\t  1. bcrypt-compare `currentPassword`. If it's wrong → throw `VALIDATION_ERROR`\n244\t     with `details.fieldErrors.currentPassword = ['Current password is incorrect.']`.\n245\t  2. Policy check, hash, and update `passwordHash` and `passwordChangedAt`.\n246\t  3. Audit `auth.password.changed`.\n247\t  4. The route handler then calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this\n248\t     session's `authTime` moves past `passwordChangedAt`. Other sessions fail\n249\t     the FR-11 check within 5 minutes.\n250\t- **`src/server/auth/email.ts`** `sendAuthEmail(user, kind: 'invite' | 'password-reset', link)`:\n251\t  - Logs `{ to, subject, link }` with `logger.info`. This is the single seam\n252\t    PRD-04 replaces with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\n253\t  - Links are built from `env.AUTH_URL`: `/invite/<raw>` and `/reset-password/<raw>`.\n254\t  - Raw tokens appear only in this log line and in the email itself, never in\n255\t    audit metadata.\n256\t- _FR-16, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, FR-31, NFR-3, NFR-8._\n257\t\n258\t### 10. Users service additions (`src/server/services/users.ts`)\n259\t- Keep `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` as they are (FR-25).\n260\t- Add `createInviteToken(userId)`, which returns `createToken(userId, 'INVITE', { days: 7 })`.\n261\t  `tokens.createToken` already invalidates older unused tokens.\n262\t- Replace the no-op body of `sendInvite(userId)` with: `createInviteToken`, then\n263\t  `sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link)`, then return the unchanged\n264\t  `{ id, inviteSentAt }` shape.\n265\t- _FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-2._\n266\t\n267\t### 11. Audit (`src/server/audit.ts`)\n268\t- Add an optional `request?: Request` to the input. Set `ip: request ? getClientIp(request) : null`.\n269\t- The function stays inside its existing try/catch and never throws.\n270\t- Defence in depth: before the insert, strip these metadata keys:\n271\t  `password`, `passwordHash`, `newPassword`, `currentPassword`, `token`, `rawToken`.\n272\t- _FR-9, FR-30, FR-31._\n273\t\n274\t### 12. App shell and navigation\n275\t- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`:\n276\t  - `const user = await requirePageUser()`.\n277\t  - Pass `user` (id, name, role, email) and `navigationForRole(user.role)` to `<AppShell>`.\n278\t    Props avoid a `SessionProvider` round-trip and the flash of empty UI it causes.\n279\t  - Filtering the nav doesn't protect anything on its own (NFR-7).\n280\t- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`:\n281\t  - Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and render the user from props: `UserAvatar`\n282\t    (initials), name, and a role `Chip`.\n283\t  - The user menu gains **\"Account security\" → `/account/security`**.\n284\t  - Sign out calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n285\t    That function doesn't need a provider.\n286\t- _FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-6, NFR-7._\n287\t\n288\t### 13. Auth UI (MUI v9 only, every component looked up through mui-mcp first, NFR-6)\n289\t- **`src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`**: a centred `Container` + `Card` layout without the AppShell.\n290\t- **`login/page.tsx`**:\n291\t  - Uses the MUI Sign-in template patterns: TextField, an InputAdornment + IconButton\n292\t    show-password toggle, and an Alert for form errors.\n293\t  - Client submit calls `signIn('credentials', {redirect: false})`, maps the error\n294\t    code to the FR-5 / FR-7 copy, and on success navigates to\n295\t    `safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)`.\n296\t  - If the page loads with `?reset=1`, it fires the `useToast` success toast for FR-21.\n297\t  - Links to `/forgot-password`. **No sign-up link** (FR-37).\n298\t- **`forgot-password/page.tsx`**: an email field. It shows the generic message on 200\n299\t  and the FR-7-style message on 429.\n300\t- **`invite/[token]/page.tsx`**:\n301\t  - A server component calls `verifyToken`. If the token is invalid, it shows the\n302\t    FR-14 Alert copy.\n303\t  - Otherwise it renders `<SetPasswordForm>` with the read-only name and email.\n304\t- **`reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`**: verifies the token the same way, then shows\n305\t  `<SetPasswordForm>`. On success it redirects to `/login?reset=1`.\n306\t- **`(app)/account/security/page.tsx`**:\n307\t  - Calls `requirePageUser()`.\n308\t  - The form has current, new and confirm password fields. On success it shows the\n309\t    \"Password updated\" toast. A field error renders on `currentPassword`.\n310\t- **Shared pieces** (in `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`):\n311\t  - **`PasswordChecklist`**: an MUI `List` with CheckCircle/RadioButtonUnchecked icons,\n312\t    driven by `passwordChecks`.\n313\t  - **`SetPasswordForm`**: password, confirm and the checklist. The invite and reset\n314\t    pages share it.\n315\t- **Form accessibility, applied to all 5 forms (NFR-5):**\n316\t  - Form-level `Alert` sits inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`.\n317\t  - react-hook-form + `zodResolver` with `shouldFocusError: true`, so focus moves to\n318\t    the first invalid field.\n319\t  - Server `details.fieldErrors` are mapped to `setError`.\n320\t- _FR-3, FR-5, FR-14, FR-15, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-23, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6._\n321\t\n322\t### 14. Seed (`prisma/seed.ts`)\n323\t- Upsert by email, so re-running the seed is safe:\n324\t  - `admin@`, `teacher@`, `teacher2@`, `student@`, `student2@` and `parent@schoolhub.test`\n325\t  - All ACTIVE, with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` as the password\n326\t- Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` as INVITED, then call `createInviteToken` and\n327\t  log the link with `logger.info`.\n328\t- `office@` stays as it is.\n329\t- _FR-35, FR-13 (all seeded tokens go through tokens.ts)._\n330\t\n331\t### 15. Tests (Vitest + Playwright, ADR-10)\n332\t- **Unit tests:**\n333\t  - `passwordChecks` / `assertPasswordAllowed`\n334\t  - `hashToken` and the verify expiry/used branches\n335\t  - `computeLockout`\n336\t  - `rateLimit`, with an injected `now`\n337\t  - `safeCallbackUrl`\n338\t- **Integration tests** (against the test DB):\n339\t  - Every `authorizeCredentials` branch\n340\t  - `acceptInvite`, `resetPassword` and `changePassword`\n341\t  - Audit metadata never contains secrets\n342\t- **Playwright:**\n343\t  - Sign-in/out with seeded users\n344\t  - The failed-login message\n345\t  - Forgot → reset. The test reads the token by creating one through\n346\t    `createToken` in a test helper, because the raw token isn't recoverable\n347\t    from the DB.\n348\t  - `@axe-core/playwright` on the auth pages\n349\t- Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. Use `logger` only.\n350\t- _FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10._\n351\t\n352\t---\n353\t\n354\t## Data Flow\n355\t\n356\t**Sign-in (FR-3–FR-10)**\n357\t1. The browser posts to `/login` → `signIn('credentials')` →\n358\t   `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials`, protected by the Auth.js CSRF token.\n359\t2. `authorize` → `authorizeCredentials`: rate limit, user lookup, one bcrypt\n360\t   compare, then the lockout/branch logic and audit.\n361\t3. The `jwt` callback (`trigger='signIn'`) writes `{id, role, names, email, authTime, checkedAt}`.\n362\t   The session cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax.\n363\t4. The client receives `ok` → `router.push(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))`.\n364\t   On error, the code maps to a message rendered in the aria-live Alert.\n365\t\n366\t**Authenticated request (FR-11, FR-12, FR-28, FR-29)**\n367\t1. `src/middleware.ts` decodes the JWT on the edge.\n368\t   - No session on a page → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`.\n369\t   - No session on `/api` → 401.\n370\t2. The page or handler calls `await requireRole(...)` → `getCurrentUser()`\n371\t   (React `cache`) → `auth()` (Node).\n372\t3. The `jwt` callback re-checks `passwordChangedAt` / `status` at most every 5 minutes.\n373\t   If the check fails, the session becomes null → UNAUTHENTICATED, or a redirect to `/login`.\n374\t4. The role check fails → FORBIDDEN 403 (API) or `/forbidden` (page).\n375\t\n376\t**Invite (FR-13–FR-16, FR-26, FR-27)**\n377\t1. PRD-03 admin `sendInvite(userId)` → `createInviteToken` → `tokens.createToken`\n378\t   (invalidates older tokens, stores the hash) → `sendAuthEmail` (logs the link).\n379\t2. The user opens `/invite/<raw>`. The server component runs `verifyToken`\n380\t   (hash lookup + timingSafeEqual) and renders the form or the invalid Alert.\n381\t3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → middleware origin check → `acceptInvite`.\n382\t   In one transaction it sets ACTIVE and the hash, then consumes the token, and audits.\n383\t4. On 200, the client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`.\n384\t\n385\t**Forgot / reset (FR-19–FR-22)**\n386\t1. `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → IP limit (429) → email limit (silent) →\n387\t   ACTIVE user? `createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min)` + `sendAuthEmail`.\n388\t   The response is always the generic message.\n389\t2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `POST /api/auth/reset-password`, which sets the hash\n390\t   and `passwordChangedAt`, clears the lockout and consumes the token. Then it\n391\t   audits and the browser goes to `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n392\t\n393\t**Change password (FR-23)**\n394\t1. `/account/security` → `POST /api/account/password` → `await requireUser()` → `changePassword`.\n395\t2. The handler calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this session gets a\n396\t   new `authTime`. Other devices fail the next 5-minute check.\n397\t3. The toast reads \"Password updated\".\n398\t\n399\t---\n400\t\n401\t## API Surface (for `arch-api-contracts`)\n402\t\n403\t| Method | Path | Auth | Handler → service | Reqs |\n404\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n405\t| GET/POST | `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` | public (Auth.js protocol) | `handlers` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-34, NFR-2 |\n406\t| POST | `/api/auth/accept-invite` | public + origin check | `acceptInvite` | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-1, NFR-8 |\n407\t| POST | `/api/auth/forgot-password` | public + origin check | `requestPasswordReset` | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-3 |\n408\t| POST | `/api/auth/reset-password` | public + origin check | `resetPassword` | FR-21, FR-17 |\n409\t| POST | `/api/account/password` | `requireUser()` | `changePassword` | FR-23, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n410\t\n411\tAll custom routes use `withHandler`, `parseBody(schema)` and `ok()`, returning the\n412\t`{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` envelopes. Codes:\n413\t- `VALIDATION_ERROR` 400: policy failures and wrong current password, with `details.fieldErrors`\n414\t- `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401\n415\t- `FORBIDDEN` 403\n416\t- `INVALID_TOKEN` 410: invalid, used or expired invite/reset tokens\n417\t- `RATE_LIMITED` 429\n418\t\n419\t`/api/health` stays public and is unchanged. There's no sign-up endpoint (FR-37).\n420\t\n421\t## New / changed files\n422\t\n423\t**New:**\n424\t- `src/middleware.ts`\n425\t- `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n426\t- `src/types/next-auth.d.ts`\n427\t- `src/server/auth/{auth.config.ts, auth.ts, credentials.ts, tokens.ts, email.ts, password-policy.ts, common-passwords.txt}`\n428\t- `src/server/rate-limit.ts`\n429\t- `src/server/services/auth.ts`\n430\t- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`\n431\t- `src/components/PasswordChecklist/{PasswordChecklist.tsx, SetPasswordForm.tsx, index.ts}`\n432\t- `src/app/(auth)/{layout.tsx, login/page.tsx, forgot-password/page.tsx, invite/[token]/page.tsx, reset-password/[token]/page.tsx}`\n433\t- `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`\n434\t- `src/app/api/auth/{[...nextauth], accept-invite, forgot-password, reset-password}/route.ts`\n435\t- `src/app/api/account/password/route.ts`\n436\t- Prisma migration `auth_reconcile`\n437\t\n438\t**Changed:**\n439\t- `prisma/schema.prisma`: 2 indexes\n440\t- `prisma/seed.ts`\n441\t- `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n442\t- `src/server/audit.ts`\n443\t- `src/server/http.ts`: `+getClientIp`\n444\t- `src/server/services/users.ts`\n445\t- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`\n446\t- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`\n447\t- The 41 `requireRole` call-site files: `await` + page variants\n448\t- ESLint config: `no-floating-promises`\n449\t- `package.json`: pin `next-auth` exactly\n450\t\n451\t**Untouched (NFR-9):** `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts`, `navigation.ts` (the\n452\tcomment on line 21 can be updated, but no logic changes).\n453\t\n454\t**Skipped on purpose:**\n455\t- SessionProvider: the shell gets the user as props.\n456\t- Prisma adapter: not needed for JWT sessions.\n457\t- Redis limiter: one process is enough for now.\n458\t- Client-side common-password list.\n459\t- Signed-in redirect away from `/login`: not required by the PRD.\n460\t\n461\t---\n462\t\n463\t## Requirements Traceability\n464\t\n465\t| Req | Design element |\n466\t|---|---|\n467\t| FR-1 | C1: additive migration `auth_reconcile` (2 AuditLog indexes; keep `ip` and ARCHIVED) |\n468\t| FR-2 | C6 `emailField` transform, used by sign-in, forgot and `createUser` (C10) |\n469\t| FR-3 | C13 login page, C2 Credentials provider |\n470\t| FR-4 | C3 `authorizeCredentials` (status/archived/locked checks, bcrypt cost 12) |\n471\t| FR-5 | C3 `AuthError` codes → C13 message mapping |\n472\t| FR-6 | C3 `computeLockout` plus the atomic increment and lock update |\n473\t| FR-7 | C5 `rateLimit('login:ip:…', 10, 5 min)` called from C3 |\n474\t| FR-8 | C6 `safeCallbackUrl`, used in C2's redirect callback and C13 |\n475\t| FR-9 | C3 audit calls (`auth.login.success`, `auth.login.failure`, `auth.lockout`) |\n476\t| FR-10 | C2 JWT session (8 h, `updateAge`) and token/session fields |\n477\t| FR-11 | C2 `jwt` callback: 5-min `passwordChangedAt > authTime` check |\n478\t| FR-12 | C8 `src/middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` |\n479\t| FR-13 | C4 `tokens.ts` (create/verify/consume, SHA-256) |\n480\t| FR-14 | C13 `invite/[token]` page + C4 `verifyToken` (7-day TTL) |\n481\t| FR-15 | C13 `SetPasswordForm` with the read-only name/email |\n482\t| FR-16 | C9 `acceptInvite` + `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` + client `signIn` |\n483\t| FR-17 | C6 `passwordChecks` + C6 server `assertPasswordAllowed` + `common-passwords.txt` |\n484\t| FR-18 | C13 `PasswordChecklist` |\n485\t| FR-19 | C9 `requestPasswordReset` (generic reply; IP 429, silent email limit) |\n486\t| FR-20 | C9 + C4 (`PASSWORD_RESET` 60 min; invalidate old tokens; no row for unknown emails) |\n487\t| FR-21 | C9 `resetPassword` + `/login?reset=1` toast |\n488\t| FR-22 | C9 `sendAuthEmail` → `logger.info` |\n489\t| FR-23 | C9 `changePassword` + `unstable_update({reauth:true})` + C13 security page |\n490\t| FR-24 | C12 user menu \"Account security\" item |\n491\t| FR-25 | C10: keep the existing `createUser` / `setUserStatus` / `unlockUser` |\n492\t| FR-26 | C10 `createInviteToken` |\n493\t| FR-27 | C10 real `sendInvite` body, same return shape |\n494\t| FR-28 | C7 `getCurrentUser` / `requireUser` / `requirePageUser`; PLACEHOLDER_USER removed |\n495\t| FR-29 | C7 async `requireRole` / `requirePageRole`; 50 call sites awaited |\n496\t| FR-30 | C11 `audit({request})` + C5 `getClientIp` |\n497\t| FR-31 | C11 metadata key stripping; C3/C9 pass explicit metadata only |\n498\t| FR-32 | C12 layout passes the session user; shell shows avatar/name/role; `signOut` |\n499\t| FR-33 | C12 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n500\t| FR-34 | C2 `api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` |\n501\t| FR-35 | C14 seed upserts + invited user's link logged |\n502\t| FR-36 | C15 unit/integration/Playwright suites |\n503\t| FR-37 | C8 no sign-up path in `public-routes.ts`; C13 no sign-up link; no sign-up endpoint |\n504\t| NFR-1 | C4 SHA-256 at rest + `timingSafeEqual` |\n505\t| NFR-2 | C2 Auth.js cookie defaults + CSRF; C8 origin check on custom POSTs |\n506\t| NFR-3 | C3 `DUMMY_HASH`, one compare on every path; C9 forgot-password always gives the same reply |\n507\t| NFR-4 | C3 single bcrypt compare, 1 query + ≤2 updates |\n508\t| NFR-5 | C13 aria-live Alert + `shouldFocusError` + server field errors |\n509\t| NFR-6 | C13 / C12 MUI v9 only, looked up through mui-mcp (Dev must confirm it's reachable) |\n510\t| NFR-7 | C7 helpers on every page/handler; C8 is only the first gate; C12 nav filtering is UX only |\n511\t| NFR-8 | C9 thin handlers with `withHandler` / `parseBody` / `ok`; API Surface codes |\n512\t| NFR-9 | Blocker resolutions; C10 reuse; access modules untouched; no renames |\n513\t| NFR-10 | C7 `no-floating-promises`; C15; logger only |\n514\t| NFR-11 | Scope: no admin UI, SSO, MFA or email infrastructure; C5 in-memory limiter |\n515\t| NFR-12 | C1 UTC columns; C3 lockout minutes as a duration; `lastLoginAt` displayed with existing `DateDisplay` in `SchoolSettings.timezone` |\n516\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"579a4bd9-1ad7-4baf-96fe-8a4735bbff00","uuid":"8fcd5403-a8d2-4e5c-9180-29248511645b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:39:28.402Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC, SCH-001)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:02:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (37 FR + 12 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (94% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-01 replaces the `PLACEHOLDER_USER` stand-ins with real authentication:\nAuth.js v5 Credentials sign-in, 8-hour JWT sessions, invite activation,\npassword reset and change, lockout and rate limiting, an edge middleware\ngate, and real session-backed `requireUser()` / `requireRole()`. This is a\nbrownfield change on Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma + MUI v9. **No new\nruntime dependency**: `next-auth` 5 beta and `bcrypt` 6 are already installed.\n\nBrownfield facts re-checked on disk for this design:\n- All User auth columns already exist (`passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`,\n  `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`).\n  `AuthToken.tokenHash` is already `@unique`. The only schema gap is the\n  two AuditLog indexes.\n- `requireRole(` has **50 call sites in 43 files: 33 `route.ts`, 8 pages/layouts,\n  1 in `navigation.ts` (a comment), 1 in `course-access.ts` (a comment)**.\n  None use `await` today, and every caller is already in an async function.\n  `course-access.ts` and `student-access.ts` take an `AccessUser {id, role}`\n  argument and don't call `requireRole`, so they stay untouched (NFR-9).\n- `navigationForRole(role)` already exists in `src/config/navigation.ts`.\n  FR-33 is just about feeding it the real role.\n- `src/server/http.ts` already has `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parseBody`\n  and the codes UNAUTHENTICATED/FORBIDDEN/RATE_LIMITED/CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR.\n- The project uses a `src/` dir, so Next only picks up middleware at\n  **`src/middleware.ts`**, not at the repo root. FR-12's \"middleware.ts\" means that file.\n\n### Intake blockers and how they're resolved\n\n| Blocker | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 schema divergences (`ip` vs `ipAddress`, extra `ARCHIVED`, different indexes) | **Resolved, additive only** (ADR-9). Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED`, keep the existing indexes. Add `@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to AuditLog in one migration, `auth_reconcile`. FR-4's `status !== 'ACTIVE'` check already rejects ARCHIVED. |\n| FR-25 `createUser` / `setUserStatus` signatures differ from PRD | **Resolved: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures.** No second `createUser`. A duplicate email already maps P2002 → CONFLICT through `withHandler`. `createUser` must lower-case the email (FR-2). Dev only verifies this and adds a one-line fix if it's missing. |\n| FR-28/29 `requireRole()` is sync, Auth.js `auth()` is async | **Resolved: go async** (ADR-2). Each of the 50 call sites gets a mechanical `await`. The return shape stays a superset of `{id, role}`. The 8 server pages/layouts switch to the redirecting page variants (Component 7). |\n| NFR-6 mui-mcp must be reachable | **Not blocking at architect time.** The `useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools are registered in this environment. The Dev phase must still confirm it can reach them before writing UI, and must stop and report a blocker if it can't. |\n\n---\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Data model (`prisma/schema.prisma`, migration `auth_reconcile`)\n- Add the two AuditLog indexes only. No renames, no drops, no column changes.\n- `User.email` stays `String @unique`. Lower-casing is enforced in app code\n  at every write and lookup through one zod transform (Component 6). Skip\n  `citext`, because switching the column type isn't additive.\n- _FR-1, FR-2, NFR-9, NFR-12 (columns are already UTC `DateTime`)._\n\n### 2. Auth.js core, split config (ADR-1)\n- **`src/server/auth/auth.config.ts`** (edge-safe, no Prisma or bcrypt imports):\n  - `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8 * 3600, updateAge: 15 * 60 }`\n  - `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, `providers: []`\n  - `callbacks.session`: copies `id, role, firstName, lastName, email` from the token to `session.user`\n  - `callbacks.redirect`: `safeCallbackUrl()` (Component 6)\n  - Cookies use the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and `__Secure-` + Secure in production. Don't override them.\n- **`src/server/auth/auth.ts`** (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })], callbacks: { ...authConfig.callbacks, jwt } })`,\n  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update }`.\n- **`jwt` callback** (Node only; does session revocation, ADR-4):\n  - On `trigger === 'signIn'`: copy the user fields, then set `authTime = now`\n    and `checkedAt = now`.\n  - On `trigger === 'update'` with `{ reauth: true }` (FR-23): set `authTime = now`.\n  - Otherwise, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`: run\n    `select { passwordChangedAt, status, role, firstName, lastName }`.\n    Return `null` if `status !== 'ACTIVE'` or `passwordChangedAt > authTime`.\n    Otherwise refresh `role` and the names, and set `checkedAt = now`.\n  - **Use the custom `authTime` claim, not JWT `iat`.** Auth.js re-signs the\n    token on every `updateAge` refresh, so `iat` moves forward and would\n    hide an older password change.\n- **`src/types/next-auth.d.ts`**: module augmentation for the typed `session.user` and JWT fields.\n- **`src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`**: `export const { GET, POST } = handlers`.\n  Static siblings like `accept-invite/` win over the catch-all in Next's\n  route matching, so they can live side by side.\n- _FR-3, FR-10, FR-11, FR-34, NFR-2._\n\n### 3. Credential verification (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts`)\nA plain exported `authorizeCredentials(input, request)` that `Credentials.authorize`\ndelegates to, so integration tests can call it without going over HTTP (FR-36).\nOrder of checks:\n1. `rateLimit('login:ip:' + getClientIp(request), 10, 5 min)`. Over the limit → throw `AuthError('rate_limited')`.\n2. Parse `{email, password}` with `signInSchema` (trim + lower-case the email).\n3. Look up the user by email.\n4. **Reject missing or ineligible users only after the bcrypt compare.**\n   Compare against the user's hash, or against a module-level `DUMMY_HASH`\n   (cost 12) if the user is missing or has no hash. Every path runs exactly\n   one bcrypt compare (NFR-3, NFR-4).\n5. Branches:\n   - missing user → `invalid`\n   - `status === 'DISABLED'` → `disabled`\n   - `status !== 'ACTIVE'` (INVITED, ARCHIVED) or `archivedAt` set → `invalid`\n   - `lockedUntil > now` → `locked:<minutes>`, where minutes = `ceil((lockedUntil - now) / 60000)`\n   - wrong password → run `registerFailure`, then `invalid` (or `locked:15` if this attempt triggered the lock)\n   - success → set `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lastLoginAt = now`, return the user\n6. Lockout logic is the pure function `computeLockout(currentCount, now)`, which returns\n   `{ failedLoginCount, lockedUntil | null }` (5 failures → lock for 15 min and reset the count to 0).\n   The DB write is one `update` with `failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }`, followed by a\n   conditional lock update when the returned count reaches 5. **Ceiling:** concurrent\n   failures can overshoot the count by one before the lock lands, which doesn't\n   matter here.\n7. Audit entries, passing the request so the IP is recorded:\n   - `auth.login.success`\n   - `auth.login.failure` with `{ email, reason }` only\n   - `auth.lockout`\n   - `actorId` is the user id when the user is known, otherwise null.\n8. `class AuthError extends CredentialsSignin { code }`. The login form reads the\n   error `code` from `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` and maps it to\n   the FR-5 / FR-7 messages. For `locked:N`, it renders \"Try again in N minutes.\"\n   N is a duration, so no timezone conversion is needed (NFR-12).\n- _FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-9, NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-12._\n\n### 4. Token module (`src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, ADR-5)\nThis is the only code that touches the `AuthToken` model.\n- `createToken(userId, type, ttl: { minutes?, days? }, tx?)`:\n  - In one transaction, `updateMany { userId, type, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`,\n    which invalidates older unused tokens (FR-20, FR-26). Then insert the new row.\n  - The raw token is `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`. Only\n    `sha256(raw)` (hex) is stored.\n  - Returns the raw token.\n- `verifyToken(raw, type)`:\n  - Find by `tokenHash`, then confirm with `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers.\n  - Returns `{ token, user }`, or `null` if the token is missing, has the wrong\n    type, is used or is expired.\n- `consumeToken(tokenId, tx?)`: `updateMany { id, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`.\n  Throws `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` if the update count is 0, which makes a\n  double-submit fail cleanly.\n- Pure `hashToken(raw)` is exported so the unit tests can use it.\n- _FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1._\n\n### 5. Rate limiter (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`, ADR-6)\n- `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs, now = Date.now()) → { ok, retryAfterMs }`\n  over a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`. It prunes old timestamps on each call.\n- Exports `__resetRateLimits()` for tests.\n- Add a `ponytail: per-process limiter` comment: it resets on restart and isn't\n  shared across instances. Swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if the app scales\n  horizontally.\n- `getClientIp(request)` goes in the existing **`src/server/http.ts`**. It returns\n  the first `x-forwarded-for` entry, trimmed, or `null`. The limiter and `audit()` share it.\n- _FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-11._\n\n### 6. Validators and pure helpers (`src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, client-safe)\n- `emailField`: `z.string().trim().toLowerCase().email()`.\n- `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `acceptInviteSchema {token, password, confirm}`,\n  `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordSchema {currentPassword, newPassword, confirm}`.\n- `passwordChecks(pw, email)` returns `{ length, letter, digit, notEmail }`. Both the\n  checklist UI and the schema's `superRefine` use it.\n- `safeCallbackUrl(url)`: returns `url` only if it starts with `/` and not with `//`\n  or `/\\`. Otherwise it returns `/dashboard`.\n- **Server-only `src/server/auth/password-policy.ts`**:\n  - Reads `common-passwords.txt` once into a `Set`.\n  - Exports `assertPasswordAllowed(pw, email)`, which runs `passwordChecks` plus\n    the common-list check and throws `VALIDATION_ERROR` with\n    `details.fieldErrors.password` if any rule fails.\n  - Every password-setting service calls it.\n- The 1,000-word list never ships to the client. The checklist shows four rules\n  live, and the \"not a common password\" rule appears only from the server's\n  error response.\n- _FR-2, FR-8, FR-17, FR-18, NFR-8._\n\n### 7. Authorization helpers (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, ADR-2)\nDelete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Every helper goes through one internal resolver:\n```ts\ntype SessionUser = { id; role; firstName; lastName; email }   // superset of AccessUser\ngetCurrentUser = cache(async (): Promise<SessionUser | null> => (await auth())?.user ?? null)\nrequireUser(): Promise<SessionUser>                // throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED\nrequireRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>        // throws UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN\nrequirePageUser(): Promise<SessionUser>            // redirect('/login?callbackUrl=…')\nrequirePageRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>    // redirect('/login…') / redirect('/forbidden')\n```\n- **Route handlers** (33 files) change from `requireRole(` to `await requireRole(`.\n  `withHandler` already maps a thrown `AppError` to the 401/403 envelope.\n- **Server pages/layouts** (8 files) change to `await requirePageRole(` because a\n  thrown AppError in a page would render `error.tsx`, not a redirect.\n  `redirect()` throws `NEXT_REDIRECT` and must never run inside `withHandler`,\n  since it would be caught there and turned into an INTERNAL error. That's why\n  the page variants are separate exports instead of a flag.\n- The page variants read the current path from the `x-pathname` request header,\n  which `src/middleware.ts` sets, to build `callbackUrl`. If the header is\n  missing, they fall back to `/dashboard`.\n- **Guardrail for missed awaits:** turn on `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises`\n  for `src/**`. Typecheck alone misses a bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statement.\n- No `permissions.ts`, no `can()`.\n- _FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9, NFR-10._\n\n### 8. Edge middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) and `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n- `public-routes.ts` exports `PUBLIC_PAGE_PATHS = ['/', '/login', '/forgot-password', '/invite/', '/reset-password/']`\n  (a trailing `/` means prefix match) and\n  `PUBLIC_API_PATHS = ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`.\n  `/api/auth/` covers the Auth.js catch-all and the three unauthenticated POSTs.\n  The list has **no sign-up path** (FR-37).\n- `export default NextAuth(authConfig).auth(req => …)` runs these steps in order:\n  1. **CSRF origin check (NFR-2):** for any non-GET/HEAD `/api/*` request that\n     isn't under `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`'s own endpoints, if `Origin` is present\n     and doesn't equal the app origin, return 403 FORBIDDEN in the JSON envelope.\n     Auth.js CSRF tokens only protect Auth.js's own endpoints. Custom POSTs rely\n     on this check plus SameSite=Lax.\n  2. If the path is public → `next()`.\n  3. If there's no session: `/api/*` → 401 `{error:{code:'UNAUTHENTICATED',…}}`.\n     Pages → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=<path+search>`.\n  4. Otherwise → `next()` and set the `x-pathname` request header.\n- `matcher` excludes `_next/static`, `_next/image`, `favicon.ico` and files\n  with extensions.\n- Middleware only decodes the JWT. It doesn't check revocation, because the\n  Node `jwt` callback does that. NFR-7's real guard is the server-side helper\n  on every page and handler.\n- _FR-12, FR-37, NFR-2, NFR-7, NFR-8._\n\n### 9. Auth services (`src/server/services/auth.ts`, Node)\nRoute handlers stay thin: zod parse → service → `ok()`. Every service below\nrecords an audit entry with the request so the IP is captured.\n- `acceptInvite({token, password}, request)`:\n  1. `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')`, or throw `INVALID_TOKEN`.\n  2. `assertPasswordAllowed(password, user.email)`.\n  3. `bcrypt.hash(password, 12)`.\n  4. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `status = ACTIVE` and\n     `passwordChangedAt = now`, then `consumeToken`.\n  5. Audit `auth.invite.accepted`.\n  6. Return `{ email }`. **The client then calls `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo: '/dashboard'})`.**\n     Minting an Auth.js session by hand in a custom route is fragile, so the\n     design reuses the one sign-in path.\n- `requestPasswordReset({email}, request)`:\n  - `rateLimit('forgot:ip:'+ip, 10, 1h)`. Over the limit → `RATE_LIMITED` 429.\n    An IP-level response doesn't reveal whether an account exists.\n  - `rateLimit('forgot:email:'+email, 3, 1h)`. Over the limit → **return the\n    generic success message silently**. A 429 here would reveal that the email\n    was tried before.\n  - If the user exists and is ACTIVE: `createToken(id, 'PASSWORD_RESET', {minutes: 60})`,\n    then `sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link)`.\n  - Unknown or inactive email: no DB write.\n  - Always return `{ message: \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" }`.\n- `resetPassword({token, password}, request)`:\n  1. `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`.\n  2. Policy check, then hash.\n  3. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `passwordChangedAt = now`,\n     `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lockedUntil = null`, then `consumeToken`.\n  4. Audit `auth.password.reset`.\n- `changePassword(user, {currentPassword, newPassword}, request)`:\n  1. bcrypt-compare `currentPassword`. If it's wrong → throw `VALIDATION_ERROR`\n     with `details.fieldErrors.currentPassword = ['Current password is incorrect.']`.\n  2. Policy check, hash, and update `passwordHash` and `passwordChangedAt`.\n  3. Audit `auth.password.changed`.\n  4. The route handler then calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this\n     session's `authTime` moves past `passwordChangedAt`. Other sessions fail\n     the FR-11 check within 5 minutes.\n- **`src/server/auth/email.ts`** `sendAuthEmail(user, kind: 'invite' | 'password-reset', link)`:\n  - Logs `{ to, subject, link }` with `logger.info`. This is the single seam\n    PRD-04 replaces with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\n  - Links are built from `env.AUTH_URL`: `/invite/<raw>` and `/reset-password/<raw>`.\n  - Raw tokens appear only in this log line and in the email itself, never in\n    audit metadata.\n- _FR-16, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, FR-31, NFR-3, NFR-8._\n\n### 10. Users service additions (`src/server/services/users.ts`)\n- Keep `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` as they are (FR-25).\n- Add `createInviteToken(userId)`, which returns `createToken(userId, 'INVITE', { days: 7 })`.\n  `tokens.createToken` already invalidates older unused tokens.\n- Replace the no-op body of `sendInvite(userId)` with: `createInviteToken`, then\n  `sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link)`, then return the unchanged\n  `{ id, inviteSentAt }` shape.\n- _FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-2._\n\n### 11. Audit (`src/server/audit.ts`)\n- Add an optional `request?: Request` to the input. Set `ip: request ? getClientIp(request) : null`.\n- The function stays inside its existing try/catch and never throws.\n- Defence in depth: before the insert, strip these metadata keys:\n  `password`, `passwordHash`, `newPassword`, `currentPassword`, `token`, `rawToken`.\n- _FR-9, FR-30, FR-31._\n\n### 12. App shell and navigation\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`:\n  - `const user = await requirePageUser()`.\n  - Pass `user` (id, name, role, email) and `navigationForRole(user.role)` to `<AppShell>`.\n    Props avoid a `SessionProvider` round-trip and the flash of empty UI it causes.\n  - Filtering the nav doesn't protect anything on its own (NFR-7).\n- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`:\n  - Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and render the user from props: `UserAvatar`\n    (initials), name, and a role `Chip`.\n  - The user menu gains **\"Account security\" → `/account/security`**.\n  - Sign out calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n    That function doesn't need a provider.\n- _FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-6, NFR-7._\n\n### 13. Auth UI (MUI v9 only, every component looked up through mui-mcp first, NFR-6)\n- **`src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`**: a centred `Container` + `Card` layout without the AppShell.\n- **`login/page.tsx`**:\n  - Uses the MUI Sign-in template patterns: TextField, an InputAdornment + IconButton\n    show-password toggle, and an Alert for form errors.\n  - Client submit calls `signIn('credentials', {redirect: false})`, maps the error\n    code to the FR-5 / FR-7 copy, and on success navigates to\n    `safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)`.\n  - If the page loads with `?reset=1`, it fires the `useToast` success toast for FR-21.\n  - Links to `/forgot-password`. **No sign-up link** (FR-37).\n- **`forgot-password/page.tsx`**: an email field. It shows the generic message on 200\n  and the FR-7-style message on 429.\n- **`invite/[token]/page.tsx`**:\n  - A server component calls `verifyToken`. If the token is invalid, it shows the\n    FR-14 Alert copy.\n  - Otherwise it renders `<SetPasswordForm>` with the read-only name and email.\n- **`reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`**: verifies the token the same way, then shows\n  `<SetPasswordForm>`. On success it redirects to `/login?reset=1`.\n- **`(app)/account/security/page.tsx`**:\n  - Calls `requirePageUser()`.\n  - The form has current, new and confirm password fields. On success it shows the\n    \"Password updated\" toast. A field error renders on `currentPassword`.\n- **Shared pieces** (in `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`):\n  - **`PasswordChecklist`**: an MUI `List` with CheckCircle/RadioButtonUnchecked icons,\n    driven by `passwordChecks`.\n  - **`SetPasswordForm`**: password, confirm and the checklist. The invite and reset\n    pages share it.\n- **Form accessibility, applied to all 5 forms (NFR-5):**\n  - Form-level `Alert` sits inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`.\n  - react-hook-form + `zodResolver` with `shouldFocusError: true`, so focus moves to\n    the first invalid field.\n  - Server `details.fieldErrors` are mapped to `setError`.\n- _FR-3, FR-5, FR-14, FR-15, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-23, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6._\n\n### 14. Seed (`prisma/seed.ts`)\n- Upsert by email, so re-running the seed is safe:\n  - `admin@`, `teacher@`, `teacher2@`, `student@`, `student2@` and `parent@schoolhub.test`\n  - All ACTIVE, with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` as the password\n- Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` as INVITED, then call `createInviteToken` and\n  log the link with `logger.info`.\n- `office@` stays as it is.\n- _FR-35, FR-13 (all seeded tokens go through tokens.ts)._\n\n### 15. Tests (Vitest + Playwright, ADR-10)\n- **Unit tests:**\n  - `passwordChecks` / `assertPasswordAllowed`\n  - `hashToken` and the verify expiry/used branches\n  - `computeLockout`\n  - `rateLimit`, with an injected `now`\n  - `safeCallbackUrl`\n- **Integration tests** (against the test DB):\n  - Every `authorizeCredentials` branch\n  - `acceptInvite`, `resetPassword` and `changePassword`\n  - Audit metadata never contains secrets\n- **Playwright:**\n  - Sign-in/out with seeded users\n  - The failed-login message\n  - Forgot → reset. The test reads the token by creating one through\n    `createToken` in a test helper, because the raw token isn't recoverable\n    from the DB.\n  - `@axe-core/playwright` on the auth pages\n- Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. Use `logger` only.\n- _FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10._\n\n---\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Sign-in (FR-3–FR-10)**\n1. The browser posts to `/login` → `signIn('credentials')` →\n   `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials`, protected by the Auth.js CSRF token.\n2. `authorize` → `authorizeCredentials`: rate limit, user lookup, one bcrypt\n   compare, then the lockout/branch logic and audit.\n3. The `jwt` callback (`trigger='signIn'`) writes `{id, role, names, email, authTime, checkedAt}`.\n   The session cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax.\n4. The client receives `ok` → `router.push(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))`.\n   On error, the code maps to a message rendered in the aria-live Alert.\n\n**Authenticated request (FR-11, FR-12, FR-28, FR-29)**\n1. `src/middleware.ts` decodes the JWT on the edge.\n   - No session on a page → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`.\n   - No session on `/api` → 401.\n2. The page or handler calls `await requireRole(...)` → `getCurrentUser()`\n   (React `cache`) → `auth()` (Node).\n3. The `jwt` callback re-checks `passwordChangedAt` / `status` at most every 5 minutes.\n   If the check fails, the session becomes null → UNAUTHENTICATED, or a redirect to `/login`.\n4. The role check fails → FORBIDDEN 403 (API) or `/forbidden` (page).\n\n**Invite (FR-13–FR-16, FR-26, FR-27)**\n1. PRD-03 admin `sendInvite(userId)` → `createInviteToken` → `tokens.createToken`\n   (invalidates older tokens, stores the hash) → `sendAuthEmail` (logs the link).\n2. The user opens `/invite/<raw>`. The server component runs `verifyToken`\n   (hash lookup + timingSafeEqual) and renders the form or the invalid Alert.\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → middleware origin check → `acceptInvite`.\n   In one transaction it sets ACTIVE and the hash, then consumes the token, and audits.\n4. On 200, the client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`.\n\n**Forgot / reset (FR-19–FR-22)**\n1. `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → IP limit (429) → email limit (silent) →\n   ACTIVE user? `createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min)` + `sendAuthEmail`.\n   The response is always the generic message.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `POST /api/auth/reset-password`, which sets the hash\n   and `passwordChangedAt`, clears the lockout and consumes the token. Then it\n   audits and the browser goes to `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n\n**Change password (FR-23)**\n1. `/account/security` → `POST /api/account/password` → `await requireUser()` → `changePassword`.\n2. The handler calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this session gets a\n   new `authTime`. Other devices fail the next 5-minute check.\n3. The toast reads \"Password updated\".\n\n---\n\n## API Surface (for `arch-api-contracts`)\n\n| Method | Path | Auth | Handler → service | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| GET/POST | `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` | public (Auth.js protocol) | `handlers` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-34, NFR-2 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/accept-invite` | public + origin check | `acceptInvite` | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-1, NFR-8 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/forgot-password` | public + origin check | `requestPasswordReset` | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-3 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/reset-password` | public + origin check | `resetPassword` | FR-21, FR-17 |\n| POST | `/api/account/password` | `requireUser()` | `changePassword` | FR-23, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n\nAll custom routes use `withHandler`, `parseBody(schema)` and `ok()`, returning the\n`{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` envelopes. Codes:\n- `VALIDATION_ERROR` 400: policy failures and wrong current password, with `details.fieldErrors`\n- `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401\n- `FORBIDDEN` 403\n- `INVALID_TOKEN` 410: invalid, used or expired invite/reset tokens\n- `RATE_LIMITED` 429\n\n`/api/health` stays public and is unchanged. There's no sign-up endpoint (FR-37).\n\n## New / changed files\n\n**New:**\n- `src/middleware.ts`\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n- `src/types/next-auth.d.ts`\n- `src/server/auth/{auth.config.ts, auth.ts, credentials.ts, tokens.ts, email.ts, password-policy.ts, common-passwords.txt}`\n- `src/server/rate-limit.ts`\n- `src/server/services/auth.ts`\n- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`\n- `src/components/PasswordChecklist/{PasswordChecklist.tsx, SetPasswordForm.tsx, index.ts}`\n- `src/app/(auth)/{layout.tsx, login/page.tsx, forgot-password/page.tsx, invite/[token]/page.tsx, reset-password/[token]/page.tsx}`\n- `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`\n- `src/app/api/auth/{[...nextauth], accept-invite, forgot-password, reset-password}/route.ts`\n- `src/app/api/account/password/route.ts`\n- Prisma migration `auth_reconcile`\n\n**Changed:**\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: 2 indexes\n- `prisma/seed.ts`\n- `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n- `src/server/audit.ts`\n- `src/server/http.ts`: `+getClientIp`\n- `src/server/services/users.ts`\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`\n- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`\n- The 41 `requireRole` call-site files: `await` + page variants\n- ESLint config: `no-floating-promises`\n- `package.json`: pin `next-auth` exactly\n\n**Untouched (NFR-9):** `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts`, `navigation.ts` (the\ncomment on line 21 can be updated, but no logic changes).\n\n**Skipped on purpose:**\n- SessionProvider: the shell gets the user as props.\n- Prisma adapter: not needed for JWT sessions.\n- Redis limiter: one process is enough for now.\n- Client-side common-password list.\n- Signed-in redirect away from `/login`: not required by the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | C1: additive migration `auth_reconcile` (2 AuditLog indexes; keep `ip` and ARCHIVED) |\n| FR-2 | C6 `emailField` transform, used by sign-in, forgot and `createUser` (C10) |\n| FR-3 | C13 login page, C2 Credentials provider |\n| FR-4 | C3 `authorizeCredentials` (status/archived/locked checks, bcrypt cost 12) |\n| FR-5 | C3 `AuthError` codes → C13 message mapping |\n| FR-6 | C3 `computeLockout` plus the atomic increment and lock update |\n| FR-7 | C5 `rateLimit('login:ip:…', 10, 5 min)` called from C3 |\n| FR-8 | C6 `safeCallbackUrl`, used in C2's redirect callback and C13 |\n| FR-9 | C3 audit calls (`auth.login.success`, `auth.login.failure`, `auth.lockout`) |\n| FR-10 | C2 JWT session (8 h, `updateAge`) and token/session fields |\n| FR-11 | C2 `jwt` callback: 5-min `passwordChangedAt > authTime` check |\n| FR-12 | C8 `src/middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `tokens.ts` (create/verify/consume, SHA-256) |\n| FR-14 | C13 `invite/[token]` page + C4 `verifyToken` (7-day TTL) |\n| FR-15 | C13 `SetPasswordForm` with the read-only name/email |\n| FR-16 | C9 `acceptInvite` + `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` + client `signIn` |\n| FR-17 | C6 `passwordChecks` + C6 server `assertPasswordAllowed` + `common-passwords.txt` |\n| FR-18 | C13 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-19 | C9 `requestPasswordReset` (generic reply; IP 429, silent email limit) |\n| FR-20 | C9 + C4 (`PASSWORD_RESET` 60 min; invalidate old tokens; no row for unknown emails) |\n| FR-21 | C9 `resetPassword` + `/login?reset=1` toast |\n| FR-22 | C9 `sendAuthEmail` → `logger.info` |\n| FR-23 | C9 `changePassword` + `unstable_update({reauth:true})` + C13 security page |\n| FR-24 | C12 user menu \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-25 | C10: keep the existing `createUser` / `setUserStatus` / `unlockUser` |\n| FR-26 | C10 `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-27 | C10 real `sendInvite` body, same return shape |\n| FR-28 | C7 `getCurrentUser` / `requireUser` / `requirePageUser`; PLACEHOLDER_USER removed |\n| FR-29 | C7 async `requireRole` / `requirePageRole`; 50 call sites awaited |\n| FR-30 | C11 `audit({request})` + C5 `getClientIp` |\n| FR-31 | C11 metadata key stripping; C3/C9 pass explicit metadata only |\n| FR-32 | C12 layout passes the session user; shell shows avatar/name/role; `signOut` |\n| FR-33 | C12 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-34 | C2 `api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` |\n| FR-35 | C14 seed upserts + invited user's link logged |\n| FR-36 | C15 unit/integration/Playwright suites |\n| FR-37 | C8 no sign-up path in `public-routes.ts`; C13 no sign-up link; no sign-up endpoint |\n| NFR-1 | C4 SHA-256 at rest + `timingSafeEqual` |\n| NFR-2 | C2 Auth.js cookie defaults + CSRF; C8 origin check on custom POSTs |\n| NFR-3 | C3 `DUMMY_HASH`, one compare on every path; C9 forgot-password always gives the same reply |\n| NFR-4 | C3 single bcrypt compare, 1 query + ≤2 updates |\n| NFR-5 | C13 aria-live Alert + `shouldFocusError` + server field errors |\n| NFR-6 | C13 / C12 MUI v9 only, looked up through mui-mcp (Dev must confirm it's reachable) |\n| NFR-7 | C7 helpers on every page/handler; C8 is only the first gate; C12 nav filtering is UX only |\n| NFR-8 | C9 thin handlers with `withHandler` / `parseBody` / `ok`; API Surface codes |\n| NFR-9 | Blocker resolutions; C10 reuse; access modules untouched; no renames |\n| NFR-10 | C7 `no-floating-promises`; C15; logger only |\n| NFR-11 | Scope: no admin UI, SSO, MFA or email infrastructure; C5 in-memory limiter |\n| NFR-12 | C1 UTC columns; C3 lockout minutes as a duration; `lastLoginAt` displayed with existing `DateDisplay` in `SchoolSettings.timezone` |\n","numLines":516,"startLine":1,"totalLines":516}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DzNtjHFPoibUKze9i4DUnB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
