{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTokMGvNBHtvgVyGvqu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I finished the `arch-api-contracts` sub-task for SH-4, which completes the architect phase. Both JSON files parse, and every FR/NFR id they cite exists in `requirements.json`.\n\nThe two files I had to write already existed on disk, but they were left over from another ticket (`abcd-1`), so I overwrote them:\n\n- **`artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json`** defines 11 endpoints across 9 route files:\n  - 5 notification endpoints for signed-in users: list, unread count, read-all, and mark one read or unread.\n  - 2 preference endpoints (GET and PUT on `/api/me/notification-preferences`).\n  - 3 admin-only endpoints: email log, retry a failed email, and send a test notification.\n  - 1 internal endpoint, `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`, protected only by the `CRON_SECRET` bearer token.\n\n  All paths stay under `/api` with no `/v1` prefix, because the existing app uses that convention and NFR-13 forbids renaming routes. They reuse the response and error shapes the app already has, with no new error codes. The file also describes the main data shapes and the function signatures of `notify`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `dispatchEmails` and `sendAuthEmail`.\n- **`artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json`** was written last, after the contracts. It has `status: complete` and `endpointCount: 11`. It carries forward one item that doesn't block dev-planning: dev must confirm the mui-mcp server is reachable before writing any UI (NFR-10).\n\nTwo things need attention before dev-planning runs:\n\n- **Cron calls will be rejected unless the middleware changes.** The middleware returns 401 to any `/api/*` request without a session. `/api/internal/` must be added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` so the cron job can reach the dispatch endpoint. The system design already lists this change, and the handoff repeats it.\n- **Other old files are still on disk.** Everything in `artifacts/dev-planning/` and `artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json` also belongs to `abcd-1`. I left them alone because they belong to other tasks. Dev-planning needs to regenerate its files for SH-4 rather than reuse them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332,"cache_read_input_tokens":63032,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":332},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"346b8f8b-0fbc-4ed8-97c5-558f3d48dba1","uuid":"3ff01c81-78a8-4838-98c3-d615990b2ace","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:05:18.167Z","request_id":"req_011CghTok78exJNwajMk8JoN"}
