{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKtvQihfJ2Svz1nfE3x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the API contracts for SH-1, then the handoff to dev-planning, which completes the architect phase. The contracts file is valid JSON and every requirement id it cites exists in the intake requirements.\n\n**API contracts** (`artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json`): this ticket adds no new endpoints, so the 7 contracts describe existing routes that the new pages and tests call:\n- **Four app routes:** `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- **Three sign-in library routes:** `callback/credentials`, `csrf` and `signout`.\n\nAll paths stay under `/api` with no `/v1` prefix, because the requirements forbid renaming existing routes.\n\n**Corrections to `system-design.md`**, found by reading the code (also listed in the contracts file):\n- **Field name:** the confirm-password field is `confirm`, not `confirmPassword`.\n- **Status code:** an invalid or expired link (`INVALID_TOKEN`) returns HTTP 410, not 400.\n- **Change-password errors:** if someone picks a common password on `/api/account/password`, the error comes back under `fieldErrors.password`, not `newPassword`. Unless the change-password form remaps it, the error is never shown. The fix belongs in that form, not the server, because existing server code must not change.\n\n**Handoff** (`handoff-to-dev-planning.json`): it reports 7 endpoints and status complete. It carries forward two blockers:\n- **MUI docs server:** dev must reach the MUI docs server before writing any UI, and stop and report if it can't.\n- **`AuditLog.ip`:** keeping the existing `ip` column instead of renaming it to `ipAddress` needs your sign-off.\n\n**Stale files:** the contracts and handoff files already on disk were from ticket SH-6, and I replaced them. These are also still from SH-6, and I left them alone because they belong to 