5 10:37 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff   352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  6738 Nov  5 10:37 ui-verification-report.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  4649 Nov  5 10:37 ui-verification-report.md\n# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z; 34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%),\n`handoff-to-architect.json` (5 blockers), `tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-5) and\n`requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B14). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the earlier SH-1 design (11:41). That version planned the seed users, the role/status\n> migration and `/login` as new work. All three are now on disk, so they have been removed from scope.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL, Auth.js v5\nCredentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The whole PRD-01 backend already exists: models, `tokens.ts`, `credentials.ts`\n(lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`), the JWT session with its 5-minute `passwordChangedAt` recheck, middleware, the rate\nlimiter, audit, validators, services, all five API routes, `/login`, the seed and the `[role, status]` index.\n\n**This ticket covers UI gaps, shell wiring and tests.** It adds 4 pages and 3 small client forms, rewires the\n`(app)` layout and shell, and adds tests. It adds **no API endpoint, service, model, migration or dependency**\n(ADR-1, ADR-5, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: design only the gaps. | §2.1 lists the existing modules as **reuse, do not modify**. New work is C1–C9 only. |\n| 2 | GAPS: 3 `(auth)` pages, `/account/security`, removing `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wiring the user, badge, initials, signOut and menu item, plus integration and e2e tests. | C1–C9. |\n| 3 | REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl, the existing API routes. | Every new component below is built from these. It also reuses `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors` (B2). |\n| 4 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip` and the existing indexes. No migration. **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 5 | **NFR-6:** dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. | **Hard gate.** Before writing JSX, dev looks up every MUI component named in §2 with `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0). If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports it; no guessing. mui-mcp was connected when this design was written. |\n\n### Additional risks found during design\n\n- **R1 (B14):** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` calls `page.goto('/dashboard')` without signing in. Once the\n  `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` (C6), that spec has to sign in first. `notifications.spec.ts`\n  already has a local `signIn(page)` helper. C9 moves it into a shared helper, and both specs use that.\n- **R2 (B5):** an invalid token returns `410 INVALID_TOKEN`, which is not in the NFR-10 code list. This is kept\n  as-is (NFR-13). The token forms treat a 410 as \"link invalid\" and switch to that state.\n- **R3:** intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date. `loginErrorMessage` already maps `rate_limited` (B7).\n  Dev verifies this and builds nothing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma`, migrations, `prisma/seed.ts` | Models, enums, `[role,status]` index, 6 ACTIVE + 1 INVITED seed user | FR-1, FR-28–FR-30, FR-32, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/auth/{auth,auth.config,credentials,tokens,requireRole}.ts` | Auth.js, authorize/lockout/dummy hash, JWT 8h + recheck, token hashing, `getCurrentUser`/`requireUser`/`requireRole`/`requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`, `SessionUser` | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8–FR-10, FR-12, FR-23, NFR-1–NFR-3 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`, 401 JSON; the `(auth)` paths are already public | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/{rate-limit,audit}.ts`, `src/server/services/{auth,users}.ts`, `src/server/auth/email.ts` | Limiter, `audit()`, `acceptInvite`/`requestPasswordReset`/`resetPassword`/`changePassword`, user services, `sendAuthEmail` → EmailOutbox | FR-6, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-22, FR-24, FR-31, NFR-8 |\n| `src/app/api/auth/**`, `src/app/api/account/password` | The 5 routes (see `api-contracts.json`) | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**` | Centred Card shell; login page with the `?reset=1` toast | FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19 |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist` | `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit})`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot`, `ApiFailure` | FR-16, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/components/FormField` (`TextFormField`), `src/components/Toast/useToast`, `src/components/UserAvatar` | RHF text field, Snackbar+Alert toast, initials avatar | FR-17, FR-20, FR-26, NFR-6 |\n\nDo not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n\n### 2.2 New and modified components\n\n| Id | File | Kind | What it does | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **C1** | `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + `ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | RHF with `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField` for email. Submits with `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email})`. A 2xx shows a success `Alert` with `data.message` (the server's `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`, so the copy is never retyped). A 429 shows an error `Alert` with \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" Known and unknown emails always get the same success copy, so the page reveals nothing about which accounts exist. Includes a \"Back to sign in\" link. | FR-17, FR-18, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| **C2** | `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" and a link to `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `TokenPasswordForm` (C4) with `mode=\"reset\"` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-19, NFR-1 |\n| **C3** | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" Otherwise render C4 with `mode=\"invite\"`, `name = firstName + ' ' + lastName` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-13, NFR-1 |\n| **C4** | `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx` | Client form (shared by C2 and C3) | Wraps `SetPasswordForm` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, `PasswordChecklist`). `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/{accept-invite\\|reset-password}', {token, password, confirmPassword})`. On **410** it switches to the page's invalid-link `Alert` (R2). Any other failure is returned so `SetPasswordForm` can call `applyFieldErrors`. **Invite success:** `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false})`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. **Reset success:** `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`, and the existing LoginForm toast fires. The raw token is only ever a prop; it is never logged. | FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n| **C5** | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | The page calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `email`. The form uses RHF with `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`: three password `TextField`s with `passwordInputSlot`, a `PasswordChecklist` under the new password, and an `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"`. It submits with `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A 400 with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors`, which shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows the `useToast` toast \"Password updated\", resets the form and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already re-issues the session (`unstable_update({reauth:true})`), and other devices drop off within 5 minutes through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck. | FR-10, FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n| **C6** | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (modify) | Server layout | Adds `const user = await requirePageUser()`, a second guard behind the middleware. Passes `user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}}` to `AppShell`. This prop is the **only** source of the current user. There is no `SessionProvider` or `useSession` (ADR-2). | FR-23, FR-25, NFR-9 |\n| **C7** | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (modify) | Client shell | Deletes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and adds `user: SessionUser` to `AppShellProps` (imported as `import type`). Uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`. The top bar shows `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials), the full name in `Typography` and the role in a `Chip`. The menu items are **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"`) and **\"Sign out\"** (`signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`). Any other existing menu items that are placeholders and only close the menu get one of these two actions. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27 |\n| **C8** | `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` | Vitest, node env | `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. Resets the limiter in `beforeEach`. **authorize:** unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked → `locked:N`, 5th failure locks and writes `auth.lockout`, rate limited, success resets the count and sets `lastLoginAt` and `auth.login.success`. **acceptInvite:** ACTIVE status, `passwordChangedAt` set, token consumed, reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`. **reset:** a known email creates a token and an EmailOutbox row; an unknown email creates no token; reset clears the lockout fields and the token can't be reused. **changePassword:** a wrong current password returns a field error; success bumps `passwordChangedAt`. Also asserts that no audit metadata contains `password` or `token`. One file, so there is no extra fixture plumbing. | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-34, NFR-8 |\n| **C9** | `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` + `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`; modify `dashboard.spec.ts` and `notifications.spec.ts` | Playwright | The helper `signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!')` is moved out of `notifications.spec.ts`. **`auth.spec.ts`** (serial): admin signs in, the user menu shows \"Alice Admin\" and ADMIN, signs out and lands on `/login`. A wrong password shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" An unauthenticated `/dashboard` goes to `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`. Forgot → reset for `student2@`: the test reads the newest EmailOutbox row via `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only app route), opens the link, sets a new password, sees the `/login` toast and signs in with it. One `AxeBuilder` scan of `/login` and `/forgot-password`. `dashboard.spec.ts` signs in first (R1). | FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13 |\n\n**MUI components used** (all need an NFR-6 lookup first): `Box`, `Stack`, `Typography`, `TextField`, `Button`,\n`Alert`, `Link` (MUI, `component={NextLink}`), `Chip`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `ListItemIcon`, `InputAdornment` and\n`IconButton` (via `passwordInputSlot`), plus `@mui/icons-material` `LockOutlined`/`Logout`. No banned libraries (NFR-7).\nCopy is English only, on stock MUI (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n**Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n```\n/forgot-password (C1) ──POST /api/auth/forgot-password──► requestPasswordReset ──► createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60m)\n       ◄── 200 {data:{message}} or 429 ─────────────────            └─► sendAuthEmail ──► EmailOutbox\nlink ► /reset-password/[t] (C2, server) ──verifyToken──► null? invalid Alert : C4(email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/reset-password──► resetPassword (hash, passwordChangedAt, clear lockout, consume, audit)\n       ◄── 200 → router.replace('/login?reset=1') → LoginForm toast   │ 410 → invalid-link state\n```\n\n**Invite (FR-13, FR-14)**\n```\n/invite/[t] (C3, server) ──verifyToken(INVITE)──► null? FR-13 Alert : C4(name, email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/accept-invite──► acceptInvite (ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt, consume, audit) ── 200 {email}\nC4 ──signIn('credentials', {email,password,redirect:false})──► /api/auth/callback ──► router.replace('/dashboard')\n```\n\n**Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n```\n/account/security (C5; requirePageUser) ──POST /api/account/password──► requireUser → changePassword\n   ──► passwordChangedAt=now ──► unstable_update({reauth}) keeps this session; other JWTs fail recheck ≤5 min\n   ◄── 200 → toast \"Password updated\" │ 400 fieldErrors.currentPassword → field error\n```\n\n**Current user (FR-25–FR-27)**\n```\nrequest ─► middleware (FR-11) ─► (app)/layout.tsx: requirePageUser() ─► <AppShell user> ─► navigationForRole(user.role),\n           avatar/name/Chip, menu: Account security → /account/security, Sign out → signOut({redirectTo:'/login'})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Key Patterns and Decisions\n\n1. **Verify on the server, mutate through the API.** The token pages call `verifyToken` (a read-only call) in a Server\n   Component, so an expired link never renders a form. Mutations go through the existing thin routes (NFR-10).\n   Only `tokens.ts` touches token hashes (FR-12, NFR-1).\n2. **One user source.** The layout passes the user to the shell as a prop. The design adds no session context\n   (FR-25, ADR-2).\n3. **Shared schemas.** Client forms use the same `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas as the routes (NFR-11).\n   Server field errors come back through `applyFieldErrors`.\n4. **Accessibility comes from reuse.** Every form has one `aria-live=\"polite\"` `Alert`, RHF `shouldFocusError`\n   and `helperText` (NFR-5). `SetPasswordForm` already does this, and C1 and C5 copy the same pattern.\n5. **Server-side enforcement.** `/account/security` and the whole `(app)` group call `requirePageUser`. The\n   API calls `requireUser`. Hiding a menu item is never the only protection (NFR-9).\n6. **Logging.** New code uses `logger` only and never logs tokens or passwords (NFR-8, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 schema (unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 `/login` (verify only); C9 e2e |\n| FR-3 | §2.1 `credentials.ts`; C8 |\n| FR-4 | §2.1 `loginErrorMessage`; C9 wrong-password test |\n| FR-5 | §2.1 `computeLockout`; C8 |\n| FR-6 | §2.1 limiter + `loginErrorMessage` (R3, verify); C8 rate-limit case |\n| FR-7 | §2.1 `safeCallbackUrl`; C9 callbackUrl test |\n| FR-8 | §2.1 authorize audit; C8 AuditLog asserts |\n| FR-9 | §2.1 `auth.config.ts` (unchanged); C6 passes the session fields |\n| FR-10 | §2.1 recheck; C5 flow; C8 changePassword |\n| FR-11 | §2.1 middleware; C9 unauthenticated redirect |\n| FR-12 | C2, C3 use `verifyToken` only |\n| FR-13 | C3 |\n| FR-14 | C4 invite branch; C8 acceptInvite |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 validators; C4/C5 `applyFieldErrors` |\n| FR-16 | C4 (via `SetPasswordForm`), C5 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-17 | C1 |\n| FR-18 | §2.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C8 |\n| FR-19 | C2, C4 reset branch; C8; C9 forgot→reset |\n| FR-20 | C5; C8 |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-22 | §2.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only) |\n| FR-23 | §2.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §2.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6, C7 (delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`) |\n| FR-26 | C7 avatar/name/Chip/Sign out; C9 sign-out test |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28, FR-29, FR-30 | §2.1 seed (unchanged); C9 uses the seed users |\n| FR-31 | §2.1 `email.ts` (unchanged); C9 reads EmailOutbox |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 4: keep `ip` |\n| FR-33 | §2.1 migration (present) |\n| FR-34 | C8, C9 |\n| NFR-1 | C2, C3 via `tokens.ts`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | Auth.js defaults; C4 uses `next-auth/react` `signIn` (CSRF) |\n| NFR-3 | §2.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | Unchanged authorize path (one bcrypt-12 compare) |\n| NFR-5 | C1, C4, C5 (§4.4); C9 axe scan |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 5; §2.2 MUI list |\n| NFR-7 | §2.2 MUI-only; no new dependency (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-8 | C4 token prop only; C8 metadata assert; §4.6 |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6; §4.5 |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 existing routes; R2 |\n| NFR-11 | C1, C4, C5; §4.3 |\n| NFR-12 | §4.6 |\n| NFR-13 | §2.1 do-not-modify list; R1; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | §2.1 public routes have no sign-up; no sign-up page is added |\n| NFR-15 | §2.2 English copy, stock MUI |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Change Footprint\n\n- **New:** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/{page,ForgotPasswordForm}.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(app)/account/security/{page,ChangePasswordForm}.tsx`, `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`,\n  `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- **Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`.\n- **Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `package.json`.\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T16:26:09Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-1 and the PRD header says SCH-001. All artifacts use SH-1.\",\n    \"Re-run of intake on 2026-11-05. The workspace was re-checked, and some gaps reported by the earlier SH-1 intake have since been closed.\",\n    \"ALREADY IMPLEMENTED (do not rebuild): the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums and the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models; src/server/auth/tokens.ts; credentials.ts (authorize, DUMMY_HASH, lockout); auth.ts/auth.config.ts (JWT 8h, 5-min passwordChangedAt recheck, signOut export); src/middleware.ts + src/config/public-routes.ts; src/server/rate-limit.ts; src/server/audit.ts; src/lib/validators/auth.ts (policy, safeCallbackUrl, signInSchema); common-passwords.txt; services/auth.ts; services/users.ts (createUser, createInviteToken, real sendInvite → sendAuthEmail); every API route in the Pages & Routes table.\",\n    \"requireRole.ts already has no PLACEHOLDER_USER. It exports getCurrentUser (React cache), requireUser, requireRole, requirePageUser and requirePageRole on the real Auth.js session. FR-9 of the PRD is satisfied.\",\n    \"NOW PRESENT (closed since the earlier intake): the /login page (src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx + LoginForm.tsx, with RHF+zod, an aria-live error Alert, a show-password toggle via passwordInputSlot, the rate-limit message, safeCallbackUrl and a forgot-password link); seed users (six ACTIVE users plus invited@schoolhub.test, whose invite link is logged via logger.info); migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index (@@index([role, status])).\",\n    \"REUSABLE UI that already exists: TextFormField (src/components/FormField/FormField), PasswordChecklist + passwordInputSlot (src/components/PasswordChecklist), useToast (src/components/Toast/useToast). New auth pages must reuse these and must not duplicate them.\",\n    \"MISSING: the pages /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token] under src/app/(auth)/; the /account/security page (only /account/notifications exists).\",\n    \"MISSING: src/app/(app)/shell.tsx still defines PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 40, 78, 162-167). No UI calls signOut(), and the user menu has no 'Account security' item.\",\n    \"MISSING TESTS: the unit tests exist (tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy, auth-validators, login-error-message). No integration tests exist for the authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password or change-password (tests/integration has only email-dispatch and timetable). No Playwright auth specs exist (tests/e2e has only dashboard, landing and notifications).\",\n    \"SCHEMA DRIFT vs the PRD FR-1 snippet: AuditLog stores the IP in a column named `ip`, not `ipAddress`, and has @@index([actorId]) and @@index([action]) rather than the PRD's [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt] indexes. Under the no-rename rule, keep `ip`.\",\n    \"PRD-04 is already present: sendAuthEmail() renders the email and enqueues it into EmailOutbox. The PRD's interim 'log via logger.info' behaviour must NOT be reintroduced.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog exist with the fields in the PRD (status default INVITED, failedLoginCount default 0, nullable passwordHash until invite accepted, AuthToken.tokenHash unique, cascade delete). Status: already present; keep as-is.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors). It has email and password fields and submits through Auth.js signIn('credentials'). Status: PRESENT (src/app/(auth)/login). Verify only; do not rebuild.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1; Pages & Routes '/login'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"The credentials authorize function lower-cases and trims the email. It rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or lockedUntil > now, and it verifies the password with bcrypt cost 12. Status: present in src/server/auth/credentials.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.' The /login UI must surface the server's message.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 2, 3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"A failed password increments failedLoginCount. At 5 failures, lockedUntil is set to now+15min and the count resets to 0. A successful sign-in resets failedLoginCount to 0 and sets lastLoginAt. Status: present (computeLockout).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4; Acceptance Criterion 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Sign-in is rate-limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using the in-memory sliding window exported from src/server/rate-limit.ts. Going over returns RATE_LIMITED, and the form shows 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' Status: limiter present; the UI message is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() from src/lib/validators/auth.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.6; Acceptance Criterion 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Sign-in writes the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.7; Acceptance Criterion 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"The JWT session lasts 8 hours and is refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email. Status: present.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"A session is invalid when passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time. The jwt callback checks this at most once every 5 minutes per token, so other devices are signed out within 5 minutes. Status: present (RECHECK_MS).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with error.code UNAUTHENTICATED, except /api/health, /api/auth/* and the paths in src/config/public-routes.ts. Status: present in src/middleware.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3; Goals 2; Acceptance Criterion 8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"All AuthToken creation, lookup and consumption goes through src/server/auth/tokens.ts: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns the raw token and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns user/token or null when missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt. Status: present; no other module may re-implement hashing.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"description\": \"A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' A valid token shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm fields. Status: MISSING (UI page). The API and service exist.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, FR-4.2; Acceptance Criteria 4, 5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-14\",\n      \"description\": \"Accepting an invite validates the password policy, hashes the password, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted. Reusing the link afterwards shows the invalid-link message. Status: the service and API exist; the UI page is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3; Acceptance Criterion 4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"description\": \"Password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10–128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub/989cf2ad-81d2-4d4b-83da-4ad0207f953c/tool-results/b5rwc1lbl.txt","persistedOutputSize":45033},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0184NgqfMioRArgRv45Ymzw3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
