{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018c8pzucFEDdNzieNKnbKzj","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T16:26:09Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 49,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"BROWNFIELD: the backend, /login, the seed users and the role/status index already exist. Design only the gaps and do not rebuild these.\",\n    \"GAPS to design: the (auth) pages /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token]; the /account/security page; removing PLACEHOLDER_USER from shell.tsx and wiring the session user, role badge, initials, signOut() and the 'Account security' menu item; integration tests (authorize, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) and Playwright auth specs.\",\n    \"REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl and the existing auth API routes.\",\n    \"FR-32 (LOW): AuditLog uses `ip`, not the PRD's `ipAddress`. Default: keep `ip` (no-rename rule).\",\n    \"NFR-6: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\nSH-1\nticketId \"SH-1\"\ntimestamp \"2026-11-05T16:26:09Z\"\nphase \"intake\"\nversion \"1.0\"\nprd \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\"\nrunMode \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\"\noverallConfidencePct 97\nconfidenceMethod \"HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40, averaged over 49 requirements (45 HIGH, 3 MEDIUM, 1 LOW).\"\nstatus \"complete\"\n== brownfieldFindings\n\"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-1 and the PRD header says SCH-001. All artifacts use SH-1.\"\n\"Re-run of intake on 2026-11-05. The workspace was re-checked, and some gaps reported by the earlier SH-1 intake have since been closed.\"\n\"ALREADY IMPLEMENTED (do not rebuild): the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums and the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models; src/server/auth/tokens.ts; credentials.ts (authorize, DUMMY_HASH, lockout); auth.ts/auth.config.ts (JWT 8h, 5-min passwordChangedAt recheck, signOut export); src/middleware.ts + src/config/public-routes.ts; src/server/rate-limit.ts; src/server/audit.ts; src/lib/validators/auth.ts \n\"requireRole.ts already has no PLACEHOLDER_USER. It exports getCurrentUser (React cache), requireUser, requireRole, requirePageUser and requirePageRole on the real Auth.js session. FR-9 of the PRD is satisfied.\"\n\"NOW PRESENT (closed since the earlier intake): the /login page (src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx + LoginForm.tsx, with RHF+zod, an aria-live error Alert, a show-password toggle via passwordInputSlot, the rate-limit message, safeCallbackUrl and a forgot-password link); seed users (six ACTIVE users plus invited@schoolhub.test, whose invite link is logged via logger.info); migration 20261106000000_user\n\"REUSABLE UI that already exists: TextFormField (src/components/FormField/FormField), PasswordChecklist + passwordInputSlot (src/components/PasswordChecklist), useToast (src/components/Toast/useToast). New auth pages must reuse these and must not duplicate them.\"\n\"MISSING: the pages /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token] under src/app/(auth)/; the /account/security page (only /account/notifications exists).\"\n\"MISSING: src/app/(app)/shell.tsx still defines PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 40, 78, 162-167). No UI calls signOut(), and the user menu has no 'Account security' item.\"\n\"MISSING TESTS: the unit tests exist (tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy, auth-validators, login-error-message). No integration tests exist for the authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password or change-password (tests/integration has only email-dispatch and timetable). No Playwright auth specs exist (tests/e2e has only dashboard, landing and notifications).\"\n\"SCHEMA DRIFT vs the PRD FR-1 snippet: AuditLog stores the IP in a column named `ip`, not `ipAddress`, and has @@index([actorId]) and @@index([action]) rather than the PRD's [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt] indexes. Under the no-rename rule, keep `ip`.\"\n\"PRD-04 is already present: sendAuthEmail() renders the email and enqueues it into EmailOutbox. The PRD's interim 'log via logger.info' behaviour must NOT be reintroduced.\"\n== functionalRequirements\n{\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog exist with the fields in the PRD (status default INVITED, failedLoginCount default 0, nullable passwordHash until invite accepted, AuthToken.tokenHash unique, cascade delete). Status: already present; keep as-is.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Functional Requirements \\u203\n{\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors). It has email and password fields and submits through Auth.js signIn('credentials'). Status: PRESENT (src/app/(auth)/login). Verify only; do not rebuild.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1; Pages & R\n{\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"The credentials authorize function lower-cases and trims the email. It rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or lockedUntil > now, and it verifies the password with bcrypt cost 12. Status: present in src/server/auth/credentials.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.' The /login UI must surface the server's message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria \n{\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"A failed password increments failedLoginCount. At 5 failures, lockedUntil is set to now+15min and the count resets to 0. A successful sign-in resets failedLoginCount to 0 and sets lastLoginAt. Status: present (computeLockout).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4; Acceptance Criterion 2\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Sign-in is rate-limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using the in-memory sliding window exported from src/server/rate-limit.ts. Going over returns RATE_LIMITED, and the form shows 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' Status: limiter present; the UI message is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.5\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() from src/lib/validators/auth.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.6; Acceptance Criterion 1\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Sign-in writes the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.7; Acceptance Criterion 2\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The JWT session lasts 8 hours and is refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"A session is invalid when passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time. The jwt callback checks this at most once every 5 minutes per token, so other devices are signed out within 5 minutes. Status: present (RECHECK_MS).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with error.code UNAUTHENTICATED, except /api/health, /api/auth/* and the paths in src/config/public-routes.ts. Status: present in src/middleware.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3; Goals 2; Acceptance Criterion 8\n{\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"All AuthToken creation, lookup and consumption goes through src/server/auth/tokens.ts: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns the raw token and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns user/token or null when missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt. Status: present; no other module may re-implement hashing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \n{\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' A valid token shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm fields. Status: MISSING (UI page). The API and service exist.\", \"confidence\": \n{\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite validates the password policy, hashes the password, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted. Reusing the link afterwards shows the invalid-link message. Status: the service and API exist; the UI page is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \n{\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10\\u2013128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled 1,000-entry src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt. 'password123' fails the common-password rule. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 10\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live strength checklist under every new-password field (invite, reset, change) shows each policy rule as met or unmet, driven by passwordChecks()/PASSWORD_RULES. Status: the PasswordChecklist component exists. It must be wired into the invite, reset and security pages.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"A public /forgot-password page has an email field. It always shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (no user enumeration) and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour. Status: the API exists; the /forgot-password UI page is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"When the email belongs to an ACTIVE user, the service creates a PASSWORD_RESET token via createToken(userId, 'PASSWORD_RESET', { minutes: 60 }) (32 random bytes, base64url), invalidates older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2; Acceptance Cri\n{\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"A public /reset-password/[token] page has new-password and confirm fields. On success the service sets the hash and passwordChangedAt=now, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, and audits auth.password.reset. The UI then redirects to /login, which shows a useToast success toast. Status: the API exists; the /reset-password/[token] UI page is MISSING.\", \"conf\n{\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"An /account/security page (any signed-in user) has current, new and confirm password fields and calls POST /api/account/password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions through passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session. Status: the API exists; t\n{\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' item, linking to /account/security, to the top-bar user menu. Status: MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.2\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"src/server/services/users.ts provides createUser (INVITED, throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken (7-day INVITE token via tokens.ts, invalidates older unused invites), sendInvite (createInviteToken + sendAuthEmail 'invite'), setUserStatus and unlockUser. Status: present; verify only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1\\u2013FR-8.4\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exposes getCurrentUser() (session user or null), requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED; pages redirect to /login) and requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN, so a STUDENT calling an ADMIN handler gets 403; pages redirect to /forbidden). There is no separate permissions.ts and no can() helper. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \n{\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"src/server/audit.ts audit({ actorId, action, entityType?, entityId?, metadata?, request? }) inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, and never throws (errors go to the logger). Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.1\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx. The shell gets the real signed-in user from the session, so the codebase has exactly one source of 'current user'. Status: MISSING (PLACEHOLDER_USER is still in shell.tsx).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.1\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The top-bar user menu shows the real user's name, a role badge and avatar initials. 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login. Status: MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.2; Acceptance Criterion 1\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Sidebar navigation filtering (navigationForRole in src/config/navigation.ts) uses the session role instead of the placeholder role. Status: MISSING (navigationForRole(PLACEHOLDER_USER.role)).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.3\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"The seed idempotently creates six ACTIVE users with password 'SchoolHub123!': admin@ Alice Admin ADMIN, teacher@ Tom Teacher TEACHER, teacher2@ Tina Tutor TEACHER, student@ Sam Student STUDENT, student2@ Sara Scholar STUDENT, parent@ Pat Parent PARENT (all @schoolhub.test). The existing seed has no users. Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"so\n{\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"The seed creates one INVITED user, invited@schoolhub.test, and logs its invite link during seeding. Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Seed Data, final sentence\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"The seed logs the invite link through logger (createInviteToken + authLink) rather than through sendAuthEmail, because PRD-04's sendAuthEmail enqueues email and deliberately never logs raw links.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Seed Data + \\u00a7Out of Scope (sendAuthEmail/PRD-04 note); inferred from workspace state\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Keep the existing PRD-04 sendAuthEmail() behaviour (render template and enqueue into EmailOutbox). Do not revert it to the interim logger.info stub described for the pre-PRD-04 state.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Out of Scope (email delivery) + \\u00a7Platform Context 'reuse existing\\u2026 never duplicate'; inferred from brownfield state\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The AuditLog IP column stays `ip` (existing name) rather than being renamed to the PRD snippet's `ipAddress`, because renaming existing model fields is prohibited. Flagged for human validation.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (AuditLog.ipAddress) vs \\u00a7Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"An additive migration adds @@index([role, status]) on User, which the PRD FR-1 model declares and the current schema lacks. Status: PRESENT (migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 User model '@@index([role, status])'\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl check (mostly existing); Vitest integration tests against the test DB for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password (MISSING); Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot \\u2192 reset, reading the link from a \n== nonFunctionalRequirements\n{\"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored, only their SHA-256 hashes, and token hashes are compared in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Non-Functional Requirements 1\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production, and SameSite=Lax. Every auth form carries Auth.js-supplied CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Non-Functional Requirements 1\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"'No such user' and 'wrong password' sign-in responses take similar time: a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Non-Functional Requirements 2\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Non-Functional Requirements 3\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\", and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit, on every auth form.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Non-Functional Requirements 4\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element uses @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, composed with Box/Stack/Grid and the theme. Before any component is used, it is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs then fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0), and only documented props, slots and imports are used. If the MCP server is unreachable, th\n{\"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"No banned UI or styling libraries are used (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, Headless UI, Chakra, AntD, Bootstrap, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, Recharts, FullCalendar, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack). Styling goes only through the theme, sx and styled(). QA checks for banned imports and verifies that every MUI import resolves to a \n{\"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.2\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Every protected page and API handler enforces access on the server through requireUser/requireRole. Hiding a UI control is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet); Goals 2\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"API handlers are thin (parse with Zod, call a service, return JSON). They use the {data} / list / {error:{code,message,details}} envelope and the standard error codes (VALIDATION_ERROR 400, UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, NOT_FOUND 404, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, INTERNAL 500).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Code layout and conventions (route\n{\"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Forms use React Hook Form with zodResolver and the Zod schemas shared from src/lib/validators/auth.ts. Client and server use the same validation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Fixed technology decisions (Validation, Forms)\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Code layout and conventions (last bullet)\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Scope and regression guard: delivered in a single run with no scope expansion. Do not modify src/server/auth/course-access.ts or student-access.ts, do not rebuild existing auth modules, and do not rename existing routes or models. npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test must keep passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Assumptions and constr\n{\"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Only invited users can sign in. There is no public sign-up route or UI.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Goals 1; \\u00a7Background\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Browser support: the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari. English-only UI.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Assumptions and constraints (Assumptions)\"}\n== clarificationLog\n{\"round\": 1, \"questions\": [\"FR-32: Should AuditLog keep its existing `ip` column (and its existing indexes), or be renamed to `ipAddress` as in the PRD FR-1 snippet?\", \"FR-30/FR-31: Since PRD-04 already enqueues auth emails into EmailOutbox, is it correct that the seed logs the invite link directly via logger and the PRD's interim logger stub is not restored?\", \"Ticket id: is SH-1 (pipeline) the c\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T12:12:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 7,\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"SH-1 adds no endpoints. The 7 contracts document existing routes: 4 business routes (forgot-password, reset-password, accept-invite, account/password) and 3 Auth.js routes (callback/credentials, csrf, signout) that the new pages and tests call. src/app/api/** and src/server/** stay untouched.\",\n    \"Fixes to system-design.md from reading the code (details in api-contracts.json designCorrections): the confirm field is `confirm`, not `confirmPassword`; INVALID_TOKEN is HTTP 410, not 400; on /api/account/password, common-password errors come back under fieldErrors.password, so ChangePasswordForm must remap them to newPassword.\",\n    \"The api-contracts.json and handoff files that were on disk belonged to SH-6 and have been replaced. These files are also stale (SH-6) and must be regenerated for SH-1: artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json, artifacts/dev-planning/*, artifacts/dev/*, artifacts/qa/* and artifacts/ui-verification/*.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"NFR-6 (carried forward; does not block dev-planning): dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0) before writing UI, and must stop and report if it is unreachable.\",\n    \"FR-32 (LOW, needs human sign-off): keep AuditLog.ip and do not rename it to ipAddress.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"989cf2ad-81d2-4d4b-83da-4ad0207f953c","uuid":"1c620373-c8e8-4519-ad58-4f49c0a5998e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:30:41.097Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T16:26:09Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 49,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"BROWNFIELD: the backend, /login, the seed users and the role/status index already exist. Design only the gaps and do not rebuild these.\",\n    \"GAPS to design: the (auth) pages /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token]; the /account/security page; removing PLACEHOLDER_USER from shell.tsx and wiring the session user, role badge, initials, signOut() and the 'Account security' menu item; integration tests (authorize, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) and Playwright auth specs.\",\n    \"REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl and the existing auth API routes.\",\n    \"FR-32 (LOW): AuditLog uses `ip`, not the PRD's `ipAddress`. Default: keep `ip` (no-rename rule).\",\n    \"NFR-6: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\nSH-1\nticketId \"SH-1\"\ntimestamp \"2026-11-05T16:26:09Z\"\nphase \"intake\"\nversion \"1.0\"\nprd \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\"\nrunMode \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\"\noverallConfidencePct 97\nconfidenceMethod \"HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40, averaged over 49 requirements (45 HIGH, 3 MEDIUM, 1 LOW).\"\nstatus \"complete\"\n== brownfieldFindings\n\"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-1 and the PRD header says SCH-001. All artifacts use SH-1.\"\n\"Re-run of intake on 2026-11-05. The workspace was re-checked, and some gaps reported by the earlier SH-1 intake have since been closed.\"\n\"ALREADY IMPLEMENTED (do not rebuild): the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums and the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models; src/server/auth/tokens.ts; credentials.ts (authorize, DUMMY_HASH, lockout); auth.ts/auth.config.ts (JWT 8h, 5-min passwordChangedAt recheck, signOut export); src/middleware.ts + src/config/public-routes.ts; src/server/rate-limit.ts; src/server/audit.ts; src/lib/validators/auth.ts \n\"requireRole.ts already has no PLACEHOLDER_USER. It exports getCurrentUser (React cache), requireUser, requireRole, requirePageUser and requirePageRole on the real Auth.js session. FR-9 of the PRD is satisfied.\"\n\"NOW PRESENT (closed since the earlier intake): the /login page (src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx + LoginForm.tsx, with RHF+zod, an aria-live error Alert, a show-password toggle via passwordInputSlot, the rate-limit message, safeCallbackUrl and a forgot-password link); seed users (six ACTIVE users plus invited@schoolhub.test, whose invite link is logged via logger.info); migration 20261106000000_user\n\"REUSABLE UI that already exists: TextFormField (src/components/FormField/FormField), PasswordChecklist + passwordInputSlot (src/components/PasswordChecklist), useToast (src/components/Toast/useToast). New auth pages must reuse these and must not duplicate them.\"\n\"MISSING: the pages /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token] under src/app/(auth)/; the /account/security page (only /account/notifications exists).\"\n\"MISSING: src/app/(app)/shell.tsx still defines PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 40, 78, 162-167). No UI calls signOut(), and the user menu has no 'Account security' item.\"\n\"MISSING TESTS: the unit tests exist (tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy, auth-validators, login-error-message). No integration tests exist for the authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password or change-password (tests/integration has only email-dispatch and timetable). No Playwright auth specs exist (tests/e2e has only dashboard, landing and notifications).\"\n\"SCHEMA DRIFT vs the PRD FR-1 snippet: AuditLog stores the IP in a column named `ip`, not `ipAddress`, and has @@index([actorId]) and @@index([action]) rather than the PRD's [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt] indexes. Under the no-rename rule, keep `ip`.\"\n\"PRD-04 is already present: sendAuthEmail() renders the email and enqueues it into EmailOutbox. The PRD's interim 'log via logger.info' behaviour must NOT be reintroduced.\"\n== functionalRequirements\n{\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog exist with the fields in the PRD (status default INVITED, failedLoginCount default 0, nullable passwordHash until invite accepted, AuthToken.tokenHash unique, cascade delete). Status: already present; keep as-is.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Functional Requirements \\u203\n{\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors). It has email and password fields and submits through Auth.js signIn('credentials'). Status: PRESENT (src/app/(auth)/login). Verify only; do not rebuild.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1; Pages & R\n{\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"The credentials authorize function lower-cases and trims the email. It rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or lockedUntil > now, and it verifies the password with bcrypt cost 12. Status: present in src/server/auth/credentials.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.' The /login UI must surface the server's message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria \n{\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"A failed password increments failedLoginCount. At 5 failures, lockedUntil is set to now+15min and the count resets to 0. A successful sign-in resets failedLoginCount to 0 and sets lastLoginAt. Status: present (computeLockout).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4; Acceptance Criterion 2\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Sign-in is rate-limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using the in-memory sliding window exported from src/server/rate-limit.ts. Going over returns RATE_LIMITED, and the form shows 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' Status: limiter present; the UI message is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.5\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() from src/lib/validators/auth.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.6; Acceptance Criterion 1\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Sign-in writes the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.7; Acceptance Criterion 2\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The JWT session lasts 8 hours and is refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"A session is invalid when passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time. The jwt callback checks this at most once every 5 minutes per token, so other devices are signed out within 5 minutes. Status: present (RECHECK_MS).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with error.code UNAUTHENTICATED, except /api/health, /api/auth/* and the paths in src/config/public-routes.ts. Status: present in src/middleware.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3; Goals 2; Acceptance Criterion 8\n{\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"All AuthToken creation, lookup and consumption goes through src/server/auth/tokens.ts: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns the raw token and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns user/token or null when missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt. Status: present; no other module may re-implement hashing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \n{\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' A valid token shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm fields. Status: MISSING (UI page). The API and service exist.\", \"confidence\": \n{\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite validates the password policy, hashes the password, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted. Reusing the link afterwards shows the invalid-link message. Status: the service and API exist; the UI page is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \n{\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10\\u2013128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled 1,000-entry src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt. 'password123' fails the common-password rule. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 10\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live strength checklist under every new-password field (invite, reset, change) shows each policy rule as met or unmet, driven by passwordChecks()/PASSWORD_RULES. Status: the PasswordChecklist component exists. It must be wired into the invite, reset and security pages.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"A public /forgot-password page has an email field. It always shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (no user enumeration) and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour. Status: the API exists; the /forgot-password UI page is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"When the email belongs to an ACTIVE user, the service creates a PASSWORD_RESET token via createToken(userId, 'PASSWORD_RESET', { minutes: 60 }) (32 random bytes, base64url), invalidates older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2; Acceptance Cri\n{\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"A public /reset-password/[token] page has new-password and confirm fields. On success the service sets the hash and passwordChangedAt=now, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, and audits auth.password.reset. The UI then redirects to /login, which shows a useToast success toast. Status: the API exists; the /reset-password/[token] UI page is MISSING.\", \"conf\n{\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"An /account/security page (any signed-in user) has current, new and confirm password fields and calls POST /api/account/password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions through passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session. Status: the API exists; t\n{\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' item, linking to /account/security, to the top-bar user menu. Status: MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.2\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"src/server/services/users.ts provides createUser (INVITED, throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken (7-day INVITE token via tokens.ts, invalidates older unused invites), sendInvite (createInviteToken + sendAuthEmail 'invite'), setUserStatus and unlockUser. Status: present; verify only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1\\u2013FR-8.4\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exposes getCurrentUser() (session user or null), requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED; pages redirect to /login) and requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN, so a STUDENT calling an ADMIN handler gets 403; pages redirect to /forbidden). There is no separate permissions.ts and no can() helper. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \n{\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"src/server/audit.ts audit({ actorId, action, entityType?, entityId?, metadata?, request? }) inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, and never throws (errors go to the logger). Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.1\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx. The shell gets the real signed-in user from the session, so the codebase has exactly one source of 'current user'. Status: MISSING (PLACEHOLDER_USER is still in shell.tsx).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.1\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The top-bar user menu shows the real user's name, a role badge and avatar initials. 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login. Status: MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.2; Acceptance Criterion 1\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Sidebar navigation filtering (navigationForRole in src/config/navigation.ts) uses the session role instead of the placeholder role. Status: MISSING (navigationForRole(PLACEHOLDER_USER.role)).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.3\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"The seed idempotently creates six ACTIVE users with password 'SchoolHub123!': admin@ Alice Admin ADMIN, teacher@ Tom Teacher TEACHER, teacher2@ Tina Tutor TEACHER, student@ Sam Student STUDENT, student2@ Sara Scholar STUDENT, parent@ Pat Parent PARENT (all @schoolhub.test). The existing seed has no users. Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"so\n{\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"The seed creates one INVITED user, invited@schoolhub.test, and logs its invite link during seeding. Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Seed Data, final sentence\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"The seed logs the invite link through logger (createInviteToken + authLink) rather than through sendAuthEmail, because PRD-04's sendAuthEmail enqueues email and deliberately never logs raw links.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Seed Data + \\u00a7Out of Scope (sendAuthEmail/PRD-04 note); inferred from workspace state\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Keep the existing PRD-04 sendAuthEmail() behaviour (render template and enqueue into EmailOutbox). Do not revert it to the interim logger.info stub described for the pre-PRD-04 state.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Out of Scope (email delivery) + \\u00a7Platform Context 'reuse existing\\u2026 never duplicate'; inferred from brownfield state\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The AuditLog IP column stays `ip` (existing name) rather than being renamed to the PRD snippet's `ipAddress`, because renaming existing model fields is prohibited. Flagged for human validation.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (AuditLog.ipAddress) vs \\u00a7Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"An additive migration adds @@index([role, status]) on User, which the PRD FR-1 model declares and the current schema lacks. Status: PRESENT (migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 User model '@@index([role, status])'\"}\n{\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl check (mostly existing); Vitest integration tests against the test DB for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password (MISSING); Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot \\u2192 reset, reading the link from a \n== nonFunctionalRequirements\n{\"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored, only their SHA-256 hashes, and token hashes are compared in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Non-Functional Requirements 1\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production, and SameSite=Lax. Every auth form carries Auth.js-supplied CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Non-Functional Requirements 1\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"'No such user' and 'wrong password' sign-in responses take similar time: a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Non-Functional Requirements 2\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Non-Functional Requirements 3\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\", and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit, on every auth form.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Non-Functional Requirements 4\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element uses @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, composed with Box/Stack/Grid and the theme. Before any component is used, it is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs then fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0), and only documented props, slots and imports are used. If the MCP server is unreachable, th\n{\"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"No banned UI or styling libraries are used (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, Headless UI, Chakra, AntD, Bootstrap, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, Recharts, FullCalendar, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack). Styling goes only through the theme, sx and styled(). QA checks for banned imports and verifies that every MUI import resolves to a \n{\"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.2\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Every protected page and API handler enforces access on the server through requireUser/requireRole. Hiding a UI control is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet); Goals 2\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"API handlers are thin (parse with Zod, call a service, return JSON). They use the {data} / list / {error:{code,message,details}} envelope and the standard error codes (VALIDATION_ERROR 400, UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, NOT_FOUND 404, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, INTERNAL 500).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Code layout and conventions (route\n{\"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Forms use React Hook Form with zodResolver and the Zod schemas shared from src/lib/validators/auth.ts. Client and server use the same validation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Fixed technology decisions (Validation, Forms)\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Code layout and conventions (last bullet)\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Scope and regression guard: delivered in a single run with no scope expansion. Do not modify src/server/auth/course-access.ts or student-access.ts, do not rebuild existing auth modules, and do not rename existing routes or models. npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test must keep passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Assumptions and constr\n{\"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Only invited users can sign in. There is no public sign-up route or UI.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Goals 1; \\u00a7Background\"}\n{\"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Browser support: the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari. English-only UI.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD \\u00a7Assumptions and constraints (Assumptions)\"}\n== clarificationLog\n{\"round\": 1, \"questions\": [\"FR-32: Should AuditLog keep its existing `ip` column (and its existing indexes), or be renamed to `ipAddress` as in the PRD FR-1 snippet?\", \"FR-30/FR-31: Since PRD-04 already enqueues auth emails into EmailOutbox, is it correct that the seed logs the invite link directly via logger and the PRD's interim logger stub is not restored?\", \"Ticket id: is SH-1 (pipeline) the c\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T12:12:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 7,\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"SH-1 adds no endpoints. The 7 contracts document existing routes: 4 business routes (forgot-password, reset-password, accept-invite, account/password) and 3 Auth.js routes (callback/credentials, csrf, signout) that the new pages and tests call. src/app/api/** and src/server/** stay untouched.\",\n    \"Fixes to system-design.md from reading the code (details in api-contracts.json designCorrections): the confirm field is `confirm`, not `confirmPassword`; INVALID_TOKEN is HTTP 410, not 400; on /api/account/password, common-password errors come back under fieldErrors.password, so ChangePasswordForm must remap them to newPassword.\",\n    \"The api-contracts.json and handoff files that were on disk belonged to SH-6 and have been replaced. These files are also stale (SH-6) and must be regenerated for SH-1: artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json, artifacts/dev-planning/*, artifacts/dev/*, artifacts/qa/* and artifacts/ui-verification/*.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"NFR-6 (carried forward; does not block dev-planning): dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0) before writing UI, and must stop and report if it is unreachable.\",\n    \"FR-32 (LOW, needs human sign-off): keep AuditLog.ip and do not rename it to ipAddress.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018c8pzucFEDdNzieNKnbKzj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
