et_requested. UI (C1): 2xx → success Alert with data.message; 429 → error Alert 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' (IP-scoped, so it reveals nothing about the account).\"\ne['/api/auth/reset-password']['description']=\"Set a new password from a reset link (C2 page → C4 TokenPasswordForm mode=reset). verifyToken(PASSWORD_RESET) → policy → bcrypt 12 → transaction(consume token, set hash, passwordChangedAt=now, failedLoginCount=0, lockedUntil=null) → audit auth.password.reset. Success → router.replace('/login?reset=1'). 410 → C4 switches to the invalid-link Alert. Other sessions are revoked within 5 min through the passwordChangedAt recheck.\"\ne['/api/auth/reset-password']['requestSchema']['properties']['confirm']['note']=\"must equal password. Field is `confirm`, NOT `confirmPassword` (system-design C4 wording is wrong). SetPasswordForm's onSubmit(password, confirm) already uses this name.\"\ne['/api/auth/accept-invite']['description']=\"Activate an invited account (C3 page → C4 TokenPasswordForm mode=invite). verifyToken(INVITE) → policy → bcrypt 12 → transaction(consume token, set hash, status=ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt=now) → audit auth.invite.accepted. Does NOT create a session: C4 then calls signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false }) and router.replace('/dashboard'). On 410 C4 renders the FR-13 copy ('This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'), not the service message.\"\ne['/api/account/password']['description']=\"Signed-in password change (C5 /account/security). requireUser → changePasswordSchema → bcrypt compare current → policy → update hash + passwordChangedAt → audit auth.password.changed → unstable_update({ reauth: true }) re-issues THIS session so only other sessions are revoked (within 5 min). Success → useToast 'Password updated', form reset, router.refresh().\"\ne['/api/account/password']['responseSchema']['400']['cases']['policyFailure']=\"details.fieldErrors.password (NOT newPassword): assertPasswordAllowed (src/server/auth/password-policy.ts) hard-codes the `password` key. ChangePasswordForm must remap password → newPassword before applyFieldErrors(), or the error renders nowhere. Client-side Zod already catches every rule except common-password, so in practice this case only appears for common passwords.\"\nd['designCorrections']=[\n \"system-design.md C4 posts `confirmPassword`; the real field is `confirm` (resetPasswordSchema / acceptInviteSchema / changePasswordSchema in src/lib/validators/auth.ts). Body is { token, password, confirm }.\",\n \"system-design.md C5 doesn't cover common-password errors on /api/account/password: they arrive under fieldErrors.password and must be remapped to newPassword in ChangePasswordForm. Fix it on the client, not in the service (NFR-13).\",\n \"system-design.md R2 is confirmed: INVALID_TOKEN → HTTP 410 (src/server/http.ts). It is not in the NFR-10 list; it is kept as-is.\"\n]\nd['status']='complete'\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open(p,'a').write('\\n')\n\nids={r['id'] for r in json.load(open('artifacts/intake/requirements.json'))['functionalRequirements']+json.load(open('artifacts/intake/requirements.json'))['nonFunctionalRequirements']}\nused={i for x in d['endpoints'] for i in x['requirementIds']}|set(d['conventions']['requirementIds'])|set(d['unauthenticatedBehaviour']['requirementIds'])\nassert used<=ids, used-ids\nh={\"ticketId\":\"SH-1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-05T17:41:00Z\",\"phase\":\"architect\",\"version\":\"1.0\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"endpointCount\":len(d['endpoints']),\n\"artifacts\":[\"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"],\n\"notes\":[\n \"SH-1 adds no endpoints. The 7 contracts document existing routes: 4 business routes (forgot-password, reset-password, accept-invite, account/password) and 3 Auth.js routes (callback/credentials, csrf, signout) that C1–C9 call. src/app/api/** and src/server/** stay untouched.\",\n \"Regenerated against the 17:30 system-design.md (C1–C9). Corrections from reading the code (see api-contracts.json designCorrections): the confirm field is `confirm`, not `confirmPassword`; on /api/account/password, policy errors arrive under fieldErrors.password and ChangePasswordForm must remap them to newPassword.\",\n \"Downstream artifacts predate this design (dev-planning 11:47, dev, qa, threat-model-notes.json 11:42) and must be regenerated from C1–C9.\"],\n\"blockers\":[\n \"NFR-6 (carried forward; does not block dev-planning): dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0) before writing UI, and must stop and report if it is unreachable.\",\n \"FR-32 (LOW, needs human sign-off): keep AuditLog.ip and do not rename it to ipAddress.\"],\n\"nextPhase\":\"dev-planning\"}\njson.dump(h,open('artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json','w'),indent=2); print('ok',len(d['endpoints']))\nEOF","description":"Rewrite api-contracts.json, validate IDs, then write handoff"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01RXfKPsY3Swmmnd6pYUdAJx":{"cwd":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub"}}}
