{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm8dh1swDnpcRqnggdWX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've finished `arch-api-contracts` for SH-7, the last architect sub-task. The two files in `artifacts/architect/` had been left over from SH-1, so I replaced both. Both are valid JSON, and every requirement id cited in the contracts exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n- **`api-contracts.json`** defines the 10 endpoints listed in system-design §4:\n  - **Attendance:** `GET /api/attendance/today`, plus `GET` and `PUT /api/attendance/register` for both course and daily registers.\n  - **Student and course tabs:** `GET /api/students/{id}/attendance` and `GET /api/courses/{id}/attendance`.\n  - **Admin:** overview, report (with a `?format=csv` export), below-threshold, and remind.\n  - **Settings:** `PATCH /api/settings/school`.\n\n  Paths start with `/api`, matching the existing routes, rather than `/api/v1` from the template, since renaming routes isn't allowed. Response shapes, error codes and the 100-row page limit follow `src/server/http.ts`. Each endpoint lists its access check, request and response shapes, error cases and requirement ids.\n- **`handoff-to-dev-planning.json`** is written last, with status complete and 10 endpoints.\n\nA few contract decisions dev-planning should know about:\n- `PUT /register` returns the same shape as `GET /register`, so the form can refresh straight from the save response.\n- A save that includes a student who isn't on the roster, or skips one, fails with `VALIDATION_ERROR`. The error lists which students are invalid or missing.\n- `PATCH /api/settings/school` only accepts the two attendance settings and rejects any other field, so it can't grow into a general settings route.\n\nOpen items, also recorded in the handoff:\n- **MUI docs server:** dev must be able to reach mui-mcp before writing any UI; if it can't, the PRD treats that as a hard blocker.\n- **Intake defaults:** three things are built on intake's guesses and need human sign-off: the settings route (FR-5), the daily register route (FR-16), and the details of two notification types (FR-23).\n- **Stale files:** `threat-model-notes.json` and everything in `artifacts/dev-planning/` and `artifacts/dev/` are still from SH-1. They need regenerating for SH-7, not reusing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":164,"cache_read_input_tokens":63265,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":164},"output_tokens":721,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f90400c-337b-4bd2-a543-f73a5eb37374","uuid":"2c2b7a4b-69e0-4c67-b07d-1b53dcaef4e7","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:36:21.064Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm8dgpTnztisa8fFw9s8"}
