{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013XKDGToSipHNcXmrhvessc","type":"tool_result","content":"23:| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts`, shared by client forms and API handlers |\n44:- `src/app/api/<feature>/…/route.ts` REST route handlers. Handlers are thin: parse with Zod → call a service → return JSON.\n45:- `src/server/services/<feature>.ts` business logic and Prisma access. Server components may call services directly; client components call the REST API. New features follow PRD-05's precedent of a feature-named subdirectory instead: `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts` (for example `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`), not this older flat path — which remains accurate only for the already-built PRD-02/03-era services that still live there.\n113:2. `POST /api/files` (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus `context`. Limits: 25 MB per file (`MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env, default 25); allowed types by extension **and** magic-number sniffing (`file-type` package): pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4, zip. Rejections return `VALIDATION_ERROR` \"File type .exe is not allowed.\" or \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"\n115:4. `GET /api/files/:id` streams the file with `Content-Disposition: attachment` (inline for images and PDFs when `?inline=1`), `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and the stored MIME type. Access is decided by a resolver registry `src/server/files/access.ts`: `registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>)`. This PRD registers `lesson` (can view the lesson), `logo` (public). Unknown context → only the owner and admins. Later PRDs register their contexts.\n195:1. Fields: title, estimated minutes, video URL, and a Markdown editor built from MUI (`Tabs` Write/Preview, a multiline `TextField`, and a `ToggleButtonGroup`/`IconButton` toolbar) (bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table, image) and a live preview tab. Images inserted via the toolbar upload through `POST /api/files` (context `lesson`) and insert `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`.\n218:## API\n222:| `POST /api/files` | any | Multipart `file`, `context` |\n223:| `GET /api/files/:id` | access registry | `?inline=1` |\n224:| `DELETE /api/files/:id` | owner, ADMIN | Only while unattached |\n225:| `GET /api/courses/:id/modules` | `assertCanViewCourse` | Visibility filtered by role; includes lessons and the caller's progress |\n226:| `POST /api/courses/:id/modules` | `assertCanManageCourse` | |\n227:| `PATCH /api/modules/:id` · `DELETE /api/modules/:id` | manage | |\n228:| `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder` | manage | `{ modules: [{ id, lessonIds: [] }] }` full ordering |\n229:| `POST /api/modules/:id/lessons` | manage | |\n230:| `GET /api/lessons/:id` | view (visibility rules) | |\n231:| `PATCH /api/lessons/:id` · `DELETE /api/lessons/:id` | manage | Includes attachments and links arrays |\n232:| `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress` | STUDENT (enrolled) | `{ completed: boolean }` |\n233:| `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` | manage | Per-student list |\n234:| `GET /api/students/:id/learning` | `assertCanViewStudent` | |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6816f41d-5eba-4155-b675-82c03913b1ab","uuid":"3bad48e6-fabf-4491-a187-c09a553c537d","timestamp":"2026-11-06T19:25:42.136Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"23:| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts`, shared by client forms and API handlers |\n44:- `src/app/api/<feature>/…/route.ts` REST route handlers. Handlers are thin: parse with Zod → call a service → return JSON.\n45:- `src/server/services/<feature>.ts` business logic and Prisma access. Server components may call services directly; client components call the REST API. New features follow PRD-05's precedent of a feature-named subdirectory instead: `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts` (for example `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`), not this older 