{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RBpEDJxYiHVxko1rMCJG5x","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:45:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"conventions\": {\n    \"basePath\": \"/api (existing project convention, no /api/v1 prefix; NFR-10 forbids renaming routes)\",\n    \"handlerPattern\": \"withHandler → requireUser/requireRole → parseQuery/parseBody (schemas from src/lib/validators/attendance.ts) → resource assert → attendance-service → ok()/paginated(). Every helper comes from src/server/http.ts (system-design §3.1).\",\n    \"successEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<responseSchema>\" },\n    \"paginatedEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<responseSchema>[]\", \"meta\": { \"page\": \"int\", \"pageSize\": \"int ≤ 100\", \"total\": \"int\" } },\n    \"errorEnvelope\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"ApiErrorCode\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"unknown?\" } },\n    \"errorCodes\": { \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400, \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401, \"FORBIDDEN\": 403, \"NOT_FOUND\": 404, \"CONFLICT\": 409, \"INTERNAL\": 500 },\n    \"validationErrorDetails\": \"A ZodError maps to VALIDATION_ERROR with details = zod flatten() { formErrors, fieldErrors }. Service-raised NFR-3 roster errors use details { invalidStudentIds: string[] } or { missingStudentIds: string[] }.\",\n    \"dates\": \"Date-only values are 'yyyy-MM-dd' strings interpreted in SchoolSettings.timezone. Timestamps are ISO 8601 UTC. Display uses formatInSchoolTz (ADR-5).\",\n    \"ids\": \"All ids are cuid strings.\",\n    \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-35\", \"FR-36\", \"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]\n  },\n  \"sharedSchemas\": {\n    \"DateOnly\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$\" },\n    \"AttendanceStatus\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"PRESENT\", \"ABSENT\", \"LATE\", \"EXCUSED\"] },\n    \"AttendanceMode\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"PER_PERIOD\", \"DAILY_HOMEROOM\", \"BOTH\"] },\n    \"RegisterKey\": {\n      \"description\": \"Zod union registerQuery (C6). Course variant or section (daily) variant; exactly one (FR-2).\",\n      \"oneOf\": [\n        { \"type\": \"object\", \"required\": [\"courseId\", \"date\", \"periodId\"], \"properties\": { \"courseId\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"date\": { \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/DateOnly\" }, \"periodId\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n        { \"type\": \"object\", \"required\": [\"sectionId\", \"date\"], \"properties\": { \"sectionId\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"date\": { \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/DateOnly\" } } }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"RegisterRecordInput\": {\n      \"description\": \"Zod registerRecord (C6). minutesLate is required (1–240) iff status = LATE and forbidden otherwise (superRefine). EXCUSED is ADMIN-only, checked in the service (FR-10).\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"studentId\", \"status\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"studentId\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"status\": { \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/AttendanceStatus\" },\n        \"minutesLate\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 1, \"maximum\": 240 },\n        \"note\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 500 }\n      }\n    },\n    \"UserRef\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"name\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n    \"Register\": {\n      \"description\": \"Returned by GET and PUT /api/attendance/register.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"key\": { \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/RegisterKey\" },\n        \"header\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"courseName\": { \"type\": \"string|null\" }, \"sectionName\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"periodName\": { \"type\": \"string|null\" }, \"date\": { \"$ref\": \"#/sharedSchemas/DateOnly\" } } },\n        \"sessionId\": { \"type\": \"string|null\", \"description\": \"null when no register has been saved yet\" },\n        \"students\n----\ndict_keys(['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prdTitle', 'prdTicketRef', 'runMode', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'overallConfidencePct', 'clarificationLog', 'brownfieldFindings', 'status', 'confidenceMethod'])\nFR-7 Enforce the field limits in Zod schemas in src/lib/validators/assignments.ts, shared by forms and handlers: title ≤150; instructions ≤50,000; maxPoints 0–1000; lateCutoffAt > dueAt; latePenaltyPercentPerDay and maxLatePenaltyPercent 0–100; maxFileCount 1–10; submission text ≤50,000; feedback ≤10,000.\n\nFR-15 A 'Duplicate to other courses' action copies the assignment as DRAFT to selected courses the teacher manages (POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}). The copy keeps the instructions, attachments, settings and rubric. The copy keeps the same due date-time, and availableFrom/lateCutoffAt keep their offsets from dueAt.\n\nFR-18 Student view of the course Assignments tab: a list grouped as Upcoming, Past due (missing), Submitted and Returned. Parents see the same view, read-only, for their linked child.\n\nFR-28 Grading page /courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade, left panel: an MUI List of all enrolled students with status Chips (Not submitted, Submitted, Late, Graded, Returned, Exempt), a status filter, and sorting by name or submission time.\n\nFR-32 Grading buttons: 'Save' (graded, not visible to the student), 'Save & return' (returns this submission and sets returnedAt) and the bulk 'Return all graded' (POST /api/assignments/:id/return; submissionIds optional, defaults to all graded and unreturned).\n\nFR-34 'Grade without submission' for students who did not submit (POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}). It creates the attemptNumber = 0 Submission described in FR-8.\n\nFR-35 An 'Exempt' toggle (PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId) writes or deletes a GradeExemption. Exempt students are removed from missing counts and lists, get no due_soon or missing reminders, cannot submit, and are flagged for exclusion from future gradebook calculation (PRD-11).\n\nFR-37 Build the /assignments page for STUDENT. It lists every assignment across the student's ACTIVE enrollments in four tabs: Upcoming (sorted by due date), Missing (past due, not submitted, not exempt), Submitted and Returned. There is a course filter.\n\nFR-39 The /assignments page for TEACHER is a 'To grade' list of submitted, ungraded submissions across the courses they teach (teacherId or coTeacherIds), oldest first.\n\nFR-48 GET /api/courses/:id/assignments (view course) returns a role-shaped list. Managers get every status with counts. Students and parents get only visible, non-archived assignments, with their own submission state.\n\nFR-49 POST /api/courses/:id/assignments (manage course) creates an assignment with its rubric and attachments.\n\nFR-50 GET /api/assignments/:id (view). For students and parents the response includes their own submission, with grading fields only once returned.\n\nFR-51 PATCH /api/assignments/:id (manage). DELETE /api/assignments/:id (manage) hard-deletes only when there are no submissions. Otherwise it sets archivedAt.\n\nFR-53 POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions (STUDENT) {text?, fileIds[]} applies the FR-22 to FR-24 rules. The fileIds must be the student's own uploads with context 'submission', and their number must be ≤ maxFileCount.\n\nFR-54 GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions (manage) lists every enrolled student, including those who have not submitted, with their status, exemption and submission summary.\n\nFR-55 GET /api/submissions/:id is open to the submitting student, their parents and course managers. SubmissionHistory is included only for managers.\n\nFR-56 PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade (manage) {rawScore, penaltyPercent, feedback, rubricScores} sets gradedById/gradedAt and the computed finalScore.\n\nFR-57 GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab= (any role) returns the role-shaped data for /assignments. studentId is accepted for parents (it must be a linked child).\n\nFR-58 GET /api/students/:id/assignments (view student; uses the existing assertCanViewStudent) returns the per-student assignment list.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"000b1731-dbaf-472c-b7e3-65e8ca26353f","uuid":"c757cac4-54e0-48fb-a402-aade7510bc57","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:29:53.379Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:45:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"conventions\": {\n    \"basePath\": \"/api (existing project convention, no /api/v1 prefix; NFR-10 forbids renaming routes)\",\n    \"handlerPattern\": \"withHandler → requireUser/requireRole → parseQuery/parseBody (schemas from src/lib/validators/attendance.ts) → resource assert → attendance-service → ok()/paginated(). Every helper comes from src/server/http.ts (system-design §3.1).\",\n    \"successEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<responseSchema>\" },\n    \"paginatedEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<responseSchema>[]\", \"meta\": { \"page\": \"int\", \"pageSize\": \"int ≤ 100\", \"total\": \"int\" } },\n    \"errorEnvelope\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"ApiErrorCode\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"unknown?\" } },\n    \"errorCodes\": { \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400, \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401, \"FORBIDDEN\": 403, \"NOT_FOUND\": 404, \"CONFLICT\": 409, \"INTERNAL\": 500 },\n    \"validationErrorDetails\": \"A ZodError maps to VALIDATION_ERROR with details = zod flatten() { formErrors, fieldErrors }. Service-raised NFR-3 roster errors use details { invalidStudentIds: string[] } or { missingStudentIds: string[] }.\",\n    \"dates\": \"Date-only values are 'yyyy-MM-dd' strings interpreted in SchoolSettings.timezone. Timestamps are ISO 8601 UTC. Display uses formatInSchoolTz (ADR-5).\",\n    \"ids\": \"All ids are cuid strings.\",\n    \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-35\", \"FR-36\", \"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]\n  },\n  \"shar