{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrokoeEvyM49j8MN2RH5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the API contracts and the handoff for SH-9, so the architect phase is complete. Both files replace older leftovers that belonged to SH-7. Both are valid JSON, and every requirement id they cite exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n**`artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json`** (status: complete) defines 16 new endpoints, one per route method in system-design §2.7:\n- **Course assignments:** list and create.\n- **Single assignment:** view, update, and delete. Delete removes it fully if nobody has submitted; otherwise it is archived.\n- **Duplicate** an assignment to other courses.\n- **Submissions:** the grading roster (the only paginated list) and student submit.\n- **Grading actions:** return all graded, grade a student who didn't submit, and exempt or un-exempt a student.\n- **Single submission:** view it, and save a grade, optionally returning it in the same request.\n- **Per-person lists:** `/api/me/assignments` and `/api/students/:id/assignments`.\n\nRules that apply across all of them:\n- Paths start with `/api` like the existing routes, not `/api/v1`.\n- Scores and points are sent as strings such as `\"14.40\"`.\n- Students and parents never see grades or feedback until a submission is returned.\n- An assignment a student isn't allowed to see returns \"not found\", not \"forbidden\".\n\nIt also lists three existing endpoints that stay unchanged: file upload, file download, and the email dispatch call that will now also send reminders.\n\n**One decision I added:** each student's list row has a server-computed group. Besides the four groups in the requirements (Upcoming, Missing, Submitted, Returned), there is a fifth, `CLOSED`. It covers assignments that are past due but don't count as missing because the student is exempt or no submission is needed. The page shows these under \"Past due\" with no missing badge.\n\n**`artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json`** (status: complete, 16 endpoints) carries these blockers forward to dev:\n- Dev must be able to reach the MUI docs server before building any UI. If it can't, dev stops and reports it.\n- The MUI version pin needs to be checked with a test build first. If it fails, the fallbacks are a plain table and a basic date-time input.\n- The PDF preview needs a narrow security-header change on the file download route. A reviewer should sign off; the fallback is an \"Open\" link instead.\n- The Assignments tab on student pages won't show up, because nothing displays that tab bar yet. The page itself works by direct URL.\n- Some low-confidence defaults from intake were adopted as written: what copying an assignment does, how archived assignments behave, and that assignments needing no submission are never counted as missing. Someone should confirm them.\n\n`threat-model-notes.json`, and everything under `artifacts/dev-planning/` and `artifacts/dev/`, are still from earlier tickets and need to be regenerated, not reused."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":175,"cache_read_input_tokens":68915,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":175},"output_tokens":685,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"000b1731-dbaf-472c-b7e3-65e8ca26353f","uuid":"7cfaa193-8e62-43d4-b319-4acd681ae6a9","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:32:17.654Z","request_id":"req_011CgrokoQrH1Shd4dP3z9z2"}
