{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrvxjGDHwV22WupM8Pib","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EE1cfCGatnQwhpMtdP7ot5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 79,100p artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md; grep -n \"^| D[0-9]\\|^### D\\|^\\*\\*D[0-9]\" artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md; grep -rn \"fixed2\\|toFixed\" src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts | head -5; ls src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/","description":"Read ADR-5, decision notes, decimal helpers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3971,"cache_read_input_tokens":53010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3971,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2cdffa8-12d1-4e17-864e-e6653bd23adc","uuid":"7f424121-4bc2-45d2-9048-7ce0e8876335","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:06:40.545Z","request_id":"req_011Cgrvxj2LSRo22D4HWUA1v","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EE1cfCGatnQwhpMtdP7ot5":{"command":"cd /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub && sed -n 79,100p artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md; grep -n \"^| D[0-9]\\|^### D\\|^\\*\\*D[0-9]\" artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md; grep -rn \"fixed2\\|toFixed\" src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts | head -5; ls src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/","description":"Read ADR-5, decision notes, decimal helpers"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01EE1cfCGatnQwhpMtdP7ot5":{"cwd":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EE1cfCGatnQwhpMtdP7ot5","type":"tool_result","content":"## ADR-5: A dedicated student serializer is the only shape students receive\n\n**Context.** NFR-1: `correct`, `explanation` and scores must never reach a student's browser before results are visible. AC-7 and NFR-8 require a unit test that asserts the `correct` key is absent.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts` exports `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt` and `toStudentResult`. Each builds its output by explicit allow-listing, never by spreading and deleting fields. Prisma `select` excludes `correct` and `explanation` on student code paths. `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` is a single pure function that decides IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL (FR-20). It gates scores, and when `showCorrectAnswers` is set, it also gates correct answers and explanations (FR-21). Server components pass only serializer output to client components.\n\n**Consequences.** One place to audit and test. The parent read-only views (FR-11, NFR-5) reuse `toStudentResult`.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher, with no new job runner\n\n**Context.** FR-18, FR-30 and FR-35 need periodic auto-submit and a one-time AFTER_CLOSE results notification. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs `sendDueReminders()` on every cron request, in its own try/catch.\n\n**Decision.** Add two calls next to `sendDueReminders()`, each in its own try/catch with `logger`, following the same pattern:\n- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`: updates rows where `status = 'IN_PROGRESS' AND deadlineAt + 30s < now`. It is idempotent because of the status guard.\n- `sendAfterCloseResultsNotifications(now)`: for closed AFTER_CLOSE quizzes. It is made idempotent by an atomic claim, either a nullable `resultsNotifiedAt` column on Quiz claimed with `updateMany ... where resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` or a unique notification marker like `AssignmentReminder`. arch-design-system picks one. The `resultsNotifiedAt` column is the smaller change.\n\nNo BullMQ, no cron library, no `setInterval` on the server.\n\n**Consequences.** Lazy auto-submit (ADR-4) covers attempts between cron ticks. The maintenance run is a backstop, so its frequency doesn't affect correctness.\n\nsrc/server/assignments/grading-math.ts:15:export const fixed2 = (v: DecimalValue) => dec(v).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP).toFixed(2);\nroute.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2cdffa8-12d1-4e17-864e-e6653bd23adc","uuid":"938b5546-a892-45a5-959f-f23c63cafa99","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:06:40.683Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## ADR-5: A dedicated student serializer is the only shape students receive\n\n**Context.** NFR-1: `correct`, `explanation` and scores must never reach a student's browser before results are visible. AC-7 and NFR-8 require a unit test that asserts the `correct` key is absent.\n\n**Decision.** `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts` exports `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt` and `toStudentResult`. Each builds its output by explicit allow-listing, never by spreading and deleting fields. Prisma `select` excludes `correct` and `explanation` on student code paths. `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` is a single pure function that decides IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL (FR-20). It gates scores, and when `showCorrectAnswers` is set, it also gates correct answers and explanations (FR-21). Server components pass only serializer output to client components.\n\n**Consequences.** One place to audit and test. The parent read-only views (FR-11, NFR-5) reuse `toStudentResult`.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher, with no new job runner\n\n**Context.** FR-18, FR-30 and FR-35 need periodic auto-submit and a one-time AFTER_CLOSE results notification. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs `sendDueReminders()` on every cron request, in its own try/catch.\n\n**Decision.** Add two calls next to `sendDueReminders()`, each in its own try/catch with `logger`, following the same pattern:\n- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`: updates rows where `status = 'IN_PROGRESS' AND deadlineAt + 30s < now`. It is idempotent because of the status guard.\n- `sendAfterCloseResultsNotifications(now)`: for closed AFTER_CLOSE quizzes. It is made idempotent by an atomic claim, either a nullable `resultsNotifiedAt` column on Quiz claimed with `updateMany ... where resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` or a unique notification marker like `AssignmentReminder`. arch-design-system picks one. The `resultsNotifiedAt` column is the smaller change.\n\nNo BullMQ, no cron library, no `setInterval` on the server.\n\n**Consequences.** Lazy auto-submit (ADR-4) covers attempts between cron ticks. The maintenance run is a backstop, so its frequency doesn't affect correctness.\n\nsrc/server/assignments/grading-math.ts:15:export const fixed2 = (v: DecimalValue) => dec(v).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP).toFixed(2);\nroute.ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EE1cfCGatnQwhpMtdP7ot5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
