{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UtS6hXeHwTvH9TCVZYBP3g","type":"tool_result","content":"93\t### FR-1 Data model\n94\t\n95\t```prisma\n96\tenum QuizStatus { DRAFT PUBLISHED CLOSED }\n97\tenum QuestionType { SINGLE_CHOICE MULTIPLE_CHOICE TRUE_FALSE SHORT_ANSWER ESSAY }\n98\tenum ResultsVisibility { IMMEDIATELY AFTER_CLOSE MANUAL }\n99\tenum AttemptStatus { IN_PROGRESS SUBMITTED NEEDS_GRADING GRADED }\n100\tenum ScoringPolicy { HIGHEST LATEST AVERAGE }\n101\t\n102\tmodel Quiz {\n103\t  id                 String            @id @default(cuid())\n104\t  courseId           String\n105\t  course             Course            @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n106\t  title              String\n107\t  instructions       String            @default(\"\")   // Markdown\n108\t  isPractice         Boolean           @default(false) // practice quizzes never reach the gradebook\n109\t  availableFrom      DateTime\n110\t  availableUntil     DateTime                          // > availableFrom\n111\t  timeLimitMinutes   Int?                              // 1–300, null = untimed\n112\t  maxAttempts        Int               @default(1)     // 1–10\n113\t  scoringPolicy      ScoringPolicy     @default(HIGHEST)\n114\t  shuffleQuestions   Boolean           @default(false)\n115\t  shuffleOptions     Boolean           @default(false)\n116\t  oneQuestionPerPage Boolean           @default(false)\n117\t  resultsVisibility  ResultsVisibility @default(AFTER_CLOSE)\n118\t  showCorrectAnswers Boolean           @default(true)  // when results are visible\n119\t  resultsReleasedAt  DateTime?                         // for MANUAL\n120\t  status             QuizStatus        @default(DRAFT)\n121\t  createdById        String\n122\t  createdAt          DateTime          @default(now())\n123\t  updatedAt          DateTime          @updatedAt\n124\t  questions          Question[]\n125\t  attempts           QuizAttempt[]\n126\t}\n127\t\n128\tmodel Question {\n129\t  id            String       @id @default(cuid())\n130\t  quizId        String\n131\t  quiz          Quiz         @relation(fields: [quizId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n132\t  type          QuestionType\n133\t  prompt        String                     // Markdown, may include an uploaded image\n134\t  points        Decimal      @db.Decimal(5, 2)   // 0.5–100\n135\t  order         Int\n136\t  options       Json?                      // choice types: [{ id, text }]\n137\t  correct       Json                       // see FR-2\n138\t  explanation   String?                    // shown with correct answers\n139\t  caseSensitive Boolean      @default(false)  // SHORT_ANSWER\n140\t}\n141\t\n142\tmodel QuizAttempt {\n143\t  id             String        @id @default(cuid())\n144\t  quizId         String\n145\t  quiz           Quiz          @relation(fields: [quizId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n146\t  studentId      String\n147\t  student        User          @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n148\t  attemptNumber  Int\n149\t  status         AttemptStatus @default(IN_PROGRESS)\n150\t  startedAt      DateTime      @default(now())\n151\t  deadlineAt     DateTime?                  // min(startedAt + limit + extraTime, availableUntil)\n152\t  submittedAt    DateTime?\n153\t  autoSubmitted  Boolean       @default(false)\n154\t  questionOrder  String[]                   // frozen order for this attempt\n155\t  score          Decimal?      @db.Decimal(7, 2)\n156\t  maxScore       Decimal       @db.Decimal(7, 2)\n157\t  answers        QuizAnswer[]\n158\t  @@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])\n159\t}\n160\t\n161\tmodel QuizAnswer {\n162\t  attemptId     String\n163\t  attempt       QuizAttempt @relation(fields: [attemptId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n164\t  questionId    String\n165\t  response      Json?\n166\t  pointsAwarded Decimal?    @db.Decimal(5, 2)\n167\t  isCorrect     Boolean?\n168\t  feedback      String?\n169\t  gradedById    String?\n170\t  updatedAt     DateTime    @updatedAt\n171\t  @@id([attemptId, questionId])\n172\t}\n173\t\n174\tmodel QuizAccommodation {\n175\t  quizId           String\n176\t  studentId        String\n177\t  extraTimeMinutes Int      @default(0)    // 0–300\n178\t  extraAttempts    Int      @default(0)    // 0–5\n179\t  @@id([quizId, studentId])\n180\t}\n181\t```\n182\t\n183\t### FR-2 Question types and auto-grading (`src/server/quiz/grading.ts`)\n184\t\n185\t| Type | `options` | `correct` | `response` | Scoring |\n186\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n187\t| SINGLE_CHOICE | 2–8 options | `{ optionId }` | `{ optionId }` | full points if equal, else 0 |\n188\t| MULTIPLE_CHOICE | 2–8 options | `{ optionIds: [] }` (≥1) | `{ optionIds: [] }` | partial credit: `points × max(0, (correctSelected − incorrectSelected) / totalCorrect)` |\n189\t| TRUE_FALSE | none | `{ value: true }` | `{ value: false }` | full or 0 |\n190\t| SHORT_ANSWER | none | `{ accepted: [\"photosynthesis\", \"photo-synthesis\"] }` (1–10) | `{ text }` | full if trimmed, whitespace-collapsed text matches any accepted answer (case-insensitive unless `caseSensitive`), else 0 — teacher can override |\n191\t| ESSAY | none | `{ guidance?: \"…\" }` | `{ text }` (max 10,000) | manual |\n192\t\n193\tExample: a MULTIPLE_CHOICE worth 4 points with correct {A, C}; a student selecting {A, B} scores `4 × max(0, (1 − 1) / 2) = 0`; selecting {A} scores 2.\n194\t\n195\t### FR-3 Quiz builder (`/courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit`)\n196\t1. Settings panel for every `Quiz` field with validation (availableUntil > availableFrom; time limit ≤ window length).\n197\t2. Question list with add (type picker), edit inline, duplicate, delete, drag reorder. Each type has a tailored editor: option rows with \"correct\" radio/checkbox, accepted answers list, essay guidance.\n198\t3. Running total of points; \"Preview as student\" opens the player in a non-recording preview mode.\n199\t4. Publishing validates: at least 1 question, every choice question has a correct answer, every question has points > 0.\n200\t5. After the first attempt exists, editing questions is limited: text, explanation and accepted answers may change (with a \"Regrade\" action that recomputes auto-graded answers for all attempts); adding/removing questions or changing points/type is blocked with an explanation.\n201\t\n202\t### FR-4 Course quizzes tab\n203\t1. Register course tab \"Quizzes\". Teacher: list with status, window, attempts count, average score, \"Needs grading\" count. Student: Upcoming (opens in…), Available now (with \"Start\" / \"Resume\"), Completed (score if visible), Missed. Parent: read-only completed results.\n204\t\n205\t### FR-5 Quiz player (`/quizzes/[quizId]/take`)\n206\t1. Start screen: instructions, question count, total points, time limit, attempts used / allowed. \"Start attempt\" confirms because the timer starts immediately.\n207\t2. Starting creates an attempt with frozen `questionOrder` (shuffled when enabled) and per-attempt option order (deterministic shuffle seeded by attempt id), and computes `deadlineAt`.\n208\t3. Layout (MUI `RadioGroup`/`FormGroup` of `Checkbox`es/`TextField` per question type, `LinearProgress` for completion): all questions on one scrollable page, or one per page with a question navigator grid of MUI `Button`s (answered / unanswered / flagged-for-review states). Sticky header with title, timer (mm:ss, turns red under 2 minutes, screen-reader announcement at 5 and 1 minutes remaining) and \"Submit\".\n209\t4. Autosave: every answer change is sent `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId` debounced 800 ms; failures are queued in `localStorage` and retried every 5 seconds; a status pill shows \"All answers saved\" / \"Saving…\" / \"Offline — answers saved on this device\".\n210\t5. Timer is display only; the server rejects answer writes after `deadlineAt + 30 s` grace and auto-submits.\n211\t6. Submit confirms, listing unanswered question count. On submit: auto-grade, set status `NEEDS_GRADING` if any ESSAY (or SHORT_ANSWER with no match flagged for review) else `GRADED`.\n212\t7. Auto-submit: any IN_PROGRESS attempt past `deadlineAt` is submitted with `autoSubmitted = true` lazily when the student or teacher next loads it, and by `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts()` in the maintenance run.\n213\t8. Only one IN_PROGRESS attempt per student per quiz; opening the quiz in a second tab resumes the same attempt.\n214\t\n215\t### FR-6 Results\n216\t1. Visibility: IMMEDIATELY → right after submit; AFTER_CLOSE → after `availableUntil`; MANUAL → after the teacher clicks \"Release results\". Until then students see \"Submitted — results will be available later.\"\n217\t2. Result page: score, percentage, per-question correctness, the student's response, correct answer and explanation (only when `showCorrectAnswers`), teacher feedback.\n218\t3. Quiz score for a student = scoring policy across GRADED attempts (HIGHEST, LATEST or AVERAGE), exposed via `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` for PRD-11.\n219\t\n220\t### FR-7 Manual grading (`/courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/grade`)\n221\t1. Two modes: \"By student\" (one attempt at a time) and \"By question\" (all students' answers to one question, ideal for essays). Inputs: points (0 – question points, step 0.5), feedback. Override for auto-graded answers.\n222\t2. When all answers of an attempt are graded, the attempt becomes GRADED and the score recomputes.\n223\t\n224\t### FR-8 Analytics tab (teacher)\n225\t1. Summary: attempts, average, median, highest, lowest, average time taken, score distribution histogram (10 % buckets, MUI X `BarChart`).\n226\t2. Per-question table: % correct, average points, and for choice questions the distribution of selected options (highlights the most chosen wrong option). CSV export of all attempts (student, attempt, score, per-question points).\n227\t\n228\t### FR-9 Accommodations\n229\t1. On the quiz settings page, a teacher can grant individual students extra time and extra attempts (`QuizAccommodation`), used in `deadlineAt` and attempt-limit checks.\n230\t\n231\t### FR-10 Notifications\n232\t1. `quiz.published` → enrolled students when published (default email false).\n233\t2. `quiz.results_released` → student + parents when results become visible (for AFTER_CLOSE, sent by the maintenance run once after close; for MANUAL on release; for IMMEDIATELY no notification).\n234\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2cdffa8-12d1-4e17-864e-e6653bd23adc","uuid":"31e9a645-13ca-4420-b965-a370bf842b8b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:06:56.922Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/10-quizzes.md","content":"### FR-1 Data model\n\n```prisma\nenum QuizStatus { DRAFT PUBLISHED CLOSED }\nenum QuestionType { SINGLE_CHOICE MULTIPLE_CHOICE TRUE_FALSE SHORT_ANSWER ESSAY }\nenum ResultsVisibility { IMMEDIATELY AFTER_CLOSE MANUAL }\nenum AttemptStatus { IN_PROGRESS SUBMITTED NEEDS_GRADING GRADED }\nenum ScoringPolicy { HIGHEST LATEST AVERAGE }\n\nmodel Quiz {\n  id                 String            @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId           String\n  course             Course            @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  title              String\n  instructions       String            @default(\"\")   // Markdown\n  isPractice         Boolean           @default(false) // practice quizzes never reach the gradebook\n  availableFrom      DateTime\n  availableUntil     DateTime                          // > availableFrom\n  timeLimitMinutes   Int?                              // 1–300, null = untimed\n  maxAttempts        Int               @default(1)     // 1–10\n  scoringPolicy      ScoringPolicy     @default(HIGHEST)\n  shuffleQuestions   Boolean           @default(false)\n  shuffleOptions     Boolean           @default(false)\n  oneQuestionPerPage Boolean           @default(false)\n  resultsVisibility  ResultsVisibility @default(AFTER_CLOSE)\n  showCorrectAnswers Boolean           @default(true)  // when results are visible\n  resultsReleasedAt  DateTime?                         // for MANUAL\n  status             QuizStatus        @default(DRAFT)\n  createdById        String\n  createdAt          DateTime          @default(now())\n  updatedAt          DateTime          @updatedAt\n  questions          Question[]\n  attempts           QuizAttempt[]\n}\n\nmodel Question {\n  id            String       @id @default(cuid())\n  quizId        String\n  quiz          Quiz         @relation(fields: [quizId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  type          QuestionType\n  prompt        String                     // Markdown, may include an uploaded image\n  points        Decimal      @db.Decimal(5, 2)   // 0.5–100\n  order         Int\n  options       Json?                      // choice types: [{ id, text }]\n  correct       Json                       // see FR-2\n  explanation   String?                    // shown with correct answers\n  caseSensitive Boolean      @default(false)  // SHORT_ANSWER\n}\n\nmodel QuizAttempt {\n  id             String        @id @default(cuid())\n  quizId         String\n  quiz           Quiz          @relation(fields: [quizId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId      String\n  student        User          @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n  attemptNumber  Int\n  status         AttemptStatus @default(IN_PROGRESS)\n  startedAt      DateTime      @default(now())\n  deadlineAt     DateTime?                  // min(startedAt + limit + extraTime, availableUntil)\n  submittedAt    DateTime?\n  autoSubmitted  Boolean       @default(false)\n  questionOrder  String[]                   // frozen order for this attempt\n  score          Decimal?      @db.Decimal(7, 2)\n  maxScore       Decimal       @db.Decimal(7, 2)\n  answers        QuizAnswer[]\n  @@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])\n}\n\nmodel QuizAnswer {\n  attemptId     String\n  attempt       QuizAttempt @relation(fields: [attemptId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  questionId    String\n  response      Json?\n  pointsAwarded Decimal?    @db.Decimal(5, 2)\n  isCorrect     Boolean?\n  feedback      String?\n  gradedById    String?\n  updatedAt     DateTime    @updatedAt\n  @@id([attemptId, questionId])\n}\n\nmodel QuizAccommodation {\n  quizId           String\n  studentId        String\n  extraTimeMinutes Int      @default(0)    // 0–300\n  extraAttempts    Int      @default(0)    // 0–5\n  @@id([quizId, studentId])\n}\n```\n\n### FR-2 Question types and auto-grading (`src/server/quiz/grading.ts`)\n\n| Type | `options` | `correct` | `response` | Scoring |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SINGLE_CHOICE | 2–8 options | `{ optionId }` | `{ optionId }` | full points if equal, else 0 |\n| MULTIPLE_CHOICE | 2–8 options | `{ optionIds: [] }` (≥1) | `{ optionIds: [] }` | partial credit: `points × max(0, (correctSelected − incorrectSelected) / totalCorrect)` |\n| TRUE_FALSE | none | `{ value: true }` | `{ value: false }` | full or 0 |\n| SHORT_ANSWER | none | `{ accepted: [\"photosynthesis\", \"photo-synthesis\"] }` (1–10) | `{ text }` | full if trimmed, whitespace-collapsed text matches any accepted answer (case-insensitive unless `caseSensitive`), else 0 — teacher can override |\n| ESSAY | none | `{ guidance?: \"…\" }` | `{ text }` (max 10,000) | manual |\n\nExample: a MULTIPLE_CHOICE worth 4 points with correct {A, C}; a student selecting {A, B} scores `4 × max(0, (1 − 1) / 2) = 0`; selecting {A} scores 2.\n\n### FR-3 Quiz builder (`/courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit`)\n1. Settings panel for every `Quiz` field with validation (availableUntil > availableFrom; time limit ≤ window length).\n2. Question list with add (type picker), edit inline, duplicate, delete, drag reorder. Each type has a tailored editor: option rows with \"correct\" radio/checkbox, accepted answers list, essay guidance.\n3. Running total of points; \"Preview as student\" opens the player in a non-recording preview mode.\n4. Publishing validates: at least 1 question, every choice question has a correct answer, every question has points > 0.\n5. After the first attempt exists, editing questions is limited: text, explanation and accepted answers may change (with a \"Regrade\" action that recomputes auto-graded answers for all attempts); adding/removing questions or changing points/type is blocked with an explanation.\n\n### FR-4 Course quizzes tab\n1. Register course tab \"Quizzes\". Teacher: list with status, window, attempts count, average score, \"Needs grading\" count. Student: Upcoming (opens in…), Available now (with \"Start\" / \"Resume\"), Completed (score if visible), Missed. Parent: read-only completed results.\n\n### FR-5 Quiz player (`/quizzes/[quizId]/take`)\n1. Start screen: instructions, question count, total points, time limit, attempts used / allowed. \"Start attempt\" confirms because the timer starts immediately.\n2. Starting creates an attempt with frozen `questionOrder` (shuffled when enabled) and per-attempt option order (deterministic shuffle seeded by attempt id), and computes `deadlineAt`.\n3. Layout (MUI `RadioGroup`/`FormGroup` of `Checkbox`es/`TextField` per question type, `LinearProgress` for completion): all questions on one scrollable page, or one per page with a question navigator grid of MUI `Button`s (answered / unanswered / flagged-for-review states). Sticky header with title, timer (mm:ss, turns red under 2 minutes, screen-reader announcement at 5 and 1 minutes remaining) and \"Submit\".\n4. Autosave: every answer change is sent `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId` debounced 800 ms; failures are queued in `localStorage` and retried every 5 seconds; a status pill shows \"All answers saved\" / \"Saving…\" / \"Offline — answers saved on this device\".\n5. Timer is display only; the server rejects answer writes after `deadlineAt + 30 s` grace and auto-submits.\n6. Submit confirms, listing unanswered question count. On submit: auto-grade, set status `NEEDS_GRADING` if any ESSAY (or SHORT_ANSWER with no match flagged for review) else `GRADED`.\n7. Auto-submit: any IN_PROGRESS attempt past `deadlineAt` is submitted with `autoSubmitted = true` lazily when the student or teacher next loads it, and by `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts()` in the maintenance run.\n8. Only one IN_PROGRESS attempt per student per quiz; opening the quiz in a second tab resumes the same attempt.\n\n### FR-6 Results\n1. Visibility: IMMEDIATELY → right after submit; AFTER_CLOSE → after `availableUntil`; MANUAL → after the teacher clicks \"Release results\". Until then students see \"Submitted — results will be available later.\"\n2. Result page: score, percentage, per-question correctness, the student's response, correct answer and explanation (only when `showCorrectAnswers`), teacher feedback.\n3. Quiz score for a student = scoring policy across GRADED attempts (HIGHEST, LATEST or AVERAGE), exposed via `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` for PRD-11.\n\n### FR-7 Manual grading (`/courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/grade`)\n1. Two modes: \"By student\" (one attempt at a time) and \"By question\" (all students' answers to one question, ideal for essays). Inputs: points (0 – question points, step 0.5), feedback. Override for auto-graded answers.\n2. When all answers of an attempt are graded, the attempt becomes GRADED and the score recomputes.\n\n### FR-8 Analytics tab (teacher)\n1. Summary: attempts, average, median, highest, lowest, average time taken, score distribution histogram (10 % buckets, MUI X `BarChart`).\n2. Per-question table: % correct, average points, and for choice questions the distribution of selected options (highlights the most chosen wrong option). CSV export of all attempts (student, attempt, score, per-question points).\n\n### FR-9 Accommodations\n1. On the quiz settings page, a teacher can grant individual students extra time and extra attempts (`QuizAccommodation`), used in `deadlineAt` and attempt-limit checks.\n\n### FR-10 Notifications\n1. `quiz.published` → enrolled students when published (default email false).\n2. `quiz.results_released` → student + parents when results become visible (for AFTER_CLOSE, sent by the maintenance run once after close; for MANUAL on release; for IMMEDIATELY no notification).\n","numLines":142,"startLine":93,"totalLines":282}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UtS6hXeHwTvH9TCVZYBP3g","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
