gn elements: StudentAttempt.serverNow (timer skew correction, display only); ManagerQuiz.locked/publishProblems/totalPoints; POST /attempts returns 201 on create and 200 on resume; submit is idempotent and returns StudentResult.\",\n    \"No HTTP endpoint for getStudentQuizScore (TS export for PRD-11), the grading workspace reads, the analytics page reads, or the accommodations list. Server pages call the services directly.\",\n    \"Stale leftovers from SH-9: artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json, artifacts/dev-planning/* and artifacts/dev/* must be regenerated for SH-10, not reused.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"devGates\": [\n    \"NFR-4 / ADR-7: dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before writing any UI component; if it is unreachable, stop and report. This does not block dev-planning.\",\n    \"ADR-2: the partial unique index quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq is raw SQL in the migration. Dev and CI must use prisma migrate, never db push.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":11,"newStart":1,"newLines":11,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T10:58:00Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"SH-10\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T13:05:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"architect\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\","," ","   \"status\": \"complete\",","-  \"endpointCount\": 16,","+  \"endpointCount\": 19,","   \"artifacts\": [","     \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",","     \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\","]},{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":19,"newStart":13,"newLines":18,"lines":["     \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"","   ],","   \"notes\": [","-    \"16 new route methods matching system-design §2.7. Base path is /api (existing convention), not /api/v1. Envelopes, error codes and pagination come from src/server/http.ts. Only the grading roster (GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions) is paginated.\",","-    \"Decimals are strings in all responses (D5). Student/parent submission payloads always go through toStudentSubmission (grade fields null until RETURNED, no history).\",","-    \"Save & return = PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade {return:true} (D6). With a rubric the server derives rawScore (D7).\",","-    \"Student list rows carry a server-computed group (UPCOMING/MISSING/SUBMITTED/RETURNED/CLOSED); CLOSED = past due but exempt or NO_SUBMISSION.\",","-    \"Reused, unchanged contracts: POST /api/files, GET /api/files/:id (new resolvers + D11 header), POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (now runs sendDueReminders).\",","-    \"artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json and artifacts/dev-planning/*, artifacts/dev/* are stale leftovers from earlier tickets and must be regenerated, not reused.\"","+    \"19 endpoint entries. 18 are new route methods in 14 route files (system-design §3.3). 1 is the existing POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, whose contract is unchanged; it gains two maintenance calls (FR-18, FR-30, FR-35).\",","+    \"Base path is /api (existing convention), not /api/v1. Envelopes, error codes and pagination come from src/server/http.ts. Only GET /api/courses/:id/quizzes is paginated.\",","+    \"Decimals are fixed2 strings in all responses. Student and parent payloads come only from serializers.ts (toStudentQuiz / toStudentAttempt / toStudentResult); `correct`/explanation appear only in StudentResult when resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers (NFR-1).\",","+    \"Contract decision: the manual grade body field is `pointsAwarded` (PRD API table), not `points` as written in system-design §3.2. manualGradeSchema must use pointsAwarded.\",","+    \"Contract additions inside existing design elements: StudentAttempt.serverNow (timer skew correction, display only); ManagerQuiz.locked/publishProblems/totalPoints; POST /attempts returns 201 on create and 200 on resume; submit is idempotent and returns StudentResult.\",","+    \"No HTTP endpoint for getStudentQuizScore (TS export for PRD-11), the grading workspace reads, the analytics page reads, or the accommodations list. Server pages call the services directly.\",","+    \"Stale leftovers from SH-9: artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json, artifacts/dev-planning/* and artifacts/dev/* must be regenerated for SH-10, not reused.\"","   ],","-  \"blockers\": [","-    \"NFR-6 (hard gate for dev, does not block dev-planning): dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs for @mui/material 9.5.0 / MUI X 9.5.0) before writing UI, and must stop and report if it is unreachable.\",","-    \"ADR-2: the @mui/x-internals 9.1.0 override must be verified (npm ls + compile) before UI work; otherwise use the D2 fallbacks (MUI Table for FR-17, datetime-local for FR-9).\",","-    \"D11 relaxes X-Frame-Options to SAMEORIGIN for /api/files/:id only. Reviewer sign-off is recommended; the fallback is a PDF 'Open' link.\",","-    \"FR-41: studentTabs has no renderer, so the Assignments student tab will not be visible (the page works by URL). The platform CSP nonce fix is also out of scope (e2e uses bypassCSP).\",","-    \"LOW-confidence intake defaults adopted (FR-15, FR-52, FR-60; see D12). Human sign-off is needed if they should change.\"","+  \"blockers\": [],","+  \"devGates\": [","+    \"NFR-4 / ADR-7: dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before writing any UI component; if it is unreachable, stop and report. This does not block dev-planning.\",","+    \"ADR-2: the partial unique index quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq is raw SQL in the migration. Dev and CI must use prisma migrate, never db push.\"","   ],","   \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\""," }"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T10:58:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 16,\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"16 new route methods matching system-design §2.7. Base path is /api (existing convention), not /api/v1. Envelopes, error codes and pagination come from src/server/http.ts. Only the grading roster (GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions) is paginated.\",\n    \"Decimals are strings in all responses (D5). Student/parent submission payloads always go through toStudentSubmission (grade fields null until RETURNED, no history).\",\n    \"Save & return = PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade {return:true} (D6). With a rubric the server derives rawScore (D7).\",\n    \"Student list rows carry a server-computed group (UPCOMING/MISSING/SUBMITTED/RETURNED/CLOSED); CLOSED = past due but exempt or NO_SUBMISSION.\",\n    \"Reused, unchanged contracts: POST /api/files, GET /api/files/:id (new resolvers + D11 header), POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (now runs sendDueReminders).\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json and artifacts/dev-planning/*, artifacts/dev/* are stale leftovers from earlier tickets and must be regenerated, not reused.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"NFR-6 (hard gate for dev, does not block dev-planning): dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs for @mui/material 9.5.0 / MUI X 9.5.0) before writing UI, and must stop and report if it is unreachable.\",\n    \"ADR-2: the @mui/x-internals 9.1.0 override must be verified (npm ls + compile) before UI work; otherwise use the D2 fallbacks (MUI Table for FR-17, datetime-local for FR-9).\",\n    \"D11 relaxes X-Frame-Options to SAMEORIGIN for /api/files/:id only. Reviewer sign-off is recommended; the fallback is a PDF 'Open' link.\",\n    \"FR-41: studentTabs has no renderer, so the Assignments student tab will not be visible (the page works by URL). The platform CSP nonce fix is also out of scope (e2e uses bypassCSP).\",\n    \"LOW-confidence intake defaults adopted (FR-15, FR-52, FR-60; see D12). Human sign-off is needed if they should change.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FjbPiCuFCcpHQ7ronMVLB9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
