{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrwBgRfZv7usMxdyiPQi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The SH-10 architect phase is finished: `artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json` is written, then `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` (status complete, no blockers). Both files parse as valid JSON, and every requirement id they cite exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n- **Old files replaced:** the `api-contracts.json` and handoff already on disk were left over from SH-9, so I overwrote both.\n- **What the contracts cover:** 19 endpoints. 18 are new and match the route list in `system-design.md` §3.3. The 19th is the existing cron route (`POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`). Its request and response stay the same; it just also auto-submits expired attempts and sends the after-close results notifications. Each endpoint lists who can call it, its request and response shapes, its errors and its requirement ids.\n- **Conventions:** the API follows the project's existing patterns rather than the template. The base path is `/api`, not `/api/v1`. Responses use the shared envelopes and error codes from `src/server/http.ts`. Decimals are returned as 2-decimal strings.\n- **Hiding answers from students:** students and parents only ever get output from the student serializers. Correct answers and explanations appear only on the result view, and only once results are visible and the quiz has \"show correct answers\" turned on.\n\nDecisions dev-planning should know about:\n- **Grade field name:** the manual-grade request body uses `pointsAwarded`, as the PRD's API table does. `system-design.md` §3.2 calls it `points`, so the validator needs to follow the contract.\n- **Small additions:**\n  - The in-progress attempt includes a `serverNow` timestamp so the display-only timer can correct for a wrong clock on the student's device.\n  - Starting an attempt returns 201 for a new attempt and 200 when resuming one.\n  - Submitting an already-submitted attempt returns its current state instead of an error.\n- **No HTTP route on purpose:**\n  - `getStudentQuizScore` is a TypeScript export that PRD-11 imports directly.\n  - The grading, analytics and accommodations pages read through the services from server pages; only their writes go through the API.\n\n`threat-model-notes.json` and everything under `artifacts/dev-planning/` and `artifacts/dev/` are still SH-9 leftovers. They need to be regenerated for SH-10, and the handoff says so."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":179,"cache_read_input_tokens":84721,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":179,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2cdffa8-12d1-4e17-864e-e6653bd23adc","uuid":"1afea44c-cdd7-49ce-ad92-cd00ab3fb90b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:09:43.908Z","request_id":"req_011CgrwBgEGCkfrrrrDKRZsv"}
