{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017oB3sKycyLrB8C1mfgDU9a","type":"tool_result","content":"229:## API\n230-\n231-| Method & path | Role | Notes |\n232-|---|---|---|\n233-| `GET/POST /api/grading-scales`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/grading-scales/:id` | GET any, write ADMIN | |\n234-| `GET/PUT /api/courses/:id/grade-categories` | GET view, PUT manage | PUT replaces full list, validates total 100 |\n235-| `GET /api/courses/:id/gradebook?termId=` | manage | Items, students, grades, computed results |\n236-| `POST /api/courses/:id/grade-items` | manage | Manual items |\n237-| `PATCH /api/grade-items/:id` · `DELETE` | manage | Manual only for most fields; `isVisible` for all |\n238-| `PUT /api/grade-items/:id/grades/:studentId` | manage | `{ score?, excused?, missing?, comment? }` |\n239-| `PUT /api/courses/:id/term-overrides/:studentId` | manage | `{ termId, percent?, letter?, teacherComment? }` |\n240-| `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId=` | view student | Only visible items |\n241-| `GET /api/report-cards?termId=&gradeLevelId=&sectionId=` | ADMIN, homeroom TEACHER | |\n242-| `POST /api/report-cards/generate` | ADMIN | `{ termId, studentIds }` |\n243-| `GET /api/report-cards/:id` | ADMIN, teachers of student, student/parents when published | |\n244-| `PATCH /api/report-cards/:id` | ADMIN, homeroom teacher (homeroom comment only) | |\n245-| `POST /api/report-cards/publish` · `/unpublish` | ADMIN | `{ ids, reason? }` |\n246-\n247-## Non-Functional Requirements\n248-\n249-1. **Correctness:** calculation lives in pure functions with exhaustive unit tests; all arithmetic in `Decimal`.\n250-2. **Performance:** gradebook for 35 students × 80 items loads in under 800 ms; computing term grades for 600 students × 8 courses for report card generation finishes in under 30 seconds.\n251-3. **Auditability:** every manual grade change and override writes an audit entry with old and new values.\n252-4. **Privacy:** hidden items and unreturned scores never appear in student or parent responses.\n253-\n254-## Acceptance Criteria\n255-\n256-1. Given the FR-3.6 example, then the gradebook and the student Grades tab both show 78.0 % C+.\n257-2. Given Homework has `dropLowest = 1` and scores 50 %, 90 %, 100 %, then the Homework category percent excludes the 50 %.\n258-3. Given a returned assignment, then its score appears in the gradebook without manual entry; given a graded-but-not-returned submission, then it does not appear to the student.\n259-4. Given category weights totalling 90, when the teacher saves, then the save is refused with the live sum showing 90 / 100.\n260-5. Given an item past due marked missing, then it counts as 0; given it is excused, then it does not count.\n261-6. Given a letter-only override of \"B\" for Sam, then Sam's card shows the computed percent and letter B.\n262-7. Given an admin generates drafts for 7A and publishes them, then Sam and Pat receive a `report_card.published` notification and can open the print view; a student in 7B cannot open Sam's card.\n263-8. Given a published report card, when a teacher changes a grade, then the published card's snapshot does not change.\n264-9. Given the print view, when printed, then each student's card fits on A4 pages without the app sidebar.\n265-\n266-## Test Requirements\n267-\n268-- Unit: full calculation matrix (no categories, empty categories, drop lowest, missing vs ungraded, overrides, rounding at band edges like 89.95 → 90.0 → A).\n269-- Integration: sync hooks from assignment return and quiz grading; backfill idempotency; snapshot immutability.\n97-enum ReportCardStatus { DRAFT PUBLISHED }\n98-\n99:model GradingScale {\n100-  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n101-  name      String                     // \"Standard A–F\"\n102-  isDefault Boolean  @default(false)\n103-  bands     Json                       // [{ letter: \"A\", minPercent: 90, gpa?: 4.0, descriptor: \"Excellent\" }], sorted desc\n104-  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n105-  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n106-}\n107-\n108-model GradeCategory {\n109-  id            String   @id @default(cuid())\n110-  courseId      String\n111-  course        Course   @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n112-  name          String                     // \"Homework\"\n113-  weightPercent Decimal  @db.Decimal(5, 2) // 0–100; a course's categories total 100\n114-  dropLowest    Int      @default(0)       // drop N lowest scores in this category per student\n115-  order         Int\n116-}\n117-\n118-model GradeItem {\n119-  id          String          @id @default(cuid())\n120-  courseId    String\n121-  course      Course          @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n122-  categoryId  String?\n123-  category    GradeCategory?  @relation(fields: [categoryId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n124-  termId      String\n125-  term        Term            @relation(fields: [termId], references: [id])\n126-  title       String\n127-  maxPoints   Decimal         @db.Decimal(6, 2)\n128-  dueAt       DateTime?\n129-  source      GradeItemSource\n130-  sourceId    String?         @unique       // assignmentId or quizId\n131-  isVisible   Boolean         @default(true) // hidden items do not show to students/parents and do not count\n132-  createdAt   DateTime        @default(now())\n133-  updatedAt   DateTime        @updatedAt\n134-  grades      Grade[]\n135-}\n136-\n137-model Grade {\n138-  gradeItemId String\n139-  gradeItem   GradeItem @relation(fields: [gradeItemId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n140-  studentId   String\n141-  score       Decimal?  @db.Decimal(6, 2)  // null = not graded yet\n142-  excused     Boolean   @default(false)    // excluded from calculation\n143-  missing     Boolean   @default(false)    // counts as 0 when the item is past due\n144-  comment     String?\n145-  updatedById String\n146-  updatedAt   DateTime  @updatedAt\n147-  @@id([gradeItemId, studentId])\n148-  @@index([studentId])\n149-}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2823560b-6b63-4da8-95f5-9dff2410c0ed","uuid":"11cada9a-7aec-41e3-a2df-9b5ae94516f5","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:09:04.551Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"229:## API\n230-\n231-| Method & path | Role | Notes |\n232-|---|---|---|\n233-| `GET/POST /api/grading-scales`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/grading-scales/:id` | GET any, write ADMIN | |\n234-| `GET/PUT /api/courses/:id/grade-categories` | GET view, PUT manage | PUT replaces full list, validates total 100 |\n235-| `GET /api/courses/:id/gradebook?termId=` | manage | Items, students, grades, computed results |\n236-| `POST /api/courses/:id/grade-items` | manage | Manual items |\n237-| `PATCH /api/grade-items/:id` · `DELETE` | manage | Manual only for most fields; `isVisible` for all |\n238-| `PUT /api/grade-items/:id/grades/:studentId` | manage | `{ score?, excused?, missing?, comment? }` |\n239-| `PUT /api/courses/:id/term-overrides/:studentId` | manage | `{ termId, percent?, letter?, teacherComment? }` |\n240-| `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId=` | view student | Only visible items |\n241-| `GET /api/report-cards?termId=&gradeLevelId=&sectionId=` | ADMIN, homeroom TEACHER | |\n242-| `POST /api/report-cards/generate` | ADMIN | `{ termId, studentIds }` |\n243-| `GET /api/report-cards/:id` | ADMIN, teachers of student, student/parents when published | |\n244-| `PATCH /api/report-cards/:id` | ADMIN, homeroom teacher (homeroom comment only) | |\n245-| `POST /api/report-cards/publish` · `/unpublish` | ADMIN | `{ ids, reason? }` |\n246-\n247-## Non-Functional Requirements\n248-\n249-1. **Correctness:** calculation lives in pure functions with exhaustive unit tests; all arithmetic in `Decimal`.\n250-2. **Performance:** gradebook for 35 students × 80 items loads in under 800 ms; computing term grades for 600 students × 8 courses for report card generation finishes in under 30 seconds.\n251-3. **Auditability:** every manual grade change and override writes an audit entry with old and new values.\n252-4. **Privacy:** hidden items and unreturned scores never appear in student or parent responses.\n253-\n254-## Acceptance Criteria\n255-\n256-1. Given the FR-3.6 example, then the gradebook and the student Grades tab both show 78.0 % C+.\n257-2. Given Homework has `dropLowest = 1` and scores 50 %, 90 %, 100 %, then the Homework category percent excludes the 50 %.\n258-3. Given a returned assignment, then its score appears in the gradebook without manual entry; given a graded-but-not-returned submission, then it does not appear to the student.\n259-4. Given category weights totalling 90, when the teacher saves, then the save is refused with the live sum showing 90 / 100.\n260-5. Given an item past due marked missing, then it counts as 0; given it is excused, then it does not count.\n261-6. Given a letter-only override of \"B\" for Sam, then Sam's card shows the computed percent and letter B.\n262-7. Given an admin generates drafts for 7A and publishes them, then Sam and Pat receive a `report_card.published` notification and can open the print view; a student in 7B cannot open Sam's card.\n263-8. Given a published report card, when a teacher changes a grade, then the published card's snapshot does not change.\n264-9. Given the print view, when printed, then each student's card fits on A4 pages without the app sidebar.\n265-\n266-## Test Requirements\n267-\n268-- Unit: full calculation matrix (no categories, empty categories, drop lowest, missing vs ungraded, overrides, rounding at band edges like 89.95 → 90.0 → A).\n269-- Integration: sync hooks from assignment return and quiz grading; backfill idempotency; snapshot immutability.\n97-enum ReportCardStatus { DRAFT PUBLISHED }\n98-\n99:model GradingScale {\n100-  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n101-  name      String                     // \"Standard A–F\"\n102-  isDefault Boolean  @default(false)\n103-  bands     Json                     