 ReportCardSnapshotV1, Bands, …). validators/gradebook.ts and snapshot.ts should mirror them.\",","+    \"Contract decisions beyond system-design: PUT grade and PUT term-override return the recomputed StudentTermResult. PATCH scale isDefault:false on the current default is a VALIDATION_ERROR. The first scale created always becomes the default. mark-missing works on any source but only touches score-null rows. Report-card comments are max 1,000 chars. Unpublish reason is 1–500 chars. GET /api/report-cards mode A includes NOT_GENERATED rows.\",","+    \"No HTTP surface (by design) for FR-1, FR-3–FR-7, FR-41 (migration, sync hooks, seed), NFR-7/NFR-9/NFR-12 (UI, reuse and test rules). These are covered in system-design §2.1, §2.2, §2.5 and §6. Print pages call services directly (nonHttpContracts).\",","+    \"Stale leftovers from SH-10: artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json, artifacts/dev-planning/*, artifacts/dev/*, artifacts/qa/* and artifacts/ui-verification/* must be regenerated for SH-11, not reused.\"","   ],","   \"blockers\": [],","   \"devGates\": [","-    \"NFR-4 / ADR-7: dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before writing any UI component; if it is unreachable, stop and report. This does not block dev-planning.\",","-    \"ADR-2: the partial unique index quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq is raw SQL in the migration. Dev and CI must use prisma migrate, never db push.\"","+    \"NFR-7: dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before writing any UI component, especially the DataGrid keyboard editing for FR-20. If it's unreachable, stop and report. This does not block dev-planning.\",","+    \"FR-1/ADR-3: the partial unique index grading_scale_one_default is raw SQL in the migration. Use prisma migrate, never db push.\"","   ],","   \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\""," }"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-10\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T13:05:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 19,\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"19 endpoint entries. 18 are new route methods in 14 route files (system-design §3.3). 1 is the existing POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, whose contract is unchanged; it gains two maintenance calls (FR-18, FR-30, FR-35).\",\n    \"Base path is /api (existing convention), not /api/v1. Envelopes, error codes and pagination come from src/server/http.ts. Only GET /api/courses/:id/quizzes is paginated.\",\n    \"Decimals are fixed2 strings in all responses. Student and parent payloads come only from serializers.ts (toStudentQuiz / toStudentAttempt / toStudentResult); `correct`/explanation appear only in StudentResult when resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers (NFR-1).\",\n    \"Contract decision: the manual grade body field is `pointsAwarded` (PRD API table), not `points` as written in system-design §3.2. manualGradeSchema must use pointsAwarded.\",\n    \"Contract additions inside existing design elements: StudentAttempt.serverNow (timer skew correction, display only); ManagerQuiz.locked/publishProblems/totalPoints; POST /attempts returns 201 on create and 200 on resume; submit is idempotent and returns StudentResult.\",\n    \"No HTTP endpoint for getStudentQuizScore (TS export for PRD-11), the grading workspace reads, the analytics page reads, or the accommodations list. Server pages call the services directly.\",\n    \"Stale leftovers from SH-9: artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json, artifacts/dev-planning/* and artifacts/dev/* must be regenerated for SH-10, not reused.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"devGates\": [\n    \"NFR-4 / ADR-7: dev must reach mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before writing any UI component; if it is unreachable, stop and report. This does not block