n**`artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json`** has 20 endpoints, covering everything in the PRD API table:\n- **Grading scales:** list, create, update and delete.\n- **Course setup:** read and replace grade categories (weights must total 100, or the list can be empty), plus the gradebook read with `?format=csv` for export.\n- **Grade items and grades:** create, edit and delete manual items, set all ungraded to missing, and save one grade cell. The term override save is also here.\n- **Student grades:** the student and parent grades view.\n- **Report cards:** list, generate drafts, read one, edit comments, publish and unpublish.\n\nIt follows the app's existing conventions: base path `/api` rather than `/api/v1`, and the success/error formats and error codes from `src/server/http.ts`. Decimals come in as a number or string with at most 2 decimals and go out as 2-decimal strings; computed percents are 1-decimal strings. Shapes used in several places are defined once and referenced. These include the per-student term result, the version-1 report card snapshot and the grading scale bands. Notifications, the backfill script and the print pages are listed separately because they have no API endpoint.\n\nI made some decisions that weren't in `system-design.md`:\n- **Mark missing:** `POST /api/grade-items/:id/mark-missing` is the only route not in the PRD. It works on any item type but only touches grades with no score, so it never changes a synced score.\n- **Default scale:** setting the current default scale to non-default is rejected, and the first scale ever created always becomes the default.\n- **Edit responses:** saving a grade cell or a term override returns the student's recalculated term result, so the grid can refresh the totals.\n- **Report card list:** without `studentId` it includes students with no card yet (\"Not generated\"). With `studentId`, students and parents see published cards only.\n- **Limits:** report card comments are capped at 1,000 characters, and the unpublish reason must be 1–500 characters.\n\n**`artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json`**: status complete, 20 endpoints, no blockers. It carries two warnings for the dev phase. Dev must reach the MUI docs server (mui-mcp) before writing UI, and the migration must be applied with `prisma migrate`, not `db push`.\n\nSome requirements have no API endpoint: the migration, the sync hooks, the seed data, and the UI, reuse and test rules. `system-design.md` covers them. `threat-model-notes.json` and everything under dev-planning, dev, qa and ui-verification are still from SH-10. Those phases need to regenerate them for SH-11.","ttft_ms":3245,"type":"result","duration_ms":206465,"uuid":"dd4fdab9-542c-49f5-ba46-c79fadea33d1","ttft_stream_ms":1887,"time_to_request_ms":145,"first_content_frame_ms":1887,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":22,"outputTokens":24153,"cacheReadInputTokens":617526,"cacheCreationInputTokens":72603,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1874772,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":4579,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":72603,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
