{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsgRBABeqXjzPJGUZC2f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `arch-api-contracts` sub-task for SH-12 is done, so the whole architect phase is now complete. I wrote both files in `artifacts/architect/`: `api-contracts.json` first, then `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` last as the completion signal.\n\n**`api-contracts.json`** replaces the old SH-11 version that was still on disk. It defines 12 endpoints across 10 route files, matching the route table in `system-design.md` and the PRD's API list. The file also has a shared `components` section of request/response shapes that the Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts` should mirror. Two existing endpoints get new behaviour but keep their contracts:\n- **`/api/internal/email/dispatch`** gains the scheduled-publish pass that sends each scheduled announcement's notification once.\n- **`/api/files/:id`** gains the new `announcement` access context for cover images and attachments.\n\nA script confirmed the JSON parses and that every requirement id it cites exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n**Error rules:**\n- **403:** a teacher targets an audience they aren't allowed to (e.g. SCHOOL), or a student or parent hits a staff-only route.\n- **404:** the caller isn't allowed to see that announcement, so its existence isn't revealed.\n- **409:** the request conflicts with the announcement's state, such as an author editing an archived announcement or acknowledging one that doesn't require it.\n- **429:** a second reminder within 24 hours, with `details.retryAfter` telling the client when it can retry.\n\n**Decisions I made that go beyond the system design** (listed in the handoff for dev-planning to check):\n- Publishing or scheduling with zero recipients returns `VALIDATION_ERROR` with `details.reason = 'NO_RECIPIENTS'`.\n- Changing a published announcement back to draft returns 409; archiving is the way to take it down. Archiving twice is harmless.\n- Acknowledging also marks the announcement as read if it wasn't already.\n- A reminder with nobody left to remind still starts the 24-hour cooldown and returns `notified: 0`.\n- On page 1 of the feed, up to 3 pinned items go on top, and the page's `total` count doesn't include them.\n- The manage list takes an optional `?status` filter and allows at most 50 rows per page.\n- Read and acknowledged percentages are whole numbers, or `null` when there are no recipients.\n\n`artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json` is left over from SH-11. It isn't owned by any architect sub-task, so I didn't touch it; it may confuse downstream phases."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1148,"cache_read_input_tokens":71508,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1148,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76e7b8df-be53-412b-af2c-ced0a46be4d2","uuid":"c36acc4a-cbda-4225-b7b7-81b3a7c64e90","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:36:37.878Z","request_id":"req_011CgsgRAv3zWwMSXYFEztpQ"}
