ikramaansari  staff   609 Nov  9 18:46 task-completion-markers.json\n\nartifacts/intake/:\ntotal 72\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  9 22:17 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    701 Nov  9 22:17 handoff-to-architect.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16742 Nov  9 22:16 requirements.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    914 Nov  9 22:17 tech-stack.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   5015 Nov  9 22:17 user-stories.md\n\nartifacts/qa/:\ntotal 48\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 ikramaansari  staff    128 Nov  9 19:37 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   7087 Nov  9 19:31 coverage-report.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  13745 Nov  9 19:37 qa-report.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry/:\ntotal 72\ndrwxr-xr-x   7 ikramaansari  staff    224 Oct 16 20:25 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  11510 Nov  9 21:40 api-retries.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    133 Nov  9 22:14 daemon-handoff.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1963 Nov  9 22:17 knowledge-log.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  12174 Nov  9 22:17 metering.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1328 Nov  9 22:24 phase-sessions.json\n\nartifacts/ui-verification/:\ntotal 104\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  9 21:01 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  43 ikramaansari  staff   1376 Nov  9 20:17 screenshots\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  18457 Nov  9 20:55 ui-verification-report.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   9530 Nov  9 21:01 ui-verification-report.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16518 Nov  9 20:12 uiv-raw.json\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-13\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-13: Direct Messaging\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-013 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-13.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageReport, MessagingSettings, MessageRevision or PendingMessageEmail models, no ReportStatus enum, and no User.isSafeguardingLead. All need one new migration plus back-relations on User and FileObject.\",\n    \"PRD-12 (Announcements) is NOT present in the workspace: there is no Announcement model, and artifacts/run-summary.json shows SH-12 with succeeded=false. PRD-13 only mentions announcements under Out of Scope, so this does not block messaging. Do not build announcements in this run.\",\n    \"Course has teacherId plus coTeacherIds String[]. 'A course the teacher manages' is read as teacherId OR coTeacherIds (MEDIUM). Section.homeroomTeacherId covers homeroom. Enrollment.status ACTIVE/DROPPED covers ended relationships. ParentStudentLink covers parent links.\",\n    \"The student detail route is src/app/(app)/students/[id], not [studentId]. Keep the existing segment name. The PRD forbids renaming routes.\",\n    \"Shared components live in src/components/<Name>/ (FileList, FileUpload, UserAvatar, UserPicker, ConfirmDialog, Toast, NotificationBell, EmptyState, PageHeader), not src/components/shared/. Reuse them where they are.\",\n    \"The maintenance run is POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (it already calls the quiz maintenance jobs). PendingMessageEmail processing hooks in there.\",\n    \"src/server/rate-limit.ts rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) already exists. Use it for 30 messages/min/user.\",\n    \"src/server/files/access.ts registerFileAccess(context, resolver) already exists. The 'message' context registers through it.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exports requireUser/requireRole/requirePageUser/requirePageRole. Notification types are in src/server/notifications/types.ts, and the COMMUNICATION category already exists.\",\n    \"There is no admin user-management page under src/app/(app)/admin. The users API exists at src/app/api/users/[id]. 'Editable on the admin user form' means extending the existing user update validator/API, plus whichever form currently edits users (architect to locate).\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageReport (+ ReportStatus enum OPEN/REVIEWED/DISMISSED) and MessagingSettings with the fields, relations, cascades and indexes given in the PRD.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model (prisma block)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add isSafeguardingLead Boolean @default(false) to User, meaningful only for ADMIN and editable on the admin user form.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model (closing paragraph)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add a MessageRevision model { messageId, body, createdAt } that stores the original body every time a message is edited.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Add a PendingMessageEmail table { userId, conversationId, dueAt } that drives deferred message emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Implement canMessage(sender, recipient) in src/server/messaging/contact-rules.ts using the full sender→recipient matrix (admin always; teacher↔admin/teacher; teacher→student/parent via ACTIVE enrollment in a managed course or homeroom section; student→own teachers/admin; parent→linked child's teachers/admin; student→student/parent and parent→parent/student never).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Creating a conversation requires canMessage(creator, each other participant) and a maximum of 25 participants. A group containing a STUDENT must include at least one TEACHER or ADMIN. Students in a staff-created group may reply but cannot start conversations with each other. On violation return 403 and create nothing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1; Acceptance Criterion 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Contact rules are re-checked on every send. If the relationship has ended, the non-staff party is refused and the composer shows 'You can no longer send messages in this conversation.' Staff can still send.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; Acceptance Criterion 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"GET /api/messaging/contacts?q= returns only messageable users, grouped by labels such as 'My teachers', 'My child's teachers (<child>)', 'Students in <course>', 'Parents of students in <course>' and 'School office'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Build the /messages inbox: two panes, collapsing to a single pane with back navigation below 768px. The conversation list is sorted by lastMessageAt and shows participant names or subject, a 'sender: text' preview, time and an unread badge. It has search by participant name/subject and Inbox/Archived tabs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Build the message thread: sender avatar and name, timestamps grouped by day (school timezone), attachments via FileList, an 'edited' marker, deleted messages shown as 'This message was deleted', and upward infinite scroll at 30 messages per page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Build the composer: textarea where Enter sends and Shift+Enter adds a newline, up to 5 attachments with file context 'message', and a character counter shown after 4,500 characters (body is 1–5,000 chars).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3; FR-1 Message.body comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Build the new-conversation dialog: multi-select recipient picker fed by the contacts endpoint, optional subject (max 120) and a first message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4; FR-1 Conversation.subject comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Polling: the visible active thread polls GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?after=<lastId> every 5s. The conversation list and the sidebar unread badge poll every 30s.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; Acceptance Criterion 8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Opening a thread updates lastReadAt. A per-conversation menu offers mute, archive/unarchive (per user), view participants, and leave group. The creator of a group that contains students cannot leave it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Senders can edit or soft-delete their own messages within 15 minutes of sending. Later edits or deletes are refused. Users can never hard-delete a message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.7; API PATCH/DELETE /api/messages/:id; NFR Retention\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Student page header actions: 'Message parents' (TEACHER/ADMIN) starts a group with the student's linked parents, and 'Message teacher' (PARENT) opens a picker of the child's teachers.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1; Goal 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Message selected students' action to the course roster (TEACHER).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar 'Messages' entry with an unread count for all roles in src/config/navigation.ts, backed by GET /api/messaging/unread-count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Register notification type message.received (COMMUNICATION, default email true). On send, give each non-muted other participant one in-app notification per conversation, replacing older unread message.received rows for that conversation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Send the message email only if the recipient has not read the conversation within 10 minutes and it is outside their quiet hours (deferred until quiet hours end). The maintenance run sends it from PendingMessageEmail.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Quiet hours' section to /account/notifications (start/end HH:mm in the school timezone, may wrap midnight), stored in MessagingSettings via GET/PUT /api/me/messaging-settings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Any participant can report a message with a reason (max 1,000 chars) via POST /api/messages/:id/report. The reporter sees 'Reported — the school will review this.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; FR-1 MessageReport.reason comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/safeguarding Reports queue (ADMIN with isSafeguardingLead only, others get 403). Open reports come first, each with the message, context of 5 messages before and after, and participants. Actions: Mark reviewed (with note) and Dismiss.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Build the safeguarding Conversations search: lists conversations with involvesStudent = true, filterable by participant and date, with a read-only view that includes deleted content and the original text of edited messages.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Every safeguarding view of a conversation writes an audit entry 'safeguarding.conversation.view' via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Register notification type message.reported (mandatory in-app, email true) and notify all safeguarding leads on each new report.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Register file-access context 'message': conversation participants and safeguarding leads may access attachments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Implement the REST API listed in the PRD: conversations list/create/get, messages list (before/after)/send, message edit/delete/report, read/mute/archive/leave, unread-count, contacts, safeguarding reports and conversations, and me/messaging-settings. Use the standard response/error shapes and pagination.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Platform Context code conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Seed: Alice Admin is a safeguarding lead. Add conversations Pat↔Tom about Sam's homework (6 msgs), Tom→MATH-7A group of 4 students (3 msgs), Tina↔Tom staff chat (4 msgs), and one reported message in a student↔teacher conversation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Conversation.involvesStudent is computed when the conversation is created (true if any participant is a STUDENT) and is used for safeguarding search.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Conversation.involvesStudent comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Message send updates Conversation.lastMessageAt so list ordering and polling reflect new activity.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1 lastMessageAt field; FR-3.1 sort order (inferred)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"'A course the teacher manages' includes courses where the teacher is Course.teacherId or appears in Course.coTeacherIds.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-2 table 'course the teacher manages' (inferred from existing Course schema)\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Security: every messaging and safeguarding endpoint and server page checks participation, role or isSafeguardingLead on the server. Conversation cuids are never treated as authorisation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 1 Security; Goal 2; Code conventions (requireRole)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: polling endpoints respond in under 100 ms using the (conversationId, createdAt) index and return empty arrays when nothing changed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 2 Performance\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Retention: users never hard-delete messages. Soft-deleted content and edit revisions stay available to safeguarding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 3 Retention; FR-1 Message.deletedAt comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Rate limit: POST /api/conversations/:id/messages allows 30 messages/min/user and returns 429 RATE_LIMITED beyond that (reuse src/server/rate-limit.ts).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table (POST messages notes)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element uses only MUI (@mui/material v9, icons-material, MUI X packages), looked up through the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs) before use. No banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, notistack, etc.). QA checks for banned imports and checks that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context — UI component rule items 1–6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Conventions: thin Zod-validated handlers (src/lib/validators/messaging.ts), services in src/server/messaging/, standard success/list/error response shapes, cuid ids, UTC storage with school-timezone display, and logger instead of console.log.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context — Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Responsive: below 768 px the inbox switches to a single pane with back navigation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Near-real-time: a message sent in one browser appears in another open thread within 6 seconds via polling. No websockets.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Acceptance Criterion 8; Out of Scope (websockets)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Scope guard: no voice/video, typing indicators, reactions, E2E encryption, websockets or broadcast messaging. Do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope; Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for the full contact-rule matrix (groups, ended relationships); integration tests for notification collapsing, quiet-hours deferral and edit revision capture; Playwright parent→teacher round trip in two contexts and student→student block. The existing lint/typecheck/test suite stays green.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements; Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Mutations on records owned by someone else (e.g. safeguarding review of reports) write an AuditLog row via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code conventions (audit rule) applied to FR-6.2 actions\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-32: Do co-teachers (Course.coTeacherIds) count as 'managing' a course for contact rules?\",\n        \"FR-1 conflicts with convention: Conversation, Message, MessageReport, MessageAttachment and MessagingSettings in the PRD's Prisma block lack updatedAt, while conventions say every model has createdAt/updatedAt. Should updatedAt be added?\",\n        \"FR-2: There is no admin user-management page in src/app/(app)/admin. Where should isSafeguardingLead be edited — an existing user edit form elsewhere, or only via PATCH /api/users/:id?\",\n        \"FR-5.1: Should quiet hours apply to all roles or only teachers? The user story mentions teachers, but the settings endpoint is open to any role.\",\n        \"PRD-12 dependency: SH-12 (Announcements) is not implemented in the workspace. Confirm messaging can proceed independently.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-32 co-teacher scope — proceeding with teacherId OR coTeacherIds (MEDIUM).\",\n        \"updatedAt on new models — architect to decide. Default: add updatedAt per the platform convention. The PRD block is treated as the minimum field set.\",\n        \"Location of the isSafeguardingLead edit UI — architect to locate the existing user edit form. If none exists, extend the user update API/validator only.\",\n        \"Quiet hours role scope — proceeding with all roles (the settings endpoint is 'any').\",\n        \"PRD-12 absence — proceeding. Messaging does not depend on announcement code.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-13\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 43,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"PRD-12 (Announcements) is not implemented in the workspace (SH-12 run failed). PRD-13 does not depend on it at the code level. Proceed.\",\n    \"Open architect decisions are listed in requirements.json clarificationLog[0].unresolved: co-teacher scope, updatedAt on new models, where isSafeguardingLead is edited, quiet-hours role scope.\",\n    \"The student route segment is [id], not [studentId]. Shared components live in src/components/<Name>/.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2e59def-a937-4e61-837c-a8e39741caba","uuid":"d5c5559b-a9fd-4a13-853d-6a499f04d954","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:25:07.893Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"artifacts/approvals/:\ntotal 24\ndrwxr-xr-x   5 ikramaansari  staff  160 Nov  5 11:58 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff  384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  173 Nov  5 11:45 architect-approval.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  176 Nov  5 11:58 dev-planning-approval.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  170 Nov  5 11:37 intake-approval.json\n\nartifacts/architect/:\ntotal 232\ndrwxr-xr-x   8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Nov  9 22:24 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  28616 Nov  9 21:36 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   2222 Nov  9 21:36 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  27731 Nov  9 22:21 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  34704 Nov  9 22:24 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16178 Nov  9 22:20 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    397 Nov  9 21:36 threat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning/:\ntotal 80\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  9 21:37 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   6467 Nov  9 21:38 file-ownership-matrix.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   5354 Nov  9 21:37 file-structure.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  17996 Nov  9 21:38 implementation-plan.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   2228 Nov  9 21:38 module-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/dev/:\ntotal 40\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff   192 Nov  9 18:54 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff   384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  8004 Nov  9 18:54 dev-log.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   150 Nov  9 21:40 dev-rerun-count.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   147 Nov  9 21:40 security-scan-report.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   609 Nov  9 18:46 task-completion-markers.json\n\nartifacts/intake/:\ntotal 72\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  9 22:17 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    701 Nov  9 22:17 handoff-to-architect.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16742 Nov  9 22:16 requirements.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    914 Nov  9 22:17 tech-stack.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   5015 Nov  9 22:17 user-stories.md\n\nartifacts/qa/:\ntotal 48\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 ikramaansari  staff    128 Nov  9 19:37 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   7087 Nov  9 19:31 coverage-report.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  13745 Nov  9 19:37 qa-report.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry/:\ntotal 72\ndrwxr-xr-x   7 ikramaansari  staff    224 Oct 16 20:25 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  11510 Nov  9 21:40 api-retries.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    133 Nov  9 22:14 daemon-handoff.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1963 Nov  9 22:17 knowledge-log.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  12174 Nov  9 22:17 metering.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1328 Nov  9 22:24 phase-sessions.json\n\nartifacts/ui-verification/:\ntotal 104\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  9 21:01 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  43 ikramaansari  staff   1376 Nov  9 20:17 screenshots\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  18457 Nov  9 20:55 ui-verification-report.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   9530 Nov  9 21:01 ui-verification-report.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16518 Nov  9 20:12 uiv-raw.json\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-13\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-13: Direct Messaging\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-013 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-13.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageReport, MessagingSettings, MessageRevision or PendingMessageEmail models, no ReportStatus enum, and no User.isSafeguardingLead. All need one new migration plus back-relations on User and FileObject.\",\n    \"PRD-12 (Announcements) is NOT present in the workspace: there is no Announcement model, and artifacts/run-summary.json shows SH-12 with succeeded=false. PRD-13 only mentions announcements under Out of Scope, so this does not block messaging. Do not build announcements in this run.\",\n    \"Course has teacherId plus coTeacherIds String[]. 'A course the teacher manages' is read as teacherId OR coTeacherIds (MEDIUM). Section.homeroomTeacherId covers homeroom. Enrollment.status ACTIVE/DROPPED covers ended relationships. ParentStudentLink covers parent links.\",\n    \"The student detail route is src/app/(app)/students/[id], not [studentId]. Keep the existing segment name. The PRD forbids renaming routes.\",\n    \"Shared components live in src/components/<Name>/ (FileList, FileUpload, UserAvatar, UserPicker, ConfirmDialog, Toast, NotificationBell, EmptyState, PageHeader), not src/components/shared/. Reuse them where they are.\",\n    \"The maintenance run is POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (it already calls the quiz maintenance jobs). PendingMessageEmail processing hooks in there.\",\n    \"src/server/rate-limit.ts rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) already exists. Use it for 30 messages/min/user.\",\n    \"src/server/files/access.ts registerFileAccess(context, resolver) already exists. The 'message' context registers through it.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exports requireUser/requireRole/requirePageUser/requirePageRole. Notification types are in src/server/notifications/types.ts, and the COMMUNICATION category already exists.\",\n    \"There is no admin user-management page under src/app/(app)/admin. The users API exists at src/app/api/users/[id]. 'Editable on the admin user form' means extending the existing user update validator/API, plus whichever form currently edits users (architect to locate).\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageReport (+ ReportStatus enum OPEN/REVIEWED/DISMISSED) and MessagingSettings with the fields, relations, cascades and indexes given in the PRD.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model (prisma block)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add isSafeguardingLead Boolean @default(false) to User, meaningful only for ADMIN and editable on the admin user form.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model (closing paragraph)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add a MessageRevision model { messageId, body, createdAt } that stores the original body every time a message is edited.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Add a PendingMessageEmail table { userId, conversationId, dueAt } that drives deferred message emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Implement canMessage(sender, recipient) in src/server/messaging/contact-rules.ts using the full sender→recipient matrix (admin always; teacher↔admin/teacher; teacher→student/parent via ACTIVE enrollment in a managed course or homeroom section; student→own teachers/admin; parent→linked child's teachers/admin; student→student/parent and parent→parent/student never).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Creating a conversation requires canMessage(creator, each other participant) and a maximum of 25 participants. A group containing a STUDENT must include at least one TEACHER or ADMIN. Students in a staff-created group may reply but cannot start conversations with each other. On violation return 403 and create nothing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1; Acceptance Criterion 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Contact rules are re-checked on every send. If the relationship has ended, the non-staff party is refused and the composer shows 'You can no longer send messages in this conversation.' Staff can still send.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; Acceptance Criterion 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"GET /api/messaging/contacts?q= returns only messageable users, grouped by labels such as 'My teachers', 'My child's teachers (<child>)', 'Students in <course>', 'Parents of students in <course>' and 'School office'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Build the /messages inbox: two panes, collapsing to a single pane with back navigation below 768px. The conversation list is sorted by lastMessageAt and shows participant names or subject, a 'sender: text' preview, time and an unread badge. It has search by participant name/subject and Inbox/Archived tabs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Build the message thread: sender avatar and name, timestamps grouped by day (school timezone), attachments via FileList, an 'edited' marker, deleted messages shown as 'This message was deleted', and upward infinite scroll at 30 messages per page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Build the composer: textarea where Enter sends and Shift+Enter adds a newline, up to 5 attachments with file context 'message', and a character counter shown after 4,500 characters (body is 1–5,000 chars).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3; FR-1 Message.body comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Build the new-conversation dialog: multi-select recipient picker fed by the contacts endpoint, optional subject (max 120) and a first message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4; FR-1 Conversation.subject comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Polling: the visible active thread polls GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?after=<lastId> every 5s. The conversation list and the sidebar unread badge poll every 30s.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; Acceptance Criterion 8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Opening a thread updates lastReadAt. A per-conversation menu offers mute, archive/unarchive (per user), view participants, and leave group. The creator of a group that contains students cannot leave it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Senders can edit or soft-delete their own messages within 15 minutes of sending. Later edits or deletes are refused. Users can never hard-delete a message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.7; API PATCH/DELETE /api/messages/:id; NFR Retention\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Student page header actions: 'Message parents' (TEACHER/ADMIN) starts a group with the student's linked parents, and 'Message teacher' (PARENT) opens a picker of the child's teachers.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1; Goal 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Message selected students' action to the course roster (TEACHER).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar 'Messages' entry with an unread count for all roles in src/config/navigation.ts, backed by GET /api/messaging/unread-count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Register notification type message.received (COMMUNICATION, default email true). On send, give each non-muted other participant one in-app notification per conversation, replacing older unread message.received rows for that conversation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Send the message email only if the recipient has not read the conversation within 10 minutes and it is outside their quiet hours (deferred until quiet hours end). The maintenance run sends it from PendingMessageEmail.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Quiet hours' section to /account/notifications (start/end HH:mm in the school timezone, may wrap midnight), stored in MessagingSettings via GET/PUT /api/me/messaging-settings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Any participant can report a message with a reason (max 1,000 chars) via POST /api/messages/:id/report. The reporter sees 'Reported — the school will review this.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; FR-1 MessageReport.reason comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/safeguarding Reports queue (ADMIN with isSafeguardingLead only, others get 403). Open reports come first, each with the message, context of 5 messages before and after, and participants. Actions: Mark reviewed (with note) and Dismiss.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Build the safeguarding Conversations search: lists conversations with involvesStudent = true, filterable by participant and date, with a read-only view that includes deleted content and the original text of edited messages.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Every safeguarding view of a conversation writes an audit entry 'safeguarding.conversation.view' via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Register notification type message.reported (mandatory in-app, email true) and notify all safeguarding leads on each new report.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Register file-access context 'message': conversation participants and safeguarding leads may access attachments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Implement the REST API listed in the PRD: conversations list/create/get, messages list (before/after)/send, message edit/delete/report, read/mute/archive/leave, unread-count, contacts, safeguarding reports and conversations, and me/messaging-settings. Use the standard response/error shapes and pagination.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Platform Context code conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Seed: Alice Admin is a safeguarding lead. Add conversations Pat↔Tom about Sam's homework (6 msgs), Tom→MATH-7A group of 4 students (3 msgs), Tina↔Tom staff chat (4 msgs), and one reported message in a student↔teacher conversation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Conversation.involvesStudent is computed when the conversation is created (true if any participant is a STUDENT) and is used for safeguarding search.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Conversation.involvesStudent comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Message send updates Conversation.lastMessageAt so list ordering and polling reflect new activity.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1 lastMessageAt field; FR-3.1 sort order (inferred)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"'A course the teacher manages' includes courses where the teacher is Course.teacherId or appears in Course.coTeacherIds.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-2 table 'course the teacher manages' (inferred from existing Course schema)\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Security: every messaging and safeguarding endpoint and server page checks participation, role or isSafeguardingLead on the server. Conversation cuids are never treated as authorisation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 1 Security; Goal 2; Code conventions (requireRole)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: polling endpoints respond in under 100 ms using the (conversationId, createdAt) index and return empty arrays when nothing changed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 2 Performance\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Retention: users never hard-delete messages. Soft-deleted content and edit revisions stay available to safeguarding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 3 Retention; FR-1 Message.deletedAt comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Rate limit: POST /api/conversations/:id/messages allows 30 messages/min/user and returns 429 RATE_LIMITED beyond that (reuse src/server/rate-limit.ts).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table (POST messages notes)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element uses only MUI (@mui/material v9, icons-material, MUI X packages), looked up through the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs) before use. No banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, notistack, etc.). QA checks for banned imports and checks that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context — UI component rule items 1–6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Conventions: thin Zod-validated handlers (src/lib/validators/messaging.ts), services in src/server/messaging/, standard success/list/error response shapes, cuid ids, UTC storage with school-timezone display, and logger instead of console.log.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context — Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Responsive: below 768 px the inbox switches to a single pane with back navigation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Near-real-time: a message sent in one browser appears in another open thread within 6 seconds via polling. No websockets.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Acceptance Criterion 8; Out of Scope (websockets)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Scope guard: no voice/video, typing indicators, reactions, E2E encryption, websockets or broadcast messaging. Do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope; Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for the full contact-rule matrix (groups, ended relationships); integration tests for notification collapsing, quiet-hours deferral and edit revision capture; Playwright parent→teacher round trip in two contexts and student→student block. The existing lint/typecheck/test suite stays green.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements; Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Mutations on records owned by someone else (e.g. safeguarding review of reports) write an AuditLog row via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code conventions (audit rule) applied to FR-6.2 actions\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-32: Do co-teachers (Course.coTeacherIds) count as 'managing' a course for contact rules?\",\n        \"FR-1 conflicts with convention: Conversation, Message, MessageReport, MessageAttachment and MessagingSettings in the PRD's Prisma block lack updatedAt, while conventions say every model has createdAt/updatedAt. Should updatedAt be added?\",\n        \"FR-2: There is no admin user-management page in src/app/(app)/admin. Where should isSafeguardingLead be edited — an existing user edit form elsewhere, or only via PATCH /api/users/:id?\",\n        \"FR-5.1: Should quiet hours apply to all roles or only teachers? The user story mentions teachers, but the settings endpoint is open to any role.\",\n        \"PRD-12 dependency: SH-12 (Announcements) is not implemented in the workspace. Confirm messaging can proceed independently.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-32 co-teacher scope — proceeding with teacherId OR coTeacherIds (MEDIUM).\",\n        \"updatedAt on new models — architect to decide. Default: add updatedAt per the platform convention. The PRD block is treated as the minimum field set.\",\n        \"Location of the isSafeguardingLead edit UI — architect to locate the existing user edit form. If none exists, extend the user update API/validator only.\",\n        \"Quiet hours role scope — proceeding with all roles (the settings endpoint is 'any').\",\n        \"PRD-12 absence — proceeding. Messaging does not depend on announcement code.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-13\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 43,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"PRD-12 (Announcements) is not implemented in the workspace (SH-12 run failed). PRD-13 does not depend on it at the code level. Proceed.\",\n    \"Open architect decisions are listed in requirements.json clarificationLog[0].unresolved: co-teacher scope, updatedAt on new models, where isSafeguardingLead is edited, quiet-hours role scope.\",\n    \"The student route segment is [id], not [studentId]. Shared components live in src/components/<Name>/.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011f4PwmXxutkvCwJJpZFZ1B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
