{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0167YnryjnDV6i5fnkW2C5N2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-12\",\n3\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:30:00Z\",\n4\t  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n5\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n6\t\n7\t  \"conventions\": {\n8\t    \"replaces\": \"This file replaces the SH-11 contracts that were here before.\",\n9\t    \"basePath\": \"/api (the existing SchoolHub convention, not /api/v1). Route files are src/app/api/**/route.ts. Requirement: FR-34.\",\n10\t    \"handlerPipeline\": \"withHandler → requireUser / requireRole → parseQuery / parseBody with a Zod schema from src/lib/validators/announcements.ts → one call into src/server/announcements/announcements-service.ts → ok(data) / ok(data, {status: 201\n11\t{\n12\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-12\",\n13\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:35:00Z\",\n14\t  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n15\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n16\t\n17\t  \"status\": \"complete\",\n18\t  \"endpointCount\": 12,\n19\t  \"blockers\": [],\n20\t  \"artifacts\": [\n21\t    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n22\t    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n23\t    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n24\t    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n25\t  ],\n26\t  \"notes\": [\n27\t    \"12 endpoints across 10 route files (matching system-design §2.6 and the PRD API table, FR-34), plus 2 existing endpoints extended without contract change: /api/internal/email/dispatch (publishDueAnnouncements, FR-27) and /api/files/:id (the 'announcement' context, FR-30).\",\n28\t    \"Base path is /api, not /api/v1. Envelopes, pagination (default 20, max 100; manage max 50) and error codes come from src/server/http.ts. RATE_LIMITED 429 already exists in ApiErrorCode.\",\n29\t    \"Error policy: targeting violations → 403 (AC-3). Non-member, not-visible or non-owner access to a specific announcement → 404. State conflicts (author editing ARCHIVED, ack without requiresAck, remind when !requiresAck) → 409. Second reminder within 24h → 429 with details.retryAfter (FR-25, ADR-4).\",\n30\t    \"Contract decisions beyond system-design: zero-recipient publish returns VALIDATION_ERROR with details.reason='NO_RECIPIENTS'. PATCH mode=draft on a PUBLISHED row is 409 (archive instead). Archive is idempotent. Ack also sets readAt if it was empty. Remind with nobody left still claims the throttle and returns notified: 0. On feed page 1, pinned items are lifted to the top and meta.total excludes them. Manage accepts an optional ?status filter on displayStatus. Percentages are integers rounded half-up, or null when the denominator is 0.\",\n31\t    \"Schema addition: Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime? (FR-25), already listed in system-design §1.\",\n32\t    \"NotifyInput gains an optional mandatoryInApp override (system-design A9) so announcement.published stays a single type key (FR-26).\",\n33\t    \"Shared DTOs (AudienceRow, AnnouncementInput, FeedItem, AnnouncementDetail, AudienceCounts) are in api-contracts.json `components`. src/lib/validators/announcements.ts should mirror them.\"\n34\t  ],\n35\t  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n36\t}\n37\t\n38\t# System Design: PRD-13 Direct Messaging\n39\t\n40\tTicket: **SH-13** · Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T22:30:00Z · Status: **complete**\n41\t\n42\tInputs read from disk: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (32 FR + 11 NFR), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..12), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1..B20, A1..A14).\n43\t\n44\t> This file replaces a stale SH-12 `system-design.md`. `api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in this folder are still stale (SH-12). `arch-api-contracts` must rewrite them from this document.\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t\n48\t## 1. Overview\n49\t\n50\tSchoolHub gets 1:1 and small-group (≤25) messaging between staff, students and parents. It runs inside the existing Next.js 14 App Router monolith, with no new dependencies and no new infrastructure:\n51\t\n52\t- **Storage:** 8 new Prisma models plus `User.isSafeguardingLead`, in one migration (ADR-2).\n53\t- **Who may message whom:** one pure rules module, `contact-rules.ts`. Create, send and the contacts list all use it (ADR-3).\n54\t- **Delivery:** HTTP polling. The open thread polls every 5 s; the inbox list and the sidebar badge poll every 30 s. There are no websockets (ADR-1, NFR-8, NFR-9).\n55\t- **Notifications:** in-app notifications are collapsed to one unread row per conversation. Email is deferred through `PendingMessageEmail`, which the existing maintenance cron drains, and it respects quiet hours (ADR-5, ADR-6).\n56\t- **Safeguarding:** the safeguarding area is server-gated on `ADMIN` plus `isSafeguardingLead`, read fresh from the database. Every view is audited. Deleted messages and edit history are retained and visible only to safeguarding leads (ADR-8, NFR-3).\n57\t- **UI:** MUI-only and built from the existing shared components (ADR-7, NFR-5).\n58\t\n59\t### Intake blockers and carried risks (Compliance Rule 5)\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2e59def-a937-4e61-837c-a8e39741caba","uuid":"b3ba54d3-5d80-4f77-8a3d-a073ea27250f","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:25:13.148Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/d2e59def-a937-4e61-837c-a8e39741caba/tool-results/bdwxtaqc3.txt","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-12\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"conventions\": {\n    \"replaces\": \"This file replaces the SH-11 contracts that were here before.\",\n    \"basePath\": \"/api (the existing SchoolHub convention, not /api/v1). Route files are src/app/api/**/route.ts. Requirement: FR-34.\",\n    \"handlerPipeline\": \"withHandler → requireUser / requireRole → parseQuery / parseBody with a Zod schema from src/lib/validators/announcements.ts → one call into src/server/announcements/announcements-service.ts → ok(data) / ok(data, {status: 201\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-12\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:35:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 12,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"12 endpoints across 10 route files (matching system-design §2.6 and the PRD API table, FR-34), plus 2 existing endpoints extended without contract change: /api/internal/email/dispatch (publishDueAnnouncements, FR-27) and /api/files/:id (the 'announcement' context, FR-30).\",\n    \"Base path is /api, not /api/v1. Envelopes, pagination (default 20, max 100; manage max 50) and error codes come from src/server/http.ts. RATE_LIMITED 429 already exists in ApiErrorCode.\",\n    \"Error policy: targeting violations → 403 (AC-3). Non-member, not-visible or non-owner access to a specific announcement → 404. State conflicts (author editing ARCHIVED, ack without requiresAck, remind when !requiresAck) → 409. Second reminder within 24h → 429 with details.retryAfter (FR-25, ADR-4).\",\n    \"Contract decisions beyond system-design: zero-recipient publish returns VALIDATION_ERROR with details.reason='NO_RECIPIENTS'. PATCH mode=draft on a PUBLISHED row is 409 (archive instead). Archive is idempotent. Ack also sets readAt if it was empty. Remind with nobody left still claims the throttle and returns notified: 0. On feed page 1, pinned items are lifted to the top and meta.total excludes them. Manage accepts an optional ?status filter on displayStatus. Percentages are integers rounded half-up, or null when the denominator is 0.\",\n    \"Schema addition: Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime? (FR-25), already listed in system-design §1.\",\n    \"NotifyInput gains an optional mandatoryInApp override (system-design A9) so announcement.published stays a single type key (FR-26).\",\n    \"Shared DTOs (AudienceRow, AnnouncementInput, FeedItem, AnnouncementDetail, AudienceCounts) are in api-contracts.json `components`. src/lib/validators/announcements.ts should mirror them.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}\n\n# System Design: PRD-13 Direct Messaging\n\nTicket: **SH-13** · Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T22:30:00Z · Status: **complete**\n\nInputs read from disk: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (32 FR + 11 NFR), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..12), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1..B20, A1..A14).\n\n> This file replaces a stale SH-12 `system-design.md`. `api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in this folder are still stale (SH-12). `arch-api-contracts` must rewrite them from this document.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub gets 1:1 and small-group (≤25) messaging between staff, students and parents. It runs inside the existing Next.js 14 App Router monolith, with no new dependencies and no new infrastructure:\n\n- **Storage:** 8 new Prisma models plus `User.isSafeguardingLead`, in one migration (ADR-2).\n- **Who may message whom:** one pure rules module, `contact-rules.ts`. Create, send and the contacts list all use it (ADR-3).\n- **Delivery:** HTTP polling. The open thread polls every 5 s; the inbox list and the sidebar badge poll every 30 s. There are no websockets (ADR-1, NFR-8, NFR-9).\n- **Notifications:** in-app notifications are collapsed to one unread row per conversation. Email is deferred through `PendingMessageEmail`, which the existing maintenance cron drains, and it respects quiet hours (ADR-5, ADR-6).\n- **Safeguarding:** the safeguarding area is server-gated on `ADMIN` plus `isSafeguardingLead`, read fresh from the database. Every view is audited. Deleted messages and edit history are retained and visible only to safeguarding leads (ADR-8, NFR-3).\n- **UI:** MUI-only and built from the existing shared components (ADR-7, NFR-5).\n\n### Intake blockers and carried risks (Compliance Rule 5)\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":418}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0167YnryjnDV6i5fnkW2C5N2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
