{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgskFLD5NhjSn7jViTYUX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `arch-api-contracts` sub-task for SH-13 is finished, so the whole architect phase is complete. I checked that `api-contracts.json` parses as valid JSON and that every requirement id it cites exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n- **`api-contracts.json`** (complete, 23 endpoints): both files in the folder were stale SH-12 copies, so I replaced them. 21 endpoints are new, taken from the route table in `system-design.md` §3.3. The other 2 are existing routes that get extended: `PATCH /api/users/:id` gains the `isSafeguardingLead` flag, and `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` also sends the deferred message emails. The file also lists the shared data shapes and the error rules.\n- **`handoff-to-dev-planning.json`**: written after the contracts, with `status: complete` and no blockers.\n\nThings the next phase should know:\n- **Error code mismatch:** `system-design.md` says an invalid `isSafeguardingLead` change returns 422. In `src/server/http.ts`, `VALIDATION_ERROR` maps to 400, so the contract uses 400 and the handoff notes the difference.\n- **Decisions I added beyond the design:**\n  - When leaving a conversation is refused, the error gives a reason: `ONE_TO_ONE` or `CREATOR_OF_STUDENT_GROUP`.\n  - Marking a report reviewed requires a note.\n  - The safeguarding view of a conversation that has no student returns 404.\n  - The maintenance run's response now also counts message emails sent, deferred and dropped.\n- **Stale dev-planning files:** `artifacts/dev-planning/` still holds files from SH-12. The dev-planning phase needs to regenerate them rather than reuse them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_read_input_tokens":67343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_