{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WMC64aRnBYH3WrdH4qSJ1T","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (54.6KB). Full output saved to: /Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/8f1e9cdf-3174-43b4-adaa-4e6aa4038a8c/tool-results/b7gamsbqf.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\nartifacts/:\napprovals\narchitect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\nqa\nrun-summary.json\ntelemetry\nui-verification\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n# System Design: PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays\n\nTicket: SH-14 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T23:58:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs:\n- `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`: 37 FR and 12 NFR, 96% confidence\n- `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`\n- `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md`: ADR-1 to ADR-13\n- `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`: B1 to B19, D1 to D9, R1 to R4\n\n> This replaces the stale SH-13 `system-design.md`. `api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in this folder are still SH-13 until `arch-api-contracts` rewrites them.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSH-14 adds a school calendar to the existing SchoolHub app (Next.js 14 App Router, Prisma/PostgreSQL, MUI 9). The pieces are:\n\n- one Prisma migration\n- one server module, `src/server/calendar/`\n- a shared audience resolver, at the path PRD-12 will use\n- about a dozen thin route handlers\n- two new pages (`/calendar`, `/account/calendar`), plus one small admin page\n- small, targeted edits to timetable, attendance, the assignment and quiz editors, notifications, the cron, navigation and the seed\n\nDesign principles:\n\n1. **One read path.** A single function, `getCalendarItems(user, range, sources, studentId?)`, feeds the `/calendar` API, the iCal feed, `getUpcomingEventsForUser`, and (with `sources=['events']`) the single-event visibility check. That way the feed cannot show anything the app hides (NFR-5).\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f1e9cdf-3174-43b4-adaa-4e6aa4038a8c","uuid":"0cddaf02-70f7-49c5-8bf6-591d6c8f71f1","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:54:03.671Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"artifacts/:\napprovals\narchitect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\nqa\nrun-summary.json\ntelemetry\nui-verification\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n# System Design: PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays\n\nTicket: SH-14 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T23:58:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs:\n- `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`: 37 FR and 12 NFR, 96% confidence\n- `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`\n- `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md`: ADR-1 to ADR-13\n- `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`: B1 to B19, D1 to D9, R1 to R4\n\n> This replaces the stale SH-13 `system-design.md`. `api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in this folder are still SH-13 until `arch-api-contracts` rewrites them.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSH-14 adds a school calendar to the existing SchoolHub app (Next.js 14 App Router, Prisma/PostgreSQL, MUI 9). The pieces are:\n\n- one Prisma migration\n- one server module, `src/server/calendar/`\n- a shared audience resolver, at the path PRD-12 will use\n- about a dozen thin route handlers\n- two new pages (`/calendar`, `/account/calendar`), plus one small admin page\n- small, targeted edits to timetable, attendance, the assignment and quiz editors, notifications, the cron, navigation and the seed\n\nDesign principles:\n\n1. **One read path.** A single function, `getCalendarItems(user, range, sources, studentId?)`, feeds the `/calendar` API, the iCal feed, `getUpcomingEventsForUser`, and (with `sources=['events']`) the single-event visibility check. That way the feed cannot show anything the app hides (NFR-5).\n2. **Recurrence is expanded on the server, at read time.** A recurring event is stored once. Clients and the scheduler only ever receive plain occurrences. The feed emits RRULE (ADR-2, ADR-3).\n3. **One holiday rule.** `isSchoolDay` in calendar-service owns the teaching-weekday rule and the no-school-event rule. Timetable, attendance, the editors and `/api/school-day` all call it (ADR-8).\n4. **Reuse before writing.** The design reuses `rateLimit`, `notify`, `audit`, `hashToken`, `csv.ts`, `DataTable`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView/Editor`, `useToast`, the dispatch cron, `getSchoolTimezone` and the access helpers (NFR-9).\n\n### Intake blockers and warnings\n\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **no blockers** (`blockers: []`). It raises three warnings, resolved as follows:\n\n| Intake warning | Resolution | Ref |\n|---|---|---|\n| PRD-12 missing: no `AudienceType`, `audience.ts` or audience builder | SH-14 adds `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }` and `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`, exactly as PRD-12 §FR-1/FR-2 specify. It also adds a minimal MUI `AudienceBuilder`. PRD-12 adopts all three without changes. No Announcement models. | ADR-9, §3.3 |\n| `/admin/academic-years/[id]` page missing | Add a minimal ADMIN server page at that exact route with a read-only term list and an \"Add term breaks\" button. | ADR-10, §3.9 |\n| New dependencies | `@mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15` (exact, installed first) with a scoped `@mui/x-internals` override. `node-ical@0.27.6` as an exact devDependency. Nothing else is added. | ADR-1, ADR-5 |\n\n### Conflicts between the research inputs, and how this design settles them\n\n| Topic | arch-research-stack | arch-research-reqs | **Decision** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Audience shape | PRD-12 enum (6 values) with `refId` and `include*` flags | 4-value enum with `targetId` and `roles[]` | **ADR-9.** PRD-14 FR-1 itself defines `EventAudience` with `refId` / `includeStudents` / `includeParents` / `includeTeachers` (verified in `14-calendar.md` L128-137), and PRD-12 L96 defines the 6 values. \"Grade 7 parents\" = `GRADE_LEVEL` with `includeStudents=false, includeTeachers=false`. No `roles[]` column. |\n| Resolver path | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` | `src/server/audience/audience.ts` | **`src/server/announcements/audience.ts`**, the path PRD-12 names, so PRD-12 doesn't need a rename. |\n| `getScheduleForDate` \"reason\" | Add `reason` to its return | Keep `ScheduleEntry[]`; callers fetch the reason separately | **Keep `ScheduleEntry[]`** (no churn for callers: attendance L130/L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Callers that need the holiday name call `isSchoolDay(date)` directly. FR-17's \"reason\" is delivered through `isSchoolDay` and `/api/school-day`. |\n| Email default per category (FR-28) | Not addressed | D5: a second type | **Two registry types:** `event.created` (`defaultEmail: false`) and `event.holiday_created` (`defaultEmail: true`, used for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK). Both keep the per-user preference override, and `notify.ts` is unchanged. This is a deliberate deviation (D-3 below). |\n| RSVP reminder \"once\" | `rsvpReminderSentAt` column | Same, claimed with conditional `updateMany` | Agreed: claim it with `updateMany({where:{id, rsvpReminderSentAt:null}})`. |\n\n### Deviations from the PRD's model and route list (all deliberate)\n\n| ID | Deviation | Why | Traces to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| D-1 | `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?` | Stores \"once per event\" for the reminder. Claimed atomically. | FR-23 |\n| D-2 | `EventAudience @@index([eventId])` and `@@index([type, refId])` | Audience filtering in SQL on the hot path. | NFR-4 |\n| D-3 | Extra notification type `event.holiday_created` | Per-category email default, within the existing preference model. | FR-28 |\n| D-4 | Back-relations on `User` (`calendarEvents`, `eventRsvps`, `calendarFeedToken`) and `onDelete: Cascade` FKs on `EventRsvp.userId` / `CalendarFeedToken.userId` | Prisma requires the relations. Cascade matches the \"cascade deletes\" instruction in FR-2. | FR-2 |\n| D-5 | Agenda view: 30-day page with next/prev in Community `EventCalendar`, instead of true infinite scroll | Community has no infinite agenda. If QA rejects this, the fallback is MUI `List` + native `IntersectionObserver` below 768 px, fetching the next 30-day window. Rejection triggers the fallback; it is not built up front. | FR-9, ADR-2 |\n| D-6 | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `url` only when it creates the first token, otherwise `{url:null, hasToken:true, createdAt}`. The page offers \"Reset link\". | The raw token cannot be re-shown because it is stored hashed. | FR-24, FR-25, NFR-5 |\n| D-7 | Seed a minimal ELECTIVE `ROBOTICS` course (teacher Tom, current year) only if it doesn't exist | The Chess club audience needs it, and it is absent from the seed. | FR-37 |\n| D-8 | Register save on a no-school date requires `holidayOverride: true` in the body, enforced on the server | Makes FR-18's extra confirmation a real rule, not only a UI dialog. | FR-18, NFR-7 |\n| D-9 | `GET /api/public/events` is rate limited per IP (`rateLimit('pubcal:'+ip, 120, 3_600_000)`) and range-capped at 100 days | Only unauthenticated JSON route; reuses the existing limiter. | FR-30, NFR-7 |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Dependencies and config (do first)\n\n| Change | Ref |\n|---|---|\n| `npm i --save-exact @mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15`. Nested override `\"@mui/x-scheduler\": {\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.17.0\"}`. Verify with `npm ls @mui/x-internals`. If npm doesn't honour the nested override, fall back to a global `9.17.0`. | FR-1, ADR-1 |\n| `import type {} from '@mui/x-scheduler/theme-augmentation'` beside the theme | FR-9, ADR-1 |\n| `npm i -D --save-exact node-ical@0.27.6` | NFR-6 |\n| Before writing scheduler code, the dev phase looks up the Quickstart, Views, Events, Editing, Timezone, Localization and Responsiveness pages via MUI MCP (`useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`). If MCP is unreachable, stop and report a blocker. | NFR-2 |\n\n### 2.2 Data model: migration `20261113000000_add_calendar`\n\n```prisma\nenum AudienceType  { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }   // PRD-12 values, owned here until PRD-12 lands\nenum EventCategory { HOLIDAY TERM_BREAK EXAM EVENT MEETING TRIP SPORTS DEADLINE OTHER }\nenum Recurrence    { NONE WEEKLY MONTHLY }\nenum RsvpResponse  { YES NO MAYBE }\n\nmodel CalendarEvent {\n  id                 String        @id @default(cuid())\n  title              String\n  description        String?\n  category           EventCategory\n  startAt            DateTime\n  endAt              DateTime\n  allDay             Boolean       @default(false)\n  location           String?\n  roomId             String?\n  recurrence         Recurrence    @default(NONE)\n  recurrenceUntil    DateTime?     @db.Date\n  isNoSchool         Boolean       @default(false)\n  rsvpEnabled        Boolean       @default(false)\n  rsvpDeadline       DateTime?\n  rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?                                  // D-1\n  isPublic           Boolean       @default(false)\n  createdById        String\n  createdBy          User          @relation(\"CalendarEventCreator\", fields: [createdById], references: [id])\n  createdAt          DateTime      @default(now())\n  updatedAt          DateTime      @updatedAt\n  audiences          EventAudience[]\n  rsvps              EventRsvp[]\n  @@index([startAt, endAt])\n}\n\nmodel EventAudience {\n  id              String        @id @default(cuid())\n  eventId         String\n  event           CalendarEvent @relation(fields: [eventId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  type            AudienceType\n  refId           String?       // gradeLevelId | sectionId | courseId | Role name (ROLE); null for SCHOOL/STAFF\n  includeStudents Boolean       @default(true)\n  includeParents  Boolean       @default(true)\n  includeTeachers Boolean       @default(true)\n  @@index([eventId])\n  @@index([type, refId])                                        // D-2\n}\n\nmodel EventRsvp {\n  eventId   String\n  event     CalendarEvent @relation(fields: [eventId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  userId    String\n  user      User          @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  response  RsvpResponse\n  guests    Int           @default(0)\n  note      String?\n  createdAt DateTime      @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime      @updatedAt\n  @@id([eventId, userId])\n}\n\nmodel CalendarFeedToken {\n  userId    String   @id\n  user      User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  tokenHash String   @unique\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n}\n```\n\nExact field lists for `EventRsvp` follow PRD §FR-1. The dev agent copies any field this sketch omits from `14-calendar.md` L139-148. Traces to FR-2, FR-3, FR-23, NFR-4, NFR-8.\n\n### 2.3 Server modules\n\n| File | Exports | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` (new, PRD-12 path) | `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)`, `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`, `audienceWhereForUser(user)` (Prisma `EventAudience` filter), `canTargetAudience(user, audience)` | Semantics are those of PRD-12 FR-2. `audienceWhereForUser` precomputes the user's keys once: their grade levels, sections and courses, the same for linked children (parents), the courses they teach and the sections they homeroom (teachers), and their role. It returns an `OR` over `{type, refId, include*}` so filtering happens in SQL (NFR-4). `canTargetAudience`: ADMIN → any. TEACHER → `COURSE` passes `assertCanManageCourse`, or `SECTION` where `homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Everything else → false. | FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-28, FR-29, FR-23, NFR-4, NFR-7 |\n| `src/server/calendar/recurrence.ts` (new, pure) | `expandOccurrences(event, from, to, tz)` | Steps in school-tz wall clock: +7 days, or +1 month on the same day of month, skipping months that lack the day. Duration is kept in wall-clock terms. Stops at the earlier of `recurrenceUntil` (end of that day, inclusive) and `to`. Occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. | FR-15, FR-4, NFR-3, ADR-3 |\n| `src/server/calendar/ical.ts` (new, pure) | `escapeText`, `foldLine`, `vtimezone(tz, from, to)`, `vevent(item, tz)`, `buildCalendar(items, tz, window)` | All-day events use `VALUE=DATE` with an exclusive `DTEND`. Timed one-off events use UTC `Z`. Recurring events use `TZID` + `RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z` (+`BYMONTHDAY`). Deadlines are zero-duration VEVENTs with `URL`. Lines are CRLF and folded at 75 octets. | FR-12, FR-26, NFR-3, NFR-6, ADR-5 |\n| `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (new) | `getEvent`, `createEvent`, `updateEvent`, `deleteEvent`, `upsertRsvp`, `listRsvps`, `isSchoolDay`, `noSchoolDays(from,to)`, `createTermBreaks(yearId, actor)`, `getOrCreateFeedToken`, `resetFeedToken`, `findUserByFeedToken` | Owns every per-entity check (NFR-7). **Imports nothing from timetable-service** (R2). It reads `prisma.schoolDay` directly, and timetable-service imports *from* it. | FR-5..8, FR-16, FR-20..23, FR-25, FR-33, FR-34, FR-36 |\n| `src/server/calendar/sources.ts` (new) | `getCalendarItems`, `getPublicEvents`, `getUpcomingEventsForUser` | The merge in §3.1. It may import timetable-service, the assignment and quiz services, and calendar-service, because nothing imports it back except routes (R2). | FR-10, FR-11, FR-15, FR-26, FR-30..32 |\n| `src/server/calendar/maintenance.ts` (new) | `sendRsvpReminders(now)` | Selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline ∈ (now, now+48h]` and `rsvpReminderSentAt = null`. For each, claims it via `updateMany({where:{id, rsvpReminderSentAt:null}, data:{rsvpReminderSentAt:now}})`. If `count===1`, resolves the audience minus existing RSVP userIds and calls `notify('event.rsvp_reminder')`. | FR-23, ADR-11 |\n| `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (new, client-safe) | `eventInputSchema`, `eventPatchSchema`, `rsvpSchema`, `calendarQuerySchema`, `schoolDayQuerySchema`, `publicEventsQuerySchema` | Rules: title ≤ 150; description ≤ 5000; `endAt ≥ startAt`; `recurrenceUntil` required for WEEKLY/MONTHLY and ≤ start + 1 year; guests 0–5; range `to − from ≤ 100 days`; `sources ⊆ {events, holidays, assignments, quizzes, timetable}`. All-day input is `yyyy-MM-dd` start and inclusive end. The **server** converts it to `[schoolMidnight(start), schoolMidnight(end+1))`. | FR-4, FR-21, FR-32, NFR-8 |\n| `src/lib/dates.ts` (edit) | add `schoolMidnight(dateStr, tz)`, `schoolDateOf(instant, tz)` | Pure and client-safe. The single source of all-day and date conversions. | FR-4, FR-16, NFR-3, ADR-4 |\n\n### 2.4 Edits to existing modules\n\n| File | Change | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` | At both `// PRD-14 holidays hook` lines, replace the inline `schoolDay` weekday check with `if (!(await isSchoolDay(date)).isSchoolDay) return [];`. The weekday rule now lives only in `isSchoolDay`, so the old check is deleted, not duplicated. The return type is unchanged. | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-9 |\n| `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` | `getToday` and `getOverview` add `noSchoolReason: string \\| null` from `isSchoolDay`. The register save path rejects with `VALIDATION_ERROR` \"holidayOverride required\" when the date is not a school day and `holidayOverride !== true` (D-8). | FR-18 |\n| Attendance landing + `RegisterForm.tsx` | Landing shows \"No classes today — <reason>\". The register shows a warning `Alert` banner, and the save button opens `ConfirmDialog` \"Record attendance on a holiday anyway\", which sends `holidayOverride: true`. | FR-18, NFR-1 |\n| Teacher/student/parent Today views (those consuming `getScheduleForDate`) | When `isSchoolDay` is false, show the holiday name instead of the empty class list. | FR-17 |\n| `AssignmentForm.tsx`, `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` | On a `dueAt`/`availableUntil` change, `fetch('/api/school-day?date=')`. If false, show a non-blocking `<Alert severity=\"warning\">This date is a holiday (<title>).</Alert>`. Save is unchanged. | FR-19, FR-34 |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `event.created` (COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail false), `event.holiday_created` (COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true), `event.updated` (COMMUNICATION, false) and `event.rsvp_reminder` (COMMUNICATION, false). All roles. | FR-23, FR-28, FR-29 |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | Add an isolated `try { await sendRsvpReminders(now) } catch (e) { logger.error(...) }` block, matching the quiz-maintenance block. | FR-23, NFR-9 |\n| `src/config/navigation.ts` | `{ label: 'Calendar', href: '/calendar', icon: CalendarMonth, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, as with the other `/account/*` pages. It is reached from the account area and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`. | FR-35 |\n| `prisma/seed.ts` | `seedCalendar()`, idempotent: match by title (+ startAt where it is stable). It seeds the 7 events from FR-37 and the ROBOTICS course if absent (D-7). \"Sports day\" has no announcement link. Grade 6–8 exams use three `GRADE_LEVEL` audiences. \"Grade 7 parents\" = `GRADE_LEVEL` with only `includeParents`. | FR-37 |\n\n### 2.5 Route handlers (thin: requireUser/requireRole → Zod parse → service → `ok`/`apiError`)\n\n| Route | Auth | Service call | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `GET /api/calendar?from&to&sources&studentId` | any user | `getCalendarItems` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-32, NFR-7 |\n| `POST /api/events` | ADMIN, TEACHER | `createEvent` | FR-5..7, FR-14, FR-28, FR-33 |\n| `GET /api/events/:id` | visible to user | `getEvent` (+`myRsvp`, totals, `canEdit`) | FR-12, FR-22, FR-33 |\n| `PATCH /api/events/:id` | creator, ADMIN | `updateEvent` | FR-6..8, FR-29, FR-33, FR-36 |\n| `DELETE /api/events/:id` | creator, ADMIN | `deleteEvent` | FR-8, FR-33, FR-36 |\n| `GET /api/events/:id/ics` | visible to user | `getEvent` → `buildCalendar([event])` | FR-12, FR-33 |\n| `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp` | audience member | `upsertRsvp` | FR-21 |\n| `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps[?format=csv]` | creator, ADMIN | `listRsvps` → JSON or `csv.ts` | FR-22 |\n| `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` | any user | `getOrCreateFeedToken` | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `POST /api/me/calendar-feed/reset` | any user | `resetFeedToken` | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `GET /api/calendar/feed/[token]` (`.ics` stripped from param) | token | `findUserByFeedToken` → `rateLimit` → `getCalendarItems` → `buildCalendar` | FR-26, FR-27, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n| `GET /api/school-day?date=` (new singular folder; `/api/school-days` untouched) | any user | `isSchoolDay` | FR-16, FR-19, FR-34 |\n| `GET /api/public/events?from&to` | public, IP rate limit | `getPublicEvents` | FR-30, D-9 |\n| `POST /api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks` | ADMIN | `createTermBreaks` | FR-20 |\n\nError mapping: not visible → 404 `NOT_FOUND`. Visible but not permitted → 403 `FORBIDDEN`. RSVP after the deadline, or with RSVP disabled → 409 `CONFLICT`. Feed token unknown → plain 404. Feed over the limit → 429 `RATE_LIMITED` + `Retry-After`. `arch-api-contracts` defines the exact shapes.\n\n### 2.6 UI\n\n| Path / component | Contents | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/(app)/calendar/page.tsx` (server) → `CalendarView.tsx` (client) | `requirePageUser`. `<EventCalendar>` from `@mui/x-scheduler/event-calendar`: `views={['month','week','agenda']}`, week `startTime:7, endTime:19`, agenda `dayCount:30`, `displayTimezone={tz}`, `readOnly`, `eventCreation={false}`. The default view is month at `useMediaQuery('(min-width:768px)')`, agenda below that. Controlled `events`, refetched on `onVisibleDateChange`/`onViewChange` with plain `fetch` and a small Map cache keyed by `from|to|sources|studentId`. The page opens the drawer when `?event=<id>` is present (notification links). | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-12 |\n| `SourceChips` | MUI `Chip`s: School events · My assignments · My quizzes · My timetable (Week view only) · Holidays. Stored in `localStorage['calendar.sources']`. Holidays = HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool`; School events = everything else, with no overlap. `timetable` is fetched only in Week view. | FR-10 |\n| Child filter (PARENT only) | `Select`: \"All children\" or one child → `studentId`. Deadline titles get the child's name prefixed by the server. | FR-11 |\n| `EventDrawer` | Right-anchored `Drawer`: title, category `Chip`, time in school tz, location, `MarkdownView` description, audience chips, RSVP controls (`ToggleButtonGroup` + guests `TextField` for parents + note; disabled after the deadline), \"Add to my calendar\" (`<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`), and edit/delete when `canEdit` (delete via `ConfirmDialog`). Creator/admin see an RSVP `DataTable` + CSV link. | FR-12, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1 |\n| Deadline click | `onEventEditingStart` → `cancel()` → `router.push(item.href)` | FR-13 |\n| `EventEditorDialog` | \"New event\" button (ADMIN/TEACHER). React Hook Form + `eventInputSchema`. Fields: title, category (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK only for admins), all-day switch, date/time pickers (`@mui/x-date-pickers`), location, `MarkdownEditor`, `AudienceBuilder`, recurrence select + until date, RSVP switch + deadline, and admin-only `isNoSchool`/`isPublic`. Results go through `useToast`. | FR-4..7, FR-14 |\n| `src/components/AudienceBuilder/` (new shared) | Rows of type `Select` + entity `Autocomplete` (grade level / section / course / role) + three include `Checkbox`es. Types are filtered by `canTargetAudience` rules on the client. The server stays authoritative. | FR-3, FR-7, FR-14 |\n| `src/app/(app)/account/calendar/page.tsx` | \"Subscribe\" card: URL `TextField` (read-only) + copy (`navigator.clipboard`), Google/Apple/Outlook instructions as static text, and \"Reset link\" behind `ConfirmDialog`. When `url` is null: \"Reset link to get a new URL\" (D-6). | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `src/app/(app)/admin/academic-years/[id]/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. Year name, read-only term list (existing terms service), and an \"Add term breaks\" button + `ConfirmDialog` that shows the number of breaks created via toast. | FR-20 |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Calendar read (`GET /api/calendar`, the feed, upcoming events)\n\n```\nroute → calendarQuerySchema (≤100 days) → getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})\n  1. scope   = studentId ? resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId) : getAccessibleStudentIds(user)   (404 for others)\n  2. where   = audienceWhereForUser(user, scope)          // keys computed once\n  3. Promise.all([\n       events:      CalendarEvent where startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR (recurrence≠NONE AND recurrenceUntil ≥ from))\n                    AND (audiences some where) OR createdById=user  (ADMIN: no audience filter)\n                    → expandOccurrences(e, from, to, tz) → split into holidays / events by category+isNoSchool,\n       assignments: existing assignment service, PUBLISHED, dueAt ∈ [from,to), scoped students/courses,\n       quizzes:     existing quiz service, PUBLISHED, availableUntil ∈ [from,to),\n       timetable:   getPersonalTimetable(target) projected onto dates in range, skipping noSchoolDays(from,to)\n     ]) – only for requested sources\n  4. map → CalendarItem union {kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', id, title, start, end, allDay, color, href?, childName?}\n```\nThe feed calls the same function with `from=now−30d, to=now+365d`, sources minus timetable, and recurring events **unexpanded**. Instead of occurrences it gets the series rows so it can emit RRULE. The 100-day cap is skipped because the call is internal. Traces to FR-10, FR-11, FR-15, FR-26, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n\n### 3.2 Event write\n\n```\nPOST/PATCH → eventInputSchema → createEvent/updateEvent(user, input)\n  - FR-6: non-admin + (isNoSchool | isPublic | HOLIDAY | TERM_BREAK) → 403\n  - FR-7: every audience must pass canTargetAudience(user, a) → else 403\n  - FR-8: PATCH/DELETE requires createdById===user.id or ADMIN\n  - FR-5: isNoSchool ??= category ∈ {HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK}\n  - all-day → schoolMidnight conversion (FR-4)\n  - prisma.$transaction: event + replace audiences\n  - after commit:\n      FR-36 audit() if ADMIN && createdById≠user.id (update/delete)\n      FR-28 create: first occurrence within 30 days → notify(HOLIDAY|TERM_BREAK ? 'event.holiday_created' : 'event.created',\n            resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences) − creator, link '/calendar?event=<id>')\n      FR-29 update: startAt|endAt|allDay|location changed AND event upcoming → notify('event.updated') once\n```\n\n### 3.3 Audience resolution (PRD-12 FR-2 semantics)\n\n| Type | refId | Students (`includeStudents`) | Parents (`includeParents`) | Teachers (`includeTeachers`) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SCHOOL | null | all active users | | |\n| STAFF | null | ADMIN + TEACHER | | |\n| ROLE | role name | users with that role | | |\n| GRADE_LEVEL | gradeLevelId | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId = refId` | their `ParentStudentLink` parents | teachers of current-year courses in sections of that grade |\n| SECTION | sectionId | current-year `SectionMember`s | their parents | homeroom teacher + teachers of courses in the section |\n| COURSE | courseId | ACTIVE `Enrollment`s | their parents | `teacherId` + `coTeacherIds` |\n\nOnly ACTIVE, non-archived users count. `isUserInAudience` and `audienceWhereForUser` give the same answer as `resolveAudienceUserIds`. A property-style integration test loops over every seed user to check this (PRD-12 test requirement). Traces to FR-3, FR-7, NFR-7.\n\n### 3.4 School-day check\n\n```\nisSchoolDay(date) → d = schoolDateOf(date, tz), isoDay\n  1. SchoolDay[isoDay].isTeaching ?? isoDay ≤ 5   → false, reason 'Not a teaching day'\n  2. isNoSchool events with a SCHOOL audience where startAt < midnight(d+1) AND (endAt > midnight(d) OR recurring)\n     → expandOccurrences within that day → first hit → false, reason 'Holiday: <title>'\n  3. → { isSchoolDay: true, reason: null }\nnoSchoolDays(from, to) = one query, same rules, returns Map<date, reason> (used by the timetable source; avoids N calls)\n```\nCallers: timetable-service (FR-17), attendance (FR-18), `/api/school-day` (FR-19, FR-34), timetable source in §3.1. Traces to FR-16..19, FR-34.\n\n### 3.5 RSVP\n\n`PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp` → `rsvpSchema` → `upsertRsvp`:\n1. Check the event is visible and `rsvpEnabled`. Otherwise 404 (not visible) or 409.\n2. Require `isUserInAudience`. Otherwise 403.\n3. Require `now < rsvpDeadline`. Otherwise 409.\n4. If the user is not a PARENT, force `guests = 0`.\n5. Upsert on `(eventId, userId)`.\n\nA recurring event has one RSVP for the whole series. The drawer gets `myRsvp` and totals `{yes, no, maybe, guests}` from `GET /api/events/:id`. Creator and admin read the full list via `/rsvps`, or `?format=csv` via `csv.ts`. Traces to FR-21, FR-22.\n\n### 3.6 Reminder job\n\nCron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` → `sendRsvpReminders(now)` → claim → audience − responders → `notify('event.rsvp_reminder', link '/calendar?event=<id>')`. Traces to FR-23.\n\n### 3.7 iCal feed\n\n```\nGET /api/calendar/feed/<token>.ics\n  token = param.replace(/\\.ics$/, '') → hashToken(token) → CalendarFeedToken by tokenHash (unique) → user ACTIVE?\n    no → 404 text/plain\n  rateLimit('calfeed:'+hash, 60, 3_600_000) → !ok → 429 + Retry-After\n  items = getCalendarItems(user, feed window, series mode)\n  body  = buildCalendar(items, tz, window)   // VTIMEZONE for transitions in window, RRULE for series\n  200 text/calendar; charset=utf-8, Cache-Control: private, max-age=900\n```\nToken lifecycle:\n- `getOrCreateFeedToken` creates the row on first use from `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stores `hashToken(raw)`, and returns the URL once.\n- `resetFeedToken` upserts a new hash, so the old URL returns 404 immediately.\n- No raw token is ever logged.\n\nTraces to FR-24..27, NFR-5, NFR-6, ADR-6, ADR-7.\n\n### 3.8 Public and dashboard hooks\n\n- `getPublicEvents(from, to)`: `isPublic` events, expanded, returning only public-safe fields (id, title, category, start, end, allDay, location, description). Traces to FR-30.\n- `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)`: `getCalendarItems(user, now..now+90d, ['events','holidays'])`, sorted, then the first `limit` items. No UI. Traces to FR-31, NFR-11.\n\n### 3.9 Term breaks\n\n`POST /api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks` (ADMIN) → `createTermBreaks`:\n1. Order the terms by `startDate`.\n2. For each consecutive pair where `next.start > prev.end + 1 day`, create an all-day TERM_BREAK with `isNoSchool=true` and a SCHOOL audience, from `prev.end+1` (inclusive) to `next.start` (exclusive).\n3. Skip any gap that already has a TERM_BREAK with the same span. This makes the call idempotent.\n4. Return `{ created }`.\n5. Write an `audit()` entry.\n\nTraces to FR-20.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cross-cutting\n\n- **Time (NFR-3, NFR-8).**\n  - Storage is in UTC. Display uses `SchoolSettings.timezone`, read via the existing `getSchoolTimezone()`. No third copy is created.\n  - All-day events run from school-tz midnight with an exclusive end.\n  - Expansion steps in wall-clock time.\n  - The feed uses `VALUE=DATE` for all-day events and `TZID` + VTIMEZONE for series.\n  - The scheduler gets `displayTimezone`.\n  - One DST-week test fixture (America/New_York 2026-11-01, or the seed tz) runs through the expansion, the all-day path and the feed.\n- **Security (NFR-5, NFR-7).**\n  - Every route calls `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (hashed token) and public events (public fields only, IP limit).\n  - Per-entity checks live in calendar-service.\n  - Students see only themselves, and parents only their linked children (`getAccessibleStudentIds` / `resolveViewedStudent`).\n  - A non-visible event returns 404, so its existence doesn't leak.\n- **Performance (NFR-4).**\n  - A parent with 3 children in month view needs about 6 indexed queries, run in parallel.\n  - The audience is filtered in SQL, and holidays are found with one `noSchoolDays` query.\n  - There is no cache layer. Add one only if the Playwright timing or a measurement exceeds 500 ms.\n- **UI rules (NFR-1, NFR-12).**\n  - Only MUI, icons and MUI X (including the scheduler) are used. Toasts go through `useToast`, side panels through `Drawer`, and confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`.\n  - English only. The breakpoint is 768 px.\n- **Scope (NFR-11).**\n  - Out of scope: p","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/8f1e9cdf-3174-43b4-adaa-4e6aa4038a8c/tool-results/b7gamsbqf.txt","persistedOutputSize":55864},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WMC64aRnBYH3WrdH4qSJ1T","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgsrug1DJzoeippY346Mn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CDcGt1oz4YiDMz7j8R2rSp","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/8f1e9cdf-3174-43b4-adaa-4e6aa4038a8c/tool-results/b7gamsbqf.txt","allow_large":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1221,"cache_read_input_tokens":26766,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1221,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f1e9cdf-3174-43b4-adaa-4e6aa4038a8c","uuid":"fe845910-e40a-43ed-90f5-1e1c08ef0fcd","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:54:05.404Z","request_id":"req_011Cgsrufmpbpw1off8w9Zzr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CDcGt1oz4YiDMz7j8R2rSp":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/8f1e9cdf-3174-43b4-adaa-4e6aa4038a8c/tool-results/b7gamsbqf.txt","allow_large":true}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CDcGt1oz4YiDMz7j8R2rSp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tartifacts/:\n2\tapprovals\n3\tarchitect\n4\tdev\n5\tdev-planning\n6\tintake\n7\tqa\n8\trun-summary.json\n9\ttelemetry\n10\tui-verification\n11\t\n12\tartifacts/architect:\n13\tapi-contracts.json\n14\thandoff-to-dev-planning.json\n15\trequirements-analysis-notes.md\n16\tsystem-design.md\n17\ttech-stack-decisions.md\n18\tthreat-model-notes.json\n19\t\n20\tartifacts/intake:\n21\thandoff-to-architect.json\n22\trequirements.json\n23\ttech-stack.json\n24\tuser-stories.md\n25\t# System Design: PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays\n26\t\n27\tTicket: SH-14 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T23:58:00Z · Status: complete\n28\t\n29\tInputs:\n30\t- `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`: 37 FR and 12 NFR, 96% confidence\n31\t- `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`\n32\t- `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md`: ADR-1 to ADR-13\n33\t- `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`: B1 to B19, D1 to D9, R1 to R4\n34\t\n35\t> This replaces the stale SH-13 `system-design.md`. `api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in this folder are still SH-13 until `arch-api-contracts` rewrites them.\n36\t\n37\t---\n38\t\n39\t## 1. Overview\n40\t\n41\tSH-14 adds a school calendar to the existing SchoolHub app (Next.js 14 App Router, Prisma/PostgreSQL, MUI 9). The pieces are:\n42\t\n43\t- one Prisma migration\n44\t- one server module, `src/server/calendar/`\n45\t- a shared audience resolver, at the path PRD-12 will use\n46\t- about a dozen thin route handlers\n47\t- two new pages (`/calendar`, `/account/calendar`), plus one small admin page\n48\t- small, targeted edits to timetable, attendance, the assignment and quiz editors, notifications, the cron, navigation and the seed\n49\t\n50\tDesign principles:\n51\t\n52\t1. **One read path.** A single function, `getCalendarItems(user, range, sources, studentId?)`, feeds the `/calendar` API, the iCal feed, `getUpcomingEventsForUser`, and (with `sources=['events']`) the single-event visibility check. That way the feed cannot show anything the app hides (NFR-5).\n53\t2. **Recurrence is expanded on the server, at read time.** A recurring event is stored once. Clients and the scheduler only ever receive plain occurrences. The feed emits RRULE (ADR-2, ADR-3).\n54\t3. **One holiday rule.** `isSchoolDay` in calendar-service owns the teaching-weekday rule and the no-school-event rule. Timetable, attendance, the editors and `/api/school-day` all call it (ADR-8).\n55\t4. **Reuse before writing.** The design reuses `rateLimit`, `notify`, `audit`, `hashToken`, `csv.ts`, `DataTable`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView/Editor`, `useToast`, the dispatch cron, `getSchoolTimezone` and the access helpers (NFR-9).\n56\t\n57\t### Intake blockers and warnings\n58\t\n59\t`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **no blockers** (`blockers: []`). It raises three warnings, resolved as follows:\n60\t\n61\t| Intake warning | Resolution | Ref |\n62\t|---|---|---|\n63\t| PRD-12 missing: no `AudienceType`, `audience.ts` or audience builder | SH-14 adds `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }` and `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`, exactly as PRD-12 §FR-1/FR-2 specify. It also adds a minimal MUI `AudienceBuilder`. PRD-12 adopts all three without changes. No Announcement models. | ADR-9, §3.3 |\n64\t| `/admin/academic-years/[id]` page missing | Add a minimal ADMIN server page at that exact route with a read-only term list and an \"Add term breaks\" button. | ADR-10, §3.9 |\n65\t| New dependencies | `@mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15` (exact, installed first) with a scoped `@mui/x-internals` override. `node-ical@0.27.6` as an exact devDependency. Nothing else is added. | ADR-1, ADR-5 |\n66\t\n67\t### Conflicts between the research inputs, and how this design settles them\n68\t\n69\t| Topic | arch-research-stack | arch-research-reqs | **Decision** |\n70\t|---|---|---|---|\n71\t| Audience shape | PRD-12 enum (6 values) with `refId` and `include*` flags | 4-value enum with `targetId` and `roles[]` | **ADR-9.** PRD-14 FR-1 itself defines `EventAudience` with `refId` / `includeStudents` / `includeParents` / `includeTeachers` (verified in `14-calendar.md` L128-137), and PRD-12 L96 defines the 6 values. \"Grade 7 parents\" = `GRADE_LEVEL` with `includeStudents=false, includeTeachers=false`. No `roles[]` column. |\n72\t| Resolver path | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` | `src/server/audience/audience.ts` | **`src/server/announcements/audience.ts`**, the path PRD-12 names, so PRD-12 doesn't need a rename. |\n73\t| `getScheduleForDate` \"reason\" | Add `reason` to its return | Keep `ScheduleEntry[]`; callers fetch the reason separately | **Keep `ScheduleEntry[]`** (no churn for callers: attendance L130/L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Callers that need the holiday name call `isSchoolDay(date)` directly. FR-17's \"reason\" is delivered through `isSchoolDay` and `/api/school-day`. |\n74\t| Email default per category (FR-28) | Not addressed | D5: a second type | **Two registry types:** `event.created` (`defaultEmail: false`) and `event.holiday_created` (`defaultEmail: true`, used for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK). Both keep the per-user preference override, and `notify.ts` is unchanged. This is a deliberate deviation (D-3 below). |\n75\t| RSVP reminder \"once\" | `rsvpReminderSentAt` column | Same, claimed with conditional `updateMany` | Agreed: claim it with `updateMany({where:{id, rsvpReminderSentAt:null}})`. |\n76\t\n77\t### Deviations from the PRD's model and route list (all deliberate)\n78\t\n79\t| ID | Deviation | Why | Traces to |\n80\t|---|---|---|---|\n81\t| D-1 | `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?` | Stores \"once per event\" for the reminder. Claimed atomically. | FR-23 |\n82\t| D-2 | `EventAudience @@index([eventId])` and `@@index([type, refId])` | Audience filtering in SQL on the hot path. | NFR-4 |\n83\t| D-3 | Extra notification type `event.holiday_created` | Per-category email default, within the existing preference model. | FR-28 |\n84\t| D-4 | Back-relations on `User` (`calendarEvents`, `eventRsvps`, `calendarFeedToken`) and `onDelete: Cascade` FKs on `EventRsvp.userId` / `CalendarFeedToken.userId` | Prisma requires the relations. Cascade matches the \"cascade deletes\" instruction in FR-2. | FR-2 |\n85\t| D-5 | Agenda view: 30-day page with next/prev in Community `EventCalendar`, instead of true infinite scroll | Community has no infinite agenda. If QA rejects this, the fallback is MUI `List` + native `IntersectionObserver` below 768 px, fetching the next 30-day window. Rejection triggers the fallback; it is not built up front. | FR-9, ADR-2 |\n86\t| D-6 | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `url` only when it creates the first token, otherwise `{url:null, hasToken:true, createdAt}`. The page offers \"Reset link\". | The raw token cannot be re-shown because it is stored hashed. | FR-24, FR-25, NFR-5 |\n87\t| D-7 | Seed a minimal ELECTIVE `ROBOTICS` course (teacher Tom, current year) only if it doesn't exist | The Chess club audience needs it, and it is absent from the seed. | FR-37 |\n88\t| D-8 | Register save on a no-school date requires `holidayOverride: true` in the body, enforced on the server | Makes FR-18's extra confirmation a real rule, not only a UI dialog. | FR-18, NFR-7 |\n89\t| D-9 | `GET /api/public/events` is rate limited per IP (`rateLimit('pubcal:'+ip, 120, 3_600_000)`) and range-capped at 100 days | Only unauthenticated JSON route; reuses the existing limiter. | FR-30, NFR-7 |\n90\t\n91\t---\n92\t\n93\t## 2. Component Breakdown\n94\t\n95\t### 2.1 Dependencies and config (do first)\n96\t\n97\t| Change | Ref |\n98\t|---|---|\n99\t| `npm i --save-exact @mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15`. Nested override `\"@mui/x-scheduler\": {\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.17.0\"}`. Verify with `npm ls @mui/x-internals`. If npm doesn't honour the nested override, fall back to a global `9.17.0`. | FR-1, ADR-1 |\n100\t| `import type {} from '@mui/x-scheduler/theme-augmentation'` beside the theme | FR-9, ADR-1 |\n101\t| `npm i -D --save-exact node-ical@0.27.6` | NFR-6 |\n102\t| Before writing scheduler code, the dev phase looks up the Quickstart, Views, Events, Editing, Timezone, Localization and Responsiveness pages via MUI MCP (`useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`). If MCP is unreachable, stop and report a blocker. | NFR-2 |\n103\t\n104\t### 2.2 Data model: migration `20261113000000_add_calendar`\n105\t\n106\t```prisma\n107\tenum AudienceType  { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }   // PRD-12 values, owned here until PRD-12 lands\n108\tenum EventCategory { HOLIDAY TERM_BREAK EXAM EVENT MEETING TRIP SPORTS DEADLINE OTHER }\n109\tenum Recurrence    { NONE WEEKLY MONTHLY }\n110\tenum RsvpResponse  { YES NO MAYBE }\n111\t\n112\tmodel CalendarEvent {\n113\t  id                 String        @id @default(cuid())\n114\t  title              String\n115\t  description        String?\n116\t  category           EventCategory\n117\t  startAt            DateTime\n118\t  endAt              DateTime\n119\t  allDay             Boolean       @default(false)\n120\t  location           String?\n121\t  roomId             String?\n122\t  recurrence         Recurrence    @default(NONE)\n123\t  recurrenceUntil    DateTime?     @db.Date\n124\t  isNoSchool         Boolean       @default(false)\n125\t  rsvpEnabled        Boolean       @default(false)\n126\t  rsvpDeadline       DateTime?\n127\t  rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?                                  // D-1\n128\t  isPublic           Boolean       @default(false)\n129\t  createdById        String\n130\t  createdBy          User          @relation(\"CalendarEventCreator\", fields: [createdById], references: [id])\n131\t  createdAt          DateTime      @default(now())\n132\t  updatedAt          DateTime      @updatedAt\n133\t  audiences          EventAudience[]\n134\t  rsvps              EventRsvp[]\n135\t  @@index([startAt, endAt])\n136\t}\n137\t\n138\tmodel EventAudience {\n139\t  id              String        @id @default(cuid())\n140\t  eventId         String\n141\t  event           CalendarEvent @relation(fields: [eventId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n142\t  type            AudienceType\n143\t  refId           String?       // gradeLevelId | sectionId | courseId | Role name (ROLE); null for SCHOOL/STAFF\n144\t  includeStudents Boolean       @default(true)\n145\t  includeParents  Boolean       @default(true)\n146\t  includeTeachers Boolean       @default(true)\n147\t  @@index([eventId])\n148\t  @@index([type, refId])                                        // D-2\n149\t}\n150\t\n151\tmodel EventRsvp {\n152\t  eventId   String\n153\t  event     CalendarEvent @relation(fields: [eventId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n154\t  userId    String\n155\t  user      User          @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n156\t  response  RsvpResponse\n157\t  guests    Int           @default(0)\n158\t  note      String?\n159\t  createdAt DateTime      @default(now())\n160\t  updatedAt DateTime      @updatedAt\n161\t  @@id([eventId, userId])\n162\t}\n163\t\n164\tmodel CalendarFeedToken {\n165\t  userId    String   @id\n166\t  user      User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n167\t  tokenHash String   @unique\n168\t  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n169\t}\n170\t```\n171\t\n172\tExact field lists for `EventRsvp` follow PRD §FR-1. The dev agent copies any field this sketch omits from `14-calendar.md` L139-148. Traces to FR-2, FR-3, FR-23, NFR-4, NFR-8.\n173\t\n174\t### 2.3 Server modules\n175\t\n176\t| File | Exports | Notes | Reqs |\n177\t|---|---|---|---|\n178\t| `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` (new, PRD-12 path) | `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)`, `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`, `audienceWhereForUser(user)` (Prisma `EventAudience` filter), `canTargetAudience(user, audience)` | Semantics are those of PRD-12 FR-2. `audienceWhereForUser` precomputes the user's keys once: their grade levels, sections and courses, the same for linked children (parents), the courses they teach and the sections they homeroom (teachers), and their role. It returns an `OR` over `{type, refId, include*}` so filtering happens in SQL (NFR-4). `canTargetAudience`: ADMIN → any. TEACHER → `COURSE` passes `assertCanManageCourse`, or `SECTION` where `homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Everything else → false. | FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-28, FR-29, FR-23, NFR-4, NFR-7 |\n179\t| `src/server/calendar/recurrence.ts` (new, pure) | `expandOccurrences(event, from, to, tz)` | Steps in school-tz wall clock: +7 days, or +1 month on the same day of month, skipping months that lack the day. Duration is kept in wall-clock terms. Stops at the earlier of `recurrenceUntil` (end of that day, inclusive) and `to`. Occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. | FR-15, FR-4, NFR-3, ADR-3 |\n180\t| `src/server/calendar/ical.ts` (new, pure) | `escapeText`, `foldLine`, `vtimezone(tz, from, to)`, `vevent(item, tz)`, `buildCalendar(items, tz, window)` | All-day events use `VALUE=DATE` with an exclusive `DTEND`. Timed one-off events use UTC `Z`. Recurring events use `TZID` + `RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z` (+`BYMONTHDAY`). Deadlines are zero-duration VEVENTs with `URL`. Lines are CRLF and folded at 75 octets. | FR-12, FR-26, NFR-3, NFR-6, ADR-5 |\n181\t| `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (new) | `getEvent`, `createEvent`, `updateEvent`, `deleteEvent`, `upsertRsvp`, `listRsvps`, `isSchoolDay`, `noSchoolDays(from,to)`, `createTermBreaks(yearId, actor)`, `getOrCreateFeedToken`, `resetFeedToken`, `findUserByFeedToken` | Owns every per-entity check (NFR-7). **Imports nothing from timetable-service** (R2). It reads `prisma.schoolDay` directly, and timetable-service imports *from* it. | FR-5..8, FR-16, FR-20..23, FR-25, FR-33, FR-34, FR-36 |\n182\t| `src/server/calendar/sources.ts` (new) | `getCalendarItems`, `getPublicEvents`, `getUpcomingEventsForUser` | The merge in §3.1. It may import timetable-service, the assignment and quiz services, and calendar-service, because nothing imports it back except routes (R2). | FR-10, FR-11, FR-15, FR-26, FR-30..32 |\n183\t| `src/server/calendar/maintenance.ts` (new) | `sendRsvpReminders(now)` | Selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline ∈ (now, now+48h]` and `rsvpReminderSentAt = null`. For each, claims it via `updateMany({where:{id, rsvpReminderSentAt:null}, data:{rsvpReminderSentAt:now}})`. If `count===1`, resolves the audience minus existing RSVP userIds and calls `notify('event.rsvp_reminder')`. | FR-23, ADR-11 |\n184\t| `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (new, client-safe) | `eventInputSchema`, `eventPatchSchema`, `rsvpSchema`, `calendarQuerySchema`, `schoolDayQuerySchema`, `publicEventsQuerySchema` | Rules: title ≤ 150; description ≤ 5000; `endAt ≥ startAt`; `recurrenceUntil` required for WEEKLY/MONTHLY and ≤ start + 1 year; guests 0–5; range `to − from ≤ 100 days`; `sources ⊆ {events, holidays, assignments, quizzes, timetable}`. All-day input is `yyyy-MM-dd` start and inclusive end. The **server** converts it to `[schoolMidnight(start), schoolMidnight(end+1))`. | FR-4, FR-21, FR-32, NFR-8 |\n185\t| `src/lib/dates.ts` (edit) | add `schoolMidnight(dateStr, tz)`, `schoolDateOf(instant, tz)` | Pure and client-safe. The single source of all-day and date conversions. | FR-4, FR-16, NFR-3, ADR-4 |\n186\t\n187\t### 2.4 Edits to existing modules\n188\t\n189\t| File | Change | Reqs |\n190\t|---|---|---|\n191\t| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` | At both `// PRD-14 holidays hook` lines, replace the inline `schoolDay` weekday check with `if (!(await isSchoolDay(date)).isSchoolDay) return [];`. The weekday rule now lives only in `isSchoolDay`, so the old check is deleted, not duplicated. The return type is unchanged. | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-9 |\n192\t| `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` | `getToday` and `getOverview` add `noSchoolReason: string \\| null` from `isSchoolDay`. The register save path rejects with `VALIDATION_ERROR` \"holidayOverride required\" when the date is not a school day and `holidayOverride !== true` (D-8). | FR-18 |\n193\t| Attendance landing + `RegisterForm.tsx` | Landing shows \"No classes today — <reason>\". The register shows a warning `Alert` banner, and the save button opens `ConfirmDialog` \"Record attendance on a holiday anyway\", which sends `holidayOverride: true`. | FR-18, NFR-1 |\n194\t| Teacher/student/parent Today views (those consuming `getScheduleForDate`) | When `isSchoolDay` is false, show the holiday name instead of the empty class list. | FR-17 |\n195\t| `AssignmentForm.tsx`, `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` | On a `dueAt`/`availableUntil` change, `fetch('/api/school-day?date=')`. If false, show a non-blocking `<Alert severity=\"warning\">This date is a holiday (<title>).</Alert>`. Save is unchanged. | FR-19, FR-34 |\n196\t| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `event.created` (COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail false), `event.holiday_created` (COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true), `event.updated` (COMMUNICATION, false) and `event.rsvp_reminder` (COMMUNICATION, false). All roles. | FR-23, FR-28, FR-29 |\n197\t| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | Add an isolated `try { await sendRsvpReminders(now) } catch (e) { logger.error(...) }` block, matching the quiz-maintenance block. | FR-23, NFR-9 |\n198\t| `src/config/navigation.ts` | `{ label: 'Calendar', href: '/calendar', icon: CalendarMonth, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, as with the other `/account/*` pages. It is reached from the account area and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`. | FR-35 |\n199\t| `prisma/seed.ts` | `seedCalendar()`, idempotent: match by title (+ startAt where it is stable). It seeds the 7 events from FR-37 and the ROBOTICS course if absent (D-7). \"Sports day\" has no announcement link. Grade 6–8 exams use three `GRADE_LEVEL` audiences. \"Grade 7 parents\" = `GRADE_LEVEL` with only `includeParents`. | FR-37 |\n200\t\n201\t### 2.5 Route handlers (thin: requireUser/requireRole → Zod parse → service → `ok`/`apiError`)\n202\t\n203\t| Route | Auth | Service call | Reqs |\n204\t|---|---|---|---|\n205\t| `GET /api/calendar?from&to&sources&studentId` | any user | `getCalendarItems` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-32, NFR-7 |\n206\t| `POST /api/events` | ADMIN, TEACHER | `createEvent` | FR-5..7, FR-14, FR-28, FR-33 |\n207\t| `GET /api/events/:id` | visible to user | `getEvent` (+`myRsvp`, totals, `canEdit`) | FR-12, FR-22, FR-33 |\n208\t| `PATCH /api/events/:id` | creator, ADMIN | `updateEvent` | FR-6..8, FR-29, FR-33, FR-36 |\n209\t| `DELETE /api/events/:id` | creator, ADMIN | `deleteEvent` | FR-8, FR-33, FR-36 |\n210\t| `GET /api/events/:id/ics` | visible to user | `getEvent` → `buildCalendar([event])` | FR-12, FR-33 |\n211\t| `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp` | audience member | `upsertRsvp` | FR-21 |\n212\t| `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps[?format=csv]` | creator, ADMIN | `listRsvps` → JSON or `csv.ts` | FR-22 |\n213\t| `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` | any user | `getOrCreateFeedToken` | FR-24, FR-25 |\n214\t| `POST /api/me/calendar-feed/reset` | any user | `resetFeedToken` | FR-24, FR-25 |\n215\t| `GET /api/calendar/feed/[token]` (`.ics` stripped from param) | token | `findUserByFeedToken` → `rateLimit` → `getCalendarItems` → `buildCalendar` | FR-26, FR-27, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n216\t| `GET /api/school-day?date=` (new singular folder; `/api/school-days` untouched) | any user | `isSchoolDay` | FR-16, FR-19, FR-34 |\n217\t| `GET /api/public/events?from&to` | public, IP rate limit | `getPublicEvents` | FR-30, D-9 |\n218\t| `POST /api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks` | ADMIN | `createTermBreaks` | FR-20 |\n219\t\n220\tError mapping: not visible → 404 `NOT_FOUND`. Visible but not permitted → 403 `FORBIDDEN`. RSVP after the deadline, or with RSVP disabled → 409 `CONFLICT`. Feed token unknown → plain 404. Feed over the limit → 429 `RATE_LIMITED` + `Retry-After`. `arch-api-contracts` defines the exact shapes.\n221\t\n222\t### 2.6 UI\n223\t\n224\t| Path / component | Contents | Reqs |\n225\t|---|---|---|\n226\t| `src/app/(app)/calendar/page.tsx` (server) → `CalendarView.tsx` (client) | `requirePageUser`. `<EventCalendar>` from `@mui/x-scheduler/event-calendar`: `views={['month','week','agenda']}`, week `startTime:7, endTime:19`, agenda `dayCount:30`, `displayTimezone={tz}`, `readOnly`, `eventCreation={false}`. The default view is month at `useMediaQuery('(min-width:768px)')`, agenda below that. Controlled `events`, refetched on `onVisibleDateChange`/`onViewChange` with plain `fetch` and a small Map cache keyed by `from|to|sources|studentId`. The page opens the drawer when `?event=<id>` is present (notification links). | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-12 |\n227\t| `SourceChips` | MUI `Chip`s: School events · My assignments · My quizzes · My timetable (Week view only) · Holidays. Stored in `localStorage['calendar.sources']`. Holidays = HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool`; School events = everything else, with no overlap. `timetable` is fetched only in Week view. | FR-10 |\n228\t| Child filter (PARENT only) | `Select`: \"All children\" or one child → `studentId`. Deadline titles get the child's name prefixed by the server. | FR-11 |\n229\t| `EventDrawer` | Right-anchored `Drawer`: title, category `Chip`, time in school tz, location, `MarkdownView` description, audience chips, RSVP controls (`ToggleButtonGroup` + guests `TextField` for parents + note; disabled after the deadline), \"Add to my calendar\" (`<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`), and edit/delete when `canEdit` (delete via `ConfirmDialog`). Creator/admin see an RSVP `DataTable` + CSV link. | FR-12, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1 |\n230\t| Deadline click | `onEventEditingStart` → `cancel()` → `router.push(item.href)` | FR-13 |\n231\t| `EventEditorDialog` | \"New event\" button (ADMIN/TEACHER). React Hook Form + `eventInputSchema`. Fields: title, category (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK only for admins), all-day switch, date/time pickers (`@mui/x-date-pickers`), location, `MarkdownEditor`, `AudienceBuilder`, recurrence select + until date, RSVP switch + deadline, and admin-only `isNoSchool`/`isPublic`. Results go through `useToast`. | FR-4..7, FR-14 |\n232\t| `src/components/AudienceBuilder/` (new shared) | Rows of type `Select` + entity `Autocomplete` (grade level / section / course / role) + three include `Checkbox`es. Types are filtered by `canTargetAudience` rules on the client. The server stays authoritative. | FR-3, FR-7, FR-14 |\n233\t| `src/app/(app)/account/calendar/page.tsx` | \"Subscribe\" card: URL `TextField` (read-only) + copy (`navigator.clipboard`), Google/Apple/Outlook instructions as static text, and \"Reset link\" behind `ConfirmDialog`. When `url` is null: \"Reset link to get a new URL\" (D-6). | FR-24, FR-25 |\n234\t| `src/app/(app)/admin/academic-years/[id]/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. Year name, read-only term list (existing terms service), and an \"Add term breaks\" button + `ConfirmDialog` that shows the number of breaks created via toast. | FR-20 |\n235\t\n236\t---\n237\t\n238\t## 3. Data Flow\n239\t\n240\t### 3.1 Calendar read (`GET /api/calendar`, the feed, upcoming events)\n241\t\n242\t```\n243\troute → calendarQuerySchema (≤100 days) → getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})\n244\t  1. scope   = studentId ? resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId) : getAccessibleStudentIds(user)   (404 for others)\n245\t  2. where   = audienceWhereForUser(user, scope)          // keys computed once\n246\t  3. Promise.all([\n247\t       events:      CalendarEvent where startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR (recurrence≠NONE AND recurrenceUntil ≥ from))\n248\t                    AND (audiences some where) OR createdById=user  (ADMIN: no audience filter)\n249\t                    → expandOccurrences(e, from, to, tz) → split into holidays / events by category+isNoSchool,\n250\t       assignments: existing assignment service, PUBLISHED, dueAt ∈ [from,to), scoped students/courses,\n251\t       quizzes:     existing quiz service, PUBLISHED, availableUntil ∈ [from,to),\n252\t       timetable:   getPersonalTimetable(target) projected onto dates in range, skipping noSchoolDays(from,to)\n253\t     ]) – only for requested sources\n254\t  4. map → CalendarItem union {kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', id, title, start, end, allDay, color, href?, childName?}\n255\t```\n256\tThe feed calls the same function with `from=now−30d, to=now+365d`, sources minus timetable, and recurring events **unexpanded**. Instead of occurrences it gets the series rows so it can emit RRULE. The 100-day cap is skipped because the call is internal. Traces to FR-10, FR-11, FR-15, FR-26, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n257\t\n258\t### 3.2 Event write\n259\t\n260\t```\n261\tPOST/PATCH → eventInputSchema → createEvent/updateEvent(user, input)\n262\t  - FR-6: non-admin + (isNoSchool | isPublic | HOLIDAY | TERM_BREAK) → 403\n263\t  - FR-7: every audience must pass canTargetAudience(user, a) → else 403\n264\t  - FR-8: PATCH/DELETE requires createdById===user.id or ADMIN\n265\t  - FR-5: isNoSchool ??= category ∈ {HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK}\n266\t  - all-day → schoolMidnight conversion (FR-4)\n267\t  - prisma.$transaction: event + replace audiences\n268\t  - after commit:\n269\t      FR-36 audit() if ADMIN && createdById≠user.id (update/delete)\n270\t      FR-28 create: first occurrence within 30 days → notify(HOLIDAY|TERM_BREAK ? 'event.holiday_created' : 'event.created',\n271\t            resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences) − creator, link '/calendar?event=<id>')\n272\t      FR-29 update: startAt|endAt|allDay|location changed AND event upcoming → notify('event.updated') once\n273\t```\n274\t\n275\t### 3.3 Audience resolution (PRD-12 FR-2 semantics)\n276\t\n277\t| Type | refId | Students (`includeStudents`) | Parents (`includeParents`) | Teachers (`includeTeachers`) |\n278\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n279\t| SCHOOL | null | all active users | | |\n280\t| STAFF | null | ADMIN + TEACHER | | |\n281\t| ROLE | role name | users with that role | | |\n282\t| GRADE_LEVEL | gradeLevelId | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId = refId` | their `ParentStudentLink` parents | teachers of current-year courses in sections of that grade |\n283\t| SECTION | sectionId | current-year `SectionMember`s | their parents | homeroom teacher + teachers of courses in the section |\n284\t| COURSE | courseId | ACTIVE `Enrollment`s | their parents | `teacherId` + `coTeacherIds` |\n285\t\n286\tOnly ACTIVE, non-archived users count. `isUserInAudience` and `audienceWhereForUser` give the same answer as `resolveAudienceUserIds`. A property-style integration test loops over every seed user to check this (PRD-12 test requirement). Traces to FR-3, FR-7, NFR-7.\n287\t\n288\t### 3.4 School-day check\n289\t\n290\t```\n291\tisSchoolDay(date) → d = schoolDateOf(date, tz), isoDay\n292\t  1. SchoolDay[isoDay].isTeaching ?? isoDay ≤ 5   → false, reason 'Not a teaching day'\n293\t  2. isNoSchool events with a SCHOOL audience where startAt < midnight(d+1) AND (endAt > midnight(d) OR recurring)\n294\t     → expandOccurrences within that day → first hit → false, reason 'Holiday: <title>'\n295\t  3. → { isSchoolDay: true, reason: null }\n296\tnoSchoolDays(from, to) = one query, same rules, returns Map<date, reason> (used by the timetable source; avoids N calls)\n297\t```\n298\tCallers: timetable-service (FR-17), attendance (FR-18), `/api/school-day` (FR-19, FR-34), timetable source in §3.1. Traces to FR-16..19, FR-34.\n299\t\n300\t### 3.5 RSVP\n301\t\n302\t`PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp` → `rsvpSchema` → `upsertRsvp`:\n303\t1. Check the event is visible and `rsvpEnabled`. Otherwise 404 (not visible) or 409.\n304\t2. Require `isUserInAudience`. Otherwise 403.\n305\t3. Require `now < rsvpDeadline`. Otherwise 409.\n306\t4. If the user is not a PARENT, force `guests = 0`.\n307\t5. Upsert on `(eventId, userId)`.\n308\t\n309\tA recurring event has one RSVP for the whole series. The drawer gets `myRsvp` and totals `{yes, no, maybe, guests}` from `GET /api/events/:id`. Creator and admin read the full list via `/rsvps`, or `?format=csv` via `csv.ts`. Traces to FR-21, FR-22.\n310\t\n311\t### 3.6 Reminder job\n312\t\n313\tCron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` → `sendRsvpReminders(now)` → claim → audience − responders → `notify('event.rsvp_reminder', link '/calendar?event=<id>')`. Traces to FR-23.\n314\t\n315\t### 3.7 iCal feed\n316\t\n317\t```\n318\tGET /api/calendar/feed/<token>.ics\n319\t  token = param.replace(/\\.ics$/, '') → hashToken(token) → CalendarFeedToken by tokenHash (unique) → user ACTIVE?\n320\t    no → 404 text/plain\n321\t  rateLimit('calfeed:'+hash, 60, 3_600_000) → !ok → 429 + Retry-After\n322\t  items = getCalendarItems(user, feed window, series mode)\n323\t  body  = buildCalendar(items, tz, window)   // VTIMEZONE for transitions in window, RRULE for series\n324\t  200 text/calendar; charset=utf-8, Cache-Control: private, max-age=900\n325\t```\n326\tToken lifecycle:\n327\t- `getOrCreateFeedToken` creates the row on first use from `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stores `hashToken(raw)`, and returns the URL once.\n328\t- `resetFeedToken` upserts a new hash, so the old URL returns 404 immediately.\n329\t- No raw token is ever logged.\n330\t\n331\tTraces to FR-24..27, NFR-5, NFR-6, ADR-6, ADR-7.\n332\t\n333\t### 3.8 Public and dashboard hooks\n334\t\n335\t- `getPublicEvents(from, to)`: `isPublic` events, expanded, returning only public-safe fields (id, title, category, start, end, allDay, location, description). Traces to FR-30.\n336\t- `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)`: `getCalendarItems(user, now..now+90d, ['events','holidays'])`, sorted, then the first `limit` items. No UI. Traces to FR-31, NFR-11.\n337\t\n338\t### 3.9 Term breaks\n339\t\n340\t`POST /api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks` (ADMIN) → `createTermBreaks`:\n341\t1. Order the terms by `startDate`.\n342\t2. For each consecutive pair where `next.start > prev.end + 1 day`, create an all-day TERM_BREAK with `isNoSchool=true` and a SCHOOL audience, from `prev.end+1` (inclusive) to `next.start` (exclusive).\n343\t3. Skip any gap that already has a TERM_BREAK with the same span. This makes the call idempotent.\n344\t4. Return `{ created }`.\n345\t5. Write an `audit()` entry.\n346\t\n347\tTraces to FR-20.\n348\t\n349\t---\n350\t\n351\t## 4. Cross-cutting\n352\t\n353\t- **Time (NFR-3, NFR-8).**\n354\t  - Storage is in UTC. Display uses `SchoolSettings.timezone`, read via the existing `getSchoolTimezone()`. No third copy is created.\n355\t  - All-day events run from school-tz midnight with an exclusive end.\n356\t  - Expansion steps in wall-clock time.\n357\t  - The feed uses `VALUE=DATE` for all-day events and `TZID` + VTIMEZONE for series.\n358\t  - The scheduler gets `displayTimezone`.\n359\t  - One DST-week test fixture (America/New_York 2026-11-01, or the seed tz) runs through the expansion, the all-day path and the feed.\n360\t- **Security (NFR-5, NFR-7).**\n361\t  - Every route calls `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (hashed token) and public events (public fields only, IP limit).\n362\t  - Per-entity checks live in calendar-service.\n363\t  - Students see only themselves, and parents only their linked children (`getAccessibleStudentIds` / `resolveViewedStudent`).\n364\t  - A non-visible event returns 404, so its existence doesn't leak.\n365\t- **Performance (NFR-4).**\n366\t  - A parent with 3 children in month view needs about 6 indexed queries, run in parallel.\n367\t  - The audience is filtered in SQL, and holidays are found with one `noSchoolDays` query.\n368\t  - There is no cache layer. Add one only if the Playwright timing or a measurement exceeds 500 ms.\n369\t- **UI rules (NFR-1, NFR-12).**\n370\t  - Only MUI, icons and MUI X (including the scheduler) are used. Toasts go through `useToast`, side panels through `Drawer`, and confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`.\n371\t  - English only. The breakpoint is 768 px.\n372\t- **Scope (NFR-11).**\n373\t  - Out of scope: per-occurrence exceptions, room booking (`roomId` is stored and unused), two-way sync, and dashboard or public-site UI.\n374\t- **Tests (NFR-10).**\n375\t  - Unit tests:\n376\t    - `expandOccurrences`: weekly, monthly on the 31st, the until bound, a DST week\n377\t    - `isSchoolDay`: weekday, holiday, recurring no-school\n378\t    - `ical`: escaping `, ; \\ \\n`, folding, RRULE, VALUE=DATE exclusive end, node-ical parse\n379\t    - all-day conversion\n380\t    - term-break gap math\n381\t    - `canTargetAudience`\n382\t  - Integration tests:\n383\t    - calendar merge per role (admin, teacher, student, parent with 3 children)\n384\t    - feed token reset (old URL 404, new URL 200 and node-ical-valid)\n385\t    - RSVP deadline (409) and parent-only guests\n386\t    - audience resolver parity across seed users\n387\t    - teacher SCHOOL create → 403\n388\t  - Playwright:\n389\t    - an admin creates a holiday, and the student's Today view shows the holiday name\n390\t    - a parent RSVPs\n391\t    - the feed URL returns a valid ICS\n392\t  - `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` stays green.\n393\t\n394\t### Risks carried forward\n395\t\n396\t| Risk | Mitigation |\n397\t|---|---|\n398\t| R1 Beta scheduler API drift | Exact pin, MCP lookup before use, and the scheduler used only as a read-only display (ADR-2). The D-5 fallback is pre-agreed. |\n399\t| R2 Import cycle between timetable and calendar | The edges run one way: timetable-service → calendar-service, and sources.ts → (timetable, assignments, quizzes, calendar-service). calendar-service reads teaching weekdays via `prisma.schoolDay` and never imports timetable-service. |\n400\t| R3 DST correctness across 4 code paths | Shared pure helpers in `src/lib/dates.ts` plus one shared DST fixture. |\n401\t| R4 Audience is both the hot path and the security boundary | A single implementation plus the parity test. |\n402\t\n403\t---\n404\t\n405\t## 5. Requirements Traceability\n406\t\n407\t| Req | Design element(s) |\n408\t|---|---|\n409\t| FR-1 | §2.1 exact pin `@mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15` + scoped override (ADR-1) |\n410\t| FR-2 | §2.2 migration `20261113000000_add_calendar`: enums, 4 models, cascades, `[startAt,endAt]` index |\n411\t| FR-3 | §2.2 `AudienceType` (PRD-12 values); §2.3 `announcements/audience.ts`; §3.3 resolution table |\n412\t| FR-4 | §2.3 `validators/calendar.ts` + `schoolMidnight`; §3.2 all-day conversion |\n413\t| FR-5 | §3.2 `isNoSchool ??= HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK` in `createEvent` |\n414\t| FR-6 | §3.2 admin-only field check; §2.6 editor hides admin fields |\n415\t| FR-7 | §2.3 `canTargetAudience`; §3.2 check on create/patch |\n416\t| FR-8 | §3.2 creator/ADMIN guard on PATCH/DELETE |\n417\t| FR-9 | §2.6 `CalendarView` with `EventCalendar` views/viewConfig/breakpoint; D-5 agenda fallback |\n418\t| FR-10 | §2.6 `SourceChips` + localStorage; §3.1 `sources` param, holidays/events split |\n419\t| FR-11 | §2.6 parent child filter; §3.1 `studentId` scope + `childName` |\n420\t| FR-12 | §2.6 `EventDrawer`; §2.5 `GET /api/events/:id`, `/ics` |\n421\t| FR-13 | §2.6 deadline click → `router.push(href)` |\n422\t| FR-14 | §2.6 `EventEditorDialog` + `AudienceBuilder` |\n423\t| FR-15 | §2.3 `recurrence.ts` `expandOccurrences`; §3.1 read-time expansion |\n424\t| FR-16 | §2.3 `isSchoolDay`; §3.4 |\n425\t| FR-17 | §2.4 timetable-service hook + Today views |\n426\t| FR-18 | §2.4 attendance `noSchoolReason`, `holidayOverride` (D-8), `RegisterForm` banner/confirm |\n427\t| FR-19 | §2.4 `AssignmentForm` / `QuizSettingsPanel` warning via `/api/school-day` |\n428\t| FR-20 | §2.6 `/admin/academic-years/[id]` page; §2.5 term-breaks route; §3.9 `createTermBreaks` |\n429\t| FR-21 | §2.5 `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp`; §3.5 `upsertRsvp` rules |\n430\t| FR-22 | §2.5 `/rsvps[?format=csv]`; §2.6 drawer totals + `DataTable` |\n431\t| FR-23 | §2.3 `maintenance.ts`; §2.4 cron hook + type; D-1 `rsvpReminderSentAt` |\n432\t| FR-24 | §2.6 `/account/calendar`; §2.5 me/calendar-feed routes |\n433\t| FR-25 | §3.7 token lifecycle with `hashToken`; D-6 |\n434\t| FR-26 | §2.3 `ical.ts`; §3.7 feed build (window, RRULE, VTIMEZONE, escaping) |\n435\t| FR-27 | §2.5 feed route; §3.7 rate limit + Cache-Control |\n436\t| FR-28 | §2.4 types `event.created` + `event.holiday_created` (D-3); §3.2 notify on create |\n437\t| FR-29 | §2.4 type `event.updated`; §3.2 notify on time/location change |\n438\t| FR-30 | §3.8 `getPublicEvents`; §2.5 `/api/public/events` (D-9) |\n439\t| FR-31 | §3.8 `getUpcomingEventsForUser` |\n440\t| FR-32 | §2.5 `GET /api/calendar`; §3.1 `getCalendarItems`; 100-day cap in validator |\n441\t| FR-33 | §2.5 event CRUD + `/ics` routes |\n442\t| FR-34 | §2.5 `GET /api/school-day` (singular, new folder) |\n443\t| FR-35 | §2.4 `navigation.ts` Calendar entry |\n444\t| FR-36 | §3.2 `audit()` on admin edits/deletes of other users' events |\n445\t| FR-37 | §2.4 `seedCalendar()` + ROBOTICS course (D-7) |\n446\t| NFR-1 | §2.6 MUI-only components; §4 UI rules |\n447\t| NFR-2 | §2.1 MCP lookup gate before scheduler use |\n448\t| NFR-3 | §2.3 wall-clock expansion, `dates.ts` helpers, ical VALUE=DATE/TZID; §4 DST fixture |\n449\t| NFR-4 | §3.1 parallel indexed queries, SQL audience filter, D-2 index; §4 performance |\n450\t| NFR-5 | §3.7 32-byte token, SHA-256 hash; §3.1 shared read path |\n451\t| NFR-6 | §2.1 `node-ical` devDep; §4 parse tests |\n452\t| NFR-7 | §2.5 auth column; §3.3; §4 security |\n453\t| NFR-8 | §2.3 module layout under `src/server/calendar/`; thin routes; Zod; UTC storage |\n454\t| NFR-9 | §1 reuse list; §2.4 edits instead of new helpers |\n455\t| NFR-10 | §4 tests |\n456\t| NFR-11 | §4 scope; §3.8 hooks only |\n457\t| NFR-12 | §2.6 768 px breakpoint, English only |\n458\t{\n459\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-14\",\n460\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:10:00Z\",\n461\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n462\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n463\t  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-14: School Calendar, Events & Holidays\",\n464\t  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-014 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-14.\",\n465\t  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n466\t  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n467\t    \"DEPENDENCY GAP: PRD-12 (Announcements) is NOT present in the workspace. prisma/schema.prisma has no AudienceType enum and no Announcement model; no audience.ts helper or audience builder component exists anywhere under src/. PRD-14 FR-1 (EventAudience.type reuses AudienceType), FR-2.2 (reuse audience.ts), FR-3.5 (audience builder from PRD-12) and the 'Sports day' seed (ties to a PRD-12 announcement) all assume it. The Architect must decide whether SH-14 introduces a minimal AudienceType + audience resolver (in a form PRD-12 can adopt later) or blocks.\",\n468\t    \"/admin/academic-years/[id] page does not exist (only the REST API under src/app/api/academic-years/[id] incl. terms and terms/generate). FR-5.5 'Add term breaks' needs a UI host; the page or an equivalent admin surface has to be created or the shortcut placed elsewhere.\",\n469\t    \"@mui/x-scheduler is not in package.json (confirmed; @mui/material, x-charts, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers are pinned at 9.5.0). Neither 'ics' nor 'node-ical' is installed.\",\n470\t    \"PRD-06 timetable service exists: src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts exports getScheduleForDate (line ~542), getSchoolScheduleForDate and listSchoolDays/updateSchoolDays (teaching weekdays). src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts calls getScheduleForDate for the register landing.\",\n471\t    \"Existing GET/PUT /api/school-days (plural, PRD-06 teaching weekdays) is distinct from the new GET /api/school-day?date= (singular) in this PRD; both must coexist and neither may be renamed.\",\n472\t    \"Rate limiter exists at src/server/rate-limit.ts (rateLimit) — reuse for the feed's 60 req/token/hour.\",\n473\t    \"Maintenance runs on the internal dispatch cron (src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; PRD-10 precedent src/server/quiz/maintenance.ts) — the event.rsvp_reminder pass should hook in there.\",\n474\t    \"Notification types are registered in src/server/notifications/types.ts (NOTIFICATION_TYPES, categories incl. COMMUNICATION/ACADEMIC).\",\n475\t    \"No src/server/calendar/ directory exists yet; FR-5.1 names src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts, consistent with the feature-subdirectory convention.\",\n476\t    \"Latest migration is 20261112000000_add_direct_messaging; seed is prisma/seed.ts (npm run db:seed).\"\n477\t  ],\n478\t\n479\t  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n480\t    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Install @mui/x-scheduler pinned to the exact version found via the MUI MCP server before any other work in this PRD.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-0 Dependency (1)\" },\n481\t    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add Prisma enums EventCategory, Recurrence, RsvpResponse and models CalendarEvent, EventAudience, EventRsvp (composite PK eventId+userId) and CalendarFeedToken exactly as specified, with cascade deletes and the [startAt, endAt] index, in one new migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model\" },\n482\t    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"EventAudience.type reuses the AudienceType enum from PRD-12; because that enum does not exist in the workspace, its values (at least SCHOOL, COURSE, SECTION, grade-level style targets implied by seed data) must be defined by this ticket or supplied by PRD-12.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (EventAudience.type comment 'reuse enum from PRD-12'); §Seed Data (Grade 6–8, Grade 7 parents, course audience); brownfield finding\" },\n483\t    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Validate events with Zod in src/lib/validators/calendar.ts: title ≤ 150 chars, description Markdown ≤ 5,000 chars, endAt ≥ startAt, all-day events stored as school-timezone midnight with exclusive endAt, recurrenceUntil required for WEEKLY/MONTHLY and ≤ 1 year after start, RSVP guests 0–5.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 field comments; §FR-4 Recurrence; §Platform Context › Validation\" },\n484\t    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"isNoSchool defaults to true for HOLIDAY and TERM_BREAK categories and false otherwise.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (isNoSchool comment)\" },\n485\t    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"ADMIN may create events with any audience; isNoSchool, isPublic and the HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK categories are admin-only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2 Permissions (1)\" },\n486\t    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"TEACHER may create events only for COURSE audiences they manage or their homeroom SECTION, using the same rule as PRD-12's audience.ts (a SCHOOL-audience create by a teacher returns 403).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2 Permissions (2); Acceptance Criterion 7\" },\n487\t    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Creators may edit/delete their own events; admins may edit/delete all events.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2 Permissions (3)\" },\n488\t    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Add /calendar page using MUI X Scheduler EventCalendar with month (default ≥ 768 px), week (07:00–19:00 time grid, all-day row; viewConfig startTime 7, endTime 19) and agenda (default < 768 px; grouped by day, 30 days ahead, infinite scroll) views plus Today/previous/next/date-picker navigation; fall back to @mui/material + @mui/x-date-pickers (DateCalendar + List) only for behaviour missing from the Community version.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 Calendar page (1)\" },\n489\t    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Calendar sources are toggleable MUI Chips persisted in localStorage: School events (coloured by category), My assignments (due dates, subject colour), My quizzes (availability window end), My timetable (Week view only, light background blocks), Holidays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 (2)\" },\n490\t    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Parents get a child filter (All children or one); deadline items for the selected children are labelled with the child's name.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 (3); Acceptance Criterion 3\" },\n491\t    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Clicking an event opens a right-anchored MUI Drawer showing title, category badge, time in school timezone, location, description (Markdown), audience chips, RSVP controls when enabled, 'Add to my calendar' (.ics download of that event) and edit/delete for permitted users.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 (4)\" },\n492\t    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Clicking an assignment or quiz deadline navigates to that assignment or quiz.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 (4); Acceptance Criterion 3\" },\n493\t    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"ADMIN/TEACHER see a 'New event' button opening an editor Dialog with all model fields, the PRD-12 audience builder, recurrence options, RSVP toggle and RSVP deadline.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 (5) (audience builder does not exist in workspace — see FR-3)\" },\n494\t    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Recurring events (NONE/WEEKLY/MONTHLY-by-date) are stored once and expanded at read time by expandOccurrences(event, from, to) up to recurrenceUntil; the calendar API returns plain expanded occurrences; edits apply to the whole series.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4 Recurrence; §FR-3 (1); §Out of Scope; Acceptance Criterion 4\" },\n495\t    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"isSchoolDay(date) in src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts returns false when the weekday is not a PRD-06 teaching day or any isNoSchool event with SCHOOL audience covers the date, and exposes the reason (e.g. holiday title).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5 Holidays integration (1); Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n496\t    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Update PRD-06 getScheduleForDate to return an empty list with reason 'Holiday: <title>' on non-school days; Today views show the holiday name instead of classes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5 (2); Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n497\t    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Update PRD-07 teacher register landing to show 'No classes today — <holiday>' on non-school days; opening a register for such a date shows a warning banner and saving requires an extra 'Record attendance on a holiday anyway' confirmation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5 (3); Acceptance Criterion 2\" },\n498\t    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"PRD-09 assignment editor and PRD-10 quiz settings show a non-blocking warning 'This date is a holiday (<title>).' when the due/close date is a non-school day, still allowing save.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5 (4); Acceptance Criterion 8\" },\n499\t    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Admin 'Add term breaks' shortcut on /admin/academic-years/[id] creates TERM_BREAK no-school events for the gaps between consecutive terms.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5 (5) (host page does not exist in workspace — only the API)\" },\n500\t    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"When RSVP is enabled, audience members answer Yes/No/Maybe with guest count (parents) and optional note via PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp until rsvpDeadline; after the deadline the API rejects and the drawer controls are disabled.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6 RSVP (1); §API; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n501\t    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"The event drawer shows the user's own response and totals; the creator and admins see the full RSVP list with CSV export (GET /api/events/:id/rsvps?format=csv).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6 (1); §API\" },\n502\t    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Register notification type event.rsvp_reminder; the maintenance run notifies non-responding audience members 48 hours before the RSVP deadline, once per event.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6 (2)\" },\n503\t    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Add /account/calendar page with a 'Subscribe' section: private URL APP_URL/api/calendar/feed/<token>.ics, copy button, Google/Apple/Outlook instructions and 'Reset link' which invalidates the old token (old URL returns 404).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7 iCal feed (1); Acceptance Criterion 5\" },\n504\t    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Feed tokens: GET /api/me/calendar-feed and POST /api/me/calendar-feed/reset return the URL; the raw token is shown only at creation/reset and stored hashed in CalendarFeedToken.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API (me/calendar-feed rows); §NFR 3\" },\n505\t    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The RFC 5545 text/calendar feed contains the user's school events (parents: all children's audiences) from 30 days past to 365 days ahead, assignment due dates and quiz close times with URL back to SchoolHub, RRULE for recurring events, a VTIMEZONE for the school timezone, and RFC escaping of commas, semicolons and newlines.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7 (2); Acceptance Criteria 4, 5\" },\n506\t    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"GET /api/calendar/feed/:token.ics is public (token-authenticated), rate limited to 60 requests per token per hour (429) and sends Cache-Control: private, max-age=900.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7 (3); §API\" },\n507\t    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Register event.created, notifying audience members when an event starting within the next 30 days is created (email default false; HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK email default true).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8 Notifications (1)\" },\n508\t    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Register event.updated, notifying audience members once per edit when time or location of an upcoming event changes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8 (2)\" },\n509\t    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Expose getPublicEvents(from, to) and GET /api/public/events?from=&to= returning isPublic events for PRD-18.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9 (1); §API\" },\n510\t    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Expose getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit) for PRD-16 dashboards.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9 (2)\" },\n511\t    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"GET /api/calendar?from=&to=&sources=&studentId= returns merged, expanded, audience-filtered items for any role; the requested range is limited to ≤ 100 days.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API (first row)\" },\n512\t    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Event CRUD API: POST /api/events (ADMIN, TEACHER with audience check); GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/events/:id (audience/creator/ADMIN); GET /api/events/:id/ics (audience, single-event download).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n513\t    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"GET /api/school-day?date= (any user) returns { isSchoolDay, reason }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API (last row)\" },\n514\t    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Add /calendar (all roles) and /account/calendar entries to src/config/navigation.ts as needed.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › Code layout ('A PRD that adds a page adds its nav entry there'); §FR-3; §FR-7\" },\n515\t    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Admin edits/deletes of events created by someone else write an AuditLog row via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › Code layout (AuditLog rule); §FR-2 (3)\" },\n516\t    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Seed 2026–2027 events: Thanksgiving break (26–27 Nov), Winter break (21 Dec – 1 Jan, TERM_BREAK), Semester 1 exams (11–15 Jan, EXAM, Grade 6–8), Parent–teacher evening (RSVP, seed date + 2 weeks, Grade 7 parents), Science fair (public), weekly Chess club (Tuesdays, Robotics Club course audience), Sports day (public, tied to the PRD-12 announcement).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" }\n517\t  ],\n518\t\n519\t  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n520\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"UI is built only from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material and the allowed MUI X packages (incl. @mui/x-scheduler); banned libraries (FullCalendar, Tailwind, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.) are not imported; toasts via shared useToast(), side panels via Drawer, confirmations via Dialog; QA verifies no banned imports and every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule (1, 3, 5, 6)\" },\n521\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Every MUI component (especially beta @mui/x-scheduler: Quickstart, Views, Events, Timezones, Localization pages) is looked up via the MUI MCP server (useMuiDocs + fetchDocs) before use; if MCP is unreachable, stop and report a blocker.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule (2); §FR-3 (1)\" },\n522\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"All-day events and DST transitions in the school timezone render on the correct dates in both UI and iCal feed, with tests covering a DST-change week.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n523\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"A month view for a parent with 3 children loads in under 500 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n524\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Feed tokens are 32 random bytes stored hashed; the feed exposes no data beyond what the user can see in the app.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n525\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"The generated feed passes an RFC 5545 validator test (parsed with node-ical in tests).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n526\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every handler and server page enforces access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and per-entity checks; parents see only linked children's data, students only their own.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › Code layout; §Roles\" },\n527\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Follow platform conventions: thin Zod-parsing route handlers, services under src/server/calendar/, { data } / list / error response shapes and error codes, pagination/sort/search params, cuid IDs, createdAt/updatedAt, UTC storage displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone, logger instead of console.log.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › Code layout and conventions\" },\n528\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Reuse existing models, services, components and helpers (timetable-service, rate-limit, notify, audit, DataTable, useToast, maintenance cron); never re-scaffold, duplicate helpers or rename existing routes/models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context (intro paragraph)\" },\n529\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing and add: unit tests (occurrence expansion, isSchoolDay, iCal escaping and RRULE, all-day exclusive end), integration tests (calendar merge per role, feed token reset, RSVP deadline enforcement), Playwright (admin holiday → student Today view; parent RSVP; feed URL returns valid ICS).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Test Requirements\" },\n530\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Scope is fixed to this PRD: no room booking, no single-occurrence exceptions or complex recurrence, no two-way external sync, no behaviour owned by later PRDs (PRD-16 dashboards and PRD-18 public site only get service/API hooks).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; §Assumptions and constraints; §FR-9\" },\n531\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Supports the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari; English-only UI; responsive with a 768 px breakpoint for default view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §FR-3 (1)\" }\n532\t  ],\n533\t\n534\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n535\t  \"confidenceMethod\": \"HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40, averaged over 49 requirements (43 HIGH, 5 MEDIUM, 1 LOW).\",\n536\t\n537\t  \"clarificationLog\": [\n538\t    {\n539\t      \"round\": 1,\n540\t      \"questions\": [\n541\t        \"PRD-12 (Announcements: AudienceType enum, audience.ts, audience builder) is not in the workspace. Should SH-14 introduce a minimal AudienceType (SCHOOL, GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION, COURSE?) + resolver designed for PRD-12 to adopt, or is PRD-12 expected to land first?\",\n542\t        \"/admin/academic-years/[id] has no page today. Should FR-20 create that page, or host 'Add term breaks' on an existing admin screen?\",\n543\t        \"The 'Holidays' source and the 'School events' source both include HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK events — should toggling 'School events' off still show holidays (i.e. Holidays wins / dedupe)?\",\n544\t        \"RSVP guest count is annotated '(parents)' — are guests allowed only for PARENT responders (others forced to 0)?\",\n545\t        \"Which feed contents apply to TEACHER and ADMIN (e.g. admins: all events or only those whose audience includes them)? Do teachers get deadlines for assignments/quizzes they set?\",\n546\t        \"Is a 'Sports day' PRD-12 announcement expected to exist for the seed to link to, given PRD-12 is absent?\"\n547\t      ],\n548\t      \"unresolved\": [\n549\t        \"AudienceType / audience.ts / audience builder ownership (PRD-12 missing) — proceeding on assumption the Architect defines a minimal, PRD-12-compatible version in this ticket (FR-3 LOW, FR-7/FR-14 MEDIUM).\",\n550\t        \"Host page for 'Add term breaks' (FR-20 MEDIUM).\",\n551\t        \"Holidays vs School events source overlap — default assumption: Holidays chip controls HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/isNoSchool events, School events chip controls the rest, no duplicates.\",\n552\t        \"Guest count for non-parents — default assumption: parents only, others 0.\",\n553\t        \"Teacher/admin feed scope — default assumption: same visibility as GET /api/calendar for that user (NFR-5).\",\n554\t        \"Sports day seed linkage — default assumption: seed the event without an announcement link if no announcement exists.\"\n555\t      ]\n556\t    }\n557\t  ],\n558\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n559\t}\n560\t{\n561\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-14\",\n562\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:12:00Z\",\n563\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n564\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n565\t\n566\t  \"status\": \"complete\",\n567\t  \"requirementsCount\": 49,\n568\t  \"functionalCount\": 37,\n569\t  \"nonFunctionalCount\": 12,\n570\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n571\t  \"blockers\": [],\n572\t  \"warnings\": [\n573\t    \"PRD-12 dependency missing in workspace: no AudienceType enum, audience.ts or audience builder. Architect must decide whether SH-14 adds a minimal PRD-12-compatible version (FR-3, FR-7, FR-14, FR-37 Sports day).\",\n574\t    \"/admin/academic-years/[id] page does not exist (API only) — FR-20 needs a host page.\",\n575\t    \"@mui/x-scheduler (beta) must be installed and version-pinned via MUI MCP first (FR-1); node-ical needed as devDependency for NFR-6.\"\n576\t  ],\n577\t  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n578\t}\n579\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f1e9cdf-3174-43b4-adaa-4e6aa4038a8c","uuid":"af796a19-fa6b-412b-ada6-ce802bcf949b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:54:05.441Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/8f1e9cdf-3174-43b4-adaa-4e6aa4038a8c/tool-results/b7gamsbqf.txt","content":"artifacts/:\napprovals\narchitect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\nqa\nrun-summary.json\ntelemetry\nui-verification\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n# System Design: PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays\n\nTicket: SH-14 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T23:58:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs:\n- `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`: 37 FR and 12 NFR, 96% confidence\n- `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`\n- `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md`: ADR-1 to ADR-13\n- `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`: B1 to B19, D1 to D9, R1 to R4\n\n> This replaces the stale SH-13 `system-design.md`. `api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in this folder are still SH-13 until `arch-api-contracts` rewrites them.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSH-14 adds a school calendar to the existing SchoolHub app (Next.js 14 App Router, Prisma/PostgreSQL, MUI 9). The pieces are:\n\n- one Prisma migration\n- one server module, `src/server/calendar/`\n- a shared audience resolver, at the path PRD-12 will use\n- about a dozen thin route handlers\n- two new pages (`/calendar`, `/account/calendar`), plus one small admin page\n- small, targeted edits to timetable, attendance, the assignment and quiz editors, notifications, the cron, navigation and the seed\n\nDesign principles:\n\n1. **One read path.** A single function, `getCalendarItems(user, range, sources, studentId?)`, feeds the `/calendar` API, the iCal feed, `getUpcomingEventsForUser`, and (with `sources=['events']`) the single-event visibility check. That way the feed cannot show anything the app hides (NFR-5).\n2. **Recurrence is expanded on the server, at read time.** A recurring event is stored once. Clients and the scheduler only ever receive plain occurrences. The feed emits RRULE (ADR-2, ADR-3).\n3. **One holiday rule.** `isSchoolDay` in calendar-service owns the teaching-weekday rule and the no-school-event rule. Timetable, attendance, the editors and `/api/school-day` all call it (ADR-8).\n4. **Reuse before writing.** The design reuses `rateLimit`, `notify`, `audit`, `hashToken`, `csv.ts`, `DataTable`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView/Editor`, `useToast`, the dispatch cron, `getSchoolTimezone` and the access helpers (NFR-9).\n\n### Intake blockers and warnings\n\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **no blockers** (`blockers: []`). It raises three warnings, resolved as follows:\n\n| Intake warning | Resolution | Ref |\n|---|---|---|\n| PRD-12 missing: no `AudienceType`, `audience.ts` or audience builder | SH-14 adds `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }` and `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`, exactly as PRD-12 §FR-1/FR-2 specify. It also adds a minimal MUI `AudienceBuilder`. PRD-12 adopts all three without changes. No Announcement models. | ADR-9, §3.3 |\n| `/admin/academic-years/[id]` page missing | Add a minimal ADMIN server page at that exact route with a read-only term list and an \"Add term breaks\" button. | ADR-10, §3.9 |\n| New dependencies | `@mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15` (exact, installed first) with a scoped `@mui/x-internals` override. `node-ical@0.27.6` as an exact devDependency. Nothing else is added. | ADR-1, ADR-5 |\n\n### Conflicts between the research inputs, and how this design settles them\n\n| Topic | arch-research-stack | arch-research-reqs | **Decision** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Audience shape | PRD-12 enum (6 values) with `refId` and `include*` flags | 4-value enum with `targetId` and `roles[]` | **ADR-9.** PRD-14 FR-1 itself defines `EventAudience` with `refId` / `includeStudents` / `includeParents` / `includeTeachers` (verified in `14-calendar.md` L128-137), and PRD-12 L96 defines the 6 values. \"Grade 7 parents\" = `GRADE_LEVEL` with `includeStudents=false, includeTeachers=false`. No `roles[]` column. |\n| Resolver path | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` | `src/server/audience/audience.ts` | **`src/server/announcements/audience.ts`**, the path PRD-12 names, so PRD-12 doesn't need a rename. |\n| `getScheduleForDate` \"reason\" | Add `reason` to its return | Keep `ScheduleEntry[]`; callers fetch the reason separately | **Keep `ScheduleEntry[]`** (no churn for callers: attendance L130/L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Callers that need the holiday name call `isSchoolDay(date)` directly. FR-17's \"reason\" is delivered through `isSchoolDay` and `/api/school-day`. |\n| Email default per category (FR-28) | Not addressed | D5: a second type | **Two registry types:** `event.created` (`defaultEmail: false`) and `event.holiday_created` (`defaultEmail: true`, used for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK). Both keep the per-user preference override, and `notify.ts` is unchanged. This is a deliberate deviation (D-3 below). |\n| RSVP reminder \"once\" | `rsvpReminderSentAt` column | Same, claimed with conditional `updateMany` | Agreed: claim it with `updateMany({where:{id, rsvpReminderSentAt:null}})`. |\n\n### Deviations from the PRD's model and route list (all deliberate)\n\n| ID | Deviation | Why | Traces to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| D-1 | `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?` | Stores \"once per event\" for the reminder. Claimed atomically. | FR-23 |\n| D-2 | `EventAudience @@index([eventId])` and `@@index([type, refId])` | Audience filtering in SQL on the hot path. | NFR-4 |\n| D-3 | Extra notification type `event.holiday_created` | Per-category email default, within the existing preference model. | FR-28 |\n| D-4 | Back-relations on `User` (`calendarEvents`, `eventRsvps`, `calendarFeedToken`) and `onDelete: Cascade` FKs on `EventRsvp.userId` / `CalendarFeedToken.userId` | Prisma requires the relations. Cascade matches the \"cascade deletes\" instruction in FR-2. | FR-2 |\n| D-5 | Agenda view: 30-day page with next/prev in Community `EventCalendar`, instead of true infinite scroll | Community has no infinite agenda. If QA rejects this, the fallback is MUI `List` + native `IntersectionObserver` below 768 px, fetching the next 30-day window. Rejection triggers the fallback; it is not built up front. | FR-9, ADR-2 |\n| D-6 | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `url` only when it creates the first token, otherwise `{url:null, hasToken:true, createdAt}`. The page offers \"Reset link\". | The raw token cannot be re-shown because it is stored hashed. | FR-24, FR-25, NFR-5 |\n| D-7 | Seed a minimal ELECTIVE `ROBOTICS` course (teacher Tom, current year) only if it doesn't exist | The Chess club audience needs it, and it is absent from the seed. | FR-37 |\n| D-8 | Register save on a no-school date requires `holidayOverride: true` in the body, enforced on the server | Makes FR-18's extra confirmation a real rule, not only a UI dialog. | FR-18, NFR-7 |\n| D-9 | `GET /api/public/events` is rate limited per IP (`rateLimit('pubcal:'+ip, 120, 3_600_000)`) and range-capped at 100 days | Only unauthenticated JSON route; reuses the existing limiter. | FR-30, NFR-7 |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Dependencies and config (do first)\n\n| Change | Ref |\n|---|---|\n| `npm i --save-exact @mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15`. Nested override `\"@mui/x-scheduler\": {\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.17.0\"}`. Verify with `npm ls @mui/x-internals`. If npm doesn't honour the nested override, fall back to a global `9.17.0`. | FR-1, ADR-1 |\n| `import type {} from '@mui/x-scheduler/theme-augmentation'` beside the theme | FR-9, ADR-1 |\n| `npm i -D --save-exact node-ical@0.27.6` | NFR-6 |\n| Before writing scheduler code, the dev phase looks up the Quickstart, Views, Events, Editing, Timezone, Localization and Responsiveness pages via MUI MCP (`useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`). If MCP is unreachable, stop and report a blocker. | NFR-2 |\n\n### 2.2 Data model: migration `20261113000000_add_calendar`\n\n```prisma\nenum AudienceType  { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }   // PRD-12 values, owned here until PRD-12 lands\nenum EventCategory { HOLIDAY TERM_BREAK EXAM EVENT MEETING TRIP SPORTS DEADLINE OTHER }\nenum Recurrence    { NONE WEEKLY MONTHLY }\nenum RsvpResponse  { YES NO MAYBE }\n\nmodel CalendarEvent {\n  id                 String        @id @default(cuid())\n  title              String\n  description        String?\n  category           EventCategory\n  startAt            DateTime\n  endAt              DateTime\n  allDay             Boolean       @default(false)\n  location           String?\n  roomId             String?\n  recurrence         Recurrence    @default(NONE)\n  recurrenceUntil    DateTime?     @db.Date\n  isNoSchool         Boolean       @default(false)\n  rsvpEnabled        Boolean       @default(false)\n  rsvpDeadline       DateTime?\n  rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?                                  // D-1\n  isPublic           Boolean       @default(false)\n  createdById        String\n  createdBy          User          @relation(\"CalendarEventCreator\", fields: [createdById], references: [id])\n  createdAt          DateTime      @default(now())\n  updatedAt          DateTime      @updatedAt\n  audiences          EventAudience[]\n  rsvps              EventRsvp[]\n  @@index([startAt, endAt])\n}\n\nmodel EventAudience {\n  id              String        @id @default(cuid())\n  eventId         String\n  event           CalendarEvent @relation(fields: [eventId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  type            AudienceType\n  refId           String?       // gradeLevelId | sectionId | courseId | Role name (ROLE); null for SCHOOL/STAFF\n  includeStudents Boolean       @default(true)\n  includeParents  Boolean       @default(true)\n  includeTeachers Boolean       @default(true)\n  @@index([eventId])\n  @@index([type, refId])                                        // D-2\n}\n\nmodel EventRsvp {\n  eventId   String\n  event     CalendarEvent @relation(fields: [eventId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  userId    String\n  user      User          @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  response  RsvpResponse\n  guests    Int           @default(0)\n  note      String?\n  createdAt DateTime      @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime      @updatedAt\n  @@id([eventId, userId])\n}\n\nmodel CalendarFeedToken {\n  userId    String   @id\n  user      User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  tokenHash String   @unique\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n}\n```\n\nExact field lists for `EventRsvp` follow PRD §FR-1. The dev agent copies any field this sketch omits from `14-calendar.md` L139-148. Traces to FR-2, FR-3, FR-23, NFR-4, NFR-8.\n\n### 2.3 Server modules\n\n| File | Exports | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` (new, PRD-12 path) | `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)`, `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`, `audienceWhereForUser(user)` (Prisma `EventAudience` filter), `canTargetAudience(user, audience)` | Semantics are those of PRD-12 FR-2. `audienceWhereForUser` precomputes the user's keys once: their grade levels, sections and courses, the same for linked children (parents), the courses they teach and the sections they homeroom (teachers), and their role. It returns an `OR` over `{type, refId, include*}` so filtering happens in SQL (NFR-4). `canTargetAudience`: ADMIN → any. TEACHER → `COURSE` passes `assertCanManageCourse`, or `SECTION` where `homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Everything else → false. | FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-28, FR-29, FR-23, NFR-4, NFR-7 |\n| `src/server/calendar/recurrence.ts` (new, pure) | `expandOccurrences(event, from, to, tz)` | Steps in school-tz wall clock: +7 days, or +1 month on the same day of month, skipping months that lack the day. Duration is kept in wall-clock terms. Stops at the earlier of `recurrenceUntil` (end of that day, inclusive) and `to`. Occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. | FR-15, FR-4, NFR-3, ADR-3 |\n| `src/server/calendar/ical.ts` (new, pure) | `escapeText`, `foldLine`, `vtimezone(tz, from, to)`, `vevent(item, tz)`, `buildCalendar(items, tz, window)` | All-day events use `VALUE=DATE` with an exclusive `DTEND`. Timed one-off events use UTC `Z`. Recurring events use `TZID` + `RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z` (+`BYMONTHDAY`). Deadlines are zero-duration VEVENTs with `URL`. Lines are CRLF and folded at 75 octets. | FR-12, FR-26, NFR-3, NFR-6, ADR-5 |\n| `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (new) | `getEvent`, `createEvent`, `updateEvent`, `deleteEvent`, `upsertRsvp`, `listRsvps`, `isSchoolDay`, `noSchoolDays(from,to)`, `createTermBreaks(yearId, actor)`, `getOrCreateFeedToken`, `resetFeedToken`, `findUserByFeedToken` | Owns every per-entity check (NFR-7). **Imports nothing from timetable-service** (R2). It reads `prisma.schoolDay` directly, and timetable-service imports *from* it. | FR-5..8, FR-16, FR-20..23, FR-25, FR-33, FR-34, FR-36 |\n| `src/server/calendar/sources.ts` (new) | `getCalendarItems`, `getPublicEvents`, `getUpcomingEventsForUser` | The merge in §3.1. It may import timetable-service, the assignment and quiz services, and calendar-service, because nothing imports it back except routes (R2). | FR-10, FR-11, FR-15, FR-26, FR-30..32 |\n| `src/server/calendar/maintenance.ts` (new) | `sendRsvpReminders(now)` | Selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline ∈ (now, now+48h]` and `rsvpReminderSentAt = null`. For each, claims it via `updateMany({where:{id, rsvpReminderSentAt:null}, data:{rsvpReminderSentAt:now}})`. If `count===1`, resolves the audience minus existing RSVP userIds and calls `notify('event.rsvp_reminder')`. | FR-23, ADR-11 |\n| `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (new, client-safe) | `eventInputSchema`, `eventPatchSchema`, `rsvpSchema`, `calendarQuerySchema`, `schoolDayQuerySchema`, `publicEventsQuerySchema` | Rules: title ≤ 150; description ≤ 5000; `endAt ≥ startAt`; `recurrenceUntil` required for WEEKLY/MONTHLY and ≤ start + 1 year; guests 0–5; range `to − from ≤ 100 days`; `sources ⊆ {events, holidays, assignments, quizzes, timetable}`. All-day input is `yyyy-MM-dd` start and inclusive end. The **server** converts it to `[schoolMidnight(start), schoolMidnight(end+1))`. | FR-4, FR-21, FR-32, NFR-8 |\n| `src/lib/dates.ts` (edit) | add `schoolMidnight(dateStr, tz)`, `schoolDateOf(instant, tz)` | Pure and client-safe. The single source of all-day and date conversions. | FR-4, FR-16, NFR-3, ADR-4 |\n\n### 2.4 Edits to existing modules\n\n| File | Change | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` | At both `// PRD-14 holidays hook` lines, replace the inline `schoolDay` weekday check with `if (!(await isSchoolDay(date)).isSchoolDay) return [];`. The weekday rule now lives only in `isSchoolDay`, so the old check is deleted, not duplicated. The return type is unchanged. | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-9 |\n| `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` | `getToday` and `getOverview` add `noSchoolReason: string \\| null` from `isSchoolDay`. The register save path rejects with `VALIDATION_ERROR` \"holidayOverride required\" when the date is not a school day and `holidayOverride !== true` (D-8). | FR-18 |\n| Attendance landing + `RegisterForm.tsx` | Landing shows \"No classes today — <reason>\". The register shows a warning `Alert` banner, and the save button opens `ConfirmDialog` \"Record attendance on a holiday anyway\", which sends `holidayOverride: true`. | FR-18, NFR-1 |\n| Teacher/student/parent Today views (those consuming `getScheduleForDate`) | When `isSchoolDay` is false, show the holiday name instead of the empty class list. | FR-17 |\n| `AssignmentForm.tsx`, `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` | On a `dueAt`/`availableUntil` change, `fetch('/api/school-day?date=')`. If false, show a non-blocking `<Alert severity=\"warning\">This date is a holiday (<title>).</Alert>`. Save is unchanged. | FR-19, FR-34 |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `event.created` (COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail false), `event.holiday_created` (COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true), `event.updated` (COMMUNICATION, false) and `event.rsvp_reminder` (COMMUNICATION, false). All roles. | FR-23, FR-28, FR-29 |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | Add an isolated `try { await sendRsvpReminders(now) } catch (e) { logger.error(...) }` block, matching the quiz-maintenance block. | FR-23, NFR-9 |\n| `src/config/navigation.ts` | `{ label: 'Calendar', href: '/calendar', icon: CalendarMonth, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, as with the other `/account/*` pages. It is reached from the account area and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`. | FR-35 |\n| `prisma/seed.ts` | `seedCalendar()`, idempotent: match by title (+ startAt where it is stable). It seeds the 7 events from FR-37 and the ROBOTICS course if absent (D-7). \"Sports day\" has no announcement link. Grade 6–8 exams use three `GRADE_LEVEL` audiences. \"Grade 7 parents\" = `GRADE_LEVEL` with only `includeParents`. | FR-37 |\n\n### 2.5 Route handlers (thin: requireUser/requireRole → Zod parse → service → `ok`/`apiError`)\n\n| Route | Auth | Service call | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `GET /api/calendar?from&to&sources&studentId` | any user | `getCalendarItems` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-32, NFR-7 |\n| `POST /api/events` | ADMIN, TEACHER | `createEvent` | FR-5..7, FR-14, FR-28, FR-33 |\n| `GET /api/events/:id` | visible to user | `getEvent` (+`myRsvp`, totals, `canEdit`) | FR-12, FR-22, FR-33 |\n| `PATCH /api/events/:id` | creator, ADMIN | `updateEvent` | FR-6..8, FR-29, FR-33, FR-36 |\n| `DELETE /api/events/:id` | creator, ADMIN | `deleteEvent` | FR-8, FR-33, FR-36 |\n| `GET /api/events/:id/ics` | visible to user | `getEvent` → `buildCalendar([event])` | FR-12, FR-33 |\n| `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp` | audience member | `upsertRsvp` | FR-21 |\n| `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps[?format=csv]` | creator, ADMIN | `listRsvps` → JSON or `csv.ts` | FR-22 |\n| `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` | any user | `getOrCreateFeedToken` | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `POST /api/me/calendar-feed/reset` | any user | `resetFeedToken` | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `GET /api/calendar/feed/[token]` (`.ics` stripped from param) | token | `findUserByFeedToken` → `rateLimit` → `getCalendarItems` → `buildCalendar` | FR-26, FR-27, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n| `GET /api/school-day?date=` (new singular folder; `/api/school-days` untouched) | any user | `isSchoolDay` | FR-16, FR-19, FR-34 |\n| `GET /api/public/events?from&to` | public, IP rate limit | `getPublicEvents` | FR-30, D-9 |\n| `POST /api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks` | ADMIN | `createTermBreaks` | FR-20 |\n\nError mapping: not visible → 404 `NOT_FOUND`. Visible but not permitted → 403 `FORBIDDEN`. RSVP after the deadline, or with RSVP disabled → 409 `CONFLICT`. Feed token unknown → plain 404. Feed over the limit → 429 `RATE_LIMITED` + `Retry-After`. `arch-api-contracts` defines the exact shapes.\n\n### 2.6 UI\n\n| Path / component | Contents | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/(app)/calendar/page.tsx` (server) → `CalendarView.tsx` (client) | `requirePageUser`. `<EventCalendar>` from `@mui/x-scheduler/event-calendar`: `views={['month','week','agenda']}`, week `startTime:7, endTime:19`, agenda `dayCount:30`, `displayTimezone={tz}`, `readOnly`, `eventCreation={false}`. The default view is month at `useMediaQuery('(min-width:768px)')`, agenda below that. Controlled `events`, refetched on `onVisibleDateChange`/`onViewChange` with plain `fetch` and a small Map cache keyed by `from|to|sources|studentId`. The page opens the drawer when `?event=<id>` is present (notification links). | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-12 |\n| `SourceChips` | MUI `Chip`s: School events · My assignments · My quizzes · My timetable (Week view only) · Holidays. Stored in `localStorage['calendar.sources']`. Holidays = HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool`; School events = everything else, with no overlap. `timetable` is fetched only in Week view. | FR-10 |\n| Child filter (PARENT only) | `Select`: \"All children\" or one child → `studentId`. Deadline titles get the child's name prefixed by the server. | FR-11 |\n| `EventDrawer` | Right-anchored `Drawer`: title, category `Chip`, time in school tz, location, `MarkdownView` description, audience chips, RSVP controls (`ToggleButtonGroup` + guests `TextField` for parents + note; disabled after the deadline), \"Add to my calendar\" (`<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`), and edit/delete when `canEdit` (delete via `ConfirmDialog`). Creator/admin see an RSVP `DataTable` + CSV link. | FR-12, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1 |\n| Deadline click | `onEventEditingStart` → `cancel()` → `router.push(item.href)` | FR-13 |\n| `EventEditorDialog` | \"New event\" button (ADMIN/TEACHER). React Hook Form + `eventInputSchema`. Fields: title, category (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK only for admins), all-day switch, date/time pickers (`@mui/x-date-pickers`), location, `MarkdownEditor`, `AudienceBuilder`, recurrence select + until date, RSVP switch + deadline, and admin-only `isNoSchool`/`isPublic`. Results go through `useToast`. | FR-4..7, FR-14 |\n| `src/components/AudienceBuilder/` (new shared) | Rows of type `Select` + entity `Autocomplete` (grade level / section / course / role) + three include `Checkbox`es. Types are filtered by `canTargetAudience` rules on the client. The server stays authoritative. | FR-3, FR-7, FR-14 |\n| `src/app/(app)/account/calendar/page.tsx` | \"Subscribe\" card: URL `TextField` (read-only) + copy (`navigator.clipboard`), Google/Apple/Outlook instructions as static text, and \"Reset link\" behind `ConfirmDialog`. When `url` is null: \"Reset link to get a new URL\" (D-6). | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `src/app/(app)/admin/academic-years/[id]/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. Year name, read-only term list (existing terms service), and an \"Add term breaks\" button + `ConfirmDialog` that shows the number of breaks created via toast. | FR-20 |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Calendar read (`GET /api/calendar`, the feed, upcoming events)\n\n```\nroute → calendarQuerySchema (≤100 days) → getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})\n  1. scope   = studentId ? resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId) : getAccessibleStudentIds(user)   (404 for others)\n  2. where   = audienceWhereForUser(user, scope)          // keys computed once\n  3. Promise.all([\n       events:      CalendarEvent where startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR (recurrence≠NONE AND recurrenceUntil ≥ from))\n                    AND (audiences some where) OR createdById=user  (ADMIN: no audience filter)\n                    → expandOccurrences(e, from, to, tz) → split into holidays / events by category+isNoSchool,\n       assignments: existing assignment service, PUBLISHED, dueAt ∈ [from,to), scoped students/courses,\n       quizzes:     existing quiz service, PUBLISHED, availableUntil ∈ [from,to),\n       timetable:   getPersonalTimetable(target) projected onto dates in range, skipping noSchoolDays(from,to)\n     ]) – only for requested sources\n  4. map → CalendarItem union {kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', id, title, start, end, allDay, color, href?, childName?}\n```\nThe feed calls the same function with `from=now−30d, to=now+365d`, sources minus timetable, and recurring events **unexpanded**. Instead of occurrences it gets the series rows so it can emit RRULE. The 100-day cap is skipped because the call is internal. Traces to FR-10, FR-11, FR-15, FR-26, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n\n### 3.2 Event write\n\n```\nPOST/PATCH → eventInputSchema → createEvent/updateEvent(user, input)\n  - FR-6: non-admin + (isNoSchool | isPublic | HOLIDAY | TERM_BREAK) → 403\n  - FR-7: every audience must pass canTargetAudience(user, a) → else 403\n  - FR-8: PATCH/DELETE requires createdById===user.id or ADMIN\n  - FR-5: isNoSchool ??= category ∈ {HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK}\n  - all-day → schoolMidnight conversion (FR-4)\n  - prisma.$transaction: event + replace audiences\n  - after commit:\n      FR-36 audit() if ADMIN && createdById≠user.id (update/delete)\n      FR-28 create: first occurrence within 30 days → notify(HOLIDAY|TERM_BREAK ? 'event.holiday_created' : 'event.created',\n            resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences) − creator, link '/calendar?event=<id>')\n      FR-29 update: startAt|endAt|allDay|location changed AND event upcoming → notify('event.updated') once\n```\n\n### 3.3 Audience resolution (PRD-12 FR-2 semantics)\n\n| Type | refId | Students (`includeStudents`) | Parents (`includeParents`) | Teachers (`includeTeachers`) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SCHOOL | null | all active users | | |\n| STAFF | null | ADMIN + TEACHER | | |\n| ROLE | role name | users with that role | | |\n| GRADE_LEVEL | gradeLevelId | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId = refId` | their `ParentStudentLink` parents | teachers of current-year courses in sections of that grade |\n| SECTION | sectionId | current-year `SectionMember`s | their parents | homeroom teacher + teachers of courses in the section |\n| COURSE | courseId | ACTIVE `Enrollment`s | their parents | `teacherId` + `coTeacherIds` |\n\nOnly ACTIVE, non-archived users count. `isUserInAudience` and `audienceWhereForUser` give the same answer as `resolveAudienceUserIds`. A property-style integration test loops over every seed user to check this (PRD-12 test requirement). Traces to FR-3, FR-7, NFR-7.\n\n### 3.4 School-day check\n\n```\nisSchoolDay(date) → d = schoolDateOf(date, tz), isoDay\n  1. SchoolDay[isoDay].isTeaching ?? isoDay ≤ 5   → false, reason 'Not a teaching day'\n  2. isNoSchool events with a SCHOOL audience where startAt < midnight(d+1) AND (endAt > midnight(d) OR recurring)\n     → expandOccurrences within that day → first hit → false, reason 'Holiday: <title>'\n  3. → { isSchoolDay: true, reason: null }\nnoSchoolDays(from, to) = one query, same rules, returns Map<date, reason> (used by the timetable source; avoids N calls)\n```\nCallers: timetable-service (FR-17), attendance (FR-18), `/api/school-day` (FR-19, FR-34), timetable source in §3.1. Traces to FR-16..19, FR-34.\n\n### 3.5 RSVP\n\n`PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp` → `rsvpSchema` → `upsertRsvp`:\n1. Check the event is visible and `rsvpEnabled`. Otherwise 404 (not visible) or 409.\n2. Require `isUserInAudience`. Otherwise 403.\n3. Require `now < rsvpDeadline`. Otherwise 409.\n4. If the user is not a PARENT, force `guests = 0`.\n5. Upsert on `(eventId, userId)`.\n\nA recurring event has one RSVP for the whole series. The drawer gets `myRsvp` and totals `{yes, no, maybe, guests}` from `GET /api/events/:id`. Creator and admin read the full list via `/rsvps`, or `?format=csv` via `csv.ts`. Traces to FR-21, FR-22.\n\n### 3.6 Reminder job\n\nCron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` → `sendRsvpReminders(now)` → claim → audience − responders → `notify('event.rsvp_reminder', link '/calendar?event=<id>')`. Traces to FR-23.\n\n### 3.7 iCal feed\n\n```\nGET /api/calendar/feed/<token>.ics\n  token = param.replace(/\\.ics$/, '') → hashToken(token) → CalendarFeedToken by tokenHash (unique) → user ACTIVE?\n    no → 404 text/plain\n  rateLimit('calfeed:'+hash, 60, 3_600_000) → !ok → 429 + Retry-After\n  items = getCalendarItems(user, feed window, series mode)\n  body  = buildCalendar(items, tz, window)   // VTIMEZONE for transitions in window, RRULE for series\n  200 text/calendar; charset=utf-8, Cache-Control: private, max-age=900\n```\nToken lifecycle:\n- `getOrCreateFeedToken` creates the row on first use from `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stores `hashToken(raw)`, and returns the URL once.\n- `resetFeedToken` upserts a new hash, so the old URL returns 404 immediately.\n- No raw token is ever logged.\n\nTraces to FR-24..27, NFR-5, NFR-6, ADR-6, ADR-7.\n\n### 3.8 Public and dashboard hooks\n\n- `getPublicEvents(from, to)`: `isPublic` events, expanded, returning only public-safe fields (id, title, category, start, end, allDay, location, description). Traces to FR-30.\n- `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)`: `getCalendarItems(user, now..now+90d, ['events','holidays'])`, sorted, then the first `limit` items. No UI. Traces to FR-31, NFR-11.\n\n### 3.9 Term breaks\n\n`POST /api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks` (ADMIN) → `createTermBreaks`:\n1. Order the terms by `startDate`.\n2. For each consecutive pair where `next.start > prev.end + 1 day`, create an all-day TERM_BREAK with `isNoSchool=true` and a SCHOOL audience, from `prev.end+1` (inclusive) to `next.start` (exclusive).\n3. Skip any gap that already has a TERM_BREAK with the same span. This makes the call idempotent.\n4. Return `{ created }`.\n5. Write an `audit()` entry.\n\nTraces to FR-20.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cross-cutting\n\n- **Time (NFR-3, NFR-8).**\n  - Storage is in UTC. Display uses `SchoolSettings.timezone`, read via the existing `getSchoolTimezone()`. No third copy is created.\n  - All-day events run from school-tz midnight with an exclusive end.\n  - Expansion steps in wall-clock time.\n  - The feed uses `VALUE=DATE` for all-day events and `TZID` + VTIMEZONE for series.\n  - The scheduler gets `displayTimezone`.\n  - One DST-week test fixture (America/New_York 2026-11-01, or the seed tz) runs through the expansion, the all-day path and the feed.\n- **Security (NFR-5, NFR-7).**\n  - Every route calls `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (hashed token) and public events (public fields only, IP limit).\n  - Per-entity checks live in calendar-service.\n  - Students see only themselves, and parents only their linked children (`getAccessibleStudentIds` / `resolveViewedStudent`).\n  - A non-visible event returns 404, so its existence doesn't leak.\n- **Performance (NFR-4).**\n  - A parent with 3 children in month view needs about 6 indexed queries, run in parallel.\n  - The audience is filtered in SQL, and holidays are found with one `noSchoolDays` query.\n  - There is no cache layer. Add one only if the Playwright timing or a measurement exceeds 500 ms.\n- **UI rules (NFR-1, NFR-12).**\n  - Only MUI, icons and MUI X (including the scheduler) are used. Toasts go through `useToast`, side panels through `Drawer`, and confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`.\n  - English only. The breakpoint is 768 px.\n- **Scope (NFR-11).**\n  - Out of scope: per-occurrence exceptions, room booking (`roomId` is stored and unused), two-way sync, and dashboard or public-site UI.\n- **Tests (NFR-10).**\n  - Unit tests:\n    - `expandOccurrences`: weekly, monthly on the 31st, the until bound, a DST week\n    - `isSchoolDay`: weekday, holiday, recurring no-school\n    - `ical`: escaping `, ; \\ \\n`, folding, RRULE, VALUE=DATE exclusive end, node-ical parse\n    - all-day conversion\n    - term-break gap math\n    - `canTargetAudience`\n  - Integration tests:\n    - calendar merge per role (admin, teacher, student, parent with 3 children)\n    - feed token reset (old URL 404, new URL 200 and node-ical-valid)\n    - RSVP deadline (409) and parent-only guests\n    - audience resolver parity across seed users\n    - teacher SCHOOL create → 403\n  - Playwright:\n    - an admin creates a holiday, and the student's Today view shows the holiday name\n    - a parent RSVPs\n    - the feed URL returns a valid ICS\n  - `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` stays green.\n\n### Risks carried forward\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|\n| R1 Beta scheduler API drift | Exact pin, MCP lookup before use, and the scheduler used only as a read-only display (ADR-2). The D-5 fallback is pre-agreed. |\n| R2 Import cycle between timetable and calendar | The edges run one way: timetable-service → calendar-service, and sources.ts → (timetable, assignments, quizzes, calendar-service). calendar-service reads teaching weekdays via `prisma.schoolDay` and never imports timetable-service. |\n| R3 DST correctness across 4 code paths | Shared pure helpers in `src/lib/dates.ts` plus one shared DST fixture. |\n| R4 Audience is both the hot path and the security boundary | A single implementation plus the parity test. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 exact pin `@mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15` + scoped override (ADR-1) |\n| FR-2 | §2.2 migration `20261113000000_add_calendar`: enums, 4 models, cascades, `[startAt,endAt]` index |\n| FR-3 | §2.2 `AudienceType` (PRD-12 values); §2.3 `announcements/audience.ts`; §3.3 resolution table |\n| FR-4 | §2.3 `validators/calendar.ts` + `schoolMidnight`; §3.2 all-day conversion |\n| FR-5 | §3.2 `isNoSchool ??= HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK` in `createEvent` |\n| FR-6 | §3.2 admin-only field check; §2.6 editor hides admin fields |\n| FR-7 | §2.3 `canTargetAudience`; §3.2 check on create/patch |\n| FR-8 | §3.2 creator/ADMIN guard on PATCH/DELETE |\n| FR-9 | §2.6 `CalendarView` with `EventCalendar` views/viewConfig/breakpoint; D-5 agenda fallback |\n| FR-10 | §2.6 `SourceChips` + localStorage; §3.1 `sources` param, holidays/events split |\n| FR-11 | §2.6 parent child filter; §3.1 `studentId` scope + `childName` |\n| FR-12 | §2.6 `EventDrawer`; §2.5 `GET /api/events/:id`, `/ics` |\n| FR-13 | §2.6 deadline click → `router.push(href)` |\n| FR-14 | §2.6 `EventEditorDialog` + `AudienceBuilder` |\n| FR-15 | §2.3 `recurrence.ts` `expandOccurrences`; §3.1 read-time expansion |\n| FR-16 | §2.3 `isSchoolDay`; §3.4 |\n| FR-17 | §2.4 timetable-service hook + Today views |\n| FR-18 | §2.4 attendance `noSchoolReason`, `holidayOverride` (D-8), `RegisterForm` banner/confirm |\n| FR-19 | §2.4 `AssignmentForm` / `QuizSettingsPanel` warning via `/api/school-day` |\n| FR-20 | §2.6 `/admin/academic-years/[id]` page; §2.5 term-breaks route; §3.9 `createTermBreaks` |\n| FR-21 | §2.5 `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp`; §3.5 `upsertRsvp` rules |\n| FR-22 | §2.5 `/rsvps[?format=csv]`; §2.6 drawer totals + `DataTable` |\n| FR-23 | §2.3 `maintenance.ts`; §2.4 cron hook + type; D-1 `rsvpReminderSentAt` |\n| FR-24 | §2.6 `/account/calendar`; §2.5 me/calendar-feed routes |\n| FR-25 | §3.7 token lifecycle with `hashToken`; D-6 |\n| FR-26 | §2.3 `ical.ts`; §3.7 feed build (window, RRULE, VTIMEZONE, escaping) |\n| FR-27 | §2.5 feed route; §3.7 rate limit + Cache-Control |\n| FR-28 | §2.4 types `event.created` + `event.holiday_created` (D-3); §3.2 notify on create |\n| FR-29 | §2.4 type `event.updated`; §3.2 notify on time/location change |\n| FR-30 | §3.8 `getPublicEvents`; §2.5 `/api/public/events` (D-9) |\n| FR-31 | §3.8 `getUpcomingEventsForUser` |\n| FR-32 | §2.5 `GET /api/calendar`; §3.1 `getCalendarItems`; 100-day cap in validator |\n| FR-33 | §2.5 event CRUD + `/ics` routes |\n| FR-34 | §2.5 `GET /api/school-day` (singular, new folder) |\n| FR-35 | §2.4 `navigation.ts` Calendar entry |\n| FR-36 | §3.2 `audit()` on admin edits/deletes of other users' events |\n| FR-37 | §2.4 `seedCalendar()` + ROBOTICS course (D-7) |\n| NFR-1 | §2.6 MUI-only components; §4 UI rules |\n| NFR-2 | §2.1 MCP lookup gate before scheduler use |\n| NFR-3 | §2.3 wall-clock expansion, `dates.ts` helpers, ical VALUE=DATE/TZID; §4 DST fixture |\n| NFR-4 | §3.1 parallel indexed queries, SQL audience filter, D-2 index; §4 performance |\n| NFR-5 | §3.7 32-byte token, SHA-256 hash; §3.1 shared read path |\n| NFR-6 | §2.1 `node-ical` devDep; §4 parse tests |\n| NFR-7 | §2.5 auth column; §3.3; §4 security |\n| NFR-8 | §2.3 module layout under `src/server/calendar/`; thin routes; Zod; UTC storage |\n| NFR-9 | §1 reuse list; §2.4 edits instead of new helpers |\n| NFR-10 | §4 tests |\n| NFR-11 | §4 scope; §3.8 hooks only |\n| NFR-12 | §2.6 768 px breakpoint, English only |\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-14\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:10:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-14: School Calendar, Events & Holidays\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-014 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-14.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"DEPENDENCY GAP: PRD-12 (Announcements) is NOT present in the workspace. prisma/schema.prisma has no AudienceType enum and no Announcement model; no audience.ts helper or audience builder component exists anywhere under src/. PRD-14 FR-1 (EventAudience.type reuses AudienceType), FR-2.2 (reuse audience.ts), FR-3.5 (audience builder from PRD-12) and the 'Sports day' seed (ties to a PRD-12 announcement) all assume it. The Architect must decide whether SH-14 introduces a minimal AudienceType + audience resolver (in a form PRD-12 can adopt later) or blocks.\",\n    \"/admin/academic-years/[id] page does not exist (only the REST API under src/app/api/academic-years/[id] incl. terms and terms/generate). FR-5.5 'Add term breaks' needs a UI host; the page or an equivalent admin surface has to be created or the shortcut placed elsewhere.\",\n    \"@mui/x-scheduler is not in package.json (confirmed; @mui/material, x-charts, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers are pinned at 9.5.0). Neither 'ics' nor 'node-ical' is installed.\",\n    \"PRD-06 timetable service exists: src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts exports getScheduleForDate (line ~542), getSchoolScheduleForDate and listSchoolDays/updateSchoolDays (teaching weekdays). src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts calls getScheduleForDate for the register landing.\",\n    \"Existing GET/PUT /api/school-days (plural, PRD-06 teaching weekdays) is distinct from the new GET /api/school-day?date= (singular) in this PRD; both must coexist and neither may be renamed.\",\n    \"Rate limiter exists at src/server/rate-limit.ts (rateLimit) — reuse for the feed's 60 req/token/hour.\",\n    \"Maintenance runs on the internal dispatch cron (src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; PRD-10 precedent src/server/quiz/maintenance.ts) — the event.rsvp_reminder pass should hook in there.\",\n    \"Notification types are registered in src/server/notifications/types.ts (NOTIFICATION_TYPES, categories incl. COMMUNICATION/ACADEMIC).\",\n    \"No src/server/calendar/ directory exists yet; FR-5.1 names src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts, consistent with the feature-subdirectory convention.\",\n    \"Latest migration is 20261112000000_add_direct_messaging; seed is prisma/seed.ts (npm run db:seed).\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Install @mui/x-scheduler pinned to the exact version found via the MUI MCP server before any other work in this PRD.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-0 Dependency (1)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add Prisma enums EventCategory, Recurrence, RsvpResponse and models CalendarEvent, EventAudience, EventRsvp (composite PK eventId+userId) and CalendarFeedToken exactly as specified, with cascade deletes and the [startAt, endAt] index, in one new migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"EventAudience.type reuses the AudienceType enum from PRD-12; because that enum does not exist in the workspace, its values (at least SCHOOL, COURSE, SECTION, grade-level style targets implied by seed data) must be defined by this ticket or supplied by PRD-12.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (EventAudience.type comment 'reuse enum from PRD-12'); §Seed Data (Grade 6–8, Grade 7 parents, course audience); brownfield finding\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Validate events with Zod in src/lib/validators/calendar.ts: title ≤ 150 chars, description Markdown ≤ 5,000 chars, endAt ≥ startAt, all-day events stored as school-timezone midnight with exclusive endAt, recurrenceUntil required for WEEKLY/MONTHLY and ≤ 1 year after start, RSVP guests 0–5.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 field comments; §FR-4 Recurrence; §Platform Context › Validation\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"isNoSchool defaults to true for HOLIDAY and TERM_BREAK categories and false otherwise.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (isNoSchool comment)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"ADMIN may create events with any audience; isNoSchool, isPublic and the HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK categories are admin-only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2 Permissions (1)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"TEACHER may create events only for COURSE audiences they manage or their homeroom SECTION, using the same rule as PRD-12's audience.ts (a SCHOOL-audience create by a teacher returns 403).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2 Permissions (2); Acceptance Criterion 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Creators may edit/delete their own events; admins may edit/delete all events.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2 Permissions (3)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Add /calendar page using MUI X Scheduler EventCalendar with month (default ≥ 768 px), week (07:00–19:00 time grid, all-day row; viewConfig startTime 7, endTime 19) and agenda (default < 768 px; grouped by day, 30 days ahead, infinite scroll) views plus Today/previous/next/date-picker navigation; fall back to @mui/material + @mui/x-date-pickers (DateCalendar + List) only for behaviour missing from the Community version.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 Calendar page (1)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Calendar sources are toggleable MUI Chips persisted in localStorage: School events (coloured by category), My assignments (due dates, subject colour), My quizzes (availability window end), My timetable (Week view only, light background blocks), Holidays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 (2)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Parents get a child filter (All children or one); deadline items for the selected children are labelled with the child's name.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 (3); Acceptance Criterion 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Clicking an event opens a right-anchored MUI Drawer showing title, category badge, time in school timezone, location, description (Markdown), audience chips, RSVP controls when enabled, 'Add to my calendar' (.ics download of that event) and edit/delete for permitted users.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 (4)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Clicking an assignment or quiz deadline navigates to that assignment or quiz.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 (4); Acceptance Criterion 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"ADMIN/TEACHER see a 'New event' button opening an editor Dialog with all model fields, the PRD-12 audience builder, recurrence options, RSVP toggle and RSVP deadline.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3 (5) (audience builder does not exist in workspace — see FR-3)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Recurring events (NONE/WEEKLY/MONTHLY-by-date) are stored once and expanded at read time by expandOccurrences(event, from, to) up to recurrenceUntil; the calendar API returns plain expanded occurrences; edits apply to the whole series.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4 Recurrence; §FR-3 (1); §Out of Scope; Acceptance Criterion 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"isSchoolDay(date) in src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts returns false when the weekday is not a PRD-06 teaching day or any isNoSchool event with SCHOOL audience covers the date, and exposes the reason (e.g. holiday title).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5 Holidays integration (1); Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Update PRD-06 getScheduleForDate to return an empty list with reason 'Holiday: <title>' on non-school days; Today views show the holiday name instead of classes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5 (2); Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Update PRD-07 teacher register landing to show 'No classes today — <holiday>' on non-school days; opening a register for such a date shows a warning banner and saving requires an extra 'Record attendance on a holiday anyway' confirmation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5 (3); Acceptance Criterion 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"PRD-09 assignment editor and PRD-10 quiz settings show a non-blocking warning 'This date is a holiday (<title>).' when the due/close date is a non-school day, still allowing save.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5 (4); Acceptance Criterion 8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Admin 'Add term breaks' shortcut on /admin/academic-years/[id] creates TERM_BREAK no-school events for the gaps between consecutive terms.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5 (5) (host page does not exist in workspace — only the API)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"When RSVP is enabled, audience members answer Yes/No/Maybe with guest count (parents) and optional note via PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp until rsvpDeadline; after the deadline the API rejects and the drawer controls are disabled.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6 RSVP (1); §API; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"The event drawer shows the user's own response and totals; the creator and admins see the full RSVP list with CSV export (GET /api/events/:id/rsvps?format=csv).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6 (1); §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Register notification type event.rsvp_reminder; the maintenance run notifies non-responding audience members 48 hours before the RSVP deadline, once per event.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6 (2)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Add /account/calendar page with a 'Subscribe' section: private URL APP_URL/api/calendar/feed/<token>.ics, copy button, Google/Apple/Outlook instructions and 'Reset link' which invalidates the old token (old URL returns 404).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7 iCal feed (1); Acceptance Criterion 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Feed tokens: GET /api/me/calendar-feed and POST /api/me/calendar-feed/reset return the URL; the raw token is shown only at creation/reset and stored hashed in CalendarFeedToken.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API (me/calendar-feed rows); §NFR 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The RFC 5545 text/calendar feed contains the user's school events (parents: all children's audiences) from 30 days past to 365 days ahead, assignment due dates and quiz close times with URL back to SchoolHub, RRULE for recurring events, a VTIMEZONE for the school timezone, and RFC escaping of commas, semicolons and newlines.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7 (2); Acceptance Criteria 4, 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"GET /api/calendar/feed/:token.ics is public (token-authenticated), rate limited to 60 requests per token per hour (429) and sends Cache-Control: private, max-age=900.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7 (3); §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Register event.created, notifying audience members when an event starting within the next 30 days is created (email default false; HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK email default true).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8 Notifications (1)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Register event.updated, notifying audience members once per edit when time or location of an upcoming event changes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8 (2)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Expose getPublicEvents(from, to) and GET /api/public/events?from=&to= returning isPublic events for PRD-18.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9 (1); §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Expose getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit) for PRD-16 dashboards.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9 (2)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"GET /api/calendar?from=&to=&sources=&studentId= returns merged, expanded, audience-filtered items for any role; the requested range is limited to ≤ 100 days.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API (first row)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Event CRUD API: POST /api/events (ADMIN, TEACHER with audience check); GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/events/:id (audience/creator/ADMIN); GET /api/events/:id/ics (audience, single-event download).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"GET /api/school-day?date= (any user) returns { isSchoolDay, reason }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API (last row)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Add /calendar (all roles) and /account/calendar entries to src/config/navigation.ts as needed.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › Code layout ('A PRD that adds a page adds its nav entry there'); §FR-3; §FR-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Admin edits/deletes of events created by someone else write an AuditLog row via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › Code layout (AuditLog rule); §FR-2 (3)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Seed 2026–2027 events: Thanksgiving break (26–27 Nov), Winter break (21 Dec – 1 Jan, TERM_BREAK), Semester 1 exams (11–15 Jan, EXAM, Grade 6–8), Parent–teacher evening (RSVP, seed date + 2 weeks, Grade 7 parents), Science fair (public), weekly Chess club (Tuesdays, Robotics Club course audience), Sports day (public, tied to the PRD-12 announcement).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"UI is built only from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material and the allowed MUI X packages (incl. @mui/x-scheduler); banned libraries (FullCalendar, Tailwind, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.) are not imported; toasts via shared useToast(), side panels via Drawer, confirmations via Dialog; QA verifies no banned imports and every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule (1, 3, 5, 6)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Every MUI component (especially beta @mui/x-scheduler: Quickstart, Views, Events, Timezones, Localization pages) is looked up via the MUI MCP server (useMuiDocs + fetchDocs) before use; if MCP is unreachable, stop and report a blocker.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule (2); §FR-3 (1)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"All-day events and DST transitions in the school timezone render on the correct dates in both UI and iCal feed, with tests covering a DST-change week.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"A month view for a parent with 3 children loads in under 500 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Feed tokens are 32 random bytes stored hashed; the feed exposes no data beyond what the user can see in the app.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"The generated feed passes an RFC 5545 validator test (parsed with node-ical in tests).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every handler and server page enforces access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and per-entity checks; parents see only linked children's data, students only their own.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › Code layout; §Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Follow platform conventions: thin Zod-parsing route handlers, services under src/server/calendar/, { data } / list / error response shapes and error codes, pagination/sort/search params, cuid IDs, createdAt/updatedAt, UTC storage displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone, logger instead of console.log.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Reuse existing models, services, components and helpers (timetable-service, rate-limit, notify, audit, DataTable, useToast, maintenance cron); never re-scaffold, duplicate helpers or rename existing routes/models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context (intro paragraph)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing and add: unit tests (occurrence expansion, isSchoolDay, iCal escaping and RRULE, all-day exclusive end), integration tests (calendar merge per role, feed token reset, RSVP deadline enforcement), Playwright (admin holiday → student Today view; parent RSVP; feed URL returns valid ICS).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Scope is fixed to this PRD: no room booking, no single-occurrence exceptions or complex recurrence, no two-way external sync, no behaviour owned by later PRDs (PRD-16 dashboards and PRD-18 public site only get service/API hooks).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; §Assumptions and constraints; §FR-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Supports the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari; English-only UI; responsive with a 768 px breakpoint for default view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §FR-3 (1)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n  \"confidenceMethod\": \"HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40, averaged over 49 requirements (43 HIGH, 5 MEDIUM, 1 LOW).\",\n\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"PRD-12 (Announcements: AudienceType enum, audience.ts, audience builder) is not in the workspace. Should SH-14 introduce a minimal AudienceType (SCHOOL, GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION, COURSE?) + resolver designed for PRD-12 to adopt, or is PRD-12 expected to land first?\",\n        \"/admin/academic-years/[id] has no page today. Should FR-20 create that page, or host 'Add term breaks' on an existing admin screen?\",\n        \"The 'Holidays' source and the 'School events' source both include HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK events — should toggling 'School events' off still show holidays (i.e. Holidays wins / dedupe)?\",\n        \"RSVP guest count is annotated '(parents)' — are guests allowed only for PARENT responders (others forced to 0)?\",\n        \"Which feed contents apply to TEACHER and ADMIN (e.g. admins: all events or only those whose audience includes them)? Do teachers get deadlines for assignments/quizzes they set?\",\n        \"Is a 'Sports day' PRD-12 announcement expected to exist for the seed to link to, given PRD-12 is absent?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"AudienceType / audience.ts / audience builder ownership (PRD-12 missing) — proceeding on assumption the Architect defines a minimal, PRD-12-compatible version in this ticket (FR-3 LOW, FR-7/FR-14 MEDIUM).\",\n        \"Host page for 'Add term breaks' (FR-20 MEDIUM).\",\n        \"Holidays vs School events source overlap — default assumption: Holidays chip controls HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/isNoSchool events, School events chip controls the rest, no duplicates.\",\n        \"Guest count for non-parents — default assumption: parents only, others 0.\",\n        \"Teacher/admin feed scope — default assumption: same visibility as GET /api/calendar for that user (NFR-5).\",\n        \"Sports day seed linkage — default assumption: seed the event without an announcement link if no announcement exists.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-14\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T19:12:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 49,\n  \"functionalCount\": 37,\n  \"nonFunctionalCount\": 12,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [\n    \"PRD-12 dependency missing in workspace: no AudienceType enum, audience.ts or audience builder. Architect must decide whether SH-14 adds a minimal PRD-12-compatible version (FR-3, FR-7, FR-14, FR-37 Sports day).\",\n    \"/admin/academic-years/[id] page does not exist (API only) — FR-20 needs a host page.\",\n    \"@mui/x-scheduler (beta) must be installed and version-pinned via MUI MCP first (FR-1); node-ical needed as devDependency for NFR-6.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\n","numLines":579,"startLine":1,"totalLines":579}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CDcGt1oz4YiDMz7j8R2rSp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
