{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgss3Zj9xvvRjBV1Q5dUt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `arch-api-contracts` sub-task for SH-14 is done, which completes the architect phase. Both files are rewritten for SH-14 (they held stale SH-13 content) and `api-contracts.json` parses as valid JSON. A script confirmed that every requirement id it cites exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n**`artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json`** (status `complete`) has 18 endpoints:\n- **14 new routes:**\n  - `/api/calendar`\n  - event create, read, update and delete under `/api/events`\n  - single-event `.ics` download\n  - RSVP answer, plus the RSVP list with CSV export\n  - get and reset for the calendar feed link\n  - the `.ics` feed itself\n  - `/api/school-day`\n  - `/api/public/events`\n  - `/api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks`\n- **4 existing routes, extended:**\n  - `GET /api/attendance/today`: adds the reason there's no school that day\n  - `GET /api/attendance/register`: adds the same reason\n  - `PUT /api/attendance/register`: adds a `holidayOverride` flag needed to save on a no-school day\n  - the email dispatch cron: adds the RSVP reminder pass\n- It also lists 4 server functions that have no route of their own: `getUpcomingEventsForUser`, `getPublicEvents`, `isSchoolDay`, and the four new notification types.\n- Response shapes and error codes follow `src/server/http.ts`. A hidden event or student returns 404. A permission problem returns 403 with `details.reason`. A closed or disabled RSVP returns 409. A rate-limit hit returns 429 with `Retry-After`. An unknown feed token returns a plain-text 404.\n\n**`artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json`** (status `complete`, `endpointCount` 18, no blockers) was written last.\n\nThings I decided that the system design didn't cover:\n- **All-day dates:** clients send `startDate`/`endDate` as calendar dates, with the end day included. Responses give UTC times with the end excluded.\n- **Event limits:** an event can have 1–20 audiences, and the RSVP deadline can't be later than the first occurrence's start.\n- **Register date check:** `GET /api/attendance/register` also returns the no-school reason, because the register form needs it for its warning banner. The design only mentioned the attendance landing page.\n- **Term breaks:** creating them sends no notifications, and the response reports how many were created and skipped.\n\n`artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json` is still the old SH-13 file. None of the four architect sub-tasks owns it, so I left it alone and noted in the handoff that it's out of date."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1245,"cache_read_input_tokens":70974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1245,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f1e9cdf-3174-43b4-adaa-4e6aa4038a8c","uuid":"0d0e1b84-a2c3-4fde-8d05-75dff9dea94e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:56:00.752Z","request_id":"req_011Cgss3ZX1VpKN7DmJxSLu7"}
