{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtXXu8vuXrBZKdUX21me","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UQqNPGystjXX7VtmpfZtED","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T13:35:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 29,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"There are 29 endpoints. 24 are new routes from system-design §2.3. 5 are existing routes that get extended: POST /api/files (absence-note context), GET /api/me/timetable (sh_child default), GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (EXCUSED pre-fill and rule, absent-notification suppression) and POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (consentReminders). There are also 3 non-HTTP contracts: the notification types, getSelectedChild, and the pure helpers.\",\n    \"The base path is /api, not /api/v1. Envelopes, paginated() meta and error codes come from src/server/http.ts. http.ts has no 422, so system-design's '422' business-rule failures map to 400 VALIDATION_ERROR with details.reason (OUTSIDE_BOOKING_WINDOW, PAST_DUE, SIGNATURE_MISMATCH, DATE_WINDOW).\",\n    \"Error policy: an unviewable student or resource returns 404. A visible resource the caller may not act on returns 403 with details.reason. Races return 409 with details.reason (SLOT_TAKEN, OVERLAP, ONE_PER_TEACHER, ALREADY_REVIEWED, SLOT_BOOKED). The remind throttle returns 429 with retryAfterMs.\",\n    \"Decisions made beyond system-design: GET /api/conferences/:id/slots?view=day serves the teacher day view (FR-34). Slot booking details are hidden from anyone except the booker, the teacher and ADMIN. GET /api/students/:id/overview accepts ?cards= to limit which cards load. PATCH /api/conferences/:id returns 409 if booked slots exist and slotMinutes or date changes. The tracking CSV ignores pagination.\",\n    \"Partial requirements carried from system-design: FR-13 (announcements returns []), FR-35 and the calendar part of FR-5 (no PRD-14 calendar page). Neither is a blocker.\",\n    \"Three schema columns go beyond the PRD (ADR-3): ConferenceSlot.blocked, ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt and ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt. The migration also adds a raw-SQL partial unique index on ConferenceSlot(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId).\",\n    \"src/lib/validators/{absence-notes,conferences,consent-forms}.ts should mirror the input shapes in api-contracts.json `components`.\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json is still the stale SH-14 file. No architect sub-task owns it, so treat it as out of date.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":410,"cache_read_input_tokens":69118,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":410},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6637fabe-b275-41d2-a9c7-8a4e5da1a9d1","uuid":"a759d09b-5e7f-4c49-9dd9-cf0199955132","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:20:43.799Z","request_id":"req_011CgtXXtnasU6QWbxbdwqoC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UQqNPGystjXX7VtmpfZtED":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T13:35:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 29,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"There are 29 endpoints. 24 are new routes from system-design §2.3. 5 are existing routes that get extended: POST /api/files (absence-note context), GET /api/me/timetable (sh_child default), GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (EXCUSED pre-fill and rule, absent-notification suppression) and POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (consentReminders). There are also 3 non-HTTP contracts: the notification types, getSelectedChild, and the pure helpers.\",\n    \"The base path is /api, not /api/v1. Envelopes, paginated() meta and error codes come from src/server/http.ts. http.ts has no 422, so system-design's '422' business-rule failures map to 400 VALIDATION_ERROR with details.reason (OUTSIDE_BOOKING_WINDOW, PAST_DUE, SIGNATURE_MISMATCH, DATE_WINDOW).\",\n    \"Error policy: an unviewable student or resource returns 404. A visible resource the caller may not act on returns 403 with details.reason. Races return 409 with details.reason (SLOT_TAKEN, OVERLAP, ONE_PER_TEACHER, ALREADY_REVIEWED, SLOT_BOOKED). The remind throttle returns 429 with retryAfterMs.\",\n    \"Decisions made beyond system-design: GET /api/conferences/:id/slots?view=day serves the teacher day view (FR-34). Slot booking details are hidden from anyone except the booker, the teacher and ADMIN. GET /api/students/:id/overview accepts ?cards= to limit which cards load. PATCH /api/conferences/:id returns 409 if booked slots exist and slotMinutes or date changes. The tracking CSV ignores pagination.\",\n    \"Partial requirements carried from system-design: FR-13 (announcements returns []), FR-35 and the calendar part of FR-5 (no PRD-14 calendar page). Neither is a blocker.\",\n    \"Three schema columns go beyond the PRD (ADR-3): ConferenceSlot.blocked, ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt and ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt. The migration also adds a raw-SQL partial unique index on ConferenceSlot(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId).\",\n    \"src/lib/validators/{absence-notes,conferences,consent-forms}.ts should mirror the input shapes in api-contracts.json `components`.\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json is still the stale SH-14 file. No architect sub-task owns it, so treat it as out of date.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UQqNPGystjXX7VtmpfZtED","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6637fabe-b275-41d2-a9c7-8a4e5da1a9d1","uuid":"b0b749c1-db3e-4c8c-a9ec-a998f045e094","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:20:43.835Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T13:35:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 29,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"There are 29 endpoints. 24 are new routes from system-design §2.3. 5 are existing routes that get extended: POST /api/files (absence-note context), GET /api/me/timetable (sh_child default), GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (EXCUSED pre-fill and rule, absent-notification suppression) and POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (consentReminders). There are also 3 non-HTTP contracts: the notification types, getSelectedChild, and the pure helpers.\",\n    \"The base path is /api, not /api/v1. Envelopes, paginated() meta and error codes come from src/server/http.ts. http.ts has no 422, so system-design's '422' business-rule failures map to 400 VALIDATION_ERROR with details.reason (OUTSIDE_BOOKING_WINDOW, PAST_DUE, SIGNATURE_MISMATCH, DATE_WINDOW).\",\n    \"Error policy: an unviewable student or resource returns 404. A visible resource the caller may not act on returns 403 with details.reason. Races return 409 with details.reason (SLOT_TAKEN, OVERLAP, ONE_PER_TEACHER, ALREADY_REVIEWED, SLOT_BOOKED). The remind throttle returns 429 with retryAfterMs.\",\n    \"Decisions made beyond system-design: GET /api/conferences/:id/slots?view=day serves the teacher day view (FR-34). Slot booking details are hidden from anyone except the booker, the teacher and ADMIN. GET /api/students/:id/overview accepts ?cards= to limit which cards load. PATCH /api/conferences/:id returns 409 if booked slots exist and slotMinutes or date changes. The tracking CSV ignores pagination.\",\n    \"Partial requirements carried from system-design: FR-13 (announcements returns []), FR-35 and the calendar part of FR-5 (no PRD-14 calendar page). Neither is a blocker.\",\n    \"Three schema columns go beyond the PRD (ADR-3): ConferenceSlot.blocked, ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt and ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt. The migration also adds a raw-SQL partial unique index on ConferenceSlot(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId).\",\n    \"src/lib/validators/{absence-notes,conferences,consent-forms}.ts should mirror the input shapes in api-contracts.json `components`.\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json is still the stale SH-14 file. No architect sub-task owns it, so treat it as out of date.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":11,"newStart":1,"newLines":11,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"SH-14\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T00:12:00Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T13:35:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"architect\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\","," ","   \"status\": \"complete\",","-  \"endpointCount\": 18,","+  \"endpointCount\": 29,","   \"blockers\": [],","   \"artifacts\": [","     \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\","]},{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":13,"newStart":14,"newLines":14,"lines":["     \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"","   ],","   \"notes\": [","-    \"There are 18 endpoints. 14 are new routes from system-design §2.5. 4 are existing routes that get extended: GET /api/attendance/today (noSchoolReason), GET /api/attendance/register (noSchoolReason), PUT /api/attendance/register (holidayOverride, D-8) and POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (sendRsvpReminders). There are also 4 non-HTTP contracts: getUpcomingEventsForUser, getPublicEvents, isSchoolDay and the notification types.\",","-    \"The base path is /api, not /api/v1. Envelopes and error codes come from src/server/http.ts, where VALIDATION_ERROR maps to 400. The feed, the single-event .ics and the RSVP CSV return raw bodies. An unknown feed token returns 404 text/plain.\",","-    \"Error policy: an event the caller cannot see, or a studentId they cannot view, returns 404. Not the creator, an admin-only field, a disallowed audience, or not in the audience returns 403 with details.reason. RSVP disabled or closed returns 409. Rate limits return 429 with details.retryAfterMs and Retry-After.\",","-    \"Decisions made beyond system-design: all-day input is startDate/endDate (yyyy-MM-dd, inclusive end) and output is an exclusive UTC end. audiences is limited to 1..20 entries. rsvpDeadline must be ≤ the first occurrence's start. Occurrence ids are '<eventId>:<startISO>', and all /api/events/:id routes take the plain eventId. GET /api/attendance/register also gains noSchoolReason (system-design names only getToday/getOverview). Term breaks send no event.created notifications and return {created, skipped, events}. The dispatch summary gains rsvpReminders {events, notified}.\",","-    \"Carried risks from system-design §4: R1 beta @mui/x-scheduler API drift (exact pin, MUI MCP lookup is mandatory, NFR-2), R2 import cycle (calendar-service must never import timetable-service), R3 DST across 4 code paths, R4 audience resolver parity test.\",","-    \"artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json is still the stale SH-13 file. No architect sub-task owns it in this phase, so treat it as out of date.\",","-    \"src/lib/validators/calendar.ts should mirror the input shapes in api-contracts.json `components` (EventInput, RsvpInput, AudienceInput).\"","+    \"There are 29 endpoints. 24 are new routes from system-design §2.3. 5 are existing routes that get extended: POST /api/files (absence-note context), GET /api/me/timetable (sh_child default), GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (EXCUSED pre-fill and rule, absent-notification suppression) and POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (consentReminders). There are also 3 non-HTTP contracts: the notification types, getSelectedChild, and the pure helpers.\",","+    \"The base path is /api, not /api/v1. Envelopes, paginated() meta and error codes come from src/server/http.ts. http.ts has no 422, so system-design's '422' business-rule failures map to 400 VALIDATION_ERROR with details.reason (OUTSIDE_BOOKING_WINDOW, PAST_DUE, SIGNATURE_MISMATCH, DATE_WINDOW).\",","+    \"Error policy: an unviewable student or resource returns 404. A visible resource the caller may not act on returns 403 with details.reason. Races return 409 with details.reason (SLOT_TAKEN, OVERLAP, ONE_PER_TEACHER, ALREADY_REVIEWED, SLOT_BOOKED). The remind throttle returns 429 with retryAfterMs.\",","+    \"Decisions made beyond system-design: GET /api/conferences/:id/slots?view=day serves the teacher day view (FR-34). Slot booking details are hidden from anyone except the booker, the teacher and ADMIN. GET /api/students/:id/overview accepts ?cards= to limit which cards load. PATCH /api/conferences/:id returns 409 if booked slots exist and slotMinutes or date changes. The tracking CSV ignores pagination.\",","+    \"Partial requirements carried from system-design: FR-13 (announcements returns []), FR-35 and the calendar part of FR-5 (no PRD-14 calendar page). Neither is a blocker.\",","+    \"Three schema columns go beyond the PRD (ADR-3): ConferenceSlot.blocked, ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt and ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt. The migration also adds a raw-SQL partial unique index on ConferenceSlot(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId).\",","+    \"src/lib/validators/{absence-notes,conferences,consent-forms}.ts should mirror the input shapes in api-contracts.json `components`.\",","+    \"artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json is still the stale SH-14 file. No architect sub-task owns it, so treat it as out of date.\"","   ],","   \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\""," }"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-14\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T00:12:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 18,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    \"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"There are 18 endpoints. 14 are new routes from system-design §2.5. 4 are existing routes that get extended: GET /api/attendance/today (noSchoolReason), GET /api/attendance/register (noSchoolReason), PUT /api/attendance/register (holidayOverride, D-8) and POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (sendRsvpReminders). There are also 4 non-HTTP contracts: getUpcomingEventsForUser, getPublicEvents, isSchoolDay and the notification types.\",\n    \"The base path is /api, not /api/v1. Envelopes and error codes come from src/server/http.ts, where VALIDATION_ERROR maps to 400. The feed, the single-event .ics and the RSVP CSV return raw bodies. An unknown feed token returns 404 text/plain.\",\n    \"Error policy: an event the caller cannot see, or a studentId they cannot view, returns 404. Not the creator, an admin-only field, a disallowed audience, or not in the audience returns 403 with details.reason. RSVP disabled or closed returns 409. Rate limits return 429 with details.retryAfterMs and Retry-After.\",\n    \"Decisions made beyond system-design: all-day input is startDate/endDate (yyyy-MM-dd, inclusive end) and output is an exclusive UTC end. audiences is limited to 1..20 entries. rsvpDeadline must be ≤ the first occurrence's start. Occurrence ids are '<eventId>:<startISO>', and all /api/events/:id routes take the plain eventId. GET /api/attendance/register also gains noSchoolReason (system-design names only getToday/getOverview). Term breaks send no event.created notifications and return {created, skipped, events}. The dispatch summary gains rsvpReminders {events, notified}.\",\n    \"Carried risks from system-design §4: R1 beta @mui/x-scheduler API drift (exact pin, MUI MCP lookup is mandatory, NFR-2), R2 import cycle (calendar-service must never import timetable-service), R3 DST across 4 code paths, R4 audience resolver parity test.\",\n    \"artifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json is still the stale SH-13 file. No architect sub-task owns it in this phase, so treat it as out of date.\",\n    \"src/lib/validators/calendar.ts should mirror the input shapes in api-contracts.json `components` (EventInput, RsvpInput, AudienceInput).\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UQqNPGystjXX7VtmpfZtED","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
