\n- **24 new routes** from section 2.3 of the system design, covering child selection, parent overview, absence notes, conferences and slots, and consent forms.\n- **5 existing routes that get extended:**\n  - `POST /api/files` gains the `absence-note` upload type.\n  - `GET /api/me/timetable` now defaults to the parent's selected child.\n  - `GET` and `PUT /api/attendance/register` gain the EXCUSED pre-fill and permission rule, and stop sending absence alerts for students covered by a note.\n  - `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` sends the 48-hour consent reminder.\n\nThe file also lists the new notification types, `getSelectedChild`, the small pure helper functions, and the shared request/response shapes.\n\n**`artifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json`**: status `complete`, `endpointCount: 29`, no blockers.\n\nDecisions you might want to check:\n- **No 422 status code:** the system design calls for 422 on rule failures (booking window closed, past due, signature mismatch), but `src/server/http.ts` has no 422. I mapped these to 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR` with a `details.reason`.\n- **Errors by case:**\n  - A student or record the caller can't see returns 404, so its existence doesn't leak.\n  - Not allowed to act on it returns 403.\n  - Booking races return 409.\n  - The remind throttle returns 429.\n- **Choices the design didn't specify:**\n  - The teacher's day view is `GET /api/conferences/:id/slots?view=day`.\n  - Only the booking parent, the teacher and admins can see who booked a slot.\n  - Changing an event's date or slot length is refused (409) once slots are booked.\n  - The consent tracking CSV ignores pagination.\n- **Still partial, as the design already said:** the announcements card returns an empty list (FR-13), and conference meetings don't appear on a calendar page (FR-35, plus the calendar filter in FR-5).\n- **Stale file:** `threat-model-notes.json` is still from SH-14, and no architect sub-task owns it.","ttft_ms":2375,"type":"result","durat