{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CVkdcp6PGLUeWqEUwWLTKA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design: PRD-16 Role Dashboards, Reports & Early-Warning Insights\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-16 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T14:00:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (FR-1 to FR-46, NFR-1 to NFR-12), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-11), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`. The SH-15 version of this file was moved to `artifacts/architect/.prev-SH-15/system-design.md`.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Overview\n10\t\n11\tPRD-16 replaces the placeholder `/dashboard` with three role dashboards (Admin, Teacher, Student), adds a rule-based early-warning engine with a persisted snapshot, an at-risk list page, a student \"Insights\" tab, and an admin Reports centre with six reports. This is a **brownfield** change (NFR-8). It adds no dependencies (ADR-1) and creates two new service folders, `src/server/dashboards/` and `src/server/reports/`.\n12\t\n13\tDesign principles:\n14\t- **Services are the single source.** Server-component widgets, the `/api/*` JSON routes and the CSV exports all call the same service functions. Routes are thin (NFR-6).\n15\t- **Scope is enforced inside services.** Every service function takes an `AccessUser` and intersects with `getAccessibleStudentIds()` (NFR-3).\n16\t- **Pure rules, batch loaders.** Risk thresholds are pure functions (NFR-9). Data for 600 students is loaded in a fixed number of grouped queries, never per student (NFR-1).\n17\t- **Cache only shared aggregates.** Admin and teacher-scoped aggregates use `unstable_cache`. Per-student widgets are cheap and not cached (ADR-3).\n18\t\n19\t### Blockers and dependency gaps\n20\t\n21\tIntake reported **no blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json: blockers: []`, confidence 91 %). The following warnings are resolved by design decisions and are degraded rather than blocked:\n22\t\n23\t| Gap | Requirements | Resolution |\n24\t|---|---|---|\n25\t| No `Announcement` model (PRD-12) | FR-8, FR-14, FR-38 | Announcement widgets render `EmptyState` \"Announcements not available yet\". The engagement report omits the read-rate metric and shows a note. The FR-9 \"New announcement\" quick action is hidden because its route does not exist. One `ANNOUNCEMENTS_AVAILABLE = false` constant in `src/server/dashboards/announcements.ts` gates all three, following the stub precedent `parent/overview-service.listUnreadAnnouncements` (ADR-11). **Dependency gap on PRD-12.** |\n26\t| No calendar service/API (PRD-14) | FR-21 | Read `CalendarEvent` directly with school-wide audience, expand recurrences with the existing `calendar/recurrence.expandOccurrences`, take the next 5. |\n27\t| FR-28 history conflicts with \"one row per student per term\" | FR-27, FR-28, FR-29, FR-31 | Keep one row per (student, term). Add `previousLevel` and a capped `history` Json (§4.1). |\n28\t| \"Missing\" is derived, not stored | FR-11, FR-25, FR-37 | One shared predicate `missingWork()` (§3.5), extracted from `assignments/reminders.ts`. |\n29\t| NFR-5 mui-mcp lookup | NFR-5 | Process step for dev and QA. If the MCP server is unavailable during dev, dev must report it as a blocker. |\n30\t\n31\t---\n32\t\n33\t## 2. Component Breakdown\n34\t\n35\t### 2.1 Pages and UI (`src/app/(app)/…`)\n36\t\n37\t| Path | Kind | Responsibility | Reqs |\n38\t|---|---|---|---|\n39\t| `dashboard/page.tsx` | Server page (edit) | Keep the PARENT → `/my-children` redirect. Switch on role and render `AdminDashboard`, `TeacherDashboard` or `StudentDashboard`. Any other role → `notFound()`. | FR-1 |\n40\t| `dashboard/_components/GreetingHeader.tsx` | Server | `greetingFor(now, tz)` + first name + school-tz date + `getCurrentTerm().name`. | FR-3, NFR-7 |\n41\t| `dashboard/_components/{Admin,Teacher,Student}Dashboard.tsx` | Server | MUI `Grid` layout of widgets. Each widget sits in `<Widget>`. | FR-1, FR-2 |\n42\t| `dashboard/_components/widgets/*.tsx` | Async server components, one per widget | Fetch through the service and render with MUI. Chart widgets pass serialisable props to a client chart component. | FR-4–FR-22 |\n43\t| `src/components/Widget/Widget.tsx` | Shared server wrapper (new) | MUI `Card` with a title, an optional \"Updated N min ago\" caption from `computedAt`, `<WidgetErrorBoundary>` and `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>`. It is used by about 20 widgets, so the wrapper pays for itself. | FR-2, FR-24 |\n44\t| `src/components/Widget/WidgetErrorBoundary.tsx` | Client (new) | Class component with `getDerivedStateFromError`. It renders an `Alert` \"This widget could not load\" and a \"Retry\" `Button` that resets state and calls `router.refresh()`. | FR-2 |\n45\t| `src/components/charts/ChartA11y.tsx` | Client (new) | Wraps an x-charts chart with `aria-label={summary}` and a `visuallyHidden` MUI `Table` of the same rows. Used by every chart. | NFR-2 |\n46\t| `dashboard/_components/RefreshButton.tsx` | Client | ADMIN only. Sends `POST /api/dashboard/refresh`, shows a toast through `useToast`, then calls `router.refresh()`. | FR-24 |\n47\t| `insights/at-risk/page.tsx` | Server page (new) | `requireRole(['ADMIN','TEACHER'])`. Filters (level, reason, grade level, section) live in the URL search params. Uses the shared `DataTable` with level `Chip` (text, not colour only), reason chips, a trend arrow icon with an `aria-label`, and actions (open student → `/students/[id]/insights`; message parents → the existing PRD-13 new-conversation flow, prefilled). A CSV button links to `/api/insights/at-risk?…&format=csv`. | FR-29, FR-30, NFR-3 |\n48\t| `students/[id]/insights/page.tsx` | Server page (new) | `assertCanViewStudent`. Shows the current signal values (attendance %, courses below 60 %, missing count), the level badge and a history list from `snapshot.history`. | FR-31, FR-43 |\n49\t| `admin/reports/page.tsx` + `admin/reports/[reportKey]/page.tsx` | Server pages (new) | ADMIN. The index lists the six reports. The report page has an academic-year/term selector and report filters (x-date-pickers for date ranges) in the URL, then a chart, a `DataTable` and a CSV link. Unknown `reportKey` → `notFound()`. | FR-33–FR-39, FR-44 |\n50\t| `src/config/navigation.ts` | Config (edit) | After \"Dashboard\": `Reports` (`/admin/reports`, ADMIN) and `At-risk students` (`/insights/at-risk`, ADMIN and TEACHER). | FR-40 |\n51\t| `src/config/student-tabs.ts` | Config (edit) | Append `{ key: 'insights', label: 'Insights', href: id => \\`/students/${id}/insights\\`, roles: ['ADMIN','TEACHER'] }`. | FR-31 |\n52\t\n53\tReused components (NFR-8): `StatCard`, `DataTable`, `LoadingSkeleton`, `PageHeader`, `EmptyState`, `Toast`/`useToast`. Charts: `LineChart` with `ChartsReferenceLine`, `BarChart` (stacked, histogram) and `Gauge` from `@mui/x-charts` 9.5.0 (NFR-4).\n54\t\n55\t### 2.2 Services — `src/server/dashboards/`\n56\t\n57\t| File | Exports | Reqs |\n58\t|---|---|---|\n59\t| `teacher.ts` | `getTodaysClasses(user)` (wraps `attendance-service.getToday` + `nowAndNext`), `getToGrade(user)` (count + oldest 5 ungraded submissions and quiz attempts needing manual grading), `getUpcomingDeadlines(user)` (next 7 days, submission rate = submissions / active enrolments, one grouped query), `getTeacherMessages(user)` (`messaging/conversations.unreadCount` + announcements stub). | FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8 |\n60\t| `student.ts` | `getStudentToday(user)` → `parent/overview-service.getToday(user, user.id)` (holiday-aware). `getDueSoon(user)` (next 7 days + `missingWork`, overdue first, flagged `overdue: true`). `getRecentGrades(user)` → overview-service. `getMyCourses(user)` (`getStudentGrades` for percent/letter, LessonProgress ratio, first incomplete visible lesson). `getTermAttendance(user)` (`countStatuses` + `attendanceRate` over the term range). | FR-10–FR-15 |\n61\t| `admin.ts` | `getKpis()` (cached): active students, active teachers, today's rate and the same weekday −7 days delta via `attendance-service.getOverview`, missing registers, pending absence notes. `getSafeguardingCount(user)` is **uncached** and only called when `isSafeguardingLead(user)`, so the count never sits in a shared cache entry. `getAttendanceTrend()` (cached). `getEnrollmentByGrade()` (cached). `getGradeDistribution()` (cached; uses the §3.4 batch loader). `getUpcomingEvents()`. `getRecentActivity()` (AuditLog `action` startsWith `user.`/`report_card.`/`settings.`, latest 10, actor joined). | FR-16–FR-19, FR-21, FR-22 |\n62\t| `insights.ts` | The `unstable_cache` wrappers and tag constants (§3.6). `getRiskSummary(user)` (counts by level and reason). `getTopAtRisk(user, n)`. | FR-7, FR-20, FR-23, FR-24 |\n63\t| `risk-rules.ts` | **Pure.** `attendanceSignal(pct, threshold)`, `gradesSignal(coursePcts)`, `missingSignal(count)`, `overallLevel(signals)`, `formatReason(signal)`. No Prisma import. | FR-25, FR-26, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n64\t| `risk.ts` | `loadRiskInputs(termId, studentIds)` (batch). `recomputeRiskSnapshots({ force })`: hourly gate, compute, upsert, history append, FR-32 notify, `revalidateTag`. `listAtRisk(user, filters, page)`. `getStudentInsights(user, studentId)`. | FR-25–FR-32, FR-42, FR-43 |\n65\t| `missing-work.ts` | `missingWork({ studentIds, from, to, now })` → `Map<studentId, {assignmentId, dueAt, courseId}[]>`. The shared predicate (§3.5). `assignments/reminders.ts` is refactored to call it with its own 8-day window, keeping its behaviour. | FR-11, FR-25, FR-37 |\n66\t| `announcements.ts` | `ANNOUNCEMENTS_AVAILABLE = false`, `latestAnnouncements()` → `[]`. | FR-8, FR-14, FR-38 |\n67\t\n68\t`greetingFor(now, tz)` and `schoolDaysBack(n, tz)` (the last n dates with at least one `AttendanceSession`) go in `src/lib/dates.ts` next to the existing helpers (ADR-9).\n69\t\n70\t### 2.3 Services — `src/server/reports/`\n71\t\n72\t| File | Responsibility | Reqs |\n73\t|---|---|---|\n74\t| `index.ts` | `REPORTS` registry: `key → { title, filterSchema (Zod), run(filters) → { chart, rows, summary }, columns }`. `REPORT_KEYS = Object.keys(REPORTS)`. The page, the API and the CSV all read this registry, so CSV rows equal table rows (FR-35 AC 7) and an unknown key is a 404. | FR-33, FR-44 |\n75\t| `enrollment.ts` | Active students by grade level × section × gender (`groupBy`). New enrollments and archives by month (`$queryRaw date_trunc('month', … AT TIME ZONE tz)`). | FR-34 |\n76\t| `attendance.ts` | Calls `attendance-service.getReport(filters)` for per-student rows, then rolls up by grade level, section or course. Daily trend. Lowest 20 students. | FR-35 |\n77\t| `performance.ts` | Uses the §3.4 batch grade loader. Average percent and letter distribution (`letterFor`) by course and by subject. Section comparison for the same grade × subject. | FR-36 |\n78\t| `completion.ts` | On-time / late (`submittedAt` vs `dueAt`) / missing (`missingWork`) rates by course and by teacher for a date range. | FR-37 |\n79\t| `engagement.ts` | Lesson completion by course (LessonProgress). Distinct parents signed in over the last 7 and 30 days (`AuditLog action='auth.login.success'` joined to PARENT users, with `User.lastLoginAt` as a fallback). Announcement read rate is omitted with a note. | FR-38 |\n80\t| `workload.ts` | Per teacher: courses, distinct students, weekly `TimetableSlot` count, grading backlog (same query as `getToGrade`, grouped by teacher). | FR-39 |\n81\t\n82\t### 2.4 API routes (`src/app/api/…`, thin: `withHandler` → `requireRole` → `parseQuery` (Zod) → service → `ok`/`paginated`/CSV)\n83\t\n84\t| Route | Roles | Service | Reqs |\n85\t|---|---|---|---|\n86\t| `GET /api/dashboard/teacher` | TEACHER | `dashboards/teacher.*` + `getTopAtRisk` | FR-41 |\n87\t| `GET /api/dashboard/student` | STUDENT | `dashboards/student.*` | FR-41 |\n88\t| `GET /api/dashboard/admin` | ADMIN | `dashboards/admin.*` + `getRiskSummary` | FR-41 |\n89\t| `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` | ADMIN | `recomputeRiskSnapshots({ force: true })`, then `revalidateTag` on all tags, then `audit({ action: 'dashboard.refresh' })` | FR-24, FR-27 |\n90\t| `GET /api/insights/at-risk` | ADMIN, TEACHER | `listAtRisk`. Query: `level, reason, gradeLevel, sectionId, page, pageSize ≤ 100, format=csv` | FR-29, FR-30, FR-42 |\n91\t| `GET /api/students/[id]/insights` | ADMIN, TEACHER of the student | `getStudentInsights` (`assertCanViewStudent` → FORBIDDEN) | FR-43 |\n92\t| `GET /api/reports/[reportKey]` | ADMIN | `REPORTS[key].run`. `?format=csv` → `toCsv(columns, rows)` with `Content-Disposition: attachment`. Unknown key → 404 `NOT_FOUND` | FR-44 |\n93\t\n94\tValidators: `src/lib/validators/dashboards.ts` (at-risk filters, insights params) and `src/lib/validators/reports.ts` (`reportKey` enum + per-report filter schemas) (NFR-6).\n95\t\n96\t### 2.5 Background job\n97\t\n98\t`src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` gets one more isolated `try { await recomputeRiskSnapshots() } catch (e) { logger.error(...) }` block. The gate is in the database: skip if `max(computedAt)` for the current term is under 60 minutes old (FR-27, NFR-12, ADR-6).\n99\t\n100\t### 2.6 Notifications\n101\t\n102\tAdd `'insights.student_high_risk'` to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (category ACADEMIC, recipient TEACHER, email default `true`). Send it through the existing `notify()` (FR-32).\n103\t\n104\t### 2.7 Seed\n105\t\n106\t- `prisma/seed-large.ts` + `\"seed:large\": \"tsx prisma/seed-large.ts\"`: a mulberry32 PRNG with a fixed seed, 600 students across Grades 6–8 (8 sections), 40 teachers, timetables, 60 school days of attendance, assignments, submissions and grades. Uses `createMany` in batches of 1,000 (FR-45).\n107\t- `prisma/seed.ts` (edit): plant at least 3 students per level (High, Medium and none) by seeding attendance, grades and missing work that cross the FR-25 thresholds. At the end it calls `recomputeRiskSnapshots({ force: true })` so the list is populated right after seeding (FR-46).\n108\t\n109\t---\n110\t\n111\t## 3. Data Flow\n112\t\n113\t### 3.1 Dashboard request\n114\t\n115\t```\n116\tGET /dashboard\n117\t  └─ page.tsx (server): getCurrentUser() ─ PARENT → redirect('/my-children')\n118\t       └─ <RoleDashboard>  → streams shell + GreetingHeader immediately (NFR-1 first content)\n119\t            ├─ <Widget title=\"To grade\"><Suspense><ToGradeWidget/></Suspense></Widget>\n120\t            │      └─ dashboards/teacher.getToGrade(user) ── Prisma (scoped)\n121\t            ├─ <Widget title=\"At-risk students\">… insights.getTopAtRisk(user,5)\n122\t            │      └─ unstable_cache(['risk','teacher',userId], {revalidate:3600, tags:['insights:at-risk']})\n123\t            │            └─ StudentRiskSnapshot WHERE studentId IN accessible\n124\t            └─ … each widget streams independently; a throw inside one → WidgetErrorBoundary → Alert + Retry\n125\t```\n126\t\n127\t### 3.2 Admin refresh\n128\t\n129\t```\n130\tRefreshButton → POST /api/dashboard/refresh (ADMIN)\n131\t  → risk.recomputeRiskSnapshots({force:true})\n132\t  → revalidateTag('dashboard:admin'), ('dashboard:teacher'), ('insights:at-risk')\n133\t  → audit('dashboard.refresh') → 200 { data: { refreshedAt } }\n134\t  → client: toast + router.refresh() → widgets re-render with new computedAt\n135\t```\n136\t\n137\t### 3.3 Risk recompute (hourly cron or Refresh)\n138\t\n139\t```\n140\trecomputeRiskSnapshots({force})\n141\t 1. term = getCurrentTerm(); none → return { skipped: 'no-term' }\n142\t 2. if !force and max(computedAt where termId) > now−60min → return { skipped: 'fresh' }\n143\t 3. students = ACTIVE students enrolled in the current term\n144\t 4. inputs = loadRiskInputs(term, students)            ← fixed number of grouped queries\n145\t      attendancePct  : AttendanceRecord groupBy(studentId,status) in term range → attendanceRate()\n146\t      coursePcts     : batch grade loader (§3.4) → computeStudentTerm per (student,course)\n147\t      missingCount   : missingWork({from: today−30d, to: now})\n148\t 5. for each student: signals = [attendanceSignal, gradesSignal, missingSignal]; level = overallLevel(signals)\n149\t 6. upsert StudentRiskSnapshot(studentId, termId):\n150\t      level changed → previousLevel = old.level; history = [ {level,reasons,computedAt}, ...old.history ].slice(0,10)\n151\t      unchanged     → update reasons, signals, computedAt only\n152\t 7. for each (old ∈ {null, MEDIUM}) → HIGH:\n153\t      claimed = updateMany(where {id, OR:[highNotifiedAt null, highNotifiedAt < now−14d]}, data {highNotifiedAt: now})\n154\t      claimed.count === 1 && homeroomTeacherId → notify(homeroomTeacher, 'insights.student_high_risk', {studentId, reasons})\n155\t      no homeroom teacher → logger.warn, skip\n156\t 8. revalidateTag('insights:at-risk')\n157\t```\n158\t\n159\tUpserts run in chunked `$transaction`s of about 100 rows. Step 7 uses an atomic claim, so two concurrent cron processes cannot double-notify (§3 Q8 of the notes).\n160\t\n161\tRisk rules (FR-25, FR-26). These are pure functions, and every boundary has a unit test (NFR-9):\n162\t\n163\t| Signal | Medium | High | No data |\n164\t|---|---|---|---|\n165\t| Attendance | `pct < threshold` (SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold, default 90) | `pct < 80` | no records → null |\n166\t| Grades | any course `< 60` | `≥ 2` courses `< 60` **or** any `< 50` | null percents ignored |\n167\t| Missing (30 days) | 3–4 | `≥ 5` | 0–2 → null |\n168\t| **Overall** | exactly one Medium | any High **or** ≥ 2 Medium | otherwise none (`level = null`) |\n169\t\n170\tThe reasons Json is an array of `{ signal: 'ATTENDANCE'|'GRADES'|'MISSING', level, value, label }`. Labels look like `\"Attendance 78 %\"`, `\"2 courses < 60 %\"` and `\"6 missing\"`, and the chips and CSV use them directly.\n171\t\n172\t### 3.4 Batch grade loader (shared by FR-19, FR-25 and FR-36)\n173\t\n174\t`gradebook/batch-grades.ts` exports `loadTermPercents(termId, studentIds?)`. It runs about 5 queries: courses in the term with their scales, grade items, grades, categories and overrides. It groups the rows in memory and calls the existing pure `computeStudentTerm` for each (student, course). The result is `Map<studentId, {courseId, percent, letter}[]>`. Because it uses the same calculation as `getStudentGrades`, dashboard and report numbers equal the Grades tab (FR-13, NFR-8). FR-13 itself calls `getStudentGrades` directly, since it is a single student.\n175\t\n176\t### 3.5 Missing-work predicate\n177\t\n178\tThe predicate is: the assignment is published (`visibleWhere(now)`), `dueAt ∈ [from, min(to, now))`, `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION`, the student is actively enrolled in the course, there is no `Submission`, and there is no `GradeExemption`. It runs as one query for the assignments in the window joined to active enrolments, then subtracts submissions and exemptions in memory. FR-11 uses a \"term start → now\" window for overdue items, FR-25 uses 30 days, and FR-37 uses the report's date range.\n179\t\n180\t### 3.6 Cache keys and tags (FR-23, NFR-3)\n181\t\n182\t| Cached function | Key parts | revalidate | Tags |\n183\t|---|---|---|---|\n184\t| `admin.getKpis` (without safeguarding) | `['dash','admin','kpis', today]` | 900 | `dashboard:admin` |\n185\t| `admin.getAttendanceTrend` | `['dash','admin','trend', today]` | 900 | `dashboard:admin` |\n186\t| `admin.getEnrollmentByGrade` | `['dash','admin','enrollment']` | 900 | `dashboard:admin` |\n187\t| `admin.getGradeDistribution` | `['dash','admin','grades', termId]` | 900 | `dashboard:admin` |\n188\t| teacher `getToGrade`, `getUpcomingDeadlines` | `['dash','teacher', userId, …]` | 900 | `dashboard:teacher` |\n189\t| `insights.getRiskSummary` / `getTopAtRisk` | `['risk', 'admin']` or `['risk','teacher', userId]` | 3600 | `insights:at-risk` |\n190\t\n191\tEvery cached value is `{ data, computedAt: string }` and contains no `Date` or `Decimal`. Teacher keys always include `userId`, so no cache entry is ever shared across teachers. The safeguarding count and all student widgets are never cached. `getTodaysClasses` is not cached either, because the attendance taken/not-taken state must be live.\n192\t\n193\t`ponytail:` the cache is per process (ADR-3). Add a shared cache handler if the app runs on more than one instance.\n194\t\n195\t### 3.7 At-risk list and CSV (FR-29, FR-30, FR-42)\n196\t\n197\t```\n198\tGET /api/insights/at-risk?level&reason&gradeLevel&sectionId&page&format\n199\t → scope = getAccessibleStudentIds(user)           // 'ALL' | ids\n200\t → where = { termId: current, level: not null,\n201\t             studentId: scope==='ALL' ? undefined : { in: scope },     // intersection: filters can't widen\n202\t             level?, reasons: reason ? { array_contains: [{signal}] } : undefined,\n203\t             student: { sectionMembers: { some: { section: { gradeLevel?, id: sectionId? } } } } }\n204\t → format=csv ? toCsv(AT_RISK_COLUMNS, allRows) : paginated(rows, page, pageSize)\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\tThe page and the CSV both call `listAtRisk`, so the CSV matches the filtered table. Sort order: HIGH before MEDIUM, then by the number of reasons descending, then by name. The trend is `up` when the level rose since `previousLevel`, `down` when it fell, and `flat` otherwise.\n208\t\n209\t---\n210\t\n211\t## 4. Data Model Changes (one migration: `add_student_risk_snapshot`)\n212\t\n213\t### 4.1 Prisma\n214\t\n215\t```prisma\n216\tenum RiskLevel {\n217\t  MEDIUM\n218\t  HIGH\n219\t}\n220\t\n221\tmodel StudentRiskSnapshot {\n222\t  id             String     @id @default(cuid())\n223\t  studentId      String\n224\t  termId         String\n225\t  level          RiskLevel?          // null = none\n226\t  previousLevel  RiskLevel?          // FR-28 trend arrow\n227\t  reasons        Json                // [{signal, level, value, label}]\n228\t  signals        Json                // {attendancePct, coursesBelow60, lowestCoursePct, missingCount} for the Insights tab\n229\t  history        Json     @default(\"[]\")  // FR-28: last 10 level changes [{level, reasons, computedAt}]\n230\t  highNotifiedAt DateTime?           // FR-32 14-day claim\n231\t  computedAt     DateTime\n232\t  createdAt      DateTime   @default(now())\n233\t  updatedAt      DateTime   @updatedAt\n234\t  student        User       @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n235\t  term           Term       @relation(fields: [termId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n236\t\n237\t  @@unique([studentId, termId])\n238\t  @@index([termId, level])\n239\t  @@index([termId, computedAt])\n240\t}\n241\t```\n242\t\n243\t`User` and `Term` get back-relations. `history` is appended only when the level changes, so hourly runs do not grow it. `ponytail:` it is capped at 10 entries. Add a history table if long-range trend analytics are ever needed (ADR-5).\n244\t\n245\t### 4.2 Optional index\n246\t\n247\tAdd `AuditLog @@index([createdAt])` only if `EXPLAIN` on `seed:large` shows the FR-22 query is slow (ADR-7). It is not in the base migration.\n248\t\n249\t---\n250\t\n251\t## 5. Security and Privacy\n252\t\n253\t- **Authorization.** Every page and handler calls `requireRole`. Services re-check scope: they take `AccessUser`, read `getAccessibleStudentIds`, and **intersect** it with filters (NFR-3, FR-42). The student insights endpoint uses `assertCanViewStudent` → 403 FORBIDDEN.\n254\t- **Cache isolation.** Teacher keys include `userId`. The safeguarding count is never cached and is shown only when `isSafeguardingLead` (FR-16).\n255\t- **CSV.** Every export goes through `src/server/csv.ts` `toCsv`/`escapeCsvCell`, which guards against formula injection (FR-30, FR-33).\n256\t- **SQL.** Only tagged-template `$queryRaw`. `$queryRawUnsafe` is never used (ADR-7).\n257\t- **Audit.** `dashboard.refresh` is audited. Report reads are not audited, which matches the existing admin read endpoints.\n258\t- **Notification content.** The notification contains the student name and reason labels only, no grades detail, and links to `/students/[id]/insights`, which is scope-checked.\n259\t\n260\t## 6. Performance (NFR-1)\n261\t\n262\t| Surface | Budget | How it is met |\n263\t|---|---|---|\n264\t| Dashboards: first content | < 1.5 s | The shell and greeting render without waiting. Widgets stream behind Suspense. Admin aggregates are cached for 15 minutes. At-risk data is read from the snapshot table and never computed live. |\n265\t| Reports | < 3 s | Grouped queries and `$queryRaw` bucketing. The batch grade loader uses about 5 queries. No per-student loops. |\n266\t| Risk recompute | Background | About 10 queries + chunked upserts for 600 students. It runs at most hourly. |\n267\t\n268\tDev must measure these against `seed:large` and add indexes only where `EXPLAIN` shows a sequential-scan hotspot.\n269\t\n270\t## 7. Testing hooks (NFR-9, NFR-10)\n271\t\n272\t- **Unit (Vitest):** `risk-rules.ts` boundaries: 90/89.9, 80/79.9, 60/59.9, 50/49.9, missing counts 2/3/4/5, Medium+Medium → High, threshold override. Also `greetingFor` hour boundaries in the tz, and the `missingWork` window edges.\n273\t- **Integration:** each report's `run()` on the default seed with known totals. CSV rows equal table rows. The at-risk scope intersection: a teacher filtering by another section gets 0 rows outside scope. Refresh revalidates the cache, so `computedAt` changes. The FR-32 14-day claim fires only once. The default seed yields at least 3 students per level (FR-46).\n274\t- **E2E (Playwright + axe):** one spec per role dashboard plus the parent redirect, `/insights/at-risk`, and `/admin/reports/attendance` with CSV download.\n275\t- **Lint:** no `console.log`. Logging uses `src/lib/logger.ts`.\n276\t\n277\t## 8. Out of scope (NFR-11)\n278\t\n279\tNo drag-and-drop layouts, no ML scoring, no scheduled report emails, and no changes to PRD-17/18 behaviour. No Announcement model or calendar API is built here (they are dependency gaps, §1).\n280\t\n281\t---\n282\t\n283\t## 9. Requirements Traceability\n284\t\n285\t| Req | Design element |\n286\t|---|---|\n287\t| FR-1 | `dashboard/page.tsx` role switch + PARENT redirect kept (§2.1) |\n288\t| FR-2 | `Widget` + `WidgetErrorBoundary` + Suspense/`LoadingSkeleton` (§2.1, §3.1) |\n289\t| FR-3 | `GreetingHeader`, `greetingFor` in `src/lib/dates.ts`, `getCurrentTerm` |\n290\t| FR-4 | `teacher.getTodaysClasses` (attendance-service `getToday` + `nowAndNext`), live |\n291\t| FR-5 | `teacher.getToGrade`, cached per teacher |\n292\t| FR-6 | `teacher.getUpcomingDeadlines` |\n293\t| FR-7 | `insights.getTopAtRisk(user, 5)` from snapshots |\n294\t| FR-8 | `teacher.getTeacherMessages`: `unreadCount` + announcements stub (§1 gap) |\n295\t| FR-9 | `QuickActionsWidget`: static MUI links; \"New announcement\" hidden (§1) |\n296\t| FR-10 | `student.getStudentToday` → overview-service `getToday` |\n297\t| FR-11 | `student.getDueSoon` + `missingWork` (§3.5) |\n298\t| FR-12 | `student.getRecentGrades` → overview-service |\n299\t| FR-13 | `student.getMyCourses` → `getStudentGrades` + LessonProgress |\n300\t| FR-14 | `announcements.latestAnnouncements` → `EmptyState` (§1) |\n301\t| FR-15 | `student.getTermAttendance` + x-charts `Gauge` |\n302\t| FR-16 | `admin.getKpis` (cached) + uncached `getSafeguardingCount` for leads |\n303\t| FR-17 | `admin.getAttendanceTrend` + `LineChart` + `ChartsReferenceLine` at the threshold |\n304\t| FR-18 | `admin.getEnrollmentByGrade` + stacked `BarChart` |\n305\t| FR-19 | `admin.getGradeDistribution` via the batch grade loader (§3.4) |\n306\t| FR-20 | `insights.getRiskSummary` |\n307\t| FR-21 | `admin.getUpcomingEvents` (CalendarEvent + `expandOccurrences`) |\n308\t| FR-22 | `admin.getRecentActivity` (AuditLog prefixes) |\n309\t| FR-23 | `insights.ts` `unstable_cache` wrappers (§3.6) |\n310\t| FR-24 | `computedAt` → \"Updated N min ago\"; `RefreshButton` + `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` (§3.2) |\n311\t| FR-25 | `risk-rules.ts` signals + `risk.loadRiskInputs` (§3.3) |\n312\t| FR-26 | `risk-rules.overallLevel` |\n313\t| FR-27 | `StudentRiskSnapshot` model + migration; cron hook with DB gate (§2.5, §4.1) |\n314\t| FR-28 | `previousLevel` + capped `history` Json (§4.1) |\n315\t| FR-29 | `/insights/at-risk` page + `risk.listAtRisk` (§3.7) |\n316\t| FR-30 | URL filters + `toCsv` from the same `listAtRisk` |\n317\t| FR-31 | `studentTabs` 'insights' entry + `students/[id]/insights` page |\n318\t| FR-32 | Step 7 of §3.3: atomic `highNotifiedAt` claim + `notify('insights.student_high_risk')` |\n319\t| FR-33 | `/admin/reports` + `REPORTS` registry + year/term selector + CSV (§2.3) |\n320\t| FR-34 | `reports/enrollment.ts` |\n321\t| FR-35 | `reports/attendance.ts` (reuses `attendance-service.getReport`) |\n322\t| FR-36 | `reports/performance.ts` (batch grade loader + `letterFor`) |\n323\t| FR-37 | `reports/completion.ts` + `missingWork` |\n324\t| FR-38 | `reports/engagement.ts`; announcement read rate omitted (§1) |\n325\t| FR-39 | `reports/workload.ts` |\n326\t| FR-40 | `src/config/navigation.ts` entries |\n327\t| FR-41 | `/api/dashboard/{teacher,student,admin}` GET + `/refresh` POST (§2.4) |\n328\t| FR-42 | `GET /api/insights/at-risk` with scope intersection (§3.7) |\n329\t| FR-43 | `GET /api/students/[id]/insights` + `assertCanViewStudent` |\n330\t| FR-44 | `GET /api/reports/[reportKey]`, registry-validated, 404 for unknown keys |\n331\t| FR-45 | `prisma/seed-large.ts` + `seed:large` script (§2.7) |\n332\t| FR-46 | `prisma/seed.ts` planted risk cohorts + forced recompute (§2.7) |\n333\t| NFR-1 | Streaming widgets, caching, batch loaders, snapshot reads (§6) |\n334\t| NFR-2 | `ChartA11y` aria summary + visually hidden table; text badges (§2.1) |\n335\t| NFR-3 | Scope in services, intersection, per-teacher cache keys (§5) |\n336\t| NFR-4 | MUI / MUI X only; shared components reused (§2.1) |\n337\t| NFR-5 | mui-mcp lookup as a dev/QA process step; unavailability = blocker (§1) |\n338\t| NFR-6 | Thin handlers, validators files, `paginated`, service folders (§2.4) |\n339\t| NFR-7 | `src/lib/dates.ts` / `schoolToday` for every window; SQL `AT TIME ZONE` |\n340\t| NFR-8 | Reuse table in §2 (attendance-service, grade-calc, overview-service, csv, notify, audit, components) |\n341\t| NFR-9 | Test hooks in §7 |\n342\t| NFR-10 | `logger` only; lint/typecheck/test green (§7) |\n343\t| NFR-11 | Out of scope (§8); rule-based `risk-rules.ts` |\n344\t| NFR-12 | 3600 s risk cache + hourly DB-gated recompute (§2.5, §3.6) |\n345\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dc3003b-f495-40f4-b937-7fc5d8e13052","uuid":"0717747b-644d-4869-9d3a-3b01453d8a14","timestamp":"2026-11-10T04:32:54.627Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: PRD-16 Role Dashboards, Reports & Early-Warning Insights\n\nTicket: SH-16 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T14:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (FR-1 to FR-46, NFR-1 to NFR-12), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-11), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`. The SH-15 version of this file was moved to `artifacts/architect/.prev-SH-15/system-design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-16 replaces the placeholder `/dashboard` with three role dashboards (Admin, Teacher, Student), adds a rule-based early-warning engine with a persisted snapshot, an at-risk list page, a student \"Insights\" tab, and an admin Reports centre with six reports. This is a **brownfield** change (NFR-8). It adds no dependencies (ADR-1) and creates two new service folders, `src/server/dashboards/` and `src/server/reports/`.\n\nDesign principles:\n- **Services are the single source.** Server-component widgets, the `/api/*` JSON routes and the CSV exports all call the same service functions. Routes are thin (NFR-6).\n- **Scope is enforced inside services.** Every service function takes an `AccessUser` and intersects with `getAccessibleStudentIds()` (NFR-3).\n- **Pure rules, batch loaders.** Risk thresholds are pure functions (NFR-9). Data for 600 students is loaded in a fixed number of grouped queries, never per student (NFR-1).\n- **Cache only shared aggregates.** Admin and teacher-scoped aggregates use `unstable_cache`. Per-student widgets are cheap and not cached (ADR-3).\n\n### Blockers and dependency gaps\n\nIntake reported **no blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json: blockers: []`, confidence 91 %). The following warnings are resolved by design decisions and are degraded rather than blocked:\n\n| Gap | Requirements | Resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| No `Announcement` model (PRD-12) | FR-8, FR-14, FR-38 | Announcement widgets render `EmptyState` \"Announcements not available yet\". The engagement report omits the read-rate metric and shows a note. The FR-9 \"New announcement\" quick action is hidden because its route does not exist. One `ANNOUNCEMENTS_AVAILABLE = false` constant in `src/server/dashboards/announcements.ts` gates all three, following the stub precedent `parent/overview-service.listUnreadAnnouncements` (ADR-11). **Dependency gap on PRD-12.** |\n| No calendar service/API (PRD-14) | FR-21 | Read `CalendarEvent` directly with school-wide audience, expand recurrences with the existing `calendar/recurrence.expandOccurrences`, take the next 5. |\n| FR-28 history conflicts with \"one row per student per term\" | FR-27, FR-28, FR-29, FR-31 | Keep one row per (student, term). Add `previousLevel` and a capped `history` Json (§4.1). |\n| \"Missing\" is derived, not stored | FR-11, FR-25, FR-37 | One shared predicate `missingWork()` (§3.5), extracted from `assignments/reminders.ts`. |\n| NFR-5 mui-mcp lookup | NFR-5 | Process step for dev and QA. If the MCP server is unavailable during dev, dev must report it as a blocker. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Pages and UI (`src/app/(app)/…`)\n\n| Path | Kind | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `dashboard/page.tsx` | Server page (edit) | Keep the PARENT → `/my-children` redirect. Switch on role and render `AdminDashboard`, `TeacherDashboard` or `StudentDashboard`. Any other role → `notFound()`. | FR-1 |\n| `dashboard/_components/GreetingHeader.tsx` | Server | `greetingFor(now, tz)` + first name + school-tz date + `getCurrentTerm().name`. | FR-3, NFR-7 |\n| `dashboard/_components/{Admin,Teacher,Student}Dashboard.tsx` | Server | MUI `Grid` layout of widgets. Each widget sits in `<Widget>`. | FR-1, FR-2 |\n| `dashboard/_components/widgets/*.tsx` | Async server components, one per widget | Fetch through the service and render with MUI. Chart widgets pass serialisable props to a client chart component. | FR-4–FR-22 |\n| `src/components/Widget/Widget.tsx` | Shared server wrapper (new) | MUI `Card` with a title, an optional \"Updated N min ago\" caption from `computedAt`, `<WidgetErrorBoundary>` and `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>`. It is used by about 20 widgets, so the wrapper pays for itself. | FR-2, FR-24 |\n| `src/components/Widget/WidgetErrorBoundary.tsx` | Client (new) | Class component with `getDerivedStateFromError`. It renders an `Alert` \"This widget could not load\" and a \"Retry\" `Button` that resets state and calls `router.refresh()`. | FR-2 |\n| `src/components/charts/ChartA11y.tsx` | Client (new) | Wraps an x-charts chart with `aria-label={summary}` and a `visuallyHidden` MUI `Table` of the same rows. Used by every chart. | NFR-2 |\n| `dashboard/_components/RefreshButton.tsx` | Client | ADMIN only. Sends `POST /api/dashboard/refresh`, shows a toast through `useToast`, then calls `router.refresh()`. | FR-24 |\n| `insights/at-risk/page.tsx` | Server page (new) | `requireRole(['ADMIN','TEACHER'])`. Filters (level, reason, grade level, section) live in the URL search params. Uses the shared `DataTable` with level `Chip` (text, not colour only), reason chips, a trend arrow icon with an `aria-label`, and actions (open student → `/students/[id]/insights`; message parents → the existing PRD-13 new-conversation flow, prefilled). A CSV button links to `/api/insights/at-risk?…&format=csv`. | FR-29, FR-30, NFR-3 |\n| `students/[id]/insights/page.tsx` | Server page (new) | `assertCanViewStudent`. Shows the current signal values (attendance %, courses below 60 %, missing count), the level badge and a history list from `snapshot.history`. | FR-31, FR-43 |\n| `admin/reports/page.tsx` + `admin/reports/[reportKey]/page.tsx` | Server pages (new) | ADMIN. The index lists the six reports. The report page has an academic-year/term selector and report filters (x-date-pickers for date ranges) in the URL, then a chart, a `DataTable` and a CSV link. Unknown `reportKey` → `notFound()`. | FR-33–FR-39, FR-44 |\n| `src/config/navigation.ts` | Config (edit) | After \"Dashboard\": `Reports` (`/admin/reports`, ADMIN) and `At-risk students` (`/insights/at-risk`, ADMIN and TEACHER). | FR-40 |\n| `src/config/student-tabs.ts` | Config (edit) | Append `{ key: 'insights', label: 'Insights', href: id => \\`/students/${id}/insights\\`, roles: ['ADMIN','TEACHER'] }`. | FR-31 |\n\nReused components (NFR-8): `StatCard`, `DataTable`, `LoadingSkeleton`, `PageHeader`, `EmptyState`, `Toast`/`useToast`. Charts: `LineChart` with `ChartsReferenceLine`, `BarChart` (stacked, histogram) and `Gauge` from `@mui/x-charts` 9.5.0 (NFR-4).\n\n### 2.2 Services — `src/server/dashboards/`\n\n| File | Exports | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `teacher.ts` | `getTodaysClasses(user)` (wraps `attendance-service.getToday` + `nowAndNext`), `getToGrade(user)` (count + oldest 5 ungraded submissions and quiz attempts needing manual grading), `getUpcomingDeadlines(user)` (next 7 days, submission rate = submissions / active enrolments, one grouped query), `getTeacherMessages(user)` (`messaging/conversations.unreadCount` + announcements stub). | FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8 |\n| `student.ts` | `getStudentToday(user)` → `parent/overview-service.getToday(user, user.id)` (holiday-aware). `getDueSoon(user)` (next 7 days + `missingWork`, overdue first, flagged `overdue: true`). `getRecentGrades(user)` → overview-service. `getMyCourses(user)` (`getStudentGrades` for percent/letter, LessonProgress ratio, first incomplete visible lesson). `getTermAttendance(user)` (`countStatuses` + `attendanceRate` over the term range). | FR-10–FR-15 |\n| `admin.ts` | `getKpis()` (cached): active students, active teachers, today's rate and the same weekday −7 days delta via `attendance-service.getOverview`, missing registers, pending absence notes. `getSafeguardingCount(user)` is **uncached** and only called when `isSafeguardingLead(user)`, so the count never sits in a shared cache entry. `getAttendanceTrend()` (cached). `getEnrollmentByGrade()` (cached). `getGradeDistribution()` (cached; uses the §3.4 batch loader). `getUpcomingEvents()`. `getRecentActivity()` (AuditLog `action` startsWith `user.`/`report_card.`/`settings.`, latest 10, actor joined). | FR-16–FR-19, FR-21, FR-22 |\n| `insights.ts` | The `unstable_cache` wrappers and tag constants (§3.6). `getRiskSummary(user)` (counts by level and reason). `getTopAtRisk(user, n)`. | FR-7, FR-20, FR-23, FR-24 |\n| `risk-rules.ts` | **Pure.** `attendanceSignal(pct, threshold)`, `gradesSignal(coursePcts)`, `missingSignal(count)`, `overallLevel(signals)`, `formatReason(signal)`. No Prisma import. | FR-25, FR-26, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n| `risk.ts` | `loadRiskInputs(termId, studentIds)` (batch). `recomputeRiskSnapshots({ force })`: hourly gate, compute, upsert, history append, FR-32 notify, `revalidateTag`. `listAtRisk(user, filters, page)`. `getStudentInsights(user, studentId)`. | FR-25–FR-32, FR-42, FR-43 |\n| `missing-work.ts` | `missingWork({ studentIds, from, to, now })` → `Map<studentId, {assignmentId, dueAt, courseId}[]>`. The shared predicate (§3.5). `assignments/reminders.ts` is refactored to call it with its own 8-day window, keeping its behaviour. | FR-11, FR-25, FR-37 |\n| `announcements.ts` | `ANNOUNCEMENTS_AVAILABLE = false`, `latestAnnouncements()` → `[]`. | FR-8, FR-14, FR-38 |\n\n`greetingFor(now, tz)` and `schoolDaysBack(n, tz)` (the last n dates with at least one `AttendanceSession`) go in `src/lib/dates.ts` next to the existing helpers (ADR-9).\n\n### 2.3 Services — `src/server/reports/`\n\n| File | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `index.ts` | `REPORTS` registry: `key → { title, filterSchema (Zod), run(filters) → { chart, rows, summary }, columns }`. `REPORT_KEYS = Object.keys(REPORTS)`. The page, the API and the CSV all read this registry, so CSV rows equal table rows (FR-35 AC 7) and an unknown key is a 404. | FR-33, FR-44 |\n| `enrollment.ts` | Active students by grade level × section × gender (`groupBy`). New enrollments and archives by month (`$queryRaw date_trunc('month', … AT TIME ZONE tz)`). | FR-34 |\n| `attendance.ts` | Calls `attendance-service.getReport(filters)` for per-student rows, then rolls up by grade level, section or course. Daily trend. Lowest 20 students. | FR-35 |\n| `performance.ts` | Uses the §3.4 batch grade loader. Average percent and letter distribution (`letterFor`) by course and by subject. Section comparison for the same grade × subject. | FR-36 |\n| `completion.ts` | On-time / late (`submittedAt` vs `dueAt`) / missing (`missingWork`) rates by course and by teacher for a date range. | FR-37 |\n| `engagement.ts` | Lesson completion by course (LessonProgress). Distinct parents signed in over the last 7 and 30 days (`AuditLog action='auth.login.success'` joined to PARENT users, with `User.lastLoginAt` as a fallback). Announcement read rate is omitted with a note. | FR-38 |\n| `workload.ts` | Per teacher: courses, distinct students, weekly `TimetableSlot` count, grading backlog (same query as `getToGrade`, grouped by teacher). | FR-39 |\n\n### 2.4 API routes (`src/app/api/…`, thin: `withHandler` → `requireRole` → `parseQuery` (Zod) → service → `ok`/`paginated`/CSV)\n\n| Route | Roles | Service | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `GET /api/dashboard/teacher` | TEACHER | `dashboards/teacher.*` + `getTopAtRisk` | FR-41 |\n| `GET /api/dashboard/student` | STUDENT | `dashboards/student.*` | FR-41 |\n| `GET /api/dashboard/admin` | ADMIN | `dashboards/admin.*` + `getRiskSummary` | FR-41 |\n| `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` | ADMIN | `recomputeRiskSnapshots({ force: true })`, then `revalidateTag` on all tags, then `audit({ action: 'dashboard.refresh' })` | FR-24, FR-27 |\n| `GET /api/insights/at-risk` | ADMIN, TEACHER | `listAtRisk`. Query: `level, reason, gradeLevel, sectionId, page, pageSize ≤ 100, format=csv` | FR-29, FR-30, FR-42 |\n| `GET /api/students/[id]/insights` | ADMIN, TEACHER of the student | `getStudentInsights` (`assertCanViewStudent` → FORBIDDEN) | FR-43 |\n| `GET /api/reports/[reportKey]` | ADMIN | `REPORTS[key].run`. `?format=csv` → `toCsv(columns, rows)` with `Content-Disposition: attachment`. Unknown key → 404 `NOT_FOUND` | FR-44 |\n\nValidators: `src/lib/validators/dashboards.ts` (at-risk filters, insights params) and `src/lib/validators/reports.ts` (`reportKey` enum + per-report filter schemas) (NFR-6).\n\n### 2.5 Background job\n\n`src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` gets one more isolated `try { await recomputeRiskSnapshots() } catch (e) { logger.error(...) }` block. The gate is in the database: skip if `max(computedAt)` for the current term is under 60 minutes old (FR-27, NFR-12, ADR-6).\n\n### 2.6 Notifications\n\nAdd `'insights.student_high_risk'` to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (category ACADEMIC, recipient TEACHER, email default `true`). Send it through the existing `notify()` (FR-32).\n\n### 2.7 Seed\n\n- `prisma/seed-large.ts` + `\"seed:large\": \"tsx prisma/seed-large.ts\"`: a mulberry32 PRNG with a fixed seed, 600 students across Grades 6–8 (8 sections), 40 teachers, timetables, 60 school days of attendance, assignments, submissions and grades. Uses `createMany` in batches of 1,000 (FR-45).\n- `prisma/seed.ts` (edit): plant at least 3 students per level (High, Medium and none) by seeding attendance, grades and missing work that cross the FR-25 thresholds. At the end it calls `recomputeRiskSnapshots({ force: true })` so the list is populated right after seeding (FR-46).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Dashboard request\n\n```\nGET /dashboard\n  └─ page.tsx (server): getCurrentUser() ─ PARENT → redirect('/my-children')\n       └─ <RoleDashboard>  → streams shell + GreetingHeader immediately (NFR-1 first content)\n            ├─ <Widget title=\"To grade\"><Suspense><ToGradeWidget/></Suspense></Widget>\n            │      └─ dashboards/teacher.getToGrade(user) ── Prisma (scoped)\n            ├─ <Widget title=\"At-risk students\">… insights.getTopAtRisk(user,5)\n            │      └─ unstable_cache(['risk','teacher',userId], {revalidate:3600, tags:['insights:at-risk']})\n            │            └─ StudentRiskSnapshot WHERE studentId IN accessible\n            └─ … each widget streams independently; a throw inside one → WidgetErrorBoundary → Alert + Retry\n```\n\n### 3.2 Admin refresh\n\n```\nRefreshButton → POST /api/dashboard/refresh (ADMIN)\n  → risk.recomputeRiskSnapshots({force:true})\n  → revalidateTag('dashboard:admin'), ('dashboard:teacher'), ('insights:at-risk')\n  → audit('dashboard.refresh') → 200 { data: { refreshedAt } }\n  → client: toast + router.refresh() → widgets re-render with new computedAt\n```\n\n### 3.3 Risk recompute (hourly cron or Refresh)\n\n```\nrecomputeRiskSnapshots({force})\n 1. term = getCurrentTerm(); none → return { skipped: 'no-term' }\n 2. if !force and max(computedAt where termId) > now−60min → return { skipped: 'fresh' }\n 3. students = ACTIVE students enrolled in the current term\n 4. inputs = loadRiskInputs(term, students)            ← fixed number of grouped queries\n      attendancePct  : AttendanceRecord groupBy(studentId,status) in term range → attendanceRate()\n      coursePcts     : batch grade loader (§3.4) → computeStudentTerm per (student,course)\n      missingCount   : missingWork({from: today−30d, to: now})\n 5. for each student: signals = [attendanceSignal, gradesSignal, missingSignal]; level = overallLevel(signals)\n 6. upsert StudentRiskSnapshot(studentId, termId):\n      level changed → previousLevel = old.level; history = [ {level,reasons,computedAt}, ...old.history ].slice(0,10)\n      unchanged     → update reasons, signals, computedAt only\n 7. for each (old ∈ {null, MEDIUM}) → HIGH:\n      claimed = updateMany(where {id, OR:[highNotifiedAt null, highNotifiedAt < now−14d]}, data {highNotifiedAt: now})\n      claimed.count === 1 && homeroomTeacherId → notify(homeroomTeacher, 'insights.student_high_risk', {studentId, reasons})\n      no homeroom teacher → logger.warn, skip\n 8. revalidateTag('insights:at-risk')\n```\n\nUpserts run in chunked `$transaction`s of about 100 rows. Step 7 uses an atomic claim, so two concurrent cron processes cannot double-notify (§3 Q8 of the notes).\n\nRisk rules (FR-25, FR-26). These are pure functions, and every boundary has a unit test (NFR-9):\n\n| Signal | Medium | High | No data |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Attendance | `pct < threshold` (SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold, default 90) | `pct < 80` | no records → null |\n| Grades | any course `< 60` | `≥ 2` courses `< 60` **or** any `< 50` | null percents ignored |\n| Missing (30 days) | 3–4 | `≥ 5` | 0–2 → null |\n| **Overall** | exactly one Medium | any High **or** ≥ 2 Medium | otherwise none (`level = null`) |\n\nThe reasons Json is an array of `{ signal: 'ATTENDANCE'|'GRADES'|'MISSING', level, value, label }`. Labels look like `\"Attendance 78 %\"`, `\"2 courses < 60 %\"` and `\"6 missing\"`, and the chips and CSV use them directly.\n\n### 3.4 Batch grade loader (shared by FR-19, FR-25 and FR-36)\n\n`gradebook/batch-grades.ts` exports `loadTermPercents(termId, studentIds?)`. It runs about 5 queries: courses in the term with their scales, grade items, grades, categories and overrides. It groups the rows in memory and calls the existing pure `computeStudentTerm` for each (student, course). The result is `Map<studentId, {courseId, percent, letter}[]>`. Because it uses the same calculation as `getStudentGrades`, dashboard and report numbers equal the Grades tab (FR-13, NFR-8). FR-13 itself calls `getStudentGrades` directly, since it is a single student.\n\n### 3.5 Missing-work predicate\n\nThe predicate is: the assignment is published (`visibleWhere(now)`), `dueAt ∈ [from, min(to, now))`, `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION`, the student is actively enrolled in the course, there is no `Submission`, and there is no `GradeExemption`. It runs as one query for the assignments in the window joined to active enrolments, then subtracts submissions and exemptions in memory. FR-11 uses a \"term start → now\" window for overdue items, FR-25 uses 30 days, and FR-37 uses the report's date range.\n\n### 3.6 Cache keys and tags (FR-23, NFR-3)\n\n| Cached function | Key parts | revalidate | Tags |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `admin.getKpis` (without safeguarding) | `['dash','admin','kpis', today]` | 900 | `dashboard:admin` |\n| `admin.getAttendanceTrend` | `['dash','admin','trend', today]` | 900 | `dashboard:admin` |\n| `admin.getEnrollmentByGrade` | `['dash','admin','enrollment']` | 900 | `dashboard:admin` |\n| `admin.getGradeDistribution` | `['dash','admin','grades', termId]` | 900 | `dashboard:admin` |\n| teacher `getToGrade`, `getUpcomingDeadlines` | `['dash','teacher', userId, …]` | 900 | `dashboard:teacher` |\n| `insights.getRiskSummary` / `getTopAtRisk` | `['risk', 'admin']` or `['risk','teacher', userId]` | 3600 | `insights:at-risk` |\n\nEvery cached value is `{ data, computedAt: string }` and contains no `Date` or `Decimal`. Teacher keys always include `userId`, so no cache entry is ever shared across teachers. The safeguarding count and all student widgets are never cached. `getTodaysClasses` is not cached either, because the attendance taken/not-taken state must be live.\n\n`ponytail:` the cache is per process (ADR-3). Add a shared cache handler if the app runs on more than one instance.\n\n### 3.7 At-risk list and CSV (FR-29, FR-30, FR-42)\n\n```\nGET /api/insights/at-risk?level&reason&gradeLevel&sectionId&page&format\n → scope = getAccessibleStudentIds(user)           // 'ALL' | ids\n → where = { termId: current, level: not null,\n             studentId: scope==='ALL' ? undefined : { in: scope },     // intersection: filters can't widen\n             level?, reasons: reason ? { array_contains: [{signal}] } : undefined,\n             student: { sectionMembers: { some: { section: { gradeLevel?, id: sectionId? } } } } }\n → format=csv ? toCsv(AT_RISK_COLUMNS, allRows) : paginated(rows, page, pageSize)\n```\n\nThe page and the CSV both call `listAtRisk`, so the CSV matches the filtered table. Sort order: HIGH before MEDIUM, then by the number of reasons descending, then by name. The trend is `up` when the level rose since `previousLevel`, `down` when it fell, and `flat` otherwise.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Model Changes (one migration: `add_student_risk_snapshot`)\n\n### 4.1 Prisma\n\n```prisma\nenum RiskLevel {\n  MEDIUM\n  HIGH\n}\n\nmodel StudentRiskSnapshot {\n  id             String     @id @default(cuid())\n  studentId      String\n  termId         String\n  level          RiskLevel?          // null = none\n  previousLevel  RiskLevel?          // FR-28 trend arrow\n  reasons        Json                // [{signal, level, value, label}]\n  signals        Json                // {attendancePct, coursesBelow60, lowestCoursePct, missingCount} for the Insights tab\n  history        Json     @default(\"[]\")  // FR-28: last 10 level changes [{level, reasons, computedAt}]\n  highNotifiedAt DateTime?           // FR-32 14-day claim\n  computedAt     DateTime\n  createdAt      DateTime   @default(now())\n  updatedAt      DateTime   @updatedAt\n  student        User       @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  term           Term       @relation(fields: [termId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n\n  @@unique([studentId, termId])\n  @@index([termId, level])\n  @@index([termId, computedAt])\n}\n```\n\n`User` and `Term` get back-relations. `history` is appended only when the level changes, so hourly runs do not grow it. `ponytail:` it is capped at 10 entries. Add a history table if long-range trend analytics are ever needed (ADR-5).\n\n### 4.2 Optional index\n\nAdd `AuditLog @@index([createdAt])` only if `EXPLAIN` on `seed:large` shows the FR-22 query is slow (ADR-7). It is not in the base migration.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Security and Privacy\n\n- **Authorization.** Every page and handler calls `requireRole`. Services re-check scope: they take `AccessUser`, read `getAccessibleStudentIds`, and **intersect** it with filters (NFR-3, FR-42). The student insights endpoint uses `assertCanViewStudent` → 403 FORBIDDEN.\n- **Cache isolation.** Teacher keys include `userId`. The safeguarding count is never cached and is shown only when `isSafeguardingLead` (FR-16).\n- **CSV.** Every export goes through `src/server/csv.ts` `toCsv`/`escapeCsvCell`, which guards against formula injection (FR-30, FR-33).\n- **SQL.** Only tagged-template `$queryRaw`. `$queryRawUnsafe` is never used (ADR-7).\n- **Audit.** `dashboard.refresh` is audited. Report reads are not audited, which matches the existing admin read endpoints.\n- **Notification content.** The notification contains the student name and reason labels only, no grades detail, and links to `/students/[id]/insights`, which is scope-checked.\n\n## 6. Performance (NFR-1)\n\n| Surface | Budget | How it is met |\n|---|---|---|\n| Dashboards: first content | < 1.5 s | The shell and greeting render without waiting. Widgets stream behind Suspense. Admin aggregates are cached for 15 minutes. At-risk data is read from the snapshot table and never computed live. |\n| Reports | < 3 s | Grouped queries and `$queryRaw` bucketing. The batch grade loader uses about 5 queries. No per-student loops. |\n| Risk recompute | Background | About 10 queries + chunked upserts for 600 students. It runs at most hourly. |\n\nDev must measure these against `seed:large` and add indexes only where `EXPLAIN` shows a sequential-scan hotspot.\n\n## 7. Testing hooks (NFR-9, NFR-10)\n\n- **Unit (Vitest):** `risk-rules.ts` boundaries: 90/89.9, 80/79.9, 60/59.9, 50/49.9, missing counts 2/3/4/5, Medium+Medium → High, threshold override. Also `greetingFor` hour boundaries in the tz, and the `missingWork` window edges.\n- **Integration:** each report's `run()` on the default seed with known totals. CSV rows equal table rows. The at-risk scope intersection: a teacher filtering by another section gets 0 rows outside scope. Refresh revalidates the cache, so `computedAt` changes. The FR-32 14-day claim fires only once. The default seed yields at least 3 students per level (FR-46).\n- **E2E (Playwright + axe):** one spec per role dashboard plus the parent redirect, `/insights/at-risk`, and `/admin/reports/attendance` with CSV download.\n- **Lint:** no `console.log`. Logging uses `src/lib/logger.ts`.\n\n## 8. Out of scope (NFR-11)\n\nNo drag-and-drop layouts, no ML scoring, no scheduled report emails, and no changes to PRD-17/18 behaviour. No Announcement model or calendar API is built here (they are dependency gaps, §1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | `dashboard/page.tsx` role switch + PARENT redirect kept (§2.1) |\n| FR-2 | `Widget` + `WidgetErrorBoundary` + Suspense/`LoadingSkeleton` (§2.1, §3.1) |\n| FR-3 | `GreetingHeader`, `greetingFor` in `src/lib/dates.ts`, `getCurrentTerm` |\n| FR-4 | `teacher.getTodaysClasses` (attendance-service `getToday` + `nowAndNext`), live |\n| FR-5 | `teacher.getToGrade`, cached per teacher |\n| FR-6 | `teacher.getUpcomingDeadlines` |\n| FR-7 | `insights.getTopAtRisk(user, 5)` from snapshots |\n| FR-8 | `teacher.getTeacherMessages`: `unreadCount` + announcements stub (§1 gap) |\n| FR-9 | `QuickActionsWidget`: static MUI links; \"New announcement\" hidden (§1) |\n| FR-10 | `student.getStudentToday` → overview-service `getToday` |\n| FR-11 | `student.getDueSoon` + `missingWork` (§3.5) |\n| FR-12 | `student.getRecentGrades` → overview-service |\n| FR-13 | `student.getMyCourses` → `getStudentGrades` + LessonProgress |\n| FR-14 | `announcements.latestAnnouncements` → `EmptyState` (§1) |\n| FR-15 | `student.getTermAttendance` + x-charts `Gauge` |\n| FR-16 | `admin.getKpis` (cached) + uncached `getSafeguardingCount` for leads |\n| FR-17 | `admin.getAttendanceTrend` + `LineChart` + `ChartsReferenceLine` at the threshold |\n| FR-18 | `admin.getEnrollmentByGrade` + stacked `BarChart` |\n| FR-19 | `admin.getGradeDistribution` via the batch grade loader (§3.4) |\n| FR-20 | `insights.getRiskSummary` |\n| FR-21 | `admin.getUpcomingEvents` (CalendarEvent + `expandOccurrences`) |\n| FR-22 | `admin.getRecentActivity` (AuditLog prefixes) |\n| FR-23 | `insights.ts` `unstable_cache` wrappers (§3.6) |\n| FR-24 | `computedAt` → \"Updated N min ago\"; `RefreshButton` + `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` (§3.2) |\n| FR-25 | `risk-rules.ts` signals + `risk.loadRiskInputs` (§3.3) |\n| FR-26 | `risk-rules.overallLevel` |\n| FR-27 | `StudentRiskSnapshot` model + migration; cron hook with DB gate (§2.5, §4.1) |\n| FR-28 | `previousLevel` + capped `history` Json (§4.1) |\n| FR-29 | `/insights/at-risk` page + `risk.listAtRisk` (§3.7) |\n| FR-30 | URL filters + `toCsv` from the same `listAtRisk` |\n| FR-31 | `studentTabs` 'insights' entry + `students/[id]/insights` page |\n| FR-32 | Step 7 of §3.3: atomic `highNotifiedAt` claim + `notify('insights.student_high_risk')` |\n| FR-33 | `/admin/reports` + `REPORTS` registry + year/term selector + CSV (§2.3) |\n| FR-34 | `reports/enrollment.ts` |\n| FR-35 | `reports/attendance.ts` (reuses `attendance-service.getReport`) |\n| FR-36 | `reports/performance.ts` (batch grade loader + `letterFor`) |\n| FR-37 | `reports/completion.ts` + `missingWork` |\n| FR-38 | `reports/engagement.ts`; announcement read rate omitted (§1) |\n| FR-39 | `reports/workload.ts` |\n| FR-40 | `src/config/navigation.ts` entries |\n| FR-41 | `/api/dashboard/{teacher,student,admin}` GET + `/refresh` POST (§2.4) |\n| FR-42 | `GET /api/insights/at-risk` with scope intersection (§3.7) |\n| FR-43 | `GET /api/students/[id]/insights` + `assertCanViewStudent` |\n| FR-44 | `GET /api/reports/[reportKey]`, registry-validated, 404 for unknown keys |\n| FR-45 | `prisma/seed-large.ts` + `seed:large` script (§2.7) |\n| FR-46 | `prisma/seed.ts` planted risk cohorts + forced recompute (§2.7) |\n| NFR-1 | Streaming widgets, caching, batch loaders, snapshot reads (§6) |\n| NFR-2 | `ChartA11y` aria summary + visually hidden table; text badges (§2.1) |\n| NFR-3 | Scope in services, intersection, per-teacher cache keys (§5) |\n| NFR-4 | MUI / MUI X only; shared components reused (§2.1) |\n| NFR-5 | mui-mcp lookup as a dev/QA process step; unavailability = blocker (§1) |\n| NFR-6 | Thin handlers, validators files, `paginated`, service folders (§2.4) |\n| NFR-7 | `src/lib/dates.ts` / `schoolToday` for every window; SQL `AT TIME ZONE` |\n| NFR-8 | Reuse table in §2 (attendance-service, grade-calc, overview-service, csv, notify, audit, components) |\n| NFR-9 | Test hooks in §7 |\n| NFR-10 | `logger` only; lint/typecheck/test green (§7) |\n| NFR-11 | Out of scope (§8); rule-based `risk-rules.ts` |\n| NFR-12 | 3600 s risk cache + hourly DB-gated recompute (§2.5, §3.6) |\n","numLines":345,"startLine":1,"totalLines":345}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CVkdcp6PGLUeWqEUwWLTKA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
