{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgtd9JPE8Ldam1oKUu1mf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `arch-api-contracts` sub-task for SH-16 is done, which completes the architect phase. Both files are written: `api-contracts.json` came first and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` last. The handoff is `complete`, with no blockers and 7 endpoints.\n\n**`artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json`** defines 7 new endpoints, all from section 2.4 of the system design:\n- **Dashboards:** `GET /api/dashboard/teacher`, `/student` and `/admin`, plus `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` (admin only; it recomputes risk, clears the cached dashboard data and records an audit entry).\n- **At-risk list:** `GET /api/insights/at-risk`, with filters, pagination and a CSV option. Teachers only ever see their own students, even if a filter points at someone else's.\n- **Student insights:** `GET /api/students/:id/insights`.\n- **Reports:** `GET /api/reports/:reportKey`. An unknown report name returns 404, and the CSV has exactly the same rows as the on-screen table.\n\nThe file also covers the shared response and error formats, the reusable data shapes, each report's filters and columns, and 4 non-HTTP contracts: the risk recompute job, the new high-risk notification type, the risk rules and the missing-work check.\n\nEvery requirement ID the file cites exists in `requirements.json`, and the JSON parses.\n\nDecisions I made that the system design didn't spell out:\n- The at-risk list returns the time the risk data was last computed.\n- The refresh endpoint returns how many students it recomputed and whether it skipped because there is no current term.\n- The admin dashboard leaves out the safeguarding count entirely unless the caller is a safeguarding lead.\n- I fixed the filters and columns for each of the six reports.\n\nThings dev-planning should know:\n- **Missing data sources:** announcements still have no data source, so the related widgets and metric return empty lists. Upcoming events read the calendar table directly.\n- **Stale file:** `threat-model-notes.json` is still the old SH-14 file, and no architect sub-task owns it.\n- **Archived files:** I moved the old SH-15 versions of both files to `artifacts/architect/.prev-SH-15/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1036,"cache_read_input_tokens":65415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1036,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dc3003b-f495-40f4-b937-7fc5d8e13052","uuid":"2724669a-bba6-46b9-a45a-e4541349c1d5","timestamp":"2026-11-10T04:34:16.825Z","request_id":"req_011Cgtd9JAZszV1J8zv9RKnW"}
